{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted","id":1265540,"title":"[Dev Blog] The Lunar Exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-08T11:52:42-08:00","id":1265540,"title":"[Dev Blog] The Lunar Exalted","content":"Let's see if this works... <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-lunar-exalted-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">New official blog post on Lunars</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T11:56:57-08:00","id":1265541,"title":"","content":"Thoughts I posted elsewhere:<br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think it looks good. I particularly like the reference to the idea that the Lunars are effectively balanced between their duel natures, rather than having to commit to one over the other (or being threatened with one overwhelming), I find the framing of how the Pact has stymied the power of the Realm to be credible (effectively complementing some new ideas introduced in What Fire Has Wrought, such as ambitions to conquer the West), and I like the way in which it introduces a variety of new name personas (including the idea of one group in which a Shogunate-era Lunar explicitly outranks a First Age elder).</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Probably more detail later.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T12:07:36-08:00","id":1265548,"title":"","content":"A great read! I just introduced my first Lunar NPC in my chronicle an these updates really help characterize her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T12:20:08-08:00","id":1265552,"title":"","content":"Oh, I neglected to quote myself mentioning the concept of schools.<br /> <br /> I like that as a way of reconciling the presence of older, more established Lunars with the idea that there's not exactly a guiding authority for Lunars, a process of systemizing their differences in strategy and philosophy (and some of the ensuing conflict over the same), and particularly the impetus it provides for Lunars to have regular meetings with one another, either one-to-one or in special gatherings. One of those actually plays off of an idea I've always had about a certain Lunar character, one who is actually fairly estranged from the Pact as a whole, but might still occasionally journey out to meet with her mentor again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T14:16:54-08:00","id":1265578,"title":"","content":"A lot of this is what I expected, from Vance and Minton's previous statements, but I'm still pleased to see it. It looks pretty decent:<br /> <br /> Several points:<br /> <br /> 1) The Lunars seem much more pro-active, due to a few small shifts. They changed their own Castes, rather than losing them. The Realm used to be even more powerful, but has been held at bay and even pushed back by the Lunars. The First-Age Lunars are no longer described as the Solar's lieutenants, but rather &quot;fighting alongside&quot; the Solars. And of course there's a specific situation of &quot;Lunar victories&quot;. This actually all ends up with a Time of Tumult whose basic situation is pretty similar as in 2nd ed, but there's a very definite presentation and background change to it.<br /> <br /> 2) I find it interesting that the Lunars specifically target the heirs to the Shogunate, rather than Dragonblood in general (obviously most Dragonblood societies do claim descent from the Shogunate, but not all). That helps build the idea of the Elders' vendetta as, well, a vendetta.<br /> <br /> 3) Though short and, perhaps obvious, I liked the bit about building support amongst anti-Realm dissidents. I can well imagine inner-threshold rebels having secret meetings with a Lunar; they may hate and distrust the Anathema, but they're willing to make a deal with the devil to drive out the Realm. It also helps give a very guerilla vibe for the Lunar war effort, as opposed to the Beastman horde idea that previous editions tended to focus on. Which, considering Lunars' shapeshifting powerset, is what a lot of Lunars would gravitate towards (its certainly how I've generally seen Lunar PCs act).<br /> <br /> 4) The factions of 2nd ed were in some cases a bit nonsensical; the Sun King Seneschals wanted to serve people who vanished in the mists of pre-history, the Winding Path wanted to do something the whole Silver Pact had agreed to anyway, the Wardens of Gaia wanted to protect nature in a pre-modern setting where it wasn't really under threat (except maybe from Deathlords). And then of course, you had the problem of size; the Crossroads Society did make sense in terms of sorcerers sharing knowledge, but it was hard to see how 100 Lunars across the entire world could really be said to belong to the same organisation.<br /> So charismatic or skilled elders surrounded by younger Lunars and allies in a local-ish area makes a lot more sense. There were a few examples; the Thousand Fangs were a pack loyal to Raksi who subjugated lands to her south-east, for example. But there wasn't much.<br /> But they've gone a bit further here and made it less leaders and followers, and more teachers and students. Which I think is even better; a)from a verisimilitude perspective, since it's pretty difficult to control Lunars, and b)from a gameplay perspective.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if you're running a Lunars' game, I think having the PCs share an NPC kung-fu sifu or sorcerous mentor who they can go and hang out with in his isolated mountaintop grove (or, say, her overgrown ancient library deep in the jungle where she can teach them Celestial spells from the Book of Three Circles) works much better than having an NPC faction-boss who orders them around. PCs tend not to react well to that, Lunar PCs especially.<br /> <br /> 5)TBH, I don't really like the Shadow Fang Vanguard. I don't like their name, they don't really inspire me with anything interesting to do, and it seems a bit odd they're so far from the Realm (though perhaps their base is merely far from the Realm for defence, and they launch far-reaching guerilla tactics). But I think it's a good example of the kind of faction you'd get; arguments not about whether the Lunars should focus on defending nature or serving their non-existent Solar Mates, but rather how best to fight the Realm. The other examples of inter-Lunar factional arguments all make sense to me too; I can definitely imagine a group of Lunar PCs squabbling over whether its okay to use Shadowlands or ally with the Fair Folk against the Realm.<br /> Incidentally, I'm interested to see that Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi went to war over the Pact's future direction. I wonder whether we'll get more details on that. And also, considering the distance, how that worked. Subversion of local tribes? Lunar vs Lunar combat? You can send Lunars that distance far easier than armies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-08-2018, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T14:17:06-08:00","id":1265579,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m loving it! It would be fun to play a game where the Circle wants to make a new Lunar prominent Delibrative! Lunar being the most Numerous Celestials, with some Solars who joined. They kill all the current generation of Sidereals and so the next generation come in as advisors. The Dragonblooded are scuttled but new Clans arise redeemed and ready to serve Creation. The Solara who aren\u2019t allied are all of a sudden switching places with Lunars, becoming insurgentsbut also guarding the rim from Fairfolk, Abyssals and the Infernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T14:18:18-08:00","id":1265580,"title":"","content":"Also I thought original talk was to have it they always had three Castes? Not displeased but just curious that they still kept the 5 caste origins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T14:35:40-08:00","id":1265586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265578#post1265578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Essentially, if you're running a Lunars' game, I think having the PCs share an NPC kung-fu sifu or sorcerous mentor who they can go and hang out with in his isolated mountaintop grove (or, say, her overgrown ancient library deep in the jungle where she can teach them Celestial spells from the Book of Three Circles) works much better than having an NPC faction-boss who orders them around. PCs tend not to react well to that, Lunar PCs especially.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or indeed, for your shanan-ha (I'll familiarise myself with the exact term eventually) to turn up on <i>your</i> door for a chat, a check-in, a moment of respite. Given what the Silver Pact is up to, I imagine that for the teachers of schools of activity to be cloistered is the exception more often than the rule.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, a conversation a while ago came up about the question of whether or not Dominions would make for good expansion material in the way that underdeveloped Terrestrial groups did for Heirs of the Shogunate. I maintain that they do not, but think that schools, present and past, sound like a very strong thing to put into that slot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5)TBH, I don't like the Shadow Fang Vanguard's name, and it seems a bit odd they're so far from the Realm (though perhaps their base is merely far from the Realm for defence, and they launch far-reaching guerilla tactics). But I think it's a good example of the kind of faction you'd get; arguments not about whether the Lunars should focus on defending nature or serving their non-existent Solar Mates, but rather how best to fight the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>In their case, I think it's going much further than how they're fighting the Realm; it's about how Lunars relate to one another! The motivation to have that kind of authority over others (or to be under it) strikes me as being on a whole other level, especially if their own freedom is a common sticking point for Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> I can imagine that there are Lunars that are in agreement with any kinds of methods employed, but are deeply offended by the idea of a bunch of Lunars being within such a hierarchical system, from whichever direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I'm interested to see that Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi went to war over the Pact's future direction. I wonder whether we'll get more details on that. And also, considering the distance, how that worked. Subversion of local tribes? Lunar vs Lunar combat? You can send Lunars that distance far easier than armies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it depends on how the armies are organized. Centrally controlled, heavily regimented blocks have difficulty, but widely distributed war bands who are communicating with one another and have common objectives, but are otherwise largely independent, engaging in a lot of things like lightning raids and surprise attacks?<br /> <br /> That kind of thing can be very effective in that kind of terrain, especially if your purpose is not to seize territory but to kill enemies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T14:40:36-08:00","id":1265589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I thought original talk was to have it they always had three Castes? Not displeased but just curious that they still kept the 5 caste origins.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they said that, just that the Lunars changed themselves to adapt to new situations.<br /> <br /> Although what the devs (I don't remember if it was the old or new devs) said was that the Lunars were one thing in the Primordial War, that they changed themselves in the First Age to fit the new world, and they changed themselves again afterwards.<br /> <br /> This gives more detail for the second change than the first: did they always have 5 castes? Did they create those 5 castes like they did the later 3? It says in the first age they became &quot;guardians, guides, world-walkers, judges and mystics&quot;: 5 things that do not really look a lot like the savage monsters described in the Divine Revolution section.<br /> But it's not very exact, and probably isn't supposed to be, as this is rather a &quot;lost in the mists of time&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-08-2018, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T15:24:04-08:00","id":1265599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265586#post1265586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or indeed, for your shanan-ha (I'll familiarise myself with the exact term eventually)</div> </div> </div> </div>Shahan-ya. I was trying to work out why they used a new term, rather than something more resonant. I couldn't find where it's from. Shahan, of course, means &quot;King (of)&quot; in Persian. (Shahanshah is King of Kings.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> to turn up on <i>your</i> door for a chat, a check-in, a moment of respite. Given what the Silver Pact is up to, I imagine that for the teachers of schools of activity to be cloistered is the exception more often than the rule. </div> </div> </div>Could be. Lunars are extremely mobile, after all (and persecution encourages that). Of course, even Lunars aren't all nomadic, but many may have multiple homes/dens/places of power over a large territory.<br /> <br /> But I was just thinking that, when running a game, it might be practical to have the PCs' mentor have a base where they can visit her for advice/teaching and probabaly find her there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, a conversation a while ago came up about the question of whether or not Dominions would make for good expansion material in the way that underdeveloped Terrestrial groups did for Heirs of the Shogunate. I maintain that they do not, but think that schools, present and past, sound like a very strong thing to put into that slot. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... tbh, I think examples of both would be good. (I mean, obviously the main Lunar book will have examples. But more is good.)<br /> Including some which are connected (to show how they can be), but generally probably mostly as separate things, in a way that Dragonblood societies and the countries they rule are not so separate.<br /> <br /> Though, I believe Heirs to the Shogunate will include some mechanics bound to those locations/societies; heirloom weapons, Gunzota armour, sorcerous initiations, etc.<br /> <br /> I'm quite happy to see more domains written up, but, tbh, I don't think they're as significant or need any mechanical support. I'm not sure if their lower significance to Lunars is why you think they'd be a bad inclusion? But I can see that &quot;we'll include rules for playing a character from the Dominion of Halta/Chiaroscoro/the Haslanti League&quot; doesn't really work well as a Kickstarter goal.<br /> (A, because they don't need any rules, and B, because the Dominions are different enough in character from TSR projects that I suspect the societies that were formerly Lunar projects may not necessarily still be. And it's harder to get people excited about Stretch Goals relating to entirely new stuff which people don't know if they'll be interested in. If they say &quot;with $X000 pledged we'll detail the exciting desert Dominion of Yuros-Ti&quot;, that doesn't encourage previous fans the way people who love Lookshy will be excited by a pledge about Lookshy).<br /> <br /> I'd be fine with &quot;we'll add another 10 pages of Dominion examples&quot;. And they don't even need that much detail: half a page on each would be more than enough. It's a fine thing to put in the book... but probably doesn't work well as a Stretch goal.<br /> <br /> Saying this... expanding plot hooks isn't always a good thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Whereas I guess a Shahan-Ya and his/her students are a bit more viable in terms of added mechanics (sorcerous initiations, an iconic martial art, etc). And you could include people like, say, Raksi, I guess.<br /> Though it still probably doesn't work quite as well as Lookshy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it depends on how the armies are organized. Centrally controlled, heavily regimented blocks have difficulty, but widely distributed war bands who are communicating with one another and have common objectives, but are otherwise largely independent, engaging in a lot of things like lightning raids and surprise attacks?<br /> <br /> That kind of thing can be very effective in that kind of terrain, especially if your purpose is not to seize territory but to kill enemies. </div> </div> </div>It's not so much the terrain, as that Mahalanka is over 3400 miles from the Nameless Lair (as the crow flies). That's why I suggested subversion of local tribes; I can't really see it as viable for a bunch of warbands to travel thousands of miles, either through the jungle or (about half the way) along the river going past a whole bunch of hostile places like Grayfalls, for lightning raids and surprise attacks on the enemy's core territories.<br /> But I could see it as viable to send your Lunar students thousands of miles (they can probably travel much faster, after all, what with the flying) to bribe and cajole local tribes to rebel and fight your rival's forces. Or perhaps encourage/help neighbouring nations to invade.<br /> <br /> It could even be a whole proxy war of course, but I think it doesn't have to be quite that. More like Germany encouraging far-off Japan to attack its enemy the USSR, that kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-08-2018, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T16:42:00-08:00","id":1265613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265599#post1265599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much the terrain, as that Mahalanka is over 3400 miles from the Nameless Lair (as the crow flies). That's why I suggested subversion of local tribes; I can't really see it as viable for a bunch of warbands to travel thousands of miles, either through the jungle or (about half the way) along the river going past a whole bunch of hostile places like Grayfalls, for lightning raids and surprise attacks on the enemy's core territories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I wasn't quite certain of how far apart they were. I can still see ways for it to work: if one is the aggressor more than the other, they send their forces to set up base right outside of the other's borders, and have them project attacks from there; they might issue it as a kind of formal challenge in which they designate a section of jungle in between both of them in which to go all Hunger Games until they agree to call it off or there's a definite winner.<br /> <br /> I would expect warriors to pack up and commit to such a distant endeavour when there's a grinning Lunar at their back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T17:07:42-08:00","id":1265622,"title":"","content":"Didn't MHS eschew contact with everyone, including the Pact, in order to do his own thing? It seems odd that he's clashing over its policy unless that policy is &quot;step to the side and stay out of my way&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T17:11:44-08:00","id":1265624,"title":"","content":"While I know Exalted doesn't have anything to do with oWoD anymore (if ever) but is anyone else getting Werewolf vibes from the Shadow Fang Vanguard? Shape-shifters from a north eastern part of the world who are all about dominance and have beef with a group with silver in the name. Feels very much like the Silver Fangs vs the Shadow Lords and if so I approve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6585-nightshrike","name":"nightshrike","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T17:19:47-08:00","id":1265626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nightshrike</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265624#post1265624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I know Exalted doesn't have anything to do with oWoD anymore (if ever) but is anyone else getting Werewolf vibes from the Shadow Fang Vanguard? Shape-shifters from a north eastern part of the world who are all about dominance and have beef with a group with silver in the name. Feels very much like the Silver Fangs vs the Shadow Lords and if so I approve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow Lords never broke off quite like that. One of the allowances afforded to a long war that's actually going in your favor without having to change your program.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T18:12:53-08:00","id":1265631,"title":"","content":"I like this quite a bit, but what interests me the most is the potential conflicts over the future of the Lunar Exalted and Creation as a whole. I think that could be an great basis of a game focusing on Silver Pact politics in place (or alongside) of fighting the legacy of the Usurpation; deciding what the Lunar Exalted should become once their long vendetta is settled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T18:13:38-08:00","id":1265632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265622#post1265622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't MHS eschew contact with everyone, including the Pact, in order to do his own thing? It seems odd that he's clashing over its policy unless that policy is &quot;step to the side and stay out of my way&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between this and a prior reference in a Lunar preview, I'm afraid it looks like they may be stepping away from that portrayal of him.<br /> <br /> Unless it's meant to be read as his cloistering having been relatively recent, or that fight with Raksi having happened a long time ago.<br /> <br /> But I think the reading of it being revised is less strained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T18:20:42-08:00","id":1265634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265632#post1265632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Between this and a prior reference in a Lunar preview, I'm afraid it looks like they may be stepping away from that portrayal of him.<br /> <br /> Unless it's meant to be read as his cloistering having been relatively recent, or that fight with Raksi having happened a long time ago.<br /> <br /> But I think the reading of it being revised is less strained.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In fact, MHS can be just as much as a jerk in past editions, but come off as a friend to the Silver Pact-less organization means less oversight and people not realizing he's gone off the deep end. To them, he's just a very old Lunar with a very understandable grudge that leads him to heading a very militant school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T18:56:35-08:00","id":1265644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265634#post1265634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In fact, MHS can be just as much as a jerk in past editions, but come off as a friend to the Silver Pact-less organization means less oversight and people not realizing he's gone off the deep end. To them, he's just a very old Lunar with a very understandable grudge that leads him to heading a very militant school.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0FaQgw33_Es\" data-code=\"0FaQgw33_Es\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0FaQgw33_Es/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T20:03:43-08:00","id":1265657,"title":"","content":"I think Ma-Ha-Suchi changed as of the Third Edition core, for anyone wondering what his basic stance was absent the context of his war with Raksi!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T20:23:17-08:00","id":1265661,"title":"","content":"I like the acknowledgement of modern reasons to oppose the Realm, and the existence of Elders hailing from different periods in Creation\u2019s history. Trying to push Lunars as having a cohesive, setting-wide organisation is never going to make much sense, though. Call it a qualified success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T21:04:11-08:00","id":1265668,"title":"","content":"For the record, long-distance warfare gets a lot easier to pull off when you can bind a Second Circle demon and send it to go mess with your enemy once a month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T21:11:25-08:00","id":1265671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265634#post1265634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In fact, MHS can be just as much as a jerk in past editions, but come off as a friend to the Silver Pact-less organization means less oversight and people not realizing he's gone off the deep end. To them, he's just a very old Lunar with a very understandable grudge that leads him to heading a very militant school.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. 2e had that terrible Nameless Lair writeup, and that past edition can keep it, buried under the other inexplicable Wyld anomalies hiding atrocity centers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T21:18:05-08:00","id":1265672,"title":"","content":"I agree with others that this is very cool, gets my brain humming...and I'm also confused about the home base of the Shadow Fang Vanguard. Granted, from that description, I'm assuming they're hanging out up near Halta, which doesn't really seem like the front lines of the War on the Realm or any other &quot;vanguard&quot; type region, but &quot;the Forests of the North East&quot; could be as far in as Medo, technically.<br /> <br /> Vance, if you're reading this, it might be worth clarifying that a bit.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the bit about Primordial War Lunars being these devastating god monsters and then changing themselves to fit the First Age inspired me to come up with a Lunar elder. During the late first age, she was a teacher, a friend, a community leader, a kind person who always had some cookies baking and never raised a hand to anyone. While many knew she was a veteran of the Divine Revolution, very few people knew any details of her war record and tended to assume she coordinated things and helped keep spirits up. But, now, she just liked to relax and enjoy life with her spouse and the children she was teaching. <br /> <br /> When the Usurpation came, due to an oversight, the Dragon Blooded strike team sent against her was not read in on her ancient records and was thus woefully unprepared for &quot;Five Valleys&quot; Sekmet, She of the Impenetrable Coat, the Slayer of Mountains, resuming her true god beast form for the first time in an age.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure she survived, but I think she could be a fun shahan-ya for a group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T21:20:07-08:00","id":1265673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265661#post1265661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the acknowledgement of modern reasons to oppose the Realm, and the existence of Elders hailing from different periods in Creation\u2019s history. Trying to push Lunars as having a cohesive, setting-wide organisation is never going to make much sense, though. Call it a qualified success.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I read their organization sounded anything but cohesive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T21:43:26-08:00","id":1265678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265599#post1265599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shahan-ya. I was trying to work out why they used a new term, rather than something more resonant. I couldn't find where it's from. Shahan, of course, means &quot;King (of)&quot; in Persian. (Shahanshah is King of Kings.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What surprises me is that it's explicitly identified as &quot;Old Realm for 'guide' or 'teacher,'&quot; which wouldn't seem to make it an inherently Lunar title. Unless there's an implicit &quot;of Lunars&quot; in the word that would be understood to native Old Realm speakers, I would expect Sidereals and Gods, and possibly other groups as well, to also use the title shahan-ya.<br /> <br /> I guess this <i>could</i> even be the start of a gradual retcon, phasing out the real-world title &quot;sifu&quot; in favor of an Exalted-specific term, analogous to the use of &quot;daiklave&quot;? But I expect not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T22:16:19-08:00","id":1265691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265661#post1265661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to push Lunars as having a cohesive, setting-wide organisation is never going to make much sense, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be why there's only twenty of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T23:33:35-08:00","id":1265704,"title":"","content":"I wonder how His Divine Lunar Presence fits into the Vanguard/Pact philosophical split, because he certainly seems to be assuming a position of leadership among Lunars in a direct fight against the Realm, but isn't apparently treated as the Vanguard are by the Silver Pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T00:18:13-08:00","id":1265708,"title":"","content":"I'd guess it's because he doesn't require the other Lunars on the Caul to join an explicitly hierarchical organisation of which he is the leader.<br /> My impression is that he's some kind of charismatic and respected elder leader. So other Lunars on the Caul are happy to take his advice and get behind his plans. Rather than him being the explicit commander of all Lunars on the Caul.<br /> <br /> I guess also, that's just the Lunars on the Caul. The Shadow Fang Vanguard (still not big into that name) believe that all Lunars should be part of a hierarchical organisation, not just ones in the North-East Forest, they just haven't convinced the rest of the Pact.<br /> <br /> So even if there are 10 Lunars on the Caul and they did all take orders from Shas Oka, that doesn't mean Shas Oka believes the other 390 Lunars should obey him. It's just a practical organisational thing in a small and discrete area, rather than an ideology.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Before I respond to other points, I wanted to point out something I thought was interesting.<br /> <br /> Holden was very big into barbarianism. He wanted it to be a key theme of Lunars. Not the ideological barbarianism of 1st ed, but a barbarian aesthetic.<br /> I haven't particularly got that from any of the 3rd ed fluff we've seen so far. I wonder if it's been dropped.<br /> Or, perhaps, since it's aesthetic, it's something that'd maybe be most noticeable in the book's art, not the fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T00:41:19-08:00","id":1265712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anaximander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265704#post1265704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how His Divine Lunar Presence fits into the Vanguard/Pact philosophical split, because he certainly seems to be assuming a position of leadership among Lunars in a direct fight against the Realm, but isn't apparently treated as the Vanguard are by the Silver Pact.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are obviously other Lunars who are followed as leaders of the Pact, but it seems that this is generally a matter of voluntarily rallying around someone. The Vanguard want an actual ordered hierarchy with ranks, a chain of command and enforced uniting laws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T00:46:34-08:00","id":1265713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265634#post1265634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In fact, MHS can be just as much as a jerk in past editions, but come off as a friend to the Silver Pact-less organization means less oversight and people not realizing he's gone off the deep end. To them, he's just a very old Lunar with a very understandable grudge that leads him to heading a very militant school.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I was discussing Ma-Ha-Suchi with Isator Levi a while ago, he reminded to actually go and re-read Ma-Ha-Suchi's description carefully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted 3rd edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ma-Ha-Suchi survived the destruction of the First Age, exile in the Wyld, the scourge of the Contagion and the armies of chaos, and he carries his scars with sullen pride. He greets visitors in his war form, a towering amalgam of man, wolf, and goat, and speaks in a voice like silver bells. Those who rouse his attention without good cause die on the end of his moonsilver lance, and their skulls mark the boundary of his domain.<br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s territory abuts the southern terminus of the Scavenger Lands, and shields the wealthy empires of the deep Southeast from the Realm-controlled coastal states\u2014not that the ancient Lunar harbors love for any of his neighbors. His beast-blooded children raid the surrounding lands ceaselessly. They suffer no permanent roads to be laid through their father\u2019s dominion, and harry what river traffic is bold enough to dare their wrath. Only those who purchase Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2019s temporary goodwill through lavish tribute may pass safely through his domain, and then only if the great beast is in the mood to be honored or flattered.<br /> Made both wrathful and weary by the turning of the ages, Ma-Ha-Suchi shuns the politics of the Exalted. He will occasionally trade rumors or choice bits of magical plunder with respectful envoys from the Silver Pact, and has at times consented to take younger Lunars under his guidance for a year or two\u2014but for the most part, he maintains his solitude. He does not speak of the personal significance of his jungle ruins, nor is he interested in the greater schemes of luminaries such as Sha\u2019a Oka or the Queen of Fangs. Luna has granted him strength of arm, quicksilver wits, keen eyes to witness the decay of the world, and endless enemies who wish to spend their lives failing to take his territory for their own. For seven centuries, that has been enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly, he's still isolationist in terms of the Pact as a whole. But there's a distinct lack of a)him being insane, and b)having a particularly militant ideology. I mean, he's just a barbarian king, doing what barbarian kings do, defending his territory. There's no &quot;we must conquer the Realm, tear down its cities and slay every single Dragonblood.&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps that was the direction they went to war over? Maybe Raksi wanted the Pact to be more organised, and he didn't?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T00:51:45-08:00","id":1265714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265672#post1265672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with others that this is very cool, gets my brain humming...and I'm also confused about the home base of the Shadow Fang Vanguard. Granted, from that description, I'm assuming they're hanging out up near Halta, which doesn't really seem like the front lines of the War on the Realm or any other &quot;vanguard&quot; type region, but &quot;the Forests of the North East&quot; could be as far in as Medo, technically.<br /> <br /> Vance, if you're reading this, it might be worth clarifying that a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually the &quot;deep Northeastern forests&quot;. So my impression is beyond even Halta (those forests go deep. Very deep). I had the same reaction as you.<br /> <br /> But I wonder if that's just their safe base where the Realm can't reach them, and they go on long crusades, travelling far on the wing, settling down in a Threshold, spending a few months screwing things up, then go home to their distant base before the Realm's army arrives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T00:53:41-08:00","id":1265716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265668#post1265668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, long-distance warfare gets a lot easier to pull off when you can bind a Second Circle demon and send it to go mess with your enemy once a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the demon (that's still 3400 miles for Octavian to trudge, and he'll probably get lost), but to some extent that's true. Certainly small strike teams of supernatural warriors seems more viable than sending armies of tribesmen who'll probably die of disease or in random fights with civilised folk before they get there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T01:03:46-08:00","id":1265717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265678#post1265678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What surprises me is that it's explicitly identified as &quot;Old Realm for 'guide' or 'teacher,'&quot; which wouldn't seem to make it an inherently Lunar title. Unless there's an implicit &quot;of Lunars&quot; in the word that would be understood to native Old Realm speakers, I would expect Sidereals and Gods, and possibly other groups as well, to also use the title shahan-ya.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. But ancient terms do often change their meaning because they're only used by specific groups.<br /> For example:<br /> Gay (cheerful)<br /> Basilica (a Roman public building for meetings)<br /> African (a member of a particular Libyan tribe)<br /> Ferret (a thief)<br /> <br /> So an ancient term can be maintained by one group while forgotten by others. A young Sidereal might read an ancient Old Realm text from 5000 years ago and be confused by talk of a mortal Shahan-Ya teaching her students the tribe's rain dance, but be told by his divine teacher that while it's only used by Lunar teachers today, it originally was a more general word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I guess this <i>could</i> even be the start of a gradual retcon, phasing out the real-world title &quot;sifu&quot; in favor of an Exalted-specific term, analogous to the use of &quot;daiklave&quot;? But I expect not. </div> </div> </div>I suspect the reason the Devs used it instead of Sifu is because Sidereals use Sifu, essentially. I don't expect Sifu to vanish, I just expect it to only be used for Sidereals and other martial-arts specific teaching roles.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, Sifu is not only for kung-fu teachers in China, you also use it for skilled tradespeople. I mostly used it to refer to taxi-drivers.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-09-2018, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T01:43:55-08:00","id":1265732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265668#post1265668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, long-distance warfare gets a lot easier to pull off when you can bind a Second Circle demon and send it to go mess with your enemy once a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is so evil i love it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T04:22:03-08:00","id":1265758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265668#post1265668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, long-distance warfare gets a lot easier to pull off when you can bind a Second Circle demon and send it to go mess with your enemy once a month.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually wonder if this is one of those points where the Silver Pact might frown upon you if you do this too much.<br /> While summoning a second circle demon every now and then to assist with a major plan is probably fine, just summoning them randomly to attack Realm holdings seems like it would both antagonize the Realm (and Sidereals, who now have even more reasons to hate you because the Second Circles are also messing with Fate), as well as distance yourself from certain elements of the pact.<br /> I'm not saying every Lunar would oppose such a thing, but I think many would consider unleashing the enemies of Creation with little to no restraint on your enemies careless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T05:53:32-08:00","id":1265776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265671#post1265671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. 2e had that terrible Nameless Lair writeup, and that past edition can keep it, buried under the other inexplicable Wyld anomalies hiding atrocity centers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, not what I was thinking. I was thinking he was more in the lines of someone who is vicious and not a good thing for humanity at large, but very good at making you agree with him. More Lucifer than a generic demon king-he is selfish and insane, but he's a very compelling variety-admirable in how totally he was able to adapt to the new world, even if his victory would be really bad in the long term for everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T05:57:59-08:00","id":1265777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265716#post1265716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">armies of tribesmen who'll probably die of disease or in random fights with civilised folk before they get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>The susceptibility of large armies to disease tends to be a result of their poor diet and living conditions in combination with a large number of people being pressed into close proximity. A smaller, more mobile and flexible force that might be used to foraging strikes me as no more likely to catch serious disease than anybody else, and probably less likely than a lot of the setting's urban dwellers.<br /> <br /> What are they doing getting into fights with what I presume you meant as settled or urbanized people? Is it for supplies?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265758#post1265758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually wonder if this is one of those points where the Silver Pact might frown upon you if you do this too much.<br /> While summoning a second circle demon every now and then to assist with a major plan is probably fine, just summoning them randomly to attack Realm holdings seems like it would both antagonize the Realm (and Sidereals, who now have even more reasons to hate you because the Second Circles are also messing with Fate), as well as distance yourself from certain elements of the pact.<br /> I'm not saying every Lunar would oppose such a thing, but I think many would consider unleashing the enemies of Creation with little to no restraint on your enemies careless?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really how any of the Exalted view demons as a general thing, and especially not when they're summoned and bound by sorcery.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T06:04:48-08:00","id":1265786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265776#post1265776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, not what I was thinking. I was thinking he was more in the lines of someone who is vicious and not a good thing for humanity at large, but very good at making you agree with him. More Lucifer than a generic demon king-he is selfish and insane, but he's a very compelling variety-admirable in how totally he was able to adapt to the new world, even if his victory would be really bad in the long term for everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I wasn't with Exalted for as long as many others before the Third Edition core came out, but it was still long enough for the overall presentation of Ma-Ha-Suchi to make an impression. I mean, the guy had a very distinct look, he had his ethos, people talked about him a lot, it would have been hard not to have a very firm image of him rooted in.<br /> <br /> So I don't get why so few people seem to have had the same response to his being <b>significantly rewritten</b> in the Third Edition core as I did. Responses such as... remembering it at all; giving the impression of ever having read it in the first place; perhaps even preferring it because it's an interesting contrast to the other Lunars and general take on somebody who's been at this game for ages.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi's ultimate victory is really bad to the extent that it makes trade and communication between the Threshold and the Southeast more difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T06:18:43-08:00","id":1265794,"title":"","content":"I know for the purposes of my own game Ma-Ha-Suchi is currently trying to figure out why his Nameless Lair has moved from over by Greyfalls. So the fact that Raksi might be on his list of potential suspects along with the Sidereals amuses me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T08:08:20-08:00","id":1265824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265777#post1265777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The susceptibility of large armies to disease tends to be a result of their poor diet and living conditions in combination with a large number of people being pressed into close proximity. A smaller, more mobile and flexible force that might be used to foraging strikes me as no more likely to catch serious disease than anybody else, and probably less likely than a lot of the setting's urban dwellers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair points.<br /> However, we're talking about the distance from Britain to Tajikistan or Lebanon (but Tajikistan's a better example; Lebanon isn't too hard to get to because of the sea. That doesn't apply here). Travelling to a different part of the world with different diseases (and jungles have particularly bad diseases; though I guess we are talking about native jungle dwellers. Though I'm not sure how well Congolese travellers to Indian jungles in the Middle Ages would do. Obviously Europeans were devastated by disease, but perhaps other jungle-dwellers do better). Though to be fair, it's probably disease+random fights+starvation+accidents+bandits+desertion that's the issue, rather than just disease.<br /> Still, you do raise a good point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are they doing getting into fights with what I presume you meant as settled or urbanized people? Is it for supplies? </div> </div> </div>That's one reason.<br /> <br /> There are multiple routes you could take to get from Mahalanka to the Nameless Lair (or rather, environs; obviously the war doesn't necessarily mean besieging each other's capitals).<br /> You could trek about 4000 miles through the forest/jungle (it shouldn't be too hard to avoid Rathess). And your various bands of hunter-gatherers can probably hunt on the go, though that'll slow them slightly. Just don't get lost!<br /> But even without hunting, trekking through forest/jungle is slow even when it's not 4000 miles. I have to admit, I've not trekked a whole day through forest, and certainly not jungle, but I suspect trekking 4000 miles through forest and jungle would take well over a year, possibly more.<br /> <br /> And of course, you're going to be walking through the territory of many other independent tribes, strange forest gods, wood spiders, weird jungle monsters, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> A much quicker way would be to trek about 650 miles to that big lake, then get some kind of boat and sail along the great river past Vaneha and Nathir. Then go south at the big fork, and travel down to the jungle. Then march to the Nameless Lair (or rather, environs).<br /> The total distance is about 4200 miles (more than the distance from Britain to Canada), but a lot of it is going downriver.<br /> <br /> Of course, this river is the heart's blood of the Scavenger Lands. A lot of societies are going to be based along that river. And, while the river is very large, it's not going to be easy for various boats full of barbarians to get all the way down there without skirmishing. There's 2 reasons: one, to acquire supplies they're going to be at best poaching, and at worst raiding, from the locals. And second, a lot of civilisations along the river are going to get very antsy when they see a ship full of armed beastmen sailing past... and then, a few days later, another one, and then another one.<br /> <br /> That's not to say this is utterly impossible. I think a Lunar <i>could</i> organise it (not that we've seen their charms yet). It's just very difficult.<br /> <br /> It seems very awkward to prosecute a war across 4000 miles of jungle/forest via mortal soldiers. That's why I'd think flying demons, monsters, raids by packs of young Lunars, paying local tribes to rebel, and proxy war support for traditional enemies (say, whatever society is near Ma-Ha-Suchi's jungle and so has to put up with his raids, and would accept the help of a strange monstrous strategist from far to the north-east), and so on, are more practical solutions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-09-2018, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T08:12:00-08:00","id":1265825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265794#post1265794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know for the purposes of my own game Ma-Ha-Suchi is currently trying to figure out why his Nameless Lair has moved from over by Greyfalls. So the fact that Raksi might be on his list of potential suspects along with the Sidereals amuses me.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it was in a few different places in previous editions. But yeah, it was east of Greyfalls in mine too.<br /> Definitely Sidereals.<br /> <br /> (Actually, in my game, Infernals blew up the Loom of Fate, and Autocthon had to make a new one. That was my explanation for any geographic changes, like say the whole new area of lakes and rivers that appeared directly north of where the PCs were, while Varang shifted from north of them to east of them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-09-2018, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T08:37:16-08:00","id":1265835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265824#post1265824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems very awkward to prosecute a war across 4000 miles of jungle/forest via mortal soldiers. That's why I'd think flying demons, monsters, raids by packs of young Lunars, paying local tribes to rebel, and proxy war support for traditional enemies (say, whatever society is near Ma-Ha-Suchi's jungle and so has to put up with his raids, and would accept the help of a strange monstrous strategist from far to the north-east), and so on, are more practical solutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd sooner the description of them &quot;going to war&quot; be a somewhat hyperbolic description of an extended personal dispute involving arguments and not infrequent one-on-one fights then imagine it in half of those terms. Something about it just rubs me the wrong way... making it all about sending other Lunars to fight on your behalf feels contrary to the general spirit of what the excerpt is presenting, making it about managing to distantly manipulate very far away groups of people makes it feel too cold and impersonal, and using a lot of demons and stuff makes it feel both insufficiently Lunar and a bit too detached from the setting's locales.<br /> <br /> I know that Second Edition, at least, presented Ma-Ha-Suchi as being able to use at least necromancy, but in an Edition in which being a sorcerer or necromancer is less of a casual thing, I feel as though such an element should be dropped from his character when his basic thesis is not of being a sorcerer, which kind of discounts him slinging magic from thousands of miles away.<br /> <br /> I don't really know what the excerpt means by it (not least because I'm not certain where they'll be going with Ma-Ha-Suchi), but I'd happily accept a lot of fudging for the sake of preserving scenarios that depict character than have something reeking of impersonal pragmatism in which Ma-Ha, at least, feels kind of interchangeable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">a lot of civilisations along the river are going to get very antsy when they see a ship full of armed beastmen sailing past... and then, a few days later, another one, and then another one</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> So, one, I'm imagining a scenario that only ever needs maybe a couple hundred fighters at a time, so I can't see it needing too many boats.<br /> <br /> Two, heh, thinking about the point of how large groups of armed people are travelling the Scavenger Lands all the time got me thinking about the idea that a fairly efficient way to transmit troops like that is probably to contract them as muscle for Guild caravans for the journey to and from their destination.<br /> <br /> Although I imagine that even without such a detail, large armed groups marching across the province into the forests because they've been contracted for mercenary work is something that happens all the time. I've got an image in which a lot of the Hundred Kingdoms won't hassle such groups unless they start it as a matter of general policy, because they don't want to risk antagonising Nexus or Lookshy, which they're probably quite dependent on.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T08:43:36-08:00","id":1265836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265825#post1265825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, it was in a few different places in previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember previous debates on the subject with ideas of it moving around like Castle Duckula or that Nameless Lairs were a franchise he'd set up (that was formerly known as Salon Provocative).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T11:27:05-08:00","id":1265877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265673#post1265673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I read their organization sounded anything but cohesive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, perhaps 'cohesive' was the wrong word, but having internal factional disagreements doesn't actually help, because it suggests to me that Lunar society is established enough, and that people are invested enough in it, for there to BE factions.<br /> <br /> Like, the Lunar Exalted are four hundred individuals scattered across the length and breadth of the entire world. They don't have any central location to call home as the Sidereals do, they aren't the dynastic noble class of large nations like the Realm, they are a bunch of random heroes seperated by an average of like, the distance between Hellenic Greece and Gaul, or the Visigoth tribes and frikkin' <i>Jin Dynasty China</i>.<br /> <br /> The passage is often quite sensible and loaded with potential, but the moment any Lunar material talks about 'recruitment' I start rolling my eyes, because I am frankly skeptical of the idea that Lunars are able to encounter each other by anything more reliable than random happenstance, and that's certainly good enough to justify a player circle getting together, but a world-spanning organisation? This is Exalted! Travelling so much as the length of the Confederation of Rivers is a major undertaking!<br /> <br /> Yes, granted, Lunars are proooobably the most mobile Exalt, but even accounting for turning into birds, we're still talking about on average days or weeks of travel to meet up with a bunch of people who are foreigners in every sense but anima colour, during which a Lunar must abandon abandoning whatever heroic irons they have in the fire back home, the place they actually care about. There are possibilities in sorcerous communication, but a) I don't actually like the idea that most Lunars are walking around carrying some manner of magical walkie-talkie, and b) that suggests the Silver Pact is less an organisation than a worldwide mailing list, which doesn't really fit with what's going on. All of this is setting aside the question of how do you go about <i>finding</i> a freshly Exalted Lunar, something the game has never been clear on.<br /> <br /> Simple geography poses a massive obstacle to any shared sense of Lunar community, and the ideological differences are also non-trivial; if 'mutual pacts against a common enemy' are enough to get a bunch of Celestial Exalted from wildly differing nationalities, ethnicities, professions, social classes, cultural traditions and philosophical outlooks to set aside their many, many, <i>many</i> differences (at least some of which are going to trend closer to bitter opposition than divergent but not actually exclusive opinions) and work together, then the 'Silver Pact' should by all rights be a Rainbow Pact of Lunars, Outcaste Dragonblooded, Terrestrial (and some Celestial) Gods, Elementals, sane-ish Ghosts, assorted halfbreeds, perhaps the occasional Ronin Sidereal, and, more recently, returning Solars and renegade Abyssals.<br /> <br /> If it's that potent as a unifying banner, it's absurd for it to be a purely Lunar thing - it'll be the rallying cry of every anti-Realm group that wants wider support in their opposition to the jackbooted empire with its heel pressing on the throat of the world. On the other hand, if 'mutual pacts against a common enemy' are <i>not</i> enough to unite all peoples from all places, then it won't unite a meaningful number of the Lunar Exalted, either.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I tend to think that the idea of a 'Silver Pact' is fundamentally incoherent, and damaging to the game's desire to stress the difficulty of long-distance travel in the ancient world; the Guild has a similar issue where it's trying to be a world-spanning mercantile conspiracy in a setting where the most advanced nation around is administrated by the cutting-edge technology of <i>semaphore.</i><br /> <br /> Personally, I think Lunars work much better if they just abandon the idea that there's any kind of worldwide Lunar community. Scattered across the face of Creation and beyond are the Lunar Exalted, enmeshed in the troubles and trevails of an Age of Sorrows. Each mighty, each champion of their respective people's, but each singular, an iconoclast, an argent island adrift in a fallen world.<br /> <br /> Sometimes they encounter each other in the course of their adventures, as they encounter Exigents and halfbloods and other heroes of the Age, and perhaps the shared flavour of their power spurs a spark of recognition that means a few more of these meetings result in friendship , and so bands of Lunars are relatively common, insofar as any phenomenon among the rarified ranks of the Exalted can be called 'common'. Sometimes a particularly old and mighty Lunar sweeps through the area, one who hails from the ancient days of the Shogunate, perhaps even the Age of Dreams itself, a ramshackle court of heroic flotsam caught up in their wake, inspired by their legend. Perhaps a few young Lunars follow them to learn at their knee - or perhaps they don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T11:49:49-08:00","id":1265885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265877#post1265877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The passage is often quite sensible and loaded with potential, but the moment any Lunar material talks about 'recruitment' I start rolling my eyes, because I am frankly skeptical of the idea that Lunars are able to encounter each other by anything more reliable than random happenstance, and that's certainly good enough to justify a player circle getting together, but a world-spanning organisation? This is Exalted! Travelling so much as the length of the Confederation of Rivers is a major undertaking!<br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yes, granted, Lunars are proooobably the most mobile Exalt, but even accounting for turning into birds, we're still talking about on average days or weeks of travel to meet up with a bunch of people who are foreigners in every sense but anima colour, during which a Lunar must abandon abandoning whatever heroic irons they have in the fire back home, the place they actually care about. There are possibilities in sorcerous communication, but a) I don't actually like the idea that most Lunars are walking around carrying some manner of magical walkie-talkie, and b) that suggests the Silver Pact is less an organisation than a worldwide mailing list, which doesn't really fit with what's going on. All of this is setting aside the question of how do you go about <i>finding</i> a freshly Exalted Lunar, something the game has never been clear on.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Let's seeeee\u2026.<br /> <br /> <b>Omniscient Instinct Concentration</b><br /><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Cost</b>: \u2014(1wp); <b>Mins</b>: Perception 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Grandfather Spider Mastery</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;amp\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Standing at the center of the changing seasons, the Lunar can scent distant strife on the wind, read portents written on the stars, and discern secret wisdom from her dreams. Whenever an event occurs within (Essence x100) miles that threatens or strongly impacts the object of one of the Lunar\u2019s Defining Ties, or her Tie to her Solar mate, she feels a tingle of prescient instinct. She may spend one Willpower to focus her senses on the distant event, receiving a brief description of it as well as the direction and distance to it. Any Survival rolls she makes to navigate her way towards the event\u2019s location double 7s. While Watchful Spider Stance is active, the Lunar can sense events at any range, as long as she is within the same realm of existence.</span></span></span></div><br /> I suppose there might be some high Essence people in the Silver Pact who are concerned enough about the survival of other Lunars to have a Defining Tie about it. It might also depend a bit on what Watchful Spider Stance does on its own, if it can enhance this Charm to allow a Lunar to sense events from a distance of an entire realm of existence.<br /> <br /> It may be that elder Lunars possess some rather potent communication Charms, such that even if they can't reach a fresh new Lunar in need in due time by themselves, they can at least get word out to somebody that owes them a favour or is invested in their cause who can.<br /> <br /> That's not even accounting for the fact that the Silver Pact contains Lunars that have at least Essence 6.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, why doesn't the Silver Pact sound like a big mailing list? I think that Third Edition has been fairly consistent up until this point that it's largely about an agreement of mutual aid and purpose, facilitated primarily by the accumulation and exchange of favours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple geography poses a massive obstacle to any shared sense of Lunar community, and the ideological differences are also non-trivial; if 'mutual pacts against a common enemy' are enough to get a bunch of Celestial Exalted from wildly differing nationalities, ethnicities, professions, social classes, cultural traditions and philosophical outlooks to set aside their many, many, <i>many</i> differences (at least some of which are going to trend closer to bitter opposition than divergent but not actually exclusive opinions) and work together, then the 'Silver Pact' should by all rights be a Rainbow Pact of Lunars, Outcaste Dragonblooded, Terrestrial (and some Celestial) Gods, Elementals, sane-ish Ghosts, assorted halfbreeds, perhaps the occasional Ronin Sidereal, and, more recently, returning Solars and renegade Abyssals.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've referenced Lunars from a variety of backgrounds, but considering that Lunars are, by definition, iconoclasts and outsiders, there's a question of how much they really belong to those backgrounds. There's a possibility that many Lunars identify more with one another than they did with society that they came from (and that rejected them?).<br /> <br /> Plus the fact that there's something damaged that is unique within the Lunar Essence, and compels them to a particular animosity against the Realm. Combined with the framework in the background of a Lunar Society from the First Age.<br /> <br /> All of those other people are still part of the equation, but like the Dominions, they are likely to often be tools. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, I tend to think that the idea of a 'Silver Pact' is fundamentally incoherent, and damaging to the game's desire to stress the difficulty of long-distance travel in the ancient world; the Guild has a similar issue where it's trying to be a world-spanning mercantile conspiracy in a setting where the most advanced nation around is administrated by the cutting-edge technology of <i>semaphore.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That puts the Realm one up over some of the largest empires in actual human history.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T11:56:57-08:00","id":1265888,"title":"","content":"Ok, here's how I think it's supposed to work: <br /> You exalt, you do some stuff, and eventually a lunar in your vague neck of the woods tracks you down. They take you to their shahan-ya, you get offered tattoos and hear the pact pitch. If you accept the elder will show you the ropes, maybe introduce you to some other young lunars or an elder they think might be a better fit. <br /> <br /> Big meetings might happen once a decade. But to people who live for centuries, that's pretty frequent.<br /> <br /> Also yeah, a lot of them do have communication spells. They're organising a guerilla war here, not having them would be stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T12:12:43-08:00","id":1265890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265888#post1265888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You exalt, you do some stuff, and eventually a lunar in your vague neck of the woods tracks you down. They take you to their shahan-ya, you get offered tattoos and hear the pact pitch. If you accept the elder will show you the ropes, maybe introduce you to some other young lunars or an elder they think might be a better fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that they'll give you your caste no matter what, it's not made conditional on a commitment to the Pact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also yeah, a lot of them do have communication spells. They're organising a guerilla war here, not having them would be stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to presume that they've got a few Charms of their own that are up to the task, if they're capable of sensing certain events from any distance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T12:35:44-08:00","id":1265898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265877#post1265877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like, the Lunar Exalted are four hundred individuals scattered across the length and breadth of the entire world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's as bad as all that, actually. There are certain areas where Lunars are going to cluster more, just given the circumstances. They're going to avoid the Realm proper, and its satrapies, for obvious reasons. Likewise, they're probably not going to be living out in Creation's true wilderness areas, because most of them will have goals that require some humans to accomplish. That leaves out the deep forests of the East, the deep deserts of the south, most of the open water of the West, and the frozen wastelands of the North.<br /> <br /> So, looking at this <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/MlgV37u.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">handy map </a>of 3e Creation, I'd estimate that the areas the Lunars are packed into is probably around 50,000,000, or maybe 55,000,000, square miles. Now, that sure sounds like a lot, but if you start doing the math, it gets less intimidating. It suggests each Lunar could have about 140,000 square miles of territory to handle personally, which, in turn, is only about 375 miles on a side. So, two Lunars will be on average only ~400 miles apart, which is actually not a long journey for a being that can fairly trivially assume the form of a bird. <br /> <br /> And Lunars are likely to cluster even more than that - a young Lunar is likely to stay near an elder who's willing to teach and protect them, and elders might accumulate several younger Lunars at once while doing so. That, in turn, ups the likelyhood that <i>someone</i> in the group has communication magic that can reach long distances, so not every Lunar needs to have it to keep groups connected. <br /> <br /> All of this is to say, I think the &quot;loosely connected group of mutual allies and friends&quot; model (or the &quot;mailing list&quot; model, as you described it) isn't that implausible as a description of how the Lunars organize themselves. And Lunars may come from a very diverse set of backgrounds, but the enmity of the Dragon-Blooded host and the Sidereals is going to be a strong motivator to overcome that and get organized, at least to the point of the loose mutual aid and information setup they have right now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T12:53:31-08:00","id":1265905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265890#post1265890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keeping in mind that they'll give you your caste no matter what, it's not made conditional on a commitment to the Pact.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was picturing them talking about the pact while doing the tattoos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T13:22:20-08:00","id":1265909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265905#post1265905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I was picturing them talking about the pact while doing the tattoos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar timeshare pitches are hardcore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T13:47:06-08:00","id":1265913,"title":"","content":"From what Vance and Minton mentioned on the Discord his war with Raksi over the future of the Silver Pact is why he's disillusioned with Exalted politics in the current game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T14:08:17-08:00","id":1265915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265885#post1265885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose there might be some high Essence people in the Silver Pact who are concerned enough about the survival of other Lunars to have a Defining Tie about it. It might also depend a bit on what Watchful Spider Stance does on its own, if it can enhance this Charm to allow a Lunar to sense events from a distance of an entire realm of existence.<br /> <br /> It may be that elder Lunars possess some rather potent communication Charms, such that even if they can't reach a fresh new Lunar in need in due time by themselves, they can at least get word out to somebody that owes them a favour or is invested in their cause who can.<br /> <br /> That's not even accounting for the fact that the Silver Pact contains Lunars that have at least Essence 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible. But vague possibilities are kind of all there are, or have ever been on this score.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265885#post1265885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the rest, why doesn't the Silver Pact sound like a big mailing list? I think that Third Edition has been fairly consistent up until this point that it's largely about an agreement of mutual aid and purpose, facilitated primarily by the accumulation and exchange of favours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because accumulating and exchanging favours and agreeing to mutual aid kind of requires, you know, meeting one another to do helpful things besides just exchange knowledge, and even then there's usually not much a Lunar from a couple countries over can tell you about your homeland that local sources can't.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265885#post1265885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've referenced Lunars from a variety of backgrounds, but considering that Lunars are, by definition, iconoclasts and outsiders, there's a question of how much they really belong to those backgrounds. There's a possibility that many Lunars identify more with one another than they did with society that they came from (and that rejected them?).<br /> <br /> Plus the fact that there's something damaged that is unique within the Lunar Essence, and compels them to a particular animosity against the Realm. Combined with the framework in the background of a Lunar Society from the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but that seems kind of naff, to be honest. Like, the game has historically had a problem with Exalted being murderhobos with no ties to the setting, so encouraging Lunars to be divorced from the cultures of Creation wouldn't be a good move - and I say 'wouldn't', because I don't think the material pushes that outlook. The neither the corebook nor the excerpted passage portray Lunars as innate outsiders, and even if they <i>were</i> 'by definition' outsiders, historical societies have plenty of room for liminal figures who exist on the edges of a culture while still assuredly being part of it.<br /> <br /> There's also a lot of value in keeping Lunars disconnected, mind you, since it serves the dual purposes of fleshing out the nations of the setting and providing models for what an Exalted game looks like. One of the reasons Solars have often been accused of blandness, I believe, is that having to share space in the corebook with explaining the setting in general leaves them relatively little room for modeling what sort of 'splat-agnostic' adventures an Exalt can get up to. 3e is particularly bad at this with the lack of a Storyteller's section, although I have hopes for the upcoming Storyteller's Guide, but Lunars also provide great opportunity for modelling the adventures of Exalts as examples to players, due to their having the most established history of Celestial Exalts operating in Creation throughout history.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265885#post1265885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That puts the Realm one up over some of the largest empires in actual human history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. It doesn't mean squat for the Guild, though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265898#post1265898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it's as bad as all that, actually. There are certain areas where Lunars are going to cluster more, just given the circumstances. They're going to avoid the Realm proper, and its satrapies, for obvious reasons. Likewise, they're probably not going to be living out in Creation's true wilderness areas, because most of them will have goals that require some humans to accomplish. That leaves out the deep forests of the East, the deep deserts of the south, most of the open water of the West, and the frozen wastelands of the North.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that should be taken for granted at all, to be honest. We've had dev quotes and 3e material expounding on how the Blessed Isle is so frikkin' large that there are places within it that still haven't even heard of the Realm, so Lunars on the Blessed Isle is entirely possible, and the true wilderness tends to offer bountiful opportunities for plumbing magical landscapes and old ruins for resources. They also aren't necessarily totally uninhabited, given the Raksha, Created Races and other oddities, and that kind of living on the magical frontier sounds like an excellent breeding ground for Lunar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 11-09-2018, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T15:30:26-08:00","id":1265948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265915#post1265915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible. But vague possibilities are kind of all there are, or have ever been on this score.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, vague? No reasonable inferences to be made from the actual text of a previewed Charm that confers a form of sensory input with a range varying between at least five hundred miles and everything within the same dimension?<br /> <br /> By the by, I expect that some of the powers of those Essence 6+ Lunars will become a bit less vague when some of those Essence 6+ Lunars actually get write-ups in the characters chapter of Fangs at the Gate.<br /> <br /> Although I must say, I feel as though when we have powers and premises such as this, a reading that refuses to follow them to conclusions that would allow the setting to remain internally consistent does not exactly come across as a reading in good faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because accumulating and exchanging favours and agreeing to mutual aid kind of requires, you know, meeting one another to do helpful things besides just exchange knowledge, and even then there's usually not much a Lunar from a couple countries over can tell you about your homeland that local sources can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it would seem that Lunars might periodically travel to meet one another, aided by procedures, shared safehouses, and divine apex predator senses that can span the universe in order to cash in their chits.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're at war against a world spanning empire, a Lunar in Whitewall might benefit from being forewarned that a few legions have landed at Medo, with the intent of moving in to start wrecking their shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but that seems kind of naff, to be honest. Like, the game has historically had a problem with Exalted being murderhobos with no ties to the setting, so encouraging Lunars to be divorced from the cultures of Creation wouldn't be a good move - and I say 'wouldn't', because I don't think the material pushes that outlook. The neither the corebook nor the excerpted passage portray Lunars as innate outsiders</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the opening line to their corebook passage talking about being Chosen from those who struggle against their chains?<br /> <br /> Still, I'll grant that a reading of significant detachment across the board is discounting elements such as them guiding (and culling) the herd, of defining societies through challenging them. And to be sure, the corebook makes mention of those who direct their passions towards things other than the Realm, including more personal and local issues.<br /> <br /> It remains that they have a keening song in their hearts raging against the existence of a pretender Realm, that the Wyld Hunt isn't exactly leaving you alone because you promise that you'll never be a threat and that it helps to have friends, that there are many cases in which the existence of the Realm infringes upon their little corner of the world, and that there are plenty of Lunar Exalted who see the downfall of the Old Realm and the Solar Exalted as their chance to reign over the ocean rather than be content with the pond, if they can just displace that big island currently inhabiting it.<br /> <br /> I will maintain that referring to my premise as murderhobos is an unnuanced perspective on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also a lot of value in keeping Lunars disconnected, mind you, since it serves the dual purposes of fleshing out the nations of the setting and providing models for what an Exalted game looks like. One of the reasons Solars have often been accused of blandness, I believe, is that having to share space in the corebook with explaining the setting in general leaves them relatively little room for modeling what sort of 'splat-agnostic' adventures an Exalt can get up to. 3e is particularly bad at this with the lack of a Storyteller's section, although I have hopes for the upcoming Storyteller's Guide, but Lunars also provide great opportunity for modelling the adventures of Exalts as examples to players, due to their having the most established history of Celestial Exalts operating in Creation throughout history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the appeals of approaching Lunars in a more laissaiz faire manner even if they're not going to be and I prefer that, but I feel as though a significant motive for that being instruction to Solars games undercuts that by a fair bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. It doesn't mean squat for the Guild, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The infrastructure that has allowed large empires to operate at times when the most sophisticated communications technology in the world was the horse relay has also allowed the functioning of transcontinental commercial and ideological entities with a level of coordination that about fits with the Guild as presented in Masters of Jade, such as the East India Company or the Catholic Church.<br /> <br /> There's also an argument on the whole matter of how sometimes it's okay to allow a story to fudge a few details so that it can fulfil its purposes as a story, but that's its whole other conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that should be taken for granted at all, to be honest. We've had dev quotes and 3e material expounding on how the Blessed Isle is so frikkin' large that there are places within it that still haven't even heard of the Realm</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might be a bit exaggerated. <br /> <br /> Not that I wouldn't expect Lunars to ever be on the Blessed Isle, but probably operating in secrecy, or else picking their moment to go loud when they've got a secure escape route. I've often maintained that a Lunar that lives on the Blessed Isle for an extended period while going unnoticed is a Lunar that is not doing anything interesting.<br /> <br /> (Isolation in the Realm probably has a lot less to do with its size than it does with the presence of things such as mountains, deserts and scattered islands, landscapes in which it's easier to disappear into)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T17:42:13-08:00","id":1266017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265948#post1265948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, vague? No reasonable inferences to be made from the actual text of a previewed Charm that confers a form of sensory input with a range varying between at least five hundred miles and everything within the same dimension?</div> </div> </div> </div>When it requires a Defining Tie to the abstract idea of an organisation that doesn't exist in order to kickstart it? No, not really. That's not a small requirement. It's the kind of thing I would expect to <i>see</i> in the lore, explicitly, (as <i>Masters of Jade</i> did with Brem Marst) if the game expects me to believe that it happened. It's a vague possibility of how the Silver Pact <i>could</i> work, <i>if</i> you build on this one thing in certain ways.<br /> <br /> Absent some published acknowledgement or exploration of this mechanism, then frankly? If the Silver Pact didn't have a long publication history establishing it, and somebody suggested that it should exist on the basis of this one Charm and the implications thereof, I would view that with about as much suspicion as the writeups of those Dragonblooded breeding camps spun out of the 2e Manse rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265948#post1265948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it would seem that Lunars might periodically travel to meet one another, aided by procedures, shared safehouses, and divine apex predator senses that can span the universe in order to cash in their chits.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're at war against a world spanning empire, a Lunar in Whitewall might benefit from being forewarned that a few legions have landed at Medo, with the intent of moving in to start wrecking their shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they might pass on word - if they know about each other, if they can contact each other. I find those to be pretty big assumptions. I find it an even bigger assumption that Lunars would travel hundreds or thousands of miles to meet and aid one another, or spend time and effort maintaining procedures and safehouses <i>across the entire world</i> to aid such travels, to help relative strangers.<br /> <br /> Like, you're effectively suggesting that the Silver Pact perpetuates itself through shared history and institutional inertia, but the problem is that I am skeptical of the institution right down to its roots. This kind of history of cooperation has to <i>start</i> somewhere, it has to <i>maintain</i> itself, and these are leviathan tasks when carried out on the scale of an entire world, tasks that I do not believe a few hundred scattered heroes are likely to perform.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265948#post1265948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the opening line to their corebook passage talking about being Chosen from those who struggle against their chains?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about it? Yeah, okay, they're driven to shatter chains binding them to a lost age of dreams - that doesn't make them strangers in their own homes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265948#post1265948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, I'll grant that a reading of significant detachment across the board is discounting elements such as them guiding (and culling) the herd, of defining societies through challenging them. And to be sure, the corebook makes mention of those who direct their passions towards things other than the Realm, including more personal and local issues.<br /> <br /> It remains that they have a keening song in their hearts raging against the existence of a pretender Realm, that the Wyld Hunt isn't exactly leaving you alone because you promise that you'll never be a threat and that it helps to have friends, that there are many cases in which the existence of the Realm infringes upon their little corner of the world, and that there are plenty of Lunar Exalted who see the downfall of the Old Realm and the Solar Exalted as their chance to reign over the ocean rather than be content with the pond, if they can just displace that big island currently inhabiting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's an excellent reason to fight the realm. It is <i>not</i> an excellent reason to unite with people hundreds or thousands of miles away with which you have next to nothing in common except that they also oppose the Realm and draw power from the same source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265948#post1265948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will maintain that referring to my premise as murderhobos is an unnuanced perspective on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did no such thing. I said that the game has a historical problem of Exalted characters being murderhobos, and should be wary of encouraging this further. Please exercise better reading comprehension.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265948#post1265948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the appeals of approaching Lunars in a more laissaiz faire manner even if they're not going to be and I prefer that, but I feel as though a significant motive for that being instruction to Solars games undercuts that by a fair bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wrote 'splat agnostic' for a reason, thank you. Every splat offers plothooks for adventures specific to them, but Lunars are uniquely well placed to model adventure hooks for everybody. That Solars particularly benefit from this is simply a happy side effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265948#post1265948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The infrastructure that has allowed large empires to operate at times when the most sophisticated communications technology in the world was the horse relay has also allowed the functioning of transcontinental commercial and ideological entities with a level of coordination that about fits with the Guild as presented in Masters of Jade, such as the East India Company or the Catholic Church.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really. Empires administrated by such means had this notable tendency to creak under their own weight <i>long</i> before they grew to the breadth of influence of the Guild - to say nothing of my narrative problems with the idea of a worldwide mercantile conspiracy, but this entire tangent isn't really germane to a discussion of Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265948#post1265948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that might be a bit exaggerated.<br /> <br /> Not that I wouldn't expect Lunars to ever be on the Blessed Isle, but probably operating in secrecy, or else picking their moment to go loud when they've got a secure escape route. I've often maintained that a Lunar that lives on the Blessed Isle for an extended period while going unnoticed is a Lunar that is not doing anything interesting.<br /> <br /> (Isolation in the Realm probably has a lot less to do with its size than it does with the presence of things such as mountains, deserts and scattered islands, landscapes in which it's easier to disappear into)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sigh. If I have to I'll dig through Nishkriya to find a quote, but I'm pretty sure it's not an exaggeration, no. The Blessed Isle is just <i>big.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T19:51:39-08:00","id":1266068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266017#post1266017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it requires a Defining Tie to the abstract idea of an organisation that doesn't exist in order to kickstart it? No, not really. That's not a small requirement. It's the kind of thing I would expect to <i>see</i> in the lore, explicitly, (as <i>Masters of Jade</i> did with Brem Marst) if the game expects me to believe that it happened. It's a vague possibility of how the Silver Pact <i>could</i> work, <i>if</i> you build on this one thing in certain ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>When a bunch of social predators with the universal motivation of &quot;kill the fucking usurpers who cast us out and stole the world&quot; gets pushed out into the cold together, having them all just go their separate ways for centuries strains credulity. Most of the 400 seem like the type hellbent to try and find a way to make it work together. It's not like the Dragon-Blooded have a monopoly on the general concept of teamwork, and there are probably a lot of Lunars with social totem beasts that might give them an inroad into greater communication capacities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T20:33:06-08:00","id":1266076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266017#post1266017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it requires a Defining Tie to the abstract idea of an organisation that doesn't exist in order to kickstart it? No, not really.That's not a small requirement. It's the kind of thing I would expect to <i>see</i> in the lore, explicitly, (as <i>Masters of Jade</i> did with Brem Marst) if the game expects me to believe that it happened. It's a vague possibility of how the Silver Pact <i>could</i> work, <i>if</i> you build on this one thing in certain ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few responses to this.<br /> <br /> One is that I was making a point about what the Charm might say about the scope of higher end Lunar powers, rather than hanging all contingencies off of that sole capability.<br /> <br /> Another is that I was thinking more about somebody having a powerful Tie to other Lunar Exalted as a whole, rather than the Silver Pact specifically.<br /> <br /> There's the matter of how the circumstances of the Usurpation might create an impetus for some people to create such a network, and be very powerfully invested in doing so, irrespective of the kind of sensory range that it affords them, just because that's the boat they're in now. I mean, the Usurpation was a big enough deal for them to change their castes over it.<br /> <br /> It's kind of weird to microfocus the whole subject of how Lunars locate, recruit and maintain communication with one another at the outset of their current situation, rather than coming at it in the Time of Tumult when it's gotten to have more than a thousand years to develop ideas and motives and protocols.<br /> <br /> Aaaaand between Arms of the Chosen and the preview about the Solar Bond, I get the impression that Lunars had a bit of society in parallel to the Solars, and pursuit of that whole &quot;guardians of the Realm&quot; thing deep into the First Age, and that the Silver Pact is something of a successor to that in several respects (particularly respects of &quot;losing the Solars caused Lunars with Bonds to kind of lose their minds&quot; and &quot;losing the Realm they were so invested in protecting caused basically all Lunars to kind of lose their minds&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absent some published acknowledgement or exploration of this mechanism, then frankly? If the Silver Pact didn't have a long publication history establishing it, and somebody suggested that it should exist on the basis of this one Charm and the implications thereof, I would view that with about as much suspicion as the writeups of those Dragonblooded breeding camps spun out of the 2e Manse rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really not. That shit was about denying and refuting the setting, an irritating tendency even before the specifics of being in service of something really skeezy. What I am talking about is using existing principles, a bit of creative license, and good faith reading to confirm and reinforce the setting as it is presented to me. In cases where it's a bit shaky, I'm happy to err on the side of suspending disbelief, because I am invested in this presentation of the Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This kind of history of cooperation has to <i>start</i> somewhere</div> </div> </div> </div>It might start somewhere around First Age institutions such as the Deliberative and the Calibration Feast.<br /> <br /> A lot of initial members of the Silver Pact might well have been in the same room together when the Sidereals and Dragon Blooded tore the world away from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it has to <i>maintain</i> itself</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't doubt that your perspective means you're against the general idea of castes being fixed by tattoos that only another Lunar can provide, but... there it is, as a part of the setting. In every Edition; among the things distinguishing the Lunar Exalted you don't get your caste when you Exalt, it has to be fixed with the aid of another Lunar. Literally every Lunar with a caste has had a rather intimate meeting with at least one other Lunar.<br /> <br /> Heck, I think First Edition extended that even to the First Age, even if it didn't require tattoos, and it was only Second Edition that said that a First Age Lunar's caste would eventually settle on its own.<br /> <br /> There can be a few reasons that Lunars feel compelled to provide castes to their newly Chosen fellows; solidarity, a sense of sacred duty, a desire for a particular tradition, possibly the castes themselves, to not die out, particular ideas and biases against castelessness verging on a concern about the result of hundred of casteless Lunars running around the world. And if you care about taking over the world, why <i>not</i> use that opportunity to try and sell this other person, with whom you share a unique, and rather intense experience and place in the world's political and cosmological structure, on your perspective and aspiration and maybe even your particular way of doing things?<br /> <br /> Whatever common cause you might have with a god, you're never going to have provided that god with its caste.<br /> <br /> And castes are hardly incidental; look at Solar and Dragon XP. That stuff has a profound impact on you; you're more strongly actualised by acting in a manner consistent with your caste than if you just ignored it. Think about what it means for Lunars to share that thing with one another, to actually rely on one another for it existing.<br /> <br /> You're free to not like that, to not have it in your rendition of the setting, but if you're genuinely asking how the setting written by the developers functions, then Lunars fixing one another's castes is something that I think makes a decent case for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about it? Yeah, okay, they're driven to shatter chains binding them to a lost age of dreams - that doesn't make them strangers in their own homes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will grant that it's possible that I read too far into the line on breaking chains and erroneously applied it to their general experience and the criteria by which they were Chosen, rather than solely about their connection to the Old Realm. I will get back to you on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh. If I have to I'll dig through Nishkriya to find a quote, but I'm pretty sure it's not an exaggeration, no. The Blessed Isle is just <i>big.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it's big, and absolutely there are areas where geographic features make it difficult to effectively exert meaningful administrative control, but the idea that those areas <i>haven't heard</i> of the Realm that surrounds them on all sides feels... unlikely.<br /> <br /> Like, even if trade caravans and prefectural governors and military detachments can't effectively get to them, they at least seem like prime target for not infrequent Immaculate missionaries.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T21:03:48-08:00","id":1266088,"title":"","content":"Personally, I've generally liked the way that the game has always presented the idea that, between similarity in nature and purpose and a historical continuity from the time in which they were most directly uplifted in common by the gods to go to war against the terrible monsters that created the world, each group of Exalted has had a sense of solidarity, if not outright community. Obviously the setting and the game presents these as strongest with the Sidereal and Terrestrial Exalted, but it still persisted as at least an underlying detail for Solars and Lunars (both among themselves and intertwined); even if they weren't getting along, there was still a common forum in which they could ultimately reconvene. I like it for the sense of ancient world mythical caste system it projects.<br /> <br /> The Solars were always distinct in how their existence in the world came after a period of that continuity being destroyed completely; they were the only Exalted who ever <i>returned</i> to the world after a lengthy absence. The Terrestrial and Sidereal Exalted didn't have that; the central hinge of the setting is on how their colleges took over the world by destroying the Solar one, with the latter group having living members who remember that instance. The Lunar Exalted aren't like that; their college was bloodied up a bit and forced underground, but there was never a case in which 98% of them disappeared completely from the world for a thousand years and returned piecemeal all of a sudden, and they <i>too</i> have living members who remember the circumstances of their status changing.<br /> <br /> Heck, the Abyssal and Infernal Exalted came about under circumstances in which fresh new communities tailor made for them were ready to accept and condition and gird them, before setting them loose on the world, substitutions for the thing that the Solars lost when they were almost completely wiped out and gone for centuries; they have solidarity (as distinct from organisation) provided for them for the sake of malefic agendas.<br /> <br /> And the Solars are quite distinct in the idea that they're returning to the world after that foundation has long since fallen away and been forgotten, with nothing waiting to take its place, almost all on an even footing, giving them a completely fresh slate such that no Exalted have had ever, meaning they're a lot more free to be themselves rather than being part of an overarching structure of Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> I think it's neat, and while I respect the idea to overturn the rest of that elsewhere, I do think that some of the core narrative of the return of the Solars would be diminished if there was no sense of contrast between their situation and that of the Exalted that have actually been alive for the past thousand years.<br /> <br /> That and I'm just attached to the other Exalted communities.<br /> <br /> It's fine to not like them, but I think it's overlooking a lot to say that they don't make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T22:32:09-08:00","id":1266096,"title":"","content":"It's... it's honestly pretty simple. You look at the stars or read some tea leaves or get visited by Luna in a dream and go &quot;yup, my old friend who just died has reincarnated two thousand miles from here, near Lookshy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then you turn into an osprey and you're there in two weeks to be like, &quot;hey, brah, you don't know me but I owe you twenty bucks from your past life.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously, the sheer distance Lunars can travel in a day is ridiculous. Look up migratory birds on Wikipedia. Then add strength and stamina charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T23:28:55-08:00","id":1266107,"title":"","content":"And then remphasize about fifty times how spreading 400 people across Creation doesn\u2019t actually put them <i>nearly</i> as far apart from each other on average as most people seem to think. I did it myself a while ago and did in fact end up with a mean distance of ~500 miles tops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T02:05:21-08:00","id":1266125,"title":"","content":"And, as people have said, humans are concentrated, as the land they live on is much smaller than the world's total area (though maybe you've included that in your calculation already).<br /> <br /> I feel at this point it'd be worth giving an actual example.<br /> <br /> So, I've just recently started playing a new character, Dr Soma, a snake-totem Lunar. She's a martial artist and doctor who lived in a big city so has good knowledge of other lands (Lore 3)). She exalted fighting some corrupt Realm soldiers.<br /> <br /> So, what to do on her first day as an Anathema? Run. Before the famous Wyld Hunt arrives to kill her.<br /> <br /> So she ran to the woods. She did some Sacred Hunting (I asked Vance, he said it's instinctual knowledge) and picked up a bird form. She then flew west.<br /> <br /> But where to go next? Well, she doesn't know much about being an Anathema. Maybe she can find an experienced Anathema sifu to teach her.<br /> Folktales, merchant's tales, and Immaculate propaganda have told her of 4 possible candidates in distant lands (but reachable as a bird): Deep in the jungle to the east is the monstrous barbarian warlord Ma-Ha-Suchi, whose beastmen are the reason you never go deep into the jungle. Closer, west, is the demon sorceress Enhenduanna, who apparently sacrifices thousands to feed her dark god. South-East is a desert city recently seized by the debauched sorcerer Babar. A bit more West is the Tangle, an impenetrable thorn-forest of barbarians led by a giant demon-bear. (Who is canon.)<br /> But it's hard to tell what's propaganda and what's real, and they didn't all sound like Lunars. So she went for the demon bear. It was hundreds of miles, but that's not far as a bird. She had to stop and ask directions a lot though.<br /> <br /> Eventually, she reached the Tangle. She sought out the locals, and impressed them with her shapeshifting. They took her to their &quot;god&quot;, the Lunar Jyudo Far-Flung, and she spent a month learning about Lunar history and powers with him. He told her about the 3 Lunars in the 1000 mile radius, and that he would occasionally meet one to co-ordinate their anti-Realm activities, maybe once a year, though he hadn't heard from him recently. He also told Soma that senior anti-Realm Lunars had a loose non-aggression and coordination agreement called the Silver Pact, and that he'd contact a No Moon, when he could, to get her mystical tattoos that'd give her some distinct powers. But one of the Solar PCs came to visit to try to make an alliance, so for now Soma is going off with them.<br /> <br /> That, I think, is a good example of how it might work in practice. It's not just a matter of elders finding new Lunars, new Lunars may also want to find other Lunars.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, I can see Imrix's point about the Guild, but that might be something for another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-10-2018, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T03:54:15-08:00","id":1266141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266125#post1266125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before the famous Would Hunt arrives to kill her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh yes, the dreadful killer Would Hunt; reviled by its enemies and allies alike for its tendency to punctuate everything it does with obnoxious questions!<br /> <br /> &quot;Would we like to kill you now? Yes, yes we would.&quot;<br /> &quot;Would we like to give you a moment for making your case? No, no we wouldn't.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bastards.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T03:58:23-08:00","id":1266143,"title":"","content":"****ing autocorrect. I already corrected 3 mistakes it made on my post, I missed that. It doesn't even point out when it's changed text.<br /> <br /> I've worked out how to turn the damn thing off now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-10-2018, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T04:03:50-08:00","id":1266144,"title":"","content":"I wasn't making fun of you, person, just turning an amusing happenstance into a silly little joke. We've all had autocorrect mishaps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T05:42:00-08:00","id":1266160,"title":"","content":"Oh I know, I know.<br /> <br /> Though I'd think the Would Hunt would be Fair Folk; since they're hypothetical and unreal.<br /> Alternately, ghosts who remember the good old days when they would hunt down Anathema on weekends.<br /> <br /> Once I accidentally asked if Lunars would still have Chinese Charms. Vance was rather confused, understandably! Come on, isn't chimaera a English word? I think this smartphone has a rather limited assumption of the kind of lexicon one might habitually use.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I am male, you can use male pronouns to refer to me. Though it's probably wise of you not to assume. I've embarrassed myself there before!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-10-2018, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T06:12:10-08:00","id":1266167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266160#post1266160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I am male, you can use male pronouns to refer to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, it's actually become my habit to use &quot;person&quot; rather than &quot;man&quot; in that colloquialism regardless of whether or not I know the person's gender for a while now, since it's kind of bullshit that colloquially referring to somebody as &quot;man&quot; conveys casualness and camaraderie, and addressing somebody as &quot;woman&quot; conveys... less nice things. Habitual to the point that a majority of the time I'm not particularly going out of my way with it (which is primarily a matter of conditioning).<br /> <br /> Hmm, how to keep things on topic...<br /> <br /> Oh, a point that I only ever brought up on the other forum: given description in the core, the game still actively supports being a Lunar outside of the Silver Pact, but I wonder if there would be something more fun in playing somebody who belongs to (or has originated) a rather obscure and marginal school.<br /> <br /> I just keep wanting to think of applications for the concept of the Lunars being distributed in that way, it's fascinating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T11:36:54-08:00","id":1266240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265758#post1265758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually wonder if this is one of those points where the Silver Pact might frown upon you if you do this too much.<br /> While summoning a second circle demon every now and then to assist with a major plan is probably fine, just summoning them randomly to attack Realm holdings seems like it would both antagonize the Realm (and Sidereals, who now have even more reasons to hate you because the Second Circles are also messing with Fate), as well as distance yourself from certain elements of the pact.<br /> I'm not saying every Lunar would oppose such a thing, but I think many would consider unleashing the enemies of Creation with little to no restraint on your enemies careless?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would be <i>quite</i> like this, because the thing about the Terrestrial/Sidereal war of extermination is that they come pretty well pre-antagonized. If the rest of the Silver Pact frowns on you for this practice, it's probably because summoned demons tend to leave easily-followed swathes of unnatural destruction that make it easy for enemies to track them back to their summoners, and also it's a waste of perfectly-useful demons. Like seriously, you get <i>at most</i> one Second Circle per month, and you blow it on a random suicide attack? That's just wasteful, you could have been amassing a fortune with Makarios or having Florivet sweet-talk the weather into being whatever you need for the next year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T12:00:21-08:00","id":1266243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266240#post1266240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's probably because summoned demons tend to leave easily-followed swathes of unnatural destruction that make it easy for enemies to track them back to their summoners</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it would be a good idea to not hang around the place that you summon the demon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">and also it's a waste of perfectly-useful demons. Like seriously, you get <i>at most</i> one Second Circle per month, and you blow it on a random suicide attack? That's just wasteful</div> </div> </div> </div>My my, I do not want to imagine what Octavian would do to somebody who brazenly displayed so little faith in him.<br /> <br /> Or, say Lucien; assassination is his jam, but you think him going to murder the enemies of the Lunars would be suicide?<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, if you're doing something incredibly stupid like ordering them to attack the Imperial Manse or the Lotus Dome (whatever the Bureau of Fate headquarters is called).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T12:46:20-08:00","id":1266247,"title":"","content":"Ma Ha Suchi would be fine. Everyone already knows damn well where he lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T12:56:40-08:00","id":1266249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266247#post1266247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ma Ha Suchi would be fine. Everyone already knows damn well where he lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also that; the occasion in which following a Lunar back to a spot where <i>they'll</i> know you'll know where they are is, in a word, incredibly dumb.<br /> <br /> Territorial Charms are apparently still a thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay gang; after Octavian went and bashed six Dragon Blooded into a mushy pulp before going home, we successfully followed the trail of black oil that will render this land uninhabitable for generations back to where we can probably find the Lunar!&quot;<br /> {quick cut to a pass leading into an overgrown, thorny, dark forest covered with spider webs, as the forlorn howl of a wolf sounds in the distance}<br /> &quot;I ain't going in there.&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah, the Lunar... probably knew that we were coming, and... ran away a long time ago, so looking around in there would just be a waste of time. We sure showed them!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T13:23:35-08:00","id":1266254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266243#post1266243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps it would be a good idea to not hang around the place that you summon the demon.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I don\u2019t mean that the Pact would frown upon the practice, per se - only being careless about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My my, I do not want to imagine what Octavian would do to somebody who brazenly displayed so little faith in him.<br /> <br /> Or, say Lucien; assassination is his jam, but you think him going to murder the enemies of the Lunars would be suicide?<br /> <br /> I mean, sure, if you're doing something incredibly stupid like ordering them to attack the Imperial Manse or the Lotus Dome (whatever the Bureau of Fate headquarters is called). </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sure that Octavian would certainly do a lot of damage before being brought down, but once the Dragon-Blooded manage to rally a sworn kinship or two and maybe a Wyld Hunt, his days in Creation are numbered. Certainly, this can have plenty of strategic value in its own right, I just think that Lunars capable of Celestial Circle Sorcery might have other projects taking priority.<br /> <br /> Lucien or Zsofika, OTOH, are pretty dang likely to kill their targets, but the nature of task-binding is such that you\u2019re only guaranteed one high-priority kill per summoning. Remember, kids - summon smarter, not harder!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T13:47:56-08:00","id":1266259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266254#post1266254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m sure that Octavian would certainly do a lot of damage before being brought down, but once the Dragon-Blooded manage to rally a sworn kinship or two and maybe a Wyld Hunt, his days in Creation are numbered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know; against Octavian's defensive and counterattacking powers, I think even a decent number of Dragon Blooded are going to be hard pressed, unless some of them are Essence 5 or they're fairly advanced in Immaculate Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> He's also hardly a mindless, rampaging monster, he doesn't need to keep pushing until he burns out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think that Lunars capable of Celestial Circle Sorcery might have other projects taking priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's better to think of these things in terms of a toolbox of available assets, distributed appropriately depending on the personalities and motivations of any given Lunar.<br /> <br /> I can probably fall into the trap of defining things in terms of absolutes myself, but my core value is to imagine a variety of scenarios; I wouldn't say that a Lunar who might be inclined to summon demons like Octavian is quite implausible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the nature of task-binding is such that you\u2019re only guaranteed one high-priority kill per summoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhh\u2026 I agree that task-binding shouldn't be gamed with trying to roll an excessive quantity and variety of things into a single Principle, but I think something holistic and multi-faceted like a list of related targets is fair. <br /> <br /> {checks the spell wording again} Maybe... it's probably least dubious if they can be identified as a reasonably compact group, rather than literally providing a list of names and tasking them with getting them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T13:53:51-08:00","id":1266262,"title":"","content":"When you order Octavian to &quot;Kill Cathak Cainan, preferably painfully, and then return to Malfeas,&quot; as your task-binding, Octavian doesn't just...go kill Cathak Cainan!<br /> <br /> First, he puts together an ARMY.<br /> Then he conquers TERRITORY.<br /> Then he DRAFTS EVERYONE IN THAT TERRITORY.<br /> He finds a couple sorcerers or occultists, and uses them to SUMMON DEMON LIEUTENANTS.<br /> Then, he takes his INFERNAL ARMY to go kill Cathak Cainan.<br /> Octavian is a warlord who wants to conquer Creation. This is an excellent test-run against Creation's main defenders that he can use to appraise their tactics, after all.<br /> <br /> The danger in sending 2nd circle demons off to go do dangerous tasks for you is...not that the demon is gonna die without accomplishing much!<br /> It's that the demon might accomplish a bunch first.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T14:06:58-08:00","id":1266266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266262#post1266262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you order Octavian to &quot;Kill Cathak Cainan, preferably painfully, and then return to Malfeas,&quot; as your task-binding</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that last part might be redundant, and otherwise kind of straying away from binding to a specific task.<br /> <br /> As for the rest... like, maybe all of that stuff happens. I think it's fair to sometimes just want to bring up a big punchy demon and point it at somebody, without having to deal with a lot of surrounding noise or just with a general attitude on being expedient, and for Storytellers to accommodate that. I think it's fair for the demon to go large a bit if you give them a task that keeps them in a limited range and with a lot of free time on their hands, but if given something small scale and relatively straightforward in concept, it's reasonable to just do that. Unless the target is remaining under circumstances in which the only way it can be expected to complete the objective is with a lot of intervening steps.<br /> <br /> And Octavian alone is bad enough, what with his oil.<br /> <br /> I think looking at him and saying that you can't give him a task without him making a meal out of it (and taking an excessive amount of time to finish it) is treating demon summoning in literal genie terms that is really against the spirit of what it's supposed to have in the game.<br /> <br /> (Also what's with so much of the all caps Jesus Christ)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T14:18:47-08:00","id":1266272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266266#post1266266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also what's with so much of the all caps Jesus Christ)</div> </div> </div> </div>Because everyone knows INFERNAL ARMIES are much cooler than infernal armies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, while I do agree raising an INFERNAL ARMY to perform an assassination is probably a bit out of bounds, the general potential for those kinds of shenanigans has nothing to do with Literal Genies and everything to do with Blood Apes Are Awful Babysitters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T14:41:19-08:00","id":1266279,"title":"","content":"Octavian strikes me as an all-caps sorta guy.<br /> <br /> There's other demons to summon if all you want is a no-nonsense assassination. Zsofika's good for that, or Mara, or Lucien. Octavian brings more baggage with him.<br /> <br /> 2nd circle demons have intimacies and motivations already. If you summon one, they'll loyally serve you or your orders, and they're smart enough and usually non-alien enough to interpret the spirit of the orders better than blood apes or agatae...but if their proclivities and your orders don't contradict, you should expect them to do the things they live while doing your will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T14:45:44-08:00","id":1266280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266272#post1266272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, while I do agree raising an INFERNAL ARMY to perform an assassination is probably a bit out of bounds, the general potential for those kinds of shenanigans has nothing to do with Literal Genies and everything to do with Blood Apes Are Awful Babysitters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood Apes are Awful Babysitters is about not setting demons tasks to which their personality, temperament and capabilities are ill-suited; blood apes are still good at going to beat people to a pulp and then eat them, and you probably don't incur too many complications from ordering them to do that.<br /> <br /> Octavian is direct, fearsome, and while an empire builder, still has a sensibility of testing and proving his personal mettle; if a person goes to the top of a mountain and calls a challenge to him for seven days straight, he's not likely going to feel the need to turn up and then start raising an army to show them what's what. Telling him to go kill somebody is not giving him something to which he's rather unsuited and liable to accomplish in a manner far outside of what works for you.<br /> <br /> Heck, even in a case in which a target is well protected, there's a question at where the line between raw force and being strategic falls as raising an army to deal with it goes; too much guile in it will rub against his Major Principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 11-10-2018, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T18:43:13-08:00","id":1266311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266266#post1266266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think it's fair to sometimes just want to bring up a big punchy demon and point it at somebody, without having to deal with a lot of surrounding noise or just with a general attitude on being expedient, and for Storytellers to accommodate that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally agree, but in this particular example he's being ordered to kill one of the most influential Dragon-Blooded alive whose presumably at least an ocean away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T18:45:12-08:00","id":1266312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266311#post1266311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally agree, but in this particular example he's being ordered to kill one of the most influential Dragon-Blooded alive whose presumably at least an ocean away.</div> </div> </div> </div>The terms of his binding are also vaguely given in this instance, so he probably would crack his knuckles and say &quot;awesome, time to do things my way!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-10T20:39:56-08:00","id":1266335,"title":"","content":"One thing in regards to Creation-spanning organizations and long distances: quite aside from the magic and real-life counterexamples, Creation isn't actually a bronze-age setting. It's a setting that has had, like, at least three world-spanning discontinuity events. That we know of. Lunars especially have more continuity of experience where even if you don't recall the First Age, at most you learned from someone who learned from someone who did. Technology isn't just flashy gadgets, but evolving process and norms.<br /> <br /> Lunars have magic, shapeshifting, and important reasons to keep in touch. The Guild, at least in Masters of Jade, is more a cartel of cartels than a monolithic organization.<br /> <br /> So no, neither the Silver Pact nor the Guild are particularly unbelievable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T03:43:31-08:00","id":1266374,"title":"","content":"Octavian comes with a free Agata so mobility wise he's actually pretty good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T04:47:44-08:00","id":1266380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266335#post1266335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing in regards to Creation-spanning organizations and long distances: quite aside from the magic and real-life counterexamples, Creation isn't actually a bronze-age setting. It's a setting that has had, like, at least three world-spanning discontinuity events.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the latter Bronze Age (aka the Bronze Dark Age) was after the Bronze Age collapse.<br /> <br /> And, mythologically, many civilisations believed themselves to have survived a massive discontinuity event; the flood, the fall of Atlantis, etc.<br /> <br /> I mean, I do see your point about the Lunars; the Silver Pact is a continuation of an organisation that developed over the 5000 years of the First Age, re-organised itself after the Usurpation, and while many of the members died in the Great Contagion, enough survived to reconstitute itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That we know of. Lunars especially have more continuity of experience where even if you don't recall the First Age, at most you learned from someone who learned from someone who did. Technology isn't just flashy gadgets, but evolving process and norms.<br /> <br /> Lunars have magic, shapeshifting, and important reasons to keep in touch. </div> </div> </div> While I agree, these don't really apply to the Guild (which is purely a post-collapse organisation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Guild, at least in Masters of Jade, is more a cartel of cartels than a monolithic organisation.<br /> <br /> So no, neither the Silver Pact nor the Guild are particularly unbelievable. </div> </div> </div>To some extent, but I have to admit, it does seem somewhat monolithic. I mean, it's somewhat of a cartel of cartels, but I do find the level of organisation required to be one thing across the entire world a bit much. I mean, I could see it in the River Province, but in the River Province and the North and the South and the distant, distant West, seems a bit much.<br /> <br /> One &quot;Guild&quot; per direction I could see, but I'd expect them to be very culturally different.<br /> <br /> I mean, not that I really mind; it's quite appropriate genre-wise (if, IMO, a bit DnD-esque). But I do find it a bit unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T05:09:46-08:00","id":1266384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266380#post1266380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To some extent, but I have to admit, it does seem somewhat monolithic. I mean, it's somewhat of a cartel of cartels, but I do find the level of organisation required to be one thing across the entire world a bit much. I mean, I could see it in the River Province, but in the River Province and the North and the South and the distant, distant West, seems a bit much.<br /> <br /> One &quot;Guild&quot; per direction I could see, but I'd expect them to be very culturally different.<br /> <br /> I mean, not that I really mind; it's quite appropriate genre-wise (if, IMO, a bit DnD-esque). But I do find it a bit unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably more for another thread, so I'll just chop it off at &quot;the Guild can use magic <i>too</i>, you know, and they have the money to afford it.&quot; Although I would expect a 3e Masters of Jade-esque book to highlight the regional differences, the way theoretically allied merchants might conflict, etc, etc. (Then again, MoJ was written just as the writers were considering what a third edition might need, wasn't it?)<br /> <br /> Anyway, Lunars. I appreciate that we're taking the distances more seriously this edition, but never forget great distances are a bit like the disease rules: they're there to make it all the more impressive when the Exalted circumvent them. It might be one or two months to go from the outermost regions of Creation to the Imperial Mountain for any mode of travel short of Stormwind Rider and high-speed flying craft, but I imagine most Lunars wouldn't be doing simple point A to point B travel but plan to accomplish things along the way. (Perhaps in a given region, one Lunar acts as a regular messenger and works a circuit, for example.)<br /> <br /> And hey, never underestimate the value of cheating via the Wyld.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T06:22:39-08:00","id":1266389,"title":"","content":"The impression I get is the guild isn\u2019t worldwide, but trying to be. They are heavily in the River Province and the South, and have some major routes in the North and East, and want a presence in the West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T08:21:02-08:00","id":1266414,"title":"","content":"I like what I'm reading.<br /> <br /> I wonder why they'd make a decision to change their own Castes, though? What's the case that three are better than five? Would one be yet-better than three? Do we still have the Casteless?<br /> <br /> (Also, when's the kick? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T08:33:05-08:00","id":1266418,"title":"","content":"I imagine it's not that 3 is better than 5, but that the new 3 had more useful power than the old.<br /> <br /> Their old castes put them into the role of guides, judges, world-walkers, mystics and guardians. Appropriate for a relatively peaceful and civilised age where they had a public high role.<br /> <br /> For a new, savage age, where Heaven and Earth were under the control of their foes, they needed to remake themselves into guerilla warrior-barbarians. And so they became bestial warriors, cunning tricksters, and dark witches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T09:23:24-08:00","id":1266425,"title":"","content":"Interesting take on it, Oz!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T09:26:14-08:00","id":1266426,"title":"","content":"And yeah, there are still casteless. They are hopefully gonna be more viable this edition than last. None of that slowly turning into a shoggoth business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T10:11:57-08:00","id":1266438,"title":"","content":"They have their own anima powers, so they should be sweet","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T10:18:20-08:00","id":1266441,"title":"","content":"Is this going to be <i>another</i> edition where the Lunars have a massive murderhateboner for all Dragon-Blooded because they killed the Solars, because the Lunars are apparently too stupid to remember that the Solars were a bunch of lunatic tyrants that committed daily atrocities on everyone else in Creation despite the fact that several of their elders <i>were alive during said time</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T11:03:51-08:00","id":1266454,"title":"","content":"Solar atrocities isn't as deep as it was in 2e now in 3e, they do act tyrannical but to realistic extent, the big worry about them was the Solars going on a giant Civil War with each other which wouldn't have been good, also remember Lunars have Limit as well. They probably weren't that well off either. Also Lunars having hateboners on the realm has less to do with what they did to the Solars in that they also killed and pushed them back to the very edges of a Creation and had been hunting them ever since as Anathema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T11:24:33-08:00","id":1266460,"title":"","content":"I like the emphasis that Lunars are equally at home in the wild and civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T12:14:44-08:00","id":1266470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266441#post1266441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this going to be <i>another</i> edition where the Lunars have a massive murderhateboner for all Dragon-Blooded because they killed the Solars, because the Lunars are apparently too stupid to remember that the Solars were a bunch of lunatic tyrants that committed daily atrocities on everyone else in Creation despite the fact that several of their elders <i>were alive during said time</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vision of Darkness hadn't happened yet.<br /> <br /> Many Lunars were standing cheerfully right at the side of their Solar mates.<br /> <br /> Losing the Solars has had a profound spiritual effect on those of them who had Bonds; the metaphysical connection makes it complicated whether or not a given Lunar's relationship with their Solar was positive.<br /> <br /> As one might note if one read the core book, many Lunars don't want their Solars back, and want to destroy the lingering remnants of the Realm so that they can be free of the memory of them.<br /> <br /> Quite a lot of Lunars are a lot more annoyed at the fact that the damn Dragon Blooded keep trying to kill <b>them</b>.<br /> <br /> I believe that those answer your question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T13:50:54-08:00","id":1266489,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Lunars are Anathema (and, in fact, are what most common people would <i>think of</i> when you say &quot;Anathema&quot;). That doesn't do a lot to win their love and admiration, so after the first round of &quot;whatever they did to get on the list&quot;, it's fairly self-perpetuating.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, please forget everything you know from Dreams of the First Age or similar materials. It is <i>not</i> canonical that Solars in the 3rd edition version of Creation were all terrible monsters. (It is almost certain a handful were, but what was done with said monsters has not been said. Maybe they got judged by a jury of their peers, maybe they were allowed to run wild in their fiefdoms, whatever. We don't know.) All we know is the Sidereal prophesy of Bronze and Gold still happened, and the Sidereals still went with the &quot;murder all the Solars&quot; option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T15:04:38-08:00","id":1266501,"title":"","content":"I mean, it seems likely that some Solars were doing bad things, otherwise why would the Dragonblood get behind the Usurpation?<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean that, you know, Lunars weren't mad about the fact that a lot of Lunars were murdered in the Usurpation, and they were then hunted across the world<br /> <br /> Not to mention that while that Solar over there might have been a monster, their good Solar friend wasn't, and also got killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T15:45:52-08:00","id":1266507,"title":"","content":"On the subject the Usurpation and the Lunars, does the Solar Bond as in 3e help explain at all why the Sidereals+Dragonblooded would be tempted to &quot;rub out&quot; the Lunars from their vision of the world? Seeing them as inherently corruptible to Solar influence? <br /> <br /> One of the tough points from previous editions is why the Sidereals+Dragonblooded would've wanted to perpetuate warfare between Dragonblooded+Lunars, after the Solars, given that the Lunars collectively abandoned the Solar Exalted and weren't complicit in atrocity or risk to the world at large. It ended up often in vague ideas that the Sidereals perceived the Lunars to be &quot;too wild&quot; or that compromise could inherently not be managed between Dragonblooded and Lunars for unspecified reasons. It would be nice if 3e actually some logic there that made it seem tenable why they would want to freeze Lunars out and not engage in post Usurpation peacemaking, while allowing for possibility that the Lunars may have been unjustly wronged.<br /> <br /> (This may be a question with very obvious answers in what's been published on the blogs so far, but I'm taking a bit of a &quot;I'll wait til it's published in a big fat book&quot; approach to material in 3rd so far, and so I'll have missed it.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T15:49:24-08:00","id":1266509,"title":"","content":"Also how the Dragon-Blooded took a civilization that was, if not <i>good</i>, at least <i>functional </i>and replaced it with a world-eating nightmare junta out of Mad Max. No matter how the Sidereals might say that it was justified, that it was necessary, that the Shogunate was only ever meant as a transitional state until a more-functional form of government could be established, that last part never happened, and we have no indication that either the Dragon-Blooded or the Sidereals <i>ever </i>offered peace to the Lunars, except in the sense of &quot;make a desert and call it...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:04:50-08:00","id":1266515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266507#post1266507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject the Usurpation and the Lunars, does the Solar Bond as in 3e help explain at all why the Sidereals+Dragonblooded would be tempted to &amp;quot;rub out&amp;quot; the Lunars from their vision of the world? Seeing them as inherently corruptible to Solar influence? <br /> <br /> One of the tough points from previous editions is why the Sidereals+Dragonblooded would've wanted to perpetuate warfare between Dragonblooded+Lunars, after the Solars, given that the Lunars collectively abandoned the Solar Exalted and weren't complicit in atrocity or risk to the world at large. It ended up often in vague ideas that the Sidereals perceived the Lunars to be &amp;quot;too wild&amp;quot; or that compromise could inherently not be managed between Dragonblooded and Lunars for unspecified reasons. It would be nice if 3e actually some logic there that made it seem tenable why they would want to freeze Lunars out and not engage in post Usurpation peacemaking, while allowing for possibility that the Lunars may have been unjustly wronged.<br /> <br /> (This may be a question with very obvious answers in what's been published on the blogs so far, but I'm taking a bit of a &amp;quot;I'll wait til it's published in a big fat book&amp;quot; approach to material in 3rd so far, and so I'll have missed it.).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I'd say no more than 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, Lunars had a 0-5 penalty on their MDV vs their mate. In 3rd ed, they have a positive intimacy (well, 1/4 don't even have mates).<br /> <br /> So I'd say they're about as influenceable in 3rd as 2nd.<br /> <br /> Though 2nd ed Solars had much more powerful social charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:10:24-08:00","id":1266517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266515#post1266515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, I'd say no more than 2nd ed.<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, Lunars had a 0-5 penalty on their MDV vs their mate. In 3rd ed, they have a positive intimacy (well, 1/4 don't even have mates).<br /> <br /> So I'd say they're about as influenceable in 3rd as 2nd.<br /> <br /> Though 2nd ed Solars had much more powerful social charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>3e seems to cut the other way a lot more often. After all, in 3e, a Lunar mate can cut through Stubborn Boar Defense, outright ignoring it. The bond is also an opt-in instead of an unavoidable albatross around the neck from the moment the Second Breath hits, at least from the chargen perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:14:52-08:00","id":1266519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266515#post1266515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 3rd ed, they have a positive intimacy</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tie doesn't have to be positive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:18:05-08:00","id":1266523,"title":"","content":"So three reasons (I can see) in 3e why the forever war exists for the Lunars:<br /> <br /> 1. The Sidereals and Dragonblooded tried to exterminate them during the ursupation and beyond. Survival requires that they either die or stop.<br /> <br /> 2. The non- bonded Lunars had friends/lovers/colleagues amongst the slain. Thats grounds enough for a vandetta in the mortal world. The bonded Lunars literally have a mental/spiritual switch that fills them with a primal rage on account of this.<br /> <br /> 3. Some Lunars think they can make a more functional world than the first age one. After all they are still miracle workers of the first stripe, and only slightly lower than the Solars in possible applications of power.<br /> <br /> But for that to happen the Realm and it\u2019s secret masters must be gutted.<br /> <br /> So a motivation for every god-Beast that wants to kill Dragonblooded and Sidereals! Also reason enough for the Sidereals and Dragonblooded to want them gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 11-11-2018, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:36:45-08:00","id":1266529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265913#post1265913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what Vance and Minton mentioned on the Discord his war with Raksi over the future of the Silver Pact is why he's disillusioned with Exalted politics in the current game.</div> </div> </div> </div>With that, I can breathe a sigh of relief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:38:29-08:00","id":1266530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266515#post1266515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, 1/4 don't even have mates</div> </div> </div> </div>Or some lucky Solars got to double up on Lunar Mates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:43:33-08:00","id":1266535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266530#post1266530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or some lucky Solars got to double up on Lunar Mates.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cLucky\u201d. 10char.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:50:32-08:00","id":1266536,"title":"","content":"During the Old Realm, I kind of gathered Lunars were the Number Two on the general political power totem pole. I think if anything, a good chunk of elders are pissed that they didn't just lose their allies, but the entire power base they had built themselves into got pulled out from under them. They got purged when they were, for many of the, second in line to succession.<br /> <br /> I think a big thing to remember how much the politics for Lunars this edition is about the <i>Shogunate</i> and its successor states. And the mess of coups in general informs a lot about Lunars in specific I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T17:20:18-08:00","id":1266546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265708#post1265708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I respond to other points, I wanted to point out something I thought was interesting.<br /> <br /> Holden was very big into barbarianism. He wanted it to be a key theme of Lunars. Not the ideological barbarianism of 1st ed, but a barbarian aesthetic.<br /> I haven't particularly got that from any of the 3rd ed fluff we've seen so far. I wonder if it's been dropped.<br /> Or, perhaps, since it's aesthetic, it's something that'd maybe be most noticeable in the book's art, not the fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>The First Edition Lunar manual had a much more distinctive and TASTY aesthetic than the second. The second was all clean lines and panels, but the first was rough-hewn rocks, ragged hide scroll-canvas, scrawling Clawspeak writing, and with illustrations that constantly showed fur, feather, fang, and scale.<br /> <br /> I would also expect the barbarian aesthetic to appear in Lunar Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T18:37:30-08:00","id":1266567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266519#post1266519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Tie doesn't have to be positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh nice! I didn\u2019t notice that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T19:39:13-08:00","id":1266582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266546#post1266546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The First Edition Lunar manual had a much more distinctive and TASTY aesthetic than the second. The second was all clean lines and panels, but the first was rough-hewn rocks, ragged hide scroll-canvas, scrawling Clawspeak writing, and with illustrations that constantly showed fur, feather, fang, and scale.<br /> <br /> I would also expect the barbarian aesthetic to appear in Lunar Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, it also had a very poor understanding of 'barbarism' beyond 'kinda looks like the Conan movies'.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the words I'd prefer for Lunars are less &quot;barbaric&quot; and more... I don't know. Nomadic? (But they can be settled.) Uncivilized? (But that implies some level of rough hewn impoliteness, and many of these cultures have quite elaborate social structures.)<br /> <br /> Untamed probably works the best, given the animal motif. They might still be friendly, they might even be allies... but like Aslan, they aren't <i>tame</i> lions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T19:55:53-08:00","id":1266587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266509#post1266509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how the Dragon-Blooded took a civilization that was, if not <i>good</i>, at least <i>functional </i>and replaced it with a world-eating nightmare junta out of Mad Max. No matter how the Sidereals might say that it was justified, that it was necessary, that the Shogunate was only ever meant as a transitional state until a more-functional form of government could be established, that last part never happened, and we have no indication that either the Dragon-Blooded or the Sidereals <i>ever </i>offered peace to the Lunars, except in the sense of &quot;make a desert and call it...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>World-Eating Nigthmare is not exactly how I would describe the Shogunate. That's by far an exaggeration. The Shogunate was a time of war, and while that has horrific effects on it's own, that's also not much different from most of history. It was certainly functional, that's its selling point. While it was an age that never could recreate the splendor of the first one it still served you its purpose. Also the era it replaced certainly wasn't functional, it was at the tipping point of collapsing. With from the sound of it threats flaring so high at a possibility of a complete Solar Civil War(though it's not like this age didn't have wars of it's own. Since 3e is making it less of a monolithic period, this one seem to possibly be the most drastic though, makes sense since at this time all the first age weaponry was in full stock unlike now)<br /> <br /> In any case though while the Shogunate has plenty of bad I don't think it's nearly at the level of unrealistic abuse","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T21:03:37-08:00","id":1266604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1265586#post1265586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or indeed, for your shanan-ha (I'll familiarise myself with the exact term eventually) to turn up on <i>your</i> door for a chat, a check-in, a moment of respite. Given what the Silver Pact is up to, I imagine that for the teachers of schools of activity to be cloistered is the exception more often than the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this new &quot;teacher and school&quot; approach to Lunar society.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much exactly the sort of thing I wanted to try with my &quot;Dragon's Uncle&quot; character. The Lunar who travels the Threshold, finding Lost Egg Dragon-Blooded and giving them guidance, advice, training, and direction. Letting them know where they could find others of their own kind, to gather together for strength. Telling them the truth about the Immaculate Faith and the Celestial Exalted, and warning them about how the Realm would really treat them and their people if they didn't resist it.<br /> <br /> There's no reason why a Lunar's school needs to be exclusively Lunar, after all, and any Exalted allies are a considerable asset.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, a conversation a while ago came up about the question of whether or not Dominions would make for good expansion material in the way that underdeveloped Terrestrial groups did for Heirs of the Shogunate. I maintain that they do not, but think that schools, present and past, sound like a very strong thing to put into that slot. </div> </div> </div>I certainly agree that Lunar schools are a stronger source of material for a stretch-goal expansion book. Lunar dominions would instead become side-material packaged under the write-ups for the leaders and luminaries of particularly powerful or unique schools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T22:45:28-08:00","id":1266613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266501#post1266501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it seems likely that some Solars were doing bad things, otherwise why would the Dragonblood get behind the Usurpation?</div> </div> </div> </div>While even I would imagine the end of the First Age as a time in which the majority of Solars had become very strongly corrupted by the Great Curse as to be on the path to making Creation into a horror story, I can't lend credibility to the idea that the worst excesses were already being engaged in, as it removes a lot of shock and surprise from the Usurpation, and certainly does make any longstanding loyalty or uncertainty on the part of, say, Celestial gods seem kind of dumb. <br /> <br /> That and some of the presentations of the Unconquered Sun turning his face from the Solars gives me a preference for the idea that it was still in the stages where the Exalted were so far gone was often rather subtle.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I see the space being open-ended enough to provide a variety of ideas, often rooted in a more realpolitik take on the latter-day Realm.<br /> <br /> The image that I've had in mind for a while was that the growth in numbers of the Dragon Blooded and complexity of their administrative tasks was convergent with an increasing consolidation of power in the Second Deliberative, that a lot of Terrestrial Exalted agitated against. There was a growing sentiments of ideas such as them deserving a seat at the major council, that the degree to which that council existed was overstepping its bounds and treading on their Exalted liberties, some of them wanting to integrate temporal power with their hereditary Exaltation, and often a general notion that they were spread so far and so deeply embedded in its functioning and institutions that they were the true foundation of the Realm.<br /> <br /> A bit less Shakespeare's depiction of war against Richard III, a bit more the barons fighting to establish the Magna Carta.<br /> <br /> There were ideologues among them who stirred up a lot of fiery rhetoric about how the Solars had become corrupted by their power and constituted a danger to all the world, who would often be focal points of the rebellion (and many of whom some original models for the Immaculate Dragons), but many would be going along with it primarily for those more pragmatic reasons and long-standing grievances (and most because, once the die was cast, they saw better prospects from throwing in with their own kind). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that while that Solar over there might have been a monster, their good Solar friend wasn't, and also got killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the mystical nature of the Bond needs to be considered, in addition to a willingness to accept, if not embrace, the idea that the Lunars are not entirely be driven by rational factors.<br /> <br /> I can readily imagine more than a few Lunars who kind of hated their Solars, and still deeply resent the other Exalted both for the loss of those particular individuals, and the general effect it had on them psychologically and spiritually to never get a replacement Solar (even if many of those are the same Lunars who would quite like to never have a Solar again).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266507#post1266507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject the Usurpation and the Lunars, does the Solar Bond as in 3e help explain at all why the Sidereals+Dragonblooded would be tempted to &quot;rub out&quot; the Lunars from their vision of the world? Seeing them as inherently corruptible to Solar influence?<br /> <br /> One of the tough points from previous editions is why the Sidereals+Dragonblooded would've wanted to perpetuate warfare between Dragonblooded+Lunars, after the Solars, given that the Lunars collectively abandoned the Solar Exalted and weren't complicit in atrocity or risk to the world at large. It ended up often in vague ideas that the Sidereals perceived the Lunars to be &quot;too wild&quot; or that compromise could inherently not be managed between Dragonblooded and Lunars for unspecified reasons. It would be nice if 3e actually some logic there that made it seem tenable why they would want to freeze Lunars out and not engage in post Usurpation peacemaking, while allowing for possibility that the Lunars may have been unjustly wronged.<br /> <br /> (This may be a question with very obvious answers in what's been published on the blogs so far, but I'm taking a bit of a &quot;I'll wait til it's published in a big fat book&quot; approach to material in 3rd so far, and so I'll have missed it.).</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer is that Lunars are being set up with a number of Charms to give them a more nuanced and deeper sense of partnership with Solars. Between that and the description of the spiritual quality of the Bond, there's an emergent property in which a lot of Lunars would have been very close with their Solars, and fought hard in their defence (including the idea of valuing a Solar primarily for the ways in which it empowers the Lunar), as well as some Lunars that will maybe have started fighting very hard and cruel once an absence of Solars took them off the proverbial leashe..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266509#post1266509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how the Dragon-Blooded took a civilization that was, if not <i>good</i>, at least <i>functional </i>and replaced it with a world-eating nightmare junta out of Mad Max.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really consistent with how any book has presented the Shogunate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T02:20:20-08:00","id":1266641,"title":"","content":"I doubt the shogunate was any more chaotic that the inter-solar wars that periodically punctuated the first age. Even if the time of the usurpation was an era of peace, it could easily have been a lull in the action before they kicked off again. And according to the sidereal prophecy, the next time it happened they were going to bring creation down with them. <br /> <br /> And that's the thing. The prophecy didn't come out of nowhere. It wasn't that the solars had been peaceful, benevolent protectors who slowly went mad. They were a bunch of volatile superhumans who had got into massive fights before and could easily do so again. The doom that was foretold could easily have been collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T03:22:14-08:00","id":1266649,"title":"","content":"Oh, and spinning off from that thought: The lunars were no better. One of the wars of the first age was them <i>against</i> the solars. So that might be the reason they were also targeted. Not just because they mostly sided with the solars during the usurpation, but because their very nature made them just as prone to civil war, and just as dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T03:47:13-08:00","id":1266658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266641#post1266641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt the shogunate was any more chaotic that the inter-solar wars that periodically punctuated the first age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, that's no fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were a bunch of volatile superhumans who had got into massive fights before and could easily do so again. The doom that was foretold could easily have been collateral damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally pretty meh on the idea that the Sidereals were foreseeing a conflict that was hardly different from any that there had been before, it was just going to be one too many. Discounts the significance of the Great Curse too much.<br /> <br /> Plus the issues with regarding the Solars as nothing more than volatile superhumans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266649#post1266649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and spinning off from that thought: The lunars were no better. One of the wars of the first age was them <i>against</i> the solars. So that might be the reason they were also targeted. Not just because they mostly sided with the solars during the usurpation, but because their very nature made them just as prone to civil war, and just as dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, the Sidereals are against the concept of war now?<br /> <br /> That must make the Department of Battles a bit nervous.<br /> <br /> I mean, until one of them remembers that she's Anys Syn, and literally punches Chejop Kejak's smug face into next week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T04:25:43-08:00","id":1266665,"title":"","content":"No, but think about it. The late First Age was a period of wonder beyond imagining. Artifice was reaching it's zenith, and naturally that meant the destructive capabilities of the exalted were also at an unprecedented high. <br /> <br /> It's like how most people these days would agree that World War 3 would shortly preclude nuclear winter. The sids got a prophecy that the solars were gonna ruin everything unless they did something. The sids looked at the world and went, &quot;yeah, I can totally see how that might go down.&quot; So they had a choice. Talk to the solars, get them to listen, and maybe make sure they steered away from anything that could take them down that path, or get rid of them. <br /> <br /> The lunars, they were a different problem. They're just as prone to war as the solars, and almost their equals at artifice. Even if they got them on board with the usurpation, they may well bring about the prophesied doom in the solars stead, somewhere down the line. Not that they were likely to get on board, as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T05:08:13-08:00","id":1266670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266665#post1266665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but think about it. The late First Age was a period of wonder beyond imagining. Artifice was reaching it's zenith, and naturally that meant the destructive capabilities of the exalted were also at an unprecedented high.<br /> <br /> It's like how most people these days would agree that World War 3 would shortly preclude nuclear winter. The sids got a prophecy that the solars were gonna ruin everything unless they did something. The sids looked at the world and went, &quot;yeah, I can totally see how that might go down.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reminded of a time when somebody suggested that the Wyld might be capable of tossing out something like a big world-ending meteorite. Like, it just coalesces a big rock with sufficient velocity that it could hit Creation with an impact that causes an explosion the size of the world. To which I said, sure, technically possible as something that might appear from the Wyld, but not really in the spirit of the game that is more focused on the clash of grandiose personalities and the question of how people apply power. <br /> <br /> The idea that the world was at risk because of the unthinking proliferation of fantasy nukes doesn't really feel in keeping with that to me.<br /> <br /> Because here's the thing about real life development of nuclear weaponry; that wasn't an inevitable path of technological development (after all, in practical terms, they have proven basically useless despite having been so very expensive). Nuclear weapons exist because of the friggin' Nazis; they exist because a bunch of Jewish physicists in America thought of ways in which the Nazis, with their ideology of killing everybody and their obsession with gigantic impractical doomsday weapons, might apply the concept of nuclear fission, and petitioned Roosevelt to try and get there first so that they would have a deterrent. It's from there you get things like &quot;well, we <i>have</i> the bomb, and invading Japan is going to be pretty damn bloody for everybody involved&quot;, and the USSR feeling that its long term survival in post-World War II tensions required them to have the bomb as well.<br /> <br /> There's a limit to the degree to which I or anybody else can effectively speculate on hypothetical alternate futures, but I feel reasonably confident in saying that nuclear weapons seem a bit less likely in a world in which you don't have people who are <i>deathly afraid of Nazis</i> (or more specifically, intimately familiar with the likelihood that Nazis would want to make weapons like that, which of course they would, they're friggin' Nazis).<br /> <br /> That's not me saying that weapons of mass destruction wouldn't exist in the First Age, that's me making a point about how the important thing is the personalities that drive their creation, whether it be the degenerate who wants to kill enormous numbers of people, or the ones who have to live alongside of them and are deeply afraid.<br /> <br /> In the context of Exalted, I would attribute either or both of those personalities found in the more powerful of the Exalted to the Great Curse. Nobody is making weapons of mass destruction to satisfy intellectual curiosity (barring an intellectual curiosity that has become deeply subverted by the Great Curse).<br /> <br /> Plus that whole angle in which wanting to destroy the world is generally not a rational thing to do, and that having access to weapons of mass destruction does not mean that they get used in every damn war, or that wars in which they almost definitely would be used just happen. Even if the Solars happen to possess such weapons, and some of them have a pressing need to go to war with one another, they're not going to just happen to employ weapons that end up blowing everything up as an unfortunate oopsie-daisy. If an occurrence such as that happens, it's not business as usual except we've unfortunately gotten to the point where the weapons are strong enough to vaporise everything and nobody noticed until it was too late, it's that something has already gone terribly wrong with the scenarios, or the people behind them.<br /> <br /> So even if one interprets the fears of the Sidereal Exalted as a really destructive war, which... fine, the very existence of such a thing still denotes that something has gone rotten in the heart of Denmark.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T07:46:44-08:00","id":1266692,"title":"","content":"Well I mean the Sword of Creation is still a thing. That is something far above then what are most powerful nukes can do, in that you can literally use it to tear apart Creation to it's very core. That's still in the setting, and it is just as destructive and not to mention well known. That is just the top of what was created. As you said we must take in the motives of why they were created, for the Realm Defense Grid its exactly for what it says, defense. Still though that doesn't mean it isn't possible to be abused by someone who knows how to use it, specifically those who created it. The Solars. It just takes one(well maybe more then one) Limit Broken Solar who knows how to deactivate its defenses to cause a lot of harm. Even if the Sword is somehow immune to being abused with how its created, its existence does show plainly that even something with a fragment of its power is something to be very afraid of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:05:35-08:00","id":1266696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266692#post1266692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is something far above then what are most powerful nukes can do</div> </div> </div> </div>It's... differently powerful. You can apparently use it to wipe out an enormous invading army of monsters without massive amounts of collateral damage, unless we're to suppose that all of those Fair Folk were still very far away when it was used.<br /> <br /> But other Editions seem to go with them having gotten as far as the Inland Sea, so it can apparently shoot around all of the cities and people.<br /> <br /> Still, that makes a different argument than &quot;an age of incomparable wonders is inevitably going to make a lot of weapons of mass destruction because that's just how making things works, and when they start fighting one another, what are they going to do, not use their weapons to the fullest, world-melting extent?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">in that you can literally use it to tear apart Creation to it's very core.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing that on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is just the top of what was created. As you said we must take in the motives of why they were created, for the Realm Defense Grid its exactly for what it says, defense. Still though that doesn't mean it isn't possible to be abused by someone who knows how to use it, specifically those who created it. The Solars. It just takes one(well maybe more then one) Limit Broken Solar who knows how to deactivate its defenses to cause a lot of harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends on the Limit Break. People always forget about Heart of Tears.<br /> <br /> You know, now I'm thinking about how What Fire Has Wrought introduced the idea of the Sword having a manse necessary to its functioning all the way in Greyfalls, and about the possibility that narrative purposes might mean that it's worthwhile for the activation of the thing to be a process that takes a bit of time and is dependent on a lot of widely distributed moving parts so that stories involving it can have a bit more variety and afford people a defensive opportunity. Just to be something more involved.<br /> <br /> (All of this under the caveat of finding the idea that the greatest threat presented by the Solars was blowing up the world to be by far the least interesting possibility... especially as it relates to the question of why the Dragon Blooded and Sidereals cast out the Lunar Exalted)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:07:58-08:00","id":1266698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266692#post1266692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I mean the Sword of Creation is still a thing. That is something far above then what are most powerful nukes can do, in that you can literally use it to tear apart Creation to it's very core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:18:35-08:00","id":1266702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266613#post1266613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While even I would imagine the end of the First Age as a time in which the majority of Solars had become very strongly corrupted by the Great Curse as to be on the path to making Creation into a horror story, I can't lend credibility to the idea that the worst excesses were already being engaged in, as it removes a lot of shock and surprise from the Usurpation, and certainly does make any longstanding loyalty or uncertainty on the part of, say, Celestial gods seem kind of dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, it doesn't require that the Solars to have been actually killing millions in experiments or breaking the very nature of reality.<br /> But it's very difficult to get people to take serious action about threats that haven't happened at all yet. They will, however, act to stop a problem that's started from getting much worse.<br /> <br /> Something like this though, I could see:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With that in mind, I see the space being open-ended enough to provide a variety of ideas, often rooted in a more realpolitik take on the latter-day Realm. </div> </div> </div><br /> Less problems like Operation Wyldhand, but generally, in addition to the realpolitik,... a certain King Saul-ishness, if you understand what I mean, to take a genre-appropriate example. (Or David himself in his later years.)<br /> Paranoia. Authoritarianism. Moral compromises that get worse and worse.<br /> <br /> Perhaps things like increasingly byzantine politics, with murders and corruption increasing. It's not that they've started destroying the world... but they're going in a very bad direction and it's getting worse.<br /> <br /> Increasing inequality amongst the Exalted. Solars becoming more and more remote from the concerns of a)the average human and b)the Dragonblood and Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The image that I've had in mind for a while was that the growth in numbers of the Dragon Blooded and complexity of their administrative tasks was convergent with an increasing consolidation of power in the Second Deliberative, that a lot of Terrestrial Exalted agitated against. There was a growing sentiments of ideas such as them deserving a seat at the major council, that the degree to which that council existed was overstepping its bounds and treading on their Exalted liberties, some of them wanting to integrate temporal power with their hereditary Exaltation, and often a general notion that they were spread so far and so deeply embedded in its functioning and institutions that they were the true foundation of the Realm.<br /> <br /> A bit less Shakespeare's depiction of war against Richard III, a bit more the barons fighting to establish the Magna Carta. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't want it to be 100% DBs annoyed at the way they were treated, but I think that could definitely be a major factor.<br /> <br /> As you said, different people would have had different motives. Which means there needs to be multiple reasons to support the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the mystical nature of the Bond needs to be considered, in addition to a willingness to accept, if not embrace, the idea that the Lunars are not entirely be driven by rational factors.<br /> <br /> I can readily imagine more than a few Lunars who kind of hated their Solars, and still deeply resent the other Exalted both for the loss of those particular individuals, and the general effect it had on them psychologically and spiritually to never get a replacement Solar (even if many of those are the same Lunars who would quite like to never have a Solar again). </div> </div> </div>I suppose there's the related fact that even tyrants have families. Even if a Solar queen was tyrannical, and her Lunar husband knew it, he'd still be deeply wounded by her assassination.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-12-2018, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T08:35:14-08:00","id":1266705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266696#post1266696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are you basing that on?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing, just a metaphor of phrase, was not meaning to be taken completely literal. Sorry about that.<br /> <br /> The thing about how destructive the Sword can be is that it can basically initiate a world wide bombardment of of damage that no one can resist. Also I do think it does leave collateral damage seeing how it was described in Arms, just not typically what we would imagine. Like constant tornadoes of fire for example.<br /> <br /> In any case I agree its probably not that easy using the sword mainly seeing the Empress never used in her wars after the Contagion meaning A) there are certain conditions of when it can be used or B) it's so broad and difficult to control it would go against her wish of conquest. In any case I'm just pointing out that Solars did create that is basically a fantasy nuke x 1000, so I can see what dangers can be had between a battle of Solars who had access to big sorcerous workings at a level like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T09:00:09-08:00","id":1266715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266705#post1266705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I do think it does leave collateral damage seeing how it was described in Arms, just not typically what we would imagine. Like constant tornadoes of fire for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm...<br /> <br /> {checks back}<br /> <br /> Kind of... the part about leaving behind the petrified bodies of a bunch of hobgoblins doesn't even really seem like a problem; can't imagine it's harming anybody, and you get to go laugh at them.<br /> <br /> There's other stuff, but it's really me starting to get pedantic in a manner that is not germane to the story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case I'm just pointing out that Solars did create that is basically a fantasy nuke x 1000, so I can see what dangers can be had between a battle of Solars who had access to big sorcerous workings at a level like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not workings, those can never be bigger than a city when they're being obvious.<br /> <br /> And yeah, Solars can still have all kinds of stuff; God-King's Shrike comes to mind. It probably wasn't new at the end of the First Age; might very well have been employed repeatedly over the millenia without the Sidereals seeing the end of the world in it.<br /> <br /> My point is that none of this stuff is used accidentally, none of it just happens because &quot;spirit of invention&quot;, and that if there was a danger of it being used on a scale beyond what can be recovered from (which I don't view as what the Sidereals foretold) the important factor is still Solars that have become severely compromised. Like, far more compromised than just &quot;Solars have had wars before and are probably going to do so again, except this time they'll just happen to have bigger weapons&quot;.<br /> <br /> Still kind of off on a tangent about Lunars and all.<br /> <br /> Mind, if I was to roll it back a bit to the point about the Lunars having had a rather significant war at the start of the First Age (perhaps before their Old Realm castes had settled), well, we run into a bit of a dilemma. Were the actions of the Sidereals driven by a fear of the memory of what Lunars were like before they became bound to Solars, or because they weren't scared <i>enough</i>?<br /> <br /> I prefer the latter; the idea that they turned their blades on the Lunars because they knew so many of them would fight in defence of their Solars (and an expectation of authority and prestige in the world without them), but had widely become very used to the image of the more calm, tamed Lunars who had resided in the Realm. If Raken Thulio wasn't an exile, he might have been able to tell his fellows about what they were like in the old days, and it might have given them pause, although even he probably wouldn't have been able to anticipate what Lunars would be like when old world fury was combined with having their lives and loves stripped away from them.<br /> <br /> Hmm, yes, I definitely feel as though Fangs at the Gate should... not pornographically linger over a number of detailed atrocities, but maybe carefully hint at many Lunars having done performed some rather fearsome actions.<br /> <br /> Heh, although I'd wonder if part of the reason to fear Lunars is being able to very effectively spread some tall tales and disturbing hearsay, combined with a bit of messing around in people's dreams, and most would never know the difference.<br /> <br /> It's probably both, which just leads into why it's so difficult to fight them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T09:18:22-08:00","id":1266717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266702#post1266702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's very difficult to get people to take serious action about threats that haven't happened at all yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would not be surprised if Sidereals literally end up with a social Charm to get people to take seriously something that hasn't happened yet.<br /> <br /> Like, there's more than just &quot;Sidereals saying that bad shit is going to go down is something to take seriously because they can see the future&quot;, they've still got Ability Charms, and prophetic themes in some are more indirect than others.<br /> <br /> But there's barely a hundred of them, and it's probably easier for a god that a Sidereal never got around to talking to to rationalize not taking them seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paranoia. Authoritarianism. Moral compromises that get worse and worse.<br /> <br /> Perhaps things like increasingly byzantine politics, with murders and corruption increasing. It's not that they've started destroying the world... but they're going in a very bad direction and it's getting worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it depends. I once had an image in which that Lookshy weapon to turn everything to crystal was made by a Solar who had become obsessed with the idea of fixing everybody into place in highly durable forms, as that was the only way to keep them all safe. Her Limit Trigger was related to people suffering while she wasn't able to keep an eye on them, and she'd had a long battle against trying to keep everything under as strict an observation as possible, struggling with the difficulty and complexity of that when they kept <i>moving</i>.<br /> <br /> (So many Limit Triggers have always been about innocents suffering, why do so few people incorporate that into their image of the Great Curse?)<br /> <br /> Most of the Dragon Blooded didn't really see that; they saw straightforward consolidation of power and invasion of privacy and unchecked surveillance systems, combined with grievances from a million other quarters and only needing a push from Sidereals who were seeing further and deeper (but never enough to really know <i>why</i> she was trying to turn everybody around her to quartz) to say &quot;what about a world with no Solars at all&quot;.<br /> <br /> As usual, I'll freely admit that this is all shaped by my personal preferences for things of an institutional bent and the limits of communication between people; the depth of a person's motives that disappear with them the moment they die. The Solar Marion Crane who dies before she could ever go home to return that embezzled money, died because she was murdered for a reason that had nothing to do with why she was running and why she wanted to go back, and so all the world can ever see of her thereafter was a thief. That's how I see the world, and so it's how I see a lot of Exalted.<br /> <br /> It goes for the Lunars as well; Sidereals see the future, but they're still human, and so the scope of their vision and depth of their comprehension is still intrinsically limited.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T01:53:09-08:00","id":1266908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266441#post1266441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this going to be <i>another</i> edition where the Lunars have a massive murderhateboner for all Dragon-Blooded because they killed the Solars, because the Lunars are apparently too stupid to remember that the Solars were a bunch of lunatic tyrants that committed daily atrocities on everyone else in Creation despite the fact that several of their elders <i>were alive during said time</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Solars? I don't fight because the Solars were overthrown. I fight because the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded conspired and launched a coup that overthrew <i>me</i> and usurped <i>my</i> place in the world, and then they perpetrated an eternal inquisition and purge against me and my kind.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Solars were a threat to everything and had to be stopped? Yeah, that's the justification the Sidereals spew. You tell me, okay, why, if you're <i>just</i> trying to get rid a threat to Creation, why you would not try to get us -- the guides, judges, world-walkers, mystics and guardians of the First Age -- to help stop them. It was and is nonsense. The Solars were powerful, and some of them were nuts, and that had all been true for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> &quot;If the last part of the First Age seemed a bit darker than previously, you know, <i>maybe</i> it was because the Sidereals had abandoned their role as advisers and guardians of fate in favor of conspiring to take over? Maybe because they convinced the Dragon-Blooded to husband <i>their</i> strength for a war rather than push for reforms?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Sidereals wanted to rule the world, not save it; that's why anyone powerful enough to resist their influence had to go, leaving only pawns they could manipulate. The Dragon-Blooded also wanted to rule, but were dumb enough that they thought the Sidereals were weak, rather than merely subtle; they've been the gauntlet over the Sidereal fist ever since.<br /> <br /> &quot;This war is going to end when the Sidereals are overthrown and punished for their crimes, the power of the Dragon-Blooded is broken, and the Silver Pact holds the palaces of the Blessed Isle. Then you're going to see the glories of the Age of Silver.&quot;<br /> <br /> -- Surviving First Age Lunar Elder, RY 531.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":572,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","user":"Verzio","date":". 11-13-2018, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T03:50:59-08:00","id":1266913,"title":"","content":"We can make arguments, but there's also a degree to which some people need to get over the idea that anybody in the setting needs to adhere to their standards of rationality and objectivity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T03:59:43-08:00","id":1266915,"title":"","content":"&quot;Well, the pact saved me when the wyld hunt had me over a barrel, so I feel like I kind of owe them, y'know?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Also a bunch of realm dragon blooded tried to kill me that one time.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T07:52:05-08:00","id":1266947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266519#post1266519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tie doesn't have to be positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an odd design choice to me considering the plan to not being mandatory, to have it represented as an intimacy, and a character can have multiple intimacies.<br /> <br /> Personally, I ran with it as always being a positive intimacy (but can be a minor); but the Lunar can also have other intimacies toward the Solar and those can be both negative and stronger. But that's me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T08:38:56-08:00","id":1266969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266947#post1266947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like an odd design choice to me considering the plan to not being mandatory, to have it represented as an intimacy, and a character can have multiple intimacies.<br /> <br /> Personally, I ran with it as always being a positive intimacy (but can be a minor); but the Lunar can also have other intimacies toward the Solar and those can be both negative and stronger. But that's me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of it being mandatory for Lunars with mates to have a positive Intimacy strikes me as a significant infringement that is not effectively alleviated by opting out of the Bond altogether.<br /> <br /> A lot of the design choices ought to be put in the context of things that put people off of the Solar Bond in Second Edition, with an eye to making it more widely engaging rather than just saying that people turned off have the option to not play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T08:45:40-08:00","id":1266973,"title":"","content":"I suppose you can choose to have your Lunar fall in love with the Solar they just met if that's the way you want to go; or you could have them hate them at first sight if that's how you want to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T08:53:31-08:00","id":1266975,"title":"","content":"You could also replace that complex system of intimacies with a single one that sums up how you feel. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T16:35:37-08:00","id":1267125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266947#post1266947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like an odd design choice to me considering the plan to not being mandatory, to have it represented as an intimacy, and a character can have multiple intimacies.<br /> <br /> Personally, I ran with it as always being a positive intimacy (but can be a minor); but the Lunar can also have other intimacies toward the Solar and those can be both negative and stronger. But that's me.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't have a Solar mate&quot; is a very different field of possible stories than &quot;My Solar mate has been my eternal rival/enemy/kismesis/etc. throughout countless lifetimes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 11-13-2018, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T17:38:13-08:00","id":1267144,"title":"","content":"A Grendel locked in an eternally repeating struggle with his Beowulf would be a really interesting Mate dynamic for a Lunar with a Solar who wasn\u2019t locked away during the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> Of course the possibility of \u201cbreaking the cycle\u201d is a great story possibility in its own right, especially when you throw in the Chosen of Mars whose job is NOT TO LET THAT HAPPEN.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T17:57:15-08:00","id":1267148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267144#post1267144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Grendel locked in an eternally repeating struggle with his Beowulf would be a really interesting Mate dynamic for a Lunar with a Solar who wasn\u2019t locked away during the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> Of course the possibility of \u201cbreaking the cycle\u201d is a great story possibility in its own right, especially when you throw in the Chosen of Mars whose job is NOT TO LET THAT HAPPEN.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grendel/Beowulf slashfic incoming. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T19:27:33-08:00","id":1267175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267125#post1267125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't have a Solar mate&quot; is a very different field of possible stories than &quot;My Solar mate has been my eternal rival/enemy/kismesis/etc. throughout countless lifetimes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And with the Homestucks in Exalted's audience, I think kismesis might even be a word most of the folks here get. But yeah, forcing the intimacy to be positive sort of misses the point; it seems intended now to be a <i>bond</i>, but not necessarily a point of weakness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T19:44:51-08:00","id":1267179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267125#post1267125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't have a Solar mate&quot; is a very different field of possible stories than &quot;My Solar mate has been my eternal rival/enemy/kismesis/etc. throughout countless lifetimes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we going to see any examples of Lunars who have such a relationship with their bonded Solar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T20:10:02-08:00","id":1267184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267179#post1267179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we going to see any examples of Lunars who have such a relationship with their bonded Solar?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're not focusing on it, in part because perceptions of the Bond in past editions have largely focused on relationships that were harmful to one or both parties involved, and we want to turn that around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T21:34:18-08:00","id":1267188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267125#post1267125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">kismesis</div> </div> </div> </div>A whatnow and why does looking it up on Wikipedia redirect to \u201cShipping (fandom)?\u201d O_o","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T21:45:17-08:00","id":1267189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267188#post1267188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A whatnow and why does looking it up on Wikipedia redirect to \u201cShipping (fandom)?\u201d O_o</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://mspaintadventures.wikia.com/wiki/Quadrants\" target=\"_blank\">Try this wiki instead.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T00:43:19-08:00","id":1267213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267125#post1267125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I don't have a Solar mate&quot; is a very different field of possible stories than &quot;My Solar mate has been my eternal rival/enemy/kismesis/etc. throughout countless lifetimes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't that just a strong &quot;normal/standard&quot; intimacy carrying over between exaltations? If that is part of the Solar bond, then wouldn't it actually limit those stories to only Lunars toward one Solar (well, and Infernals if the &quot;no mind-whipe&quot; still stands)?<br /> <br /> I'm curious, what is the in-game rational for those eternal grudges being part of the bond?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T01:07:39-08:00","id":1267218,"title":"","content":"A scenario I envision:<br /> <br /> Stalking Shadow has a grudge against Invincible Sword Princess. It\u2019s one that was set in the first age, a minor irritation at the rigidness of her demeanour.<br /> <br /> So they set out to prank her (Lunar pranks can run the gamut from eating all the cakes to eviscerating your rivals, because nyah, marked them first!)<br /> <br /> And in doing so they discover that ISP is good and noble, not to mention skilled and beautiful. <br /> <br /> And ISP starts to appreciate the sulky shadow that dogs her steps like a playful puppy-Kaiju.<br /> <br /> But they never stop being irritated by ISP\u2019s straight as an arrow soul. And she has a similar aversion to Stalking Shadow\u2019s love of subterfuge.<br /> <br /> So even a minor negative intimacy can lead to a whole raft of positive ones (or not). It\u2019s just a hook, really.<br /> <br /> Or a red thread, if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 11-14-2018, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T02:07:38-08:00","id":1267228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267213#post1267213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But isn't that just a strong &quot;normal/standard&quot; intimacy carrying over between exaltations? If that is part of the Solar bond, then wouldn't it actually limit those stories to only Lunars toward one Solar (well, and Infernals if the &quot;no mind-whipe&quot; still stands)?<br /> <br /> I'm curious, what is the in-game rational for those eternal grudges being part of the bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you actually reading Vance's post as saying that all Solar Bonds are a matter of recurring enemies and rivals?<br /> <br /> Also, what does &quot;wouldn't it actually limit those stories to only Lunars toward one Solar&quot; mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T02:52:50-08:00","id":1267232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267228#post1267228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you actually reading Vance's post as saying that all Solar Bonds are a matter of recurring enemies and rivals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reading him as saying that the Solar Bond are supposed to be both positive and negative in Ex3, yes. I'm reading his rational for this is to also support those stories, yes.<br /> <br /> My comment is, both stories around positive and negative emotions spanning lifetimes is supported under the current intimacy system; which earlier editions didn't really handled mechanical wise (and probably neither very well fluff wise). For example, I personally don't see Lilith to have a negative Solar Bond. I see her having a pile of other negative intimacies toward Desus' Exaltation and things he represented.<br /> <br /> Back in second edition, due to how the intimacies worked there, it would make more sense to say &quot;the bond can be negative&quot; (especially when it was seen as mandatory) as it would basically be all those things wrapped into one single value. Hey, there is a reason why I ran with Ex3's intimacies and social system when running my 2.5ish game.<br /> <br /> If the bond itself can be negative, then I'm interested in the in-game rational for the creation of the Bond (it could for example be accidental or from a deeper deception from Luna toward UCS, which would be two ways to explain why a the Bond itself can be negative).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what does &quot;wouldn't it actually limit those stories to only Lunars toward one Solar&quot; mean? </div> </div> </div>That should have been: &quot;wouldn't it actually limit those stories to only Lunars, and toward one Solar each&quot;<br /> <br /> I expect Solar Bonds to be between a Lunar and a Solar, not between say two Solars or between a Solar and a Sidereal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T03:27:20-08:00","id":1267238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267232#post1267232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading him as saying that the Solar Bond are supposed to be both positive and negative in Ex3, yes. I'm reading his rational for this is to also support those stories, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Bond can be either. The Intimacy can in fact change over time in the same Lunar towards the same Solar; although it will always reassert itself, it <i>can</i> be degraded to nothing, and the emotional context of it when it returns is liable to be different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My comment is, both stories around positive and negative emotions spanning lifetimes is supported under the current intimacy system; which earlier editions didn't really handled mechanical wise (and probably neither very well fluff wise). For example, I personally don't see Lilith to have a negative Solar Bond. I see her having a pile of other negative intimacies toward Desus' Exaltation and things he represented.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're still thinking in terms of stories in which Lunars are obligated to feel positively towards their mates, which is still cutting off a lot of possibilities and touching on that whole issue of infringing on an important part of people's characters.<br /> <br /> If you want to advocate for that, you ought to provide a basis for why it should be valued over letting the player and the game scenarios have more control over the manner in which the Bond manifests.<br /> <br /> (Also, one should consider how some of Lilith's story is going to be rewritten)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the bond itself can be negative, then I'm interested in the in-game rational for the creation of the Bond (it could for example be accidental or from a deeper deception from Luna toward UCS, which would be two ways to explain why a the Bond itself can be negative).</div> </div> </div> </div>It would appear that you missed the previews about it (I'll find a link later), but for the moment I'll summarise it as something that has nothing to do with the gods; in the early First Age, a lot of Lunars got into a significant conflict with many Solars, which was ultimately resolved by a truce founded on a kind of ritualistic marriage, that the Lunar Exaltation ultimately integrated as a recurring metaphysical connection to an associated Solar, from which Lunars could draw strength and stability.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the Bond being optional is a matter of how there are 100 more Lunars than there are Solars, so even if one assumes that every Solar has a Lunar mate, there aren't enough Solars for every Lunar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That should have been: &quot;wouldn't it actually limit those stories to only Lunars, and toward one Solar each&quot;<br /> <br /> I expect Solar Bonds to be between a Lunar and a Solar, not between say two Solars or between a Solar and a Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Various Exalted can have recurring reincarnated relationships, but the connection between Solars and Lunars is made distinct and codified and gives the latter Exalted a bunch of special conditions and applications in a lot of their Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T03:47:25-08:00","id":1267242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267238#post1267238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would appear that you missed the previews about it (I'll find a link later), but for the moment I'll summarise it as something that has nothing to do with the gods; in the early First Age, a lot of Lunars got into a significant conflict with many Solars, which was ultimately resolved by a truce founded on a kind of ritualistic marriage, that the Lunar Exaltation ultimately integrated as a recurring metaphysical connection to an associated Solar, from which Lunars could draw strength and stability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to not derail the thread more, I accept that as an answer and backs out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T04:00:08-08:00","id":1267246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267242#post1267242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, to not derail the thread more, I accept that as an answer and backs out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh come now, it's explicitly a thread for the discussion of previews of the Lunar Exalted in the new Edition. Talking about how you feel about a change in depiction is in no way a derail, and I for one would welcome the conversation.<br /> <br /> Good Lord, the tangent into First Age weapons of mass destruction was more of a derail than talking about the Solar Bond would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T05:00:12-08:00","id":1267260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267246#post1267246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh come now, it's explicitly a thread for the discussion of previews of the Lunar Exalted in the new Edition. Talking about how you feel about a change in depiction is in no way a derail, and I for one would welcome the conversation.<br /> <br /> Good Lord, the tangent into First Age weapons of mass destruction was more of a derail than talking about the Solar Bond would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as I've mentioned a few times before, I only buy Ex3 to poach things for my 2.5-ish setting. I guess my interpretation/hack of the setting isn't closer to 2.5 than what Ex3 is, but Ex3 seems to be taking Exalted in a 90 degrees angle from where I'm personally takes things, so 2.5 is still closer to what I want than Ex3.<br /> <br /> So personally I feel the discussion should mainly be held by people wanting to play Ex3 and like the general direction it is taking, and any discussion about what I feel about changes should mainly be held in some other thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hm... Maybe I should make an &quot;Edition L&quot; thread or something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T05:51:49-08:00","id":1267267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267238#post1267238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would appear that you missed the previews about it (I'll find a link later), but for the moment I'll summarise it as something that has nothing to do with the gods; in the early First Age, a lot of Lunars got into a significant conflict with many Solars, which was ultimately resolved by a truce founded on a kind of ritualistic marriage, that the Lunar Exaltation ultimately integrated as a recurring metaphysical connection to an associated Solar, from which Lunars could draw strength and stability.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that the Bond being optional is a matter of how there are 100 more Lunars than there are Solars, so even if one assumes that every Solar has a Lunar mate, there aren't enough Solars for every Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me one of the story ideas for a small group, which is typically what I played in, that was inspired by the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/solar-bonds-exalted-3rd-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">Bond</a> write up would be to follow a Bond through the various incarnations, especially since the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-lunar-exalted-exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">newest update</a> for Lunars discusses the, sometime, drastic changes that Lunars have under gone over the years.<br /> <br /> The other, perhaps bigger thing, that these two updates have done is to bring back to looking at Exalted. I played a lot of 1e stuff, looked at 2e, and then initially felt that the 3e changes were not going in a direction I wanted. After reading the Lunar updates, I'm excited to give Lunars a try, as they have been my favorite Exalt since their intro in 1e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T06:21:20-08:00","id":1267270,"title":"","content":"My internet went down, so I didn't get round to responding to this, but there's probably some interesting things to discuss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266717#post1266717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would not be surprised if Sidereals literally end up with a social Charm to get people to take seriously something that hasn't happened yet.</div> </div> </div> </div> That would be very useful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But there's barely a hundred of them, and it's probably easier for a god that a Sidereal never got around to talking to to rationalize not taking them seriously. </div> </div> </div>True, but in this case I was thinking about the Dragonblooded, of whom there were thousands to convince, and who had social defences against Sidereal charms. As you say, it's easy to rationalise not taking them seriously if you don't hear them personally, but I think it's also pretty easy to rationalise ignoring a Sidereal who says &quot;I want you and your family to murder your really nice Queen who you've served loyally for generations, who gave you birthday presents every year, built you a lovely house with their own two hands, and who trusted you with important jobs, because I've foreseen that she'll murder your family.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whereas I think the Dragonblooded would be much more likely to respond to &quot;I have foreseen that your increasingly erratic boss, who's become obsessed with their strange esoteric research, and responds with irrational anger to attempts to force her to actually administrate her kingdom properly, but also refuses to let you do it for her, is going to get worse until eventually she flips out and murders your whole family.&quot;<br /> <br /> Essentially, I think it's easier to rationalise the Dragonblood's decision if the Solars were noticeably worse (as a whole, not necessarily individually) than in the past.<br /> Also, of course, it motivates the Sidereals themselves. First, to cast the Great Prophecy, an unprecedented act. Secondly, that they eventually decided that revolution was the solution, as they believed restraining the Solars was too difficult. If things had been pretty fine, they probably would have believed they could maintain it. If things had been getting worse and they hadn't been able to stop it, then that explains their desperate choice.<br /> <br /> Earlier, you said something about the depiction of why the Unconquered Sun turned his back on the Solars, and how this lead you to have a more subtle view of the Solars? Could you say more about that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, it depends. I once had an image in which that Lookshy weapon to turn everything to crystal was made by a Solar who had become obsessed with the idea of fixing everybody into place in highly durable forms, as that was the only way to keep them all safe. Her Limit Trigger was related to people suffering while she wasn't able to keep an eye on them, and she'd had a long battle against trying to keep everything under as strict an observation as possible, struggling with the difficulty and complexity of that when they kept <i>moving</i>. </div> </div> </div>I think that's a great concept. But surely it's of the &quot;worst excesses of the Solars&quot; school, which you were arguing against?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (So many Limit Triggers have always been about innocents suffering, why do so few people incorporate that into their image of the Great Curse?) </div> </div> </div>I know DotFA and its Signature circle get a bad rap, and it does have its problems, but I always thought that the Heirophant's curse made sense; that, unable to bear the suffering of the world, he'd just convinced himself that everything was great, and he stayed in his ivory tower where everything seemed perfect, because viewing real suffering was just too depressing.<br /> <br /> One of the players in my group maintains that the best example of the dangers of the Great Curse on the Solars is Salina. She wasn't evil or corrupt. She wanted to help humanity. And so, in her compassion, she reshaped the very nature of reality to make it easier to acquire dangerous weapons. Unsurprisingly, the Five-Score Fellowship, whose raison d'etre was to maintain the nature of reality, were horrified, and terrified.<br /> <br /> I think though, there is a reason why people rarely think of compassion when thinking of the Great Curse.<br /> Once our characters were in a foreign city trying to track down an ancient Dragon King necromancer. We failed to find him quick enough, and he unleashed an army of ghosts, zombies, and skeletons, in the middle of the city.<br /> My No Moon, his daughter the Changing Moon and the Slayer ran towards the middle of the city to help. We two Lunars went into DBT and battled ghosts and zombies, while the Slayer reached the middle of the city, turned into a 30 foot monster, and fought the Kaiju-sized Dragon King necromancer.<br /> The Night Caste... sat in his apartment weeping and crying because he was overwhelmed by knowing that hundreds of people had been killed by monsters and he'd been unable to save them.<br /> Which was very annoying for the rest of us, because he wasn't saving more people.<br /> But it's not the kind of thing that'd make you want to kill him.<br /> <br /> Whereas the Twilight's occasional habit of emotionally shutting down under great stress and acting on callous logic (like the time he murdered our injured prisoners), is a pretty obvious reason why, were he a King, his underlings might want to kill him.<br /> <br /> Saying that... <br /> We had a Zenith who had Red Rage of Compassion. We went to negotiate rescuing captives from a Wood King. The Zenith flipped out and attacked the Wood King when he saw the miserable captives, and several captives died in the fight. Another time, we found a woman who'd been cruelly exiled from her village for some venal reason (I forget what). The Zenith flipped out and wiped out the village. There was a couple of other things he did while limit breaking, but I don't remember what. <br /> They were bad enough that he eventually killed himself.<br /> <br /> So, I think the Great Curse can of course be something that twists people's own good motives (compassion, virtue, etc) and ends up causing problems for society with their extreme actions. Whether that be liberal interventionism or putting everyone in crystal.<br /> <br /> But it's the actions that led to the Usurpation, not the Solar's motives (I mean, many Sidereals considered the Solars insane rather than evil), so I think it ends up much the same. &quot;The Solars of the First Age became mad and committed atrocities&quot; is still the same if some of those Solars were doing it for good motives.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T08:36:21-08:00","id":1267303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267260#post1267260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the discussion should mainly be held by people wanting to play Ex3 and like the general direction it is taking</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it could get kind of dull if the conversation consisted only of people that agreed, and if nothing else, a bit of contrasting viewpoints could be stimulating. <br /> <br /> I'll admit to an ulterior motive of wanting something to get my teeth into in a general manner; not for a fight or anything, just something that demands a bit of invested conversation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T09:02:28-08:00","id":1267310,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to clarify something. The origins of the Bond actually changed during 2nd edition, the story in MoEP: Lunars about the Unconquered Sun trying to force Luna to make her chosen bow to his is utterly incompatible it was with their characterisations in Glories of the Most High and the Ink Monkeys era treated a lot of what that book had to say as apocryphal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T09:10:10-08:00","id":1267317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267270#post1267270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but in this case I was thinking about the Dragonblooded, of whom there were thousands to convince, and who had social defences against Sidereal charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say it like that, and it sounds like convincing them one at a time rather than doing so on an institutional level, which of all Exalted the Terrestrials have to be the most readily imagined in those terms.<br /> <br /> Still, it's part of why my thinking leans towards the institutions of the Dragon Blooded having had a number of extensive, ongoing grievances with the Solars that created entry points for arguments that they ought to be removed altogether.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you say, it's easy to rationalise not taking them seriously if you don't hear them personally, but I think it's also pretty easy to rationalise ignoring a Sidereal who says &quot;I want you and your family to murder your really nice Queen who you've served loyally for generations, who gave you birthday presents every year, built you a lovely house with their own two hands, and who trusted you with important jobs, because I've foreseen that she'll murder your family.&quot;<br /> <br /> Whereas I think the Dragonblooded would be much more likely to respond to &quot;I have foreseen that your increasingly erratic boss, who's become obsessed with their strange esoteric research, and responds with irrational anger to attempts to force her to actually administrate her kingdom properly, but also refuses to let you do it for her, is going to get worse until eventually she flips out and murders your whole family.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I've honestly started to lose track of the conversation, such that I can't immediately backtrack this to prior points. Is this an argument to the effect that the Usurpation needs a lot of the Solars to have been overtly terrible in order to make sense?<br /> <br /> The former description there feels like a bit of a reduction to absurdity, and even then I can think of scenarios in which people could plausibly end up against them; either effectively pointing out problems around the Solar that aren't affecting you personally, or even just... not targeting that particular group, and letting them make their own choice about what to do when the hammer comes down.<br /> <br /> After all, each Edition has maintained that there were Dragon Blooded who died fighting for the Solars, the Sidereals could have plausibly been aware of that and ready to write a lot of Terrestrials off.<br /> <br /> The other side that I've maintained for a while is that, when the other Dragon Blooded already started without you, and the choice is thrust upon you very suddenly, it's plausible for there to have been people who gritted their teeth and decided that the usurpers were the better bet, begrudgingly making some actions and necessary gestures to display their allegiance rather than be designated as enemies while outnumbered. I can imagine cases in which that choice will have been made easier when some Limit Breaking Solars were gripped with indiscriminate rage and fear, and started turning against any Dragon Blooded in proximity to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earlier, you said something about the depiction of why the Unconquered Sun turned his back on the Solars, and how this lead you to have a more subtle view of the Solars? Could you say more about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The publication timeline as I can vaguely recall or infer it had Games of Divinity depict the point about the Sun growing so disgusted at their actions that he turned away from them, Caste Book: Zenith kind of implying that the final straw was a Solar high priest wrongfully invoking his authority over an administrative issue (based in solidifying the power of the Deliberative), and the Sidereals book presenting the Sun's disavowal as the inciting incident that got them worried enough to make the big prophecy.<br /> <br /> If that holds up, it's a scenario in which the Solars having gone very bad is not yet self-evident, but can be inferred by people in the know enough to see that the Sun has lost faith in them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's a great concept. But surely it's of the &quot;worst excesses of the Solars&quot; school, which you were arguing against?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something a bit more coherent than turning people into meat trees for no reason, or any other expression of doing something excessively brutal just for the sake of it.<br /> <br /> That and being only a preliminary step that hadn't been initiated yet, and hardly anybody (even Sidereals) was aware of the intended trajectory of.<br /> <br /> Even then, in my framework, it's on the far end of the scale, and would be small in scope compared to the general impact of Solars. I mostly just think it's an easy way to illustrate a far gone Solar that is actually connected to the Great Curse rules. For the most part, when I imagine a world straining under the weight of the fully corrupted Solars, it's one in which the full effect of trying to sate their Limit Triggers or ending up existing in a constant feedback loop of Limit gain and Break (and any kind of highly erratic behaviour that creates) or becoming so inured to trying to save things and addicted to the cathartic sensation of Limit Break has many self-destructively leaning into things antithetical to them, that they've widely created systems and actions that leave the world in a deep, persistent and inescapable misery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the players in my group maintains that the best example of the dangers of the Great Curse on the Solars is Salina. She wasn't evil or corrupt. She wanted to help humanity. And so, in her compassion, she reshaped the very nature of reality to make it easier to acquire dangerous weapons. Unsurprisingly, the Five-Score Fellowship, whose raison d'etre was to maintain the nature of reality, were horrified, and terrified.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's already written verbatim in a couple of the books.<br /> <br /> Without going into too much detail on it here, I'll reiterate that I don't care much for the Salina example, largely because it's not really an accurate representation of sorcery or her working, and partially because it seems like it's trying just a little bit too hard to be really clever and subvert expectations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think though, there is a reason why people rarely think of compassion when thinking of the Great Curse.<br /> Once our characters were in a foreign city trying to track down an ancient Dragon King necromancer. We failed to find him quick enough, and he unleashed an army of ghosts, zombies, and skeletons, in the middle of the city.<br /> My No Moon, his daughter the Changing Moon and the Slayer ran towards the middle of the city to help. We two Lunars went into DBT and battled ghosts and zombies, while the Slayer reached the middle of the city, turned into a 30 foot monster, and fought the Kaiju-sized Dragon King necromancer.<br /> The Night Caste... sat in his apartment weeping and crying because he was overwhelmed by knowing that hundreds of people had been killed by monsters and he'd been unable to save them.<br /> Which was very annoying for the rest of us, because he wasn't saving more people.<br /> But it's not the kind of thing that'd make you want to kill him.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly helps make the idea of long-term pervasive corruption by the Curse be a lot more plausible when the actual Virtue Flaw can be almost anything, and it's given leeway to be timed more dramatically than just happening the moment the Limit track fills up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's the actions that led to the Usurpation, not the Solar's motives (I mean, many Sidereals considered the Solars insane rather than evil), so I think it ends up much the same. &quot;The Solars of the First Age became mad and committed atrocities&quot; is still the same if some of those Solars were doing it for good motives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference makes it easier to conceptualise what the Solars actually were doing or would end up doing, and creates a more nuanced picture of how and why that can inspire ways to play with the Great Curse as it actually functions in gameplay. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T10:41:53-08:00","id":1267350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267310#post1267310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just like to clarify something. The origins of the Bond actually changed during 2nd edition, the story in MoEP: Lunars about the Unconquered Sun trying to force Luna to make her chosen bow to his is utterly incompatible it was with their characterisations in Glories of the Most High and the Ink Monkeys era treated a lot of what that book had to say as apocryphal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. During First Edition, the Solar/Lunar bond was a result of a long-ago conflict between the Solar and Lunar Hosts being solved via a ritualistic marriage pact which resulted in relationships that persisted across many lives and thousands of year, which forged bonds of intense emotional familiarity between certain Solars and Lunars that persist to this day. But it didn't really have mechanics, aside from I think a few Charms keying off it.<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, they gave it mechanics, and then to justify those mechanics made it an occult bond forged between certain Solar and Lunar Exaltations, and wrote in backstory about the Unconquered Sun forcing it on Luna because making the Unconquered Sun a huge bastard and setting everyone at everyone else's throats was often how 2e was written.<br /> <br /> So in Third Edition, the Solar/Lunar bond is a result of a long-ago conflict between the Solar and Lunar Hosts being solved via a ritualistic marriage pact which resulted in relationships that persisted across many lives and thousands of year, which forge bonds of intense emotional familiarity between certain Solars and Lunars that persist to this day. And it uses the Intimacy mechanics because we have Intimacy mechanics now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T10:47:14-08:00","id":1267352,"title":"","content":"I mean, it still seems to be written as though it has an occult connection element, just one that emerged out of that original scenario rather than being built in for the sake of god agendas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T10:57:47-08:00","id":1267358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267352#post1267352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it still seems to be written as though it has an occult connection element, just one that emerged out of that original scenario rather than being built in for the sake of god agendas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Charms in 1e keyed off it? So it had an occult connection element emerging naturally out of the scenario in 1e, too. That's what happens when Essence is the fundament of the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T12:53:52-08:00","id":1267393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267358#post1267358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, Charms in 1e keyed off it? So it had an occult connection element emerging naturally out of the scenario in 1e, too. That's what happens when Essence is the fundament of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did First Edition present it as something that affected their nature, and caused a kind of psychic shockwave when the Solars were lost?<br /> <br /> I'm asking seriously, as I don't yet own a copy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T13:21:12-08:00","id":1267405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267393#post1267393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did First Edition present it as something that affected their nature, and caused a kind of psychic shockwave when the Solars were lost?<br /> <br /> I'm asking seriously, as I don't yet own a copy.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, <i>that\u2019s</i> new to the 3e core Lunar prestige spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T14:11:08-08:00","id":1267415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267405#post1267405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, <i>that\u2019s</i> new to the 3e core Lunar prestige spread.</div> </div> </div> </div>All right, there you go then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmm, going back to the thought on a certain Lunar character concept in terms of schools...<br /> <br /> One thing that I might alter is the some of the context of her eventual restlessness and ensuing wanderlust, from Sidereal shenanigans to finally deciding to give what her mentor was always advocating a try.<br /> <br /> And something else...<br /> <br /> I'm firmly of the idea that the Silver Pact is basically Lunars, but I wonder if it can incorporate Moon-Touched as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T14:25:54-08:00","id":1267419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267415#post1267415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm firmly of the idea that the Silver Pact is basically Lunars, but I wonder if it can incorporate Moon-Touched as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it's ultimately a Lunar organization, allied non-Lunars have been known to attend Pact councils.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T16:30:15-08:00","id":1267441,"title":"","content":"Would Moon-Touched ever be taken on as students by... those guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T16:42:10-08:00","id":1267443,"title":"","content":"Ultimately I guess my view on the last days of the First Age is that, for most people\u2019s actions to make sense, things had to be getting bad, but they couldn\u2019t yet be quite bad enough for the writing to be on the wall and the Usurpation an inevitable conflict.<br /> <br /> The thing though is that defining \u201cbad, but not TOO bad\u201d is tricky and depends a fair amount on other setting factors as well as the people making the determination. I agree with Isator that it should be nuanced, but I think it might be difficult to pin down to everyone\u2019s satisfaction.<br /> <br /> I will be curious to see, when the Sids book rolls around, what it has to say about \u201caccidentally creating a forever war with the Lunars\u201d and how that fit into the Bronze Faction\u2019s Grand Plans. I think it\u2019s pretty obvious these days that Creation has gone heavily \u201coff script\u201d and something is going to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-14T16:49:12-08:00","id":1267444,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m also curious how difficult it would be for a Lunar to trigger the Realm Civil War, by sneaking onto the Blessed Isle, gaining the form of a Dynast from one house and attacking a Dynast of another...in broad daylight in the capital city. Or, even better, inciting them into attacking and \u201cmurdering\u201d you, preferably setting off a riot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T01:16:54-08:00","id":1267517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267303#post1267303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it could get kind of dull if the conversation consisted only of people that agreed, and if nothing else, a bit of contrasting viewpoints could be stimulating.<br /> <br /> I'll admit to an ulterior motive of wanting something to get my teeth into in a general manner; not for a fight or anything, just something that demands a bit of invested conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like there are plenty of contradicting opinions in the thread already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I find 2ed and Ex3 being a bit like Wod and CofD. Both having a lot in common, but when looking beneath the surface they have a lot of differences. Some might like both, but then it is more often by different reasons. So trying to please both groups often pleases none.<br /> <br /> Ex3 seems to go back to ideas in first edition, and while I hadn't heard about Exalted until just under six years ago, I have the impression that quite a few of those changes from 1ed to 2ed were because quite a few had issues with them.<br /> <br /> While I do like certain things in Ex3; as the new social system with intimacies, the new map, sorcerous workings, that I'm a lot closer to the new ideas of the Silver Pact than the version in 2ed, etc, I'm so far removed from the underlying assumptions for Ex3 that this probably would be a good vetting system for ideas:<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, we have two alternatives. Should we go with A or B?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hm... I don't know, lets ask Lundgren. Hey, Lundgren, which one do you like?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I like A.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;B it is.&quot;<br /> <br /> My &quot;I accept that as an answer and backs out&quot; was just a polite way of writing &quot;Oh no. Not that kind of shit.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I don't mind talking/arguing more about it, but doing it in this thread would be far to similar, in my opinion, to arguing against class and levels in a thread about how a new class should be designed on a D&amp;D forum.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T03:51:52-08:00","id":1267534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267517#post1267517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ex3 seems to go back to ideas in first edition, and while I hadn't heard about Exalted until just under six years ago, I have the impression that quite a few of those changes from 1ed to 2ed were because quite a few had issues with them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not really.<br /> <br /> The main issues with 1e that I recall were mostly system and design related.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T04:36:57-08:00","id":1267541,"title":"","content":"The Lunar book was criticised for its fluff being too &quot;Rargh! Barbarians smash!&quot; (It did have some good stuff in I felt, but generally it was a bit simplistic.)<br /> Oh, and some of the 1st art was terrible, look at Typhon in the back of the Core (or in the case of Savant and Sorcerer, just very inappropriate due to an amusing misunderstanding). 2nd ed art is far, far better.<br /> <br /> But other than that, yeah I think pretty much with 1st ed it was mostly just mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m also curious how difficult it would be for a Lunar to trigger the Realm Civil War, by sneaking onto the Blessed Isle, gaining the form of a Dynast from one house and attacking a Dynast of another...in broad daylight in the capital city. Or, even better, inciting them into attacking and \u201cmurdering\u201d you, preferably setting off a riot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I think there's enough institutional weight, desire to stop the Civil War going off right now, and knowledge that Lunars are a thing (&quot;our House didn't murder him, that's Fake News!)&quot;, to stop it going too far. I mean, you could probably start a riot. The hardest part is getting a DB's form in the first place. But getting that to war is harder.<br /> But it's not impossible.<br /> And I think a more general Lunar campaign to frame, mislead, agitate, etc, is certainly viable, and something Lunars would be keen on (at least, the ones willing to take radical, and perhaps risky, steps to start things now; other Lunars have an institutional inertia, since their plan of slowly squeezing Satrapies is working. Not saying they wouldn't do the same, I'm sure they would, but maybe only in Satrapies, not the Realm proper, which is a much riskier area to operate in).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T04:44:18-08:00","id":1267542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267419#post1267419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's ultimately a Lunar organization, allied non-Lunars have been known to attend Pact councils.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of a Lunar game, and mentioned this to my friends as maybe something we could do next year. But of course, just as some players in Solar games always want to be Lunars, some of them wanted to play Solars.<br /> <br /> And I think you can have a &quot;Lunar game&quot; that feels very Lunars with 5 Lunars and 2 Solars, especially as the Lunars have the institutional weight and overriding culture, and the Solars are new kids on the block who probably just tag along with the Lunars, who seem to know what's what with all this Anathema business.<br /> <br /> So, I realised that, for the sake of games, you kind of have to say that it's okay for a pack of Lunars to bring their Solar buddy (though I could see Lunar elders not being keen on a whole circle of Solars turning up, as they might feel the Solars will dominate them).<br /> And obviously that's a new development, but since the point of the Silver Pact is to defeat the Realm, it does make sense for Lunars to bring other powerful allies to meetings, whether they be spirits, powerful warlords, etc.<br /> <br /> After all, if you have a meeting between 5 Lunars who live around the Dreaming Sea on how to battle Prasad, it makes sense to allow one of the Lunars to bring a representative of the sorcerers of Ysyr. Not to tell them what to do, but to give their perspective and make agreements for military aid.<br /> <br /> Since the Silver Pact is presented as a non-hierarchical mutual defence and coordination agreement, rather than a heavily organised military unit, it makes more sense to allow non-Lunars to speak at meetings when relevant, than not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T04:46:22-08:00","id":1267543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267350#post1267350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it didn't really have mechanics, aside from I think a few Charms keying off it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was there a thing where you could roll to detect your Solar Mate?<br /> <br /> Our ST didn't like the 2nd ed Solar Bond, so he said we'd use rules from 1st ed (as my Lunar was his son-in-law's Mate), and you could make a roll to find your Solar Mate with Essence+Perception or something. But it might be rules he'd got from a merit or artefact or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T05:02:48-08:00","id":1267545,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a charm.<br /> <br /> It does other stuff too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T05:11:02-08:00","id":1267548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267541#post1267541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think there's enough institutional weight, desire to stop the Civil War going off right now, and knowledge that Lunars are a thing (&quot;our House didn't murder him, that's Fake News!)&quot;, to stop it going too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I was attempting something of this nature, I'd get try to get the forms of <i>two</i> dynasts, preferably ones from houses thay aren't on the best of terms, and attack <i>both</i> of the houses while disguised as the other.<br /> <br /> Possibly at the same time using that duplication charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T05:15:18-08:00","id":1267551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267517#post1267517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ex3 seems to go back to ideas in first edition</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the developers often said it was more accurate to describe it as going back to the tone and sensibility of First Edition, as a starting point. After all, in setting and mechanics, there are a number of things that are different, sometimes dramatically.<br /> <br /> The Lunar Exalted being among the more prominent, I think. Hell, in a lot of respects, they might lean closer to the Second Edition portrayal than the First Edition one, even if they're ultimately fairly different from either.<br /> <br /> Heh, I just had an amusing notion about the differences between the Solar Bond in each Edition; First made it a fairly basic historical root for reincarnated relationships, Second overthought it a lot, and Third has taken the outline of the basic First version and... overthought it (in a direction that I happen to like).<br /> <br /> In any case, describing it just as going back to First Edition is a bit of a simplification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the impression that quite a few of those changes from 1ed to 2ed were because quite a few had issues with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that makes me a bit curious... I wasn't there for the transition myself, having been drawn to the game only a couple of years before you and only reading a lot of First Edition books some time after similar Second Edition ones. I can only ever speculate based on my own conclusions from comparing books, and extrapolating from a lot of what people said in retrospect.<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking specifically about Lunars?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so far removed from the underlying assumptions for Ex3 that this probably would be a good vetting system for ideas:<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, we have two alternatives. Should we go with A or B?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hm... I don't know, lets ask Lundgren. Hey, Lundgren, which one do you like?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I like A.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;B it is.&quot;<br /> <br /> My &quot;I accept that as an answer and backs out&quot; was just a polite way of writing &quot;Oh no. Not <u>that kind of shit</u>.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>By that, do you mean a scenario in which you think you'll be taking the wrong track on something?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind talking/arguing more about it, but doing it in this thread would be far to similar, in my opinion, to arguing against class and levels in a thread about how a new class should be designed on a D&amp;D forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I know just enough about Dungeons and Dragons to be able to imagine the issues with that kind of conversation, but for my money, in a smaller community concerning a less intricate system such as this, it can be fair enough for a conversation about &quot;how X&quot; to include at least one viewpoint of &quot;why X&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T05:18:13-08:00","id":1267552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Okay, I've honestly started to lose track of the conversation, such that I can't immediately backtrack this to prior points. Is this an argument to the effect that the Usurpation needs a lot of the Solars to have been overtly terrible in order to make sense?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I realise that, with these long threads, various stuff goes all over the place, and nuance gets lost.<br /> <br /> So, basically, a couple of times you seem to have been saying that you'd prefer an Usurpation where the problems of the Solars aren't self-evident. That it's too subtle to be obvious, but rather something that a small number of people consider, leading them to cast the Great Prophecy. (This was my point about your concept of the Solar who turns her people into unchanging crystal; I think it's a good concept, but is not quite unsubtle?)<br /> <br /> And, I am kind of saying that I think it makes sense for a lot of Dragonblood to rise up (as you said, it doesn't have to be all of them. There could be those who stay loyal, or stay out of it) if<i> some</i> Solars are overtly terrible. But I don't think it needs to be a lot. Probably about the level whereby people can argue about whether they show an inherent problem with the Solars, or they're just a &quot;few bad apples&quot;. Say, 10% of the Solars, including some in key positions, who don't seem to be restrained enough by their fellows.<br /> Or where the DBs who serve those bad Solars (by bad, I don't necessarily mean evil. Just dangerous, due to insanity) form a vanguard of anti-Solar extremists who are contacted by the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> But for other Dragonbloods to grit their teeth and side with the Usurpers, it seems more likely there'd be general problems that were already evident to them.<br /> <br /> I think BrilliantRain summed this up well:</span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately I guess my view on the last days of the First Age is that, for most people\u2019s actions to make sense, things had to be getting bad, but they couldn\u2019t yet be quite bad enough for the writing to be on the wall and the Usurpation an inevitable conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Of course, it could be purely more institutional problems that annoyed the Dragonblood (the Deliberative withdrawing traditional rights of the Dragonblood, or asserting its authority over areas where they'd previously been ignored).<br /> <br /> And, you know, history is not inevitable. Just because the Usurpation was more likely with more overt Solar problems, doesn't mean it definitely couldn't happen otherwise.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think a more key point is that making all the problems more subtle means they'll almost certain be entirely lost to history, as opposed to just being mostly lost to history. Saying a few Solars were doing really bad things means I can have, say, a lost city full of monsters that an ancient evil God-King created by twisting his human subjects into hideous forms; or an ancient Solar-forged vampire sword that consumes the souls of its victims that she catalysed by sacrificing her Lunar husband; or an ancient ritual that will blot out the sky made by a Solar who was jealous of the Unconquered Sun, which the PCs must acquire before an Abyssal does; or a virtuous spirit who sides with the local Dragonblood against the PCs because her father was bound by a Solar to power his magic.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, obviously, you want there to have plenty of Solars who have pretty innocent backgrounds, so that PCs can have non-dubious previous incarnations, if that's how you want to go.<br /> <br /> This of course, also applies to Lunars in terms of their relations with their Solar Mates (and their own actions during that timeframe).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the difference makes it easier to conceptualise what the Solars actually were doing or would end up doing, and creates a more nuanced picture of how and why that can inspire ways to play with the Great Curse as it actually functions in gameplay. </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that your point is &quot;I want well-written and nuanced depictions of the First Age Solars.&quot; Which I'm not arguing against per-se.* Who'd argue for bad writing?<br /> <br /> My point wasn't &quot;it doesn't matter that some Solars did things out of compassion.&quot; It's just that when you said earlier &quot;Why don't people remember that many limit breaks are based on Compassion?&quot; I assumed this wasn't a response to the Devs' writing, but rather to people posting on the forum. And I just meant that, I don't think people were saying &quot;all Solar problems were caused by their pure evil&quot;, but rather they were talking about the effects of the Solars' actions, not their motives.<br /> <br /> But that was like 5 pages ago now, so maybe it's not that important.<br /> <br /> *Except of course, the problem is that since the Devs and many fans don't want to go into too much detail about the First Age, it's quite hard to look at motives. Motives are much easier to be lost to pre-history than actions.<br /> For example, if PCs find a sunken city in the Fangs of Mela, and realise that once the whole White Sea was dammed off until the dam was destroyed, then even if they somehow manage to learn the dam was destroyed by a Solar during the Usurpation, it's going to be virtually impossible to learn if he did it out of petty vengeance, as a desperate move to stay alive, by accident, or even to defeat a Dragonblood army that would kill even more people somewhere else.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmm... anyone have any ideas how one might portray the motives of the Solar actions that led to the Usurpation as including various nuanced motives, without giving much detail about what exactly happened? The memories of Lunar Elders, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-15-2018, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T05:50:24-08:00","id":1267559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267552#post1267552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just dangerous, due to insanity</div> </div> </div> </div>This touches on the basis of another of my motives for figuring out a model of Solar corruption that goes a bit deeper, as I find &quot;just dangerous due to insanity&quot; to be alternately boring, lazy, and have problematic real world connotations.<br /> <br /> There's a degree to which I think some things should be allowed to slide for narrative purposes or mythic invocation, but that's one where I don't feel very compelled to give it a lot of slack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think BrilliantRain summed this up well:[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Say what?<br /> <br /> Oh for God's sake, did a post I responded to get edited while I was quoting it again? I hate when that happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a more key point is that making all the problems more subtle means they'll almost certain be entirely lost to history, as opposed to just being mostly lost to history. Saying a few Solars were doing really bad things means I can have, say, a lost city full of monsters that an ancient evil God-King created by twisting his human subjects into hideous forms; or an ancient Solar-forged vampire sword that consumes the souls of its victims that she catalysed by sacrificing her Lunar husband; or an ancient ritual that will blot out the sky made by a Solar who was jealous of the Unconquered Sun, which the PCs must acquire before an Abyssal does; or a virtuous spirit who sides with the local Dragonblood against the PCs because her father was bound by a Solar to power his magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of two minds about this. One is acknowledging the point about wanting a background that primarily serves the needs of creating plot hooks for the benefit of gameplay (even if my own standards would question what compelled the Solar to do something like turn the inhabitants of the city into monsters).<br /> <br /> The other is thinking that everything but blocking out the sun doesn't exactly feel outside the bounds of what some players might actually have their characters do, if they were willing to really go with the &quot;old world justice&quot; angle.<br /> <br /> That and it all touching on the issue of how much real world evil makes it difficult for me to personally take small-scale, flashy fantasy evil particularly seriously. I can't really view a Solar having made a vampire sword as this great signifier that the whole system was rotten and needed to be burned down to the roots when House Cynis is over there trafficking in sex slavery.<br /> <br /> Any time something like this comes up, I think of that scene in Good Omens where Crowley is meeting some of his fellow demons (who are generally higher ranked than he is), and they're all crowing about how much effort they've put into effectively corrupting righteous individuals, and unable to appreciate the significance of Crowley having manipulated civil engineering to ensure that commutes are less efficient, causing a lot of people to treat one another badly and contributing to a pervasive atmosphere of misery.<br /> <br /> Which is amusing considering how the book went on to portray three of the Four Horsemen; for instance, Famine finds a lot of work from promoting fast food franchises.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that your point is &quot;I want well-written and nuanced depictions of the First Age Solars.&quot; Which I'm not arguing against per-se.* Who'd argue for bad writing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want it to be written, I want to talk about it, and have other people share in the conversation. We don't need to Ask the Devs for everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point wasn't &quot;it doesn't matter that some Solars did things out of compassion.&quot; It's just that when you said earlier &quot;Why don't people remember that many limit breaks are based on Compassion?&quot; I assumed this wasn't a response to the Devs' writing, but rather to people posting on the forum. And I just meant that, I don't think people were saying &quot;all Solar problems were caused by their pure evil&quot;, but rather they were talking about the effects of the Solars' actions, not their motives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, there are definitely people who complain about the Great Curse because they read it as this intrusive thing that forces their characters to become bad people or think it punishes them for actually trying to do things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T06:43:50-08:00","id":1267563,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why, but this Usurpation topic is sending me into a bit of a spiral, so I'm going to leave it alone for a while and within the scope of this thread so that I can get my head together.<br /> <br /> Christ, I miss RPG.Net.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T08:05:10-08:00","id":1267575,"title":"","content":"No problem. To be honest, I was mostly responding because it felt rude not to respond to you responding to me, rather than any great enjoyment of that particular tangent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I was attempting something of this nature, I'd get try to get the forms of <i>two</i> dynasts, preferably ones from houses thay aren't on the best of terms, and attack <i>both</i> of the houses while disguised as the other.<br /> <br /> Possibly at the same time using that duplication charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work, but I'd actually want to not do it at the same time.<br /> <br /> Rather, pretend to be Cynis Kebaz, and get into an argument with Ragara Tiran over politics at an expensive teahouse, and then stab her and flee.<br /> Then murder (mortal) Cynis Yoseth, Kebaz's daughter, at their house, and generally trash the place. Kebaz is never seen again.<br /> Pretend next to be Cynis Ashani, and publically accuse House Ragara of having abducted Kebaz and killed his daughter in the fight, rather than going through proper judicial channels. Demand Kebaz is freed.<br /> Then pretend to be Ragara Naerun, get into an argument with Cynis Udema in a Geisha house, duel her, and kill her.<br /> Do this over, like, a week.<br /> And, of course, the important thing is to use lots of Charisma and Manipulation charms on bystanders and people you talk to it about it. <br /> <br /> The point is to keep ramping up the tension in a way that seems believable; if both houses are targeted at exactly the same time, people might wonder if it's a third party (maybe Lunars, more likely another House).<br /> <br /> Also, unless you're very powerful, you probably want to impersonate and target mortal dynasts, not Dragonblood, because attacking Dragonblood (especially when you can't flare) is very dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T08:15:44-08:00","id":1267579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267559#post1267559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This touches on the basis of another of my motives for figuring out a model of Solar corruption that goes a bit deeper, as I find &quot;just dangerous due to insanity&quot; to be alternately boring, lazy, and have problematic real world connotations.</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds me of the recently-all-too-pervasive screenwriting clich\u00e9 that goes something like, &quot;Let's just say the bad guy is insane! Then we don't have to have his goal or the actions he takes to achieve it make any kind of sense!&quot; Which, like you said, isn't just lazy and boring, it's really shitty to the folks who have to live with the disorders and disabilities Hollywood is maligning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T08:29:25-08:00","id":1267584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267575#post1267575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rather, pretend to be Cynis Kebaz, and get into an argument with Ragara Tiran over politics at an expensive teahouse, and then stab her and flee.<br /> Then murder (mortal) Cynis Yoseth, Kebaz's daughter, at their house, and generally trash the place. Kebaz is never seen again.<br /> Pretend next to be Cynis Ashani, and publically accuse House Ragara of having abducted Kebaz and killed his daughter in the fight, rather than going through proper judicial channels. Demand Kebaz is freed.<br /> Then pretend to be Ragara Naerun, get into an argument with Cynis Udema in a Geisha house, duel her, and kill her.<br /> Do this over, like, a week.<br /> And, of course, the important thing is to use lots of Charisma and Manipulation charms on bystanders and people you talk to it about it.<br /> <br /> The point is to keep ramping up the tension in a way that seems believable; if both houses are targeted at exactly the same time, people might wonder if it's a third party (maybe Lunars, more likely another House).</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly sounds like the kind of plan that shortens a lot of the odds and has enough moving parts to interfere with that it's not an easy win.<br /> <br /> For the simpler option, while I imagine that in a lot of cases being impersonated by a Lunar can be an effective defence against an accusation of having done something extremely overt, I can imagine the Realm as it is now or in the near future as being enough of a powder keg that the right action at the right time causes the kind of rapid escalation that by the time people start questioning the authenticity of the inciting incident, it's too late to walk things back (assuming many of the leading actors want to).<br /> <br /> It's like, you show your hand, you reveal some of your alliances or opening strategic moves and deployments, you might just have to commit to those, because you won't have the element of surprise in future and you can't rely on having time to draw up new plans (assuming you could; suppose Cathak revealed who they would side with, other Houses might not want to entertain their offers).<br /> <br /> And while news probably travels faster than a lot of people would anticipate, it probably still travels slowly enough that not everybody hears about the allegations of being a Lunar before they've gone too far, or at the kind of pace at which your supporters understand why you're suddenly trying to put a lid on it. Or even if they do, well, things get moving and you suddenly cry &quot;sorry fellows, false alarm&quot;, how does that make you look?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T09:12:23-08:00","id":1267589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267575#post1267575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem. To be honest, I was mostly responding because it felt rude not to respond to you responding to me, rather than any great enjoyment of that particular tangent.<br /> <br /> <br /> That could work, but I'd actually want to not do it at the same time.<br /> <br /> Rather, pretend to be Cynis Kebaz, and get into an argument with Ragara Tiran over politics at an expensive teahouse, and then stab her and flee.<br /> Then murder (mortal) Cynis Yoseth, Kebaz's daughter, at their house, and generally trash the place. Kebaz is never seen again.<br /> Pretend next to be Cynis Ashani, and publically accuse House Ragara of having abducted Kebaz and killed his daughter in the fight, rather than going through proper judicial channels. Demand Kebaz is freed.<br /> Then pretend to be Ragara Naerun, get into an argument with Cynis Udema in a Geisha house, duel her, and kill her.<br /> Do this over, like, a week.<br /> And, of course, the important thing is to use lots of Charisma and Manipulation charms on bystanders and people you talk to it about it.<br /> <br /> The point is to keep ramping up the tension in a way that seems believable; if both houses are targeted at exactly the same time, people might wonder if it's a third party (maybe Lunars, more likely another House).<br /> <br /> Also, unless you're very powerful, you probably want to impersonate and target mortal dynasts, not Dragonblood, because attacking Dragonblood (especially when you can't flare) is very dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically, the likely upshot of this was that while you'd cause some havoc and might get away scot-free, a representative of the Empress would tamp down on the chaos before it got completely out of hand, and then a magistrate stood a good chance of figuring out what happened. And this wouldn't threaten you directly, but a whole lot of Dragon-Blooded who previously only considered Lunar Anathema to be a distant, abstract threat would suddenly be very personally invested, resulting in a surge of Wyld Hunt activity backed by several new volunteers, and ending up with some other, unrelated Lunar getting killed somewhere in the Threshold.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, of course, such a plan has much better odds of achieving your desired goals, and Silver Pact inertia means that it's most likely to be attempted first by your PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:00:35-08:00","id":1267604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267551#post1267551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, describing it just as going back to First Edition is a bit of a simplification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going back to ideas don't mean making the same thing. But from quite a few discussions I have seen, it seems like it at times can be summed down to &quot;2nd edition was 1st edition and then turning left; Ex3 is going back to 1st edition and then go right&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By that, do you mean a scenario in which you think you'll be taking the wrong track on something? </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm not on the wrong track. I like the track I'm on. However, it seems like I'm on another track <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Just a few points:<br /> <br /> * I like &quot;mechanics as physics&quot;. Ex3 has too much of a narrative focus on the mechanics for my taste.<br /> <br /> * I like the &quot;self searching missile shards&quot; (with a bit of self-awareness, so they might pick a suitable person close to a loved person), where a Lunar is selected on how they have resisted, endured, or refused to conform to something; not &quot;the Incarna selects their Exalts.<br /> <br /> * I want the shards to be extremely hard to change, and it took probably 3-4000 years for the Yozi to figure out how to make their alterations, where most is things tacked on and not really changed. Ideas that the Lunars changed the Castes themselves, and the Bond is from a ritual to solve an inability to work together, is in opposite to that.<br /> <br /> * My preference is to have the 2nd edition style Silver Pact around perhaps 20-30 Lunars, considered as crazy extremists by quite a few other Lunars. Some are loosely organized, and most just knows about a handful of others. So when it comes to the Silver Pact, Ex3 might actually end up too close to 2nd edition for my taste. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> * I see most post Great Contagion Lunars prioritizing other things than the Realm, and elder Lunars can rave about fighting them but as most haven't seen the first age nor the Shogunate, not many agrees with them; Ex3 preview have &quot;the war against the Realm&quot;.<br /> <br /> * I see the Solar Bond as &quot;mate as in buddy/pal&quot;, not &quot;mate as in spouse&quot;. More like lives-spanning &quot;police partner&quot; (without any frowning on department romances <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). My dislike for the possibility of the bond itself being a negative intimacy is already stated up-thread.<br /> <br /> * While my own take on Exalted doesn't require the Sacred Hunt for taking a shape; it do involve eating a heart, egg, seed, or equivalent (or having it transferred from another Lunar). Taking someones form through something like &quot;Heart-Drinking Allure&quot;, or through a court of law or whatever was talked about way back, is a big nope for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:22:10-08:00","id":1267608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267604#post1267604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I want the shards to be extremely hard to change, and it took probably 3-4000 years for the Yozi to figure out how to make their alterations, where most is things tacked on and not really changed. Ideas that the Lunars changed the Castes themselves, and the Bond is from a ritual to solve an inability to work together, is in opposite to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they've only ever had three Castes?<br /> <br /> I'm not quite sure the development of the Solar Bond was quite in the form of performing a ritual; the impression I'm getting is that it did solidify over an extended period of time, emerging from the behaviour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* My preference is to have the 2nd edition style Silver Pact around perhaps 20-30 Lunars, considered as crazy extremists by quite a few other Lunars. Some are loosely organized, and most just knows about a handful of others. So when it comes to the Silver Pact, Ex3 might actually end up too close to 2nd edition for my taste. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think any Edition has portrayed the Silver Pact like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I see the Solar Bond as &quot;mate as in buddy/pal&quot;, not &quot;mate as in spouse&quot;. More like lives-spanning &quot;police partner&quot; (without any frowning on department romances <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). My dislike for the possibility of the bond itself being a negative intimacy is already stated up-thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean that in the sense of reading Lea's references to First Age ritual marriages very literally, or a preference for reading the use of the term &quot;mate&quot; in the more informal sense, as a stereotypical caricature of an Australian person might use?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:34:51-08:00","id":1267612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267604#post1267604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it took probably 3-4000 years for the Yozi to figure out how to make their alterations.</div> </div> </div> </div>They got their hands on the solar exaltations about 5 years ago at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:55:26-08:00","id":1267619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267608#post1267608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they've only ever had three Castes?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2nd ed, it was some form of wyld taint changing it from 5 to 3. I though that was stupid as well, possible even more so as it would mean the wyld managed to change all shards uniformly. I'm comparing Ex3 to my preference, not 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not quite sure the development of the Solar Bond was quite in the form of performing a ritual; the impression I'm getting is that it did solidify over an extended period of time, emerging from the behaviour. </div> </div> </div>If so, it would be another version of individual interaction making an uniform change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think any Edition has portrayed the Silver Pact like that. </div> </div> </div>I think the second edition Silver Pact, with its oats and how they can challenge each other and then demand a task to be done, etc, being a group of loony extremist. Having almost everyone of the supposed most individualistic splat conform to something like that is quite ridiculous to me. However, 5-10% of them being in an organisation like that? Sure, why not; and it might be interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you mean that in the sense of reading Lea's references to First Age ritual marriages very literally, or a preference for reading the use of the term &quot;mate&quot; in the more informal sense, as a stereotypical caricature of an Australian person might use? </div> </div> </div>The talk of Solar Bond as a sort of &quot;marriage&quot; goes way back. While I can see it ending up as leading to that kind of dynamic in quite a few cases, I dislike it at as the assumed default. So my preference is the &quot;Australian version&quot; of &quot;mate&quot; being the default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T10:56:58-08:00","id":1267621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They got their hands on the solar exaltations about 5 years ago at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Lundgren's talking about his preferences, not canon, and how it's so different from the actual fluff that he feels he can't add anything to the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I see the Solar Bond as &quot;mate as in buddy/pal&quot;, not &quot;mate as in spouse&quot;. More like lives-spanning &quot;police partner&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that lacks mythic weight.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it's actually what mostly gets played. My character's Lunar Mate was his son-in-law. In the game I ran, the Full Moon and his Solar Mate, the Twilight, initially had mixed feelings, but grew into having a deep friendship. There was nothing romantic there though.<br /> <br /> The only time we did have a romantic PC-PC bond... it didn't work. The guy playing the Solar wasn't interested, and he left the game because there were too many players (and his character married another Solar, an NPC) and the Lunar was very depressed that the man she felt a deep mythic romantic bond with had just not been interested in her.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the romantic bonds, between PCs at least, feel a bit forced. With NPCs romantic bonds work better, but we still don't do all of them as romantic bonds. The other Twilight, Cid Hawkwind, is married to a Fox Spirit who slowly wooed him, while his Lunar Mate is a lesbian and has no sexual or romantic interest in him at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-15-2018, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T11:02:24-08:00","id":1267623,"title":"","content":"Talking about the Great Curse and how it manifested made me realise, I don't think we've seen anything about the Lunar Great Curse. I know mechanically it's going to be somewhat similar to the Solar one, with a limit track and so on (not like the DB Great Curse). And I think the Devs (but it might have been the old Devs) said that the limit condition would no longer be the light of the full moon.<br /> <br /> But can anyone remember anything else that's been said?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T11:03:51-08:00","id":1267624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267612#post1267612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They got their hands on the solar exaltations about 5 years ago at most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Akumas, prisoners, and getting information from individuals researching exaltations?<br /> <br /> They knew at least how to trap the shards before bringing it up with the Deathlords, and if it had been that easy to change them, why didn't they do it earlier.<br /> <br /> As I see it, they figured it out before the jade prison was broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T11:12:20-08:00","id":1267628,"title":"","content":"As far as I can recall, the particulars of the Lunar Great Curse are something that the developers are opting to keep close to their chest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267621#post1267621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that lacks mythic weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Gilgamesh and Enkidu were reincarnated, what would you expect their relationship to be?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T11:13:03-08:00","id":1267629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267621#post1267621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lundgren's talking about his preferences, not canon, and how it's so different from the actual fluff that he feels he can't add anything to the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. That sums it up quite well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The reason I say 2.5-ish is because I'm a lot closer to that canon. Ex3 canon is a few bridges too far at times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T11:56:12-08:00","id":1267639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267543#post1267543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there a thing where you could roll to detect your Solar Mate?<br /> <br /> Our ST didn't like the 2nd ed Solar Bond, so he said we'd use rules from 1st ed (as my Lunar was his son-in-law's Mate), and you could make a roll to find your Solar Mate with Essence+Perception or something. But it might be rules he'd got from a merit or artefact or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure in 1e the only actual mechanics tied to the Bond was the merit in the Player's Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T12:03:03-08:00","id":1267643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267575#post1267575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem. To be honest, I was mostly responding because it felt rude not to respond to you responding to me, rather than any great enjoyment of that particular tangent.<br /> <br /> <br /> That could work, but I'd actually want to not do it at the same time.<br /> <br /> Rather, pretend to be Cynis Kebaz, and get into an argument with Ragara Tiran over politics at an expensive teahouse, and then stab her and flee.<br /> Then murder (mortal) Cynis Yoseth, Kebaz's daughter, at their house, and generally trash the place. Kebaz is never seen again.<br /> Pretend next to be Cynis Ashani, and publically accuse House Ragara of having abducted Kebaz and killed his daughter in the fight, rather than going through proper judicial channels. Demand Kebaz is freed.<br /> Then pretend to be Ragara Naerun, get into an argument with Cynis Udema in a Geisha house, duel her, and kill her.<br /> Do this over, like, a week.<br /> And, of course, the important thing is to use lots of Charisma and Manipulation charms on bystanders and people you talk to it about it. <br /> <br /> The point is to keep ramping up the tension in a way that seems believable; if both houses are targeted at exactly the same time, people might wonder if it's a third party (maybe Lunars, more likely another House).<br /> <br /> Also, unless you're very powerful, you probably want to impersonate and target mortal dynasts, not Dragonblood, because attacking Dragonblood (especially when you can't flare) is very dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that seems like a good way to turn \u201cRomeo kills Tybalt and then has to live in the provinces for awhile\u201d into \u201cthe Shot heard round the World.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T12:04:16-08:00","id":1267644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267589#post1267589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Historically, the likely upshot of this was that while you'd cause some havoc and might get away scot-free, a representative of the Empress would tamp down on the chaos before it got completely out of hand, and then a magistrate stood a good chance of figuring out what happened. And this wouldn't threaten you directly, but a whole lot of Dragon-Blooded who previously only considered Lunar Anathema to be a distant, abstract threat would suddenly be very personally invested, resulting in a surge of Wyld Hunt activity backed by several new volunteers, and ending up with some other, unrelated Lunar getting killed somewhere in the Threshold.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, of course, such a plan has much better odds of achieving your desired goals, and Silver Pact inertia means that it's most likely to be attempted first by your PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I hope some discussion about this kind of thing made it into the appropriate books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T12:07:34-08:00","id":1267646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267628#post1267628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I can recall, the particulars of the Lunar Great Curse are something that the developers are opting to keep close to their chest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If Gilgamesh and Enkidu were reincarnated, what would you expect their relationship to be?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be right, though I may ask in general terms.<br /> <br /> So, how would people like it to be presented?<br /> <br /> <br /> I would characterise them as blood brothers, sworn companions, etc. Liu Bei and Guan Yu, David and Jonathon, etc.<br /> <br /> Not mates or buddies. Mates is who you go to pre-drinks or a cheeky Nando's with, have some banter, and split an Uber to 'Spoons before the club. You don't swear to die on the self-same day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T12:14:38-08:00","id":1267649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267646#post1267646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would characterise them as blood brothers, sworn companions, etc. Liu Bei and Guan Yu, David and Jonathon, etc.<br /> <br /> Not mates or buddies. Mates is who you go to pre-drinks or a cheeky Nando's with, have some banter, and split an Uber to 'Spoons before the club. You don't swear to die on the self-same day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's arguing semantics, and disregarding the context in which Lundgren was drawing a dichotomy between the Bond as between friends and the Bond as between spouses/lovers.<br /> <br /> I'll also note that, per this Edition's take, Lunars aren't necessarily sworn to die for their other half either; by default, it's a Minor Tie. That doesn't mean it's an insignificant relationship, but not necessarily one of the form in which one will feel deeply compelled to make major sacrifices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T12:37:13-08:00","id":1267657,"title":"","content":"What I was getting at is that I think it lacks mythic weight to just, kind of, quite like your Solar Mate (the reincarnated police partner buddy/pal does seem like a minor intimacy), but you don't really, really like them; yet, in practice, it probably has to work like that, because in practice I find that making players have Major intimacies that haven't been built up doesn't work that well.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure if that was what Lundgren was trying to get across, or purely that it should be friends not lovers. Which I think everyone is happy with as a possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-15-2018, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T13:17:11-08:00","id":1267667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266717#post1266717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, it depends. I once had an image in which that Lookshy weapon to turn everything to crystal was made by a Solar who had become obsessed with the idea of fixing everybody into place in highly durable forms, as that was the only way to keep them all safe. Her Limit Trigger was related to people suffering while she wasn't able to keep an eye on them, and she'd had a long battle against trying to keep everything under as strict an observation as possible, struggling with the difficulty and complexity of that when they kept <i>moving</i>.<br /> <br /> (So many Limit Triggers have always been about innocents suffering, why do so few people incorporate that into their image of the Great Curse?)</div> </div> </div> </div>By way of trying to explain this, tentatively I think it may because you have in a sense in Exalted really got two competing versions of the Solar Great Curse going on that led to the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> The Curse as operates within characters; where an excess of overflowing virtue bursts out leads to acts of unbalanced extremity that lacks moral wisdom, and are so inevitably destructive to the world around them. (I'll call it A).<br /> <br /> This is the version of the Curse that's suited to the heroes the Solars are for PCs; great heroes, who have great potential for epic tragedy where they are undone by the contradictions and unforeseen consequences of their own great virtue.<br /> <br /> The Curse as originally described in its first, pithiest and most compelling form of imagery within Exalted; a kind of dark forces that ate at the hearts of the Solar Exalted, turning them to impiety, hubris, decadence, dishonor, selfishness, vanity, tyranny and to singularly fail in their position as leaders of mankind and champions of the Unconquered Sun. (I'll call it B).<br /> <br /> This is the Curse of what I would argue here is Exalted's wider narrative about the nature of power and accountability, which stresses that unchecked and unaccountable authority will inevitably turn to moral corruption, abuse of power, and self serving ends, until it is destroyed or reformed by those underneath it by making it accountable and calling it to account. (No matter how those authorities are chosen; for their excellence, from the common people and ranks of the poor, from those who have known adversity, &amp;c.)<br /> <br /> Manifestations of the GC, as it caused the downfall of the Solars as depicted in the setting, seem to me to tend to try to square the two streams, and while these grand excesses of compassion are easy to work with Great Curse A, there is something perhaps that is dissonant about them with B...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T13:34:05-08:00","id":1267671,"title":"","content":"Well, in unchecked and unaccountable leaders, I think compassion can lead to devastating consequences. They do things they <i>think</i> are good, but they make mistakes. This happens in even leaders who are accountable, but it's worse when they're not, with no-one to point out their mistakes. This could be a matter of economic or government reform based on ideology or lack of information. It could be liberal interventionism, where desire to stop the suffering in a neighbouring country leads to a war that goes horribly, horribly wrong.<br /> And this isn't even getting into utopian leaders who radically reform society to, say, save the poor or their oppressed ethnic group, or whatever, but in the revolution they unleash a terror.<br /> <br /> <br /> The thing about Curse B, tbh, is I never really saw the need to make it, well, a Curse. One of my friends told me Grabowski indicated that he essentially put the Great Curse in as an explanation for what he felt was just a realistic depiction of a super-powered monarchy, but he didn't want people arguing that the Solars were too awesome to end up as the bad guys, so he made it a Curse.<br /> (I'm not sure if that's actually true, but that's what I heard.)<br /> <br /> And of course, there's no actual rules for it, which then gets into the argument where people go &quot;okay, what is the Great Curse supposed to be like, let's look at Solars in the Core book, oh it's A. So the High First Age was A.&quot;<br /> <br /> TBH, I think if Grabowski had never written the Great Curse, the Usurpation could still work fine. But it would probably lead to us characterising its lead-up differently.<br /> (And, I suppose, the Great Curse ought to make the Solars more sympathetic to players. I'm not sure it really makes much difference in practice though.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-15-2018, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T14:06:37-08:00","id":1267681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267657#post1267657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I was getting at is that I think it lacks mythic weight to just, kind of, quite like your Solar Mate (the reincarnated police partner buddy/pal does seem like a minor intimacy)</div> </div> </div> </div>But police partners in reality can often be extremely close, owing to the experiences they share and the need to place their lives in one another's hands. This has often been borne out in fiction depicting them, across a variety of tones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">yet, in practice, it probably has to work like that, because in practice I find that making players have Major intimacies that haven't been built up doesn't work that well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that can be substituted a bit by the implication that many of one's past lives had very strong relationships with one another, and even if you don't quite feel that way yet, it underlies your perspective.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T14:10:01-08:00","id":1267682,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think that works. You feel a bond, a resonance, a familiarity as if you've always known them... But you're still going to judge them on their actions in this life before swearing eternal brotherhood.<br /> <br /> (Unless that's what you want. But I've found it rarely works well for PCs. Can work for NPCs. And might work for other play groups.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T14:35:15-08:00","id":1267690,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a>, in theory I think you're quite right on unchecked compassionate behaviour in rulers, and those are things where you can draw on human experience, but I'm a bit more skeptical about the degree to which this is as prominent a part of the human general experience of that kind of rule (and is so rather down the list on thinking about what I termed &quot;Curse B&quot; type things). I think about the rest of the post, agree that's all fairly plausible (Curse to achieve those ends and also add a flavor of heroic tragedy, probably setting could work fine without it but would force a different mindframe) but of course Grabowski to my knowledge never confirmed one way or the other!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T14:40:44-08:00","id":1267691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267671#post1267671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in unchecked and unaccountable leaders, I think compassion can lead to devastating consequences. They do things they <i>think</i> are good, but they make mistakes. This happens in even leaders who are accountable, but it's worse when they're not, with no-one to point out their mistakes. This could be a matter of economic or government reform based on ideology or lack of information. It could be liberal interventionism, where desire to stop the suffering in a neighbouring country leads to a war that goes horribly, horribly wrong.<br /> And this isn't even getting into utopian leaders who radically reform society to, say, save the poor or their oppressed ethnic group, or whatever, but in the revolution they unleash a terror.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Pests_Campaign\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6f/Kill_bird_and_insect.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Pests_Campaign\" target=\"_blank\"> Four Pests campaign - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Pests_Campaign\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Pests_Campaign </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T00:26:23-08:00","id":1267785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267681#post1267681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But police partners in reality can often be extremely close, owing to the experiences they share and the need to place their lives in one another's hands. This has often been borne out in fiction depicting them, across a variety of tones.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was why I mentioned police Partners <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that can be substituted a bit by the implication that many of one's past lives had very strong relationships with one another, and even if you don't quite feel that way yet, it underlies your perspective. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267682#post1267682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I think that works. You feel a bond, a resonance, a familiarity as if you've always known them... But you're still going to judge them on their actions in this life before swearing eternal brotherhood.<br /> <br /> (Unless that's what you want. But I've found it rarely works well for PCs. Can work for NPCs. And might work for other play groups.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If other intimacies can carry over as well, and I don't see any reason why a carried over intimacy has to be minor, it can be used for a lot of different scenarios.<br /> <br /> Solar Bond, minor -&gt; &quot;there is something familiar with that person; seems to be nice, I should probably introduce myself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Solar Bond, Defining; Love of my life, Defining -&gt; Starts out madly in love. Which can be an uninterrupted epic love-story, or a very creepy stalker horror story.<br /> <br /> Solar Bond, minor; I hate his guts, Defining -&gt; The &quot;eternal&quot; grudge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T02:38:57-08:00","id":1267791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267623#post1267623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But can anyone remember anything else that's been said?</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to remember Vance saying that it\u2019s basically the same as for Solars except for some currently unrevealed method of venting/clearing Limit that all the writers immediately fell in love with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T04:04:44-08:00","id":1267800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267785#post1267785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If other intimacies can carry over as well, and I don't see any reason why a carried over intimacy has to be minor, it can be used for a lot of different scenarios.<br /> <br /> Solar Bond, minor -&gt; &quot;there is something familiar with that person; seems to be nice, I should probably introduce myself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Solar Bond, Defining; Love of my life, Defining -&gt; Starts out madly in love. Which can be an uninterrupted epic love-story, or a very creepy stalker horror story.<br /> <br /> Solar Bond, minor; I hate his guts, Defining -&gt; The &quot;eternal&quot; grudge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Third Edition Solar Bond isn't a &quot;carried over&quot; Intimacy; it's still the Lunar's own Intimacy, and seems to primarily work from the basis of their initial impression of the actual Solar whom they meet, and thereafter changes depending on the nature of that relationship. I don't think it will even really be described among other Intimacies with a special designator or anything.<br /> <br /> What you're suggesting here feels way overcomplicated, and still a matter of infringing a lot upon somebody's character.<br /> <br /> Vance mentioned the idea of recurring rivals, but given the way that the Bond was actually described, that's still going to be dependent primarily on either or both Exalted consistently having the disposition for it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T04:27:49-08:00","id":1267803,"title":"","content":"Although I could see the lunar just taking one look at their mate and getting a good/bad vibe from them depending on how their relationship was the last time.<br /> <br /> And in the first age, when a lunar was likely to have known the solar's previous incarnation, I suspect that could colour their impression of the new guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T06:13:19-08:00","id":1267817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267800#post1267800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're suggesting here feels way overcomplicated, and still a matter of infringing a lot upon somebody's character.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can only infringe on someone's character, if they are not part of the process. Personally, as a ST/GM/Referee/Narrator/Whatyawannacallit I never let a player create a character without me present or having some other type of communication where we bounce things back and forth. So for me, it would come from what the player have expressed an interest in. I'm well aware not everyone do things that way.<br /> <br /> Considering I consider Phoenix Command to be a nifty little system, I'm also aware that I tend to not have the same frame of reference when it comes to how complicated something is. That didn't even register as potentially complicated for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T06:51:14-08:00","id":1267824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267800#post1267800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Third Edition Solar Bond isn't a &quot;carried over&quot; Intimacy; it's still the Lunar's own Intimacy, and seems to primarily work from the basis of their initial impression of the actual Solar whom they meet, and thereafter changes depending on the nature of that relationship.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm...<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a good idea to mechanically demand that the intimacy be carried over. That's too limiting, definitely.<br /> <br /> But saying it is just based on their initial impression of them would seem to make it little different from other intimacy. I mean, your first feelings about anyone is based on your initial impression of them. There's nothing magical there.<br /> <br /> The genre-myth behind it is reincarnated lovers/companions who find each other in each incarnation. I'd say the point of the bond is that this feeling is one that's crossed lifespans.<br /> <br /> <br /> For example, our Lunar, Timid Silk Blossom, was in love with the Dawn, Brasidas. Their previous incarnations had been sworn blood-brothers. But he left the group and later died.<br /> <br /> If she were to meet his reincarnation, she'd immediately, no matter how boring or forgettable that person was in that circumstance, know they were her Solar Mate, and have some relatively strong feeling towards them.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't tell the player what Intimacy to pick, because he can decide how to describe it, but the story of the bond is it's a relationship over lifetimes. Story-wise, the Intimacy represents a bond that's lasted through the aeons. So Timid's opinion of her new mate is going to be a continuation of their previous relationship. Perhaps love again; perhaps rage at being rejected. Perhaps fear of falling into that relationship again. Perhaps protectiveness because Brasidas died. It's up to the player, but I wouldn't tell him &quot;your intimacy is about your initial impression of this person you just met.&quot; It's about Brasidas and Timid, Righteous Lion and the Dread Wolf, and a hundred other partnerships stretching back to the end of the Solar-Lunar war.*<br /> <br /> <br /> *Obviously one big change with 2nd ed is that the Solars didn't have bonded mates in the Primordial War, or for a while after that. But I imagine that when the Solar-Lunar war was over, and the Solars and Lunars bonded together, many tried to choose partners they already knew and got on with.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if my Lunar died, and I introduced his reincarnation to the group as my new character, and Prince Meek was rude or arrogant to him on our initial meeting (as Meek often is), I might still pick a positive intimacy because of Prince Meek's generally positive relationship with his Lunar father-in-law, or the strong (if evil) partnership between the identity-stealing First Age Night Caste and his devoted assassin that they once were.<br /> <br /> Tldr; I agree with Elfive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-16-2018, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T06:57:12-08:00","id":1267827,"title":"","content":"Lundgren, I didn't quite get the point you were making. Was it that you think the Lunar Bond should be able to start at a higher level than Minor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T07:12:35-08:00","id":1267831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267691#post1267691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Pests_Campaign\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Pests_Campaign</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I'd replied to this, but I guess I didn't.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that was one of the examples I was thinking of.<br /> <br /> Both Stalin and Mao definitely were not saints, but alongside their more murderous policies, they had a number of policies that, I think, really were born out of a desire to help people, but went horribly wrong. The interesting thing about the Four Pests Campaign and the Great Leap Forward more generally is that the problem wasn't just that it was a bad policy, but also that no-one was willing to tell Mao. And as things got worse, they kept not telling Mao. Cadre leaders lied about its grass-roots effects, their leaders passed bad information up, and up, and up. And if anyone said &quot;wait, this is going horribly wrong&quot; their superiors could point out all the other places where, apparently, everything was fine. So what's wrong with your cadre?<br /> <br /> The campaign lasted much longer than it should have, because Mao thought it was actually going pretty well.<br /> <br /> The other example I was thinking of was Tony Blair. As far as he could see/was told, he'd heroically saved Sierra Leone with military forces, he'd saved Kosovo with military forces (and been hailed as a hero by Kosovan refugees), and he'd recently liberated Kabul from the Taleban. Iraqi exiles told him how Saddam's forces tortured, raped and oppressed. And so when Bush wanted to invade based on dubious intelligence, Blair was primed to agree to some good old liberal interventionism. And we can all see how well that went.<br /> <br /> Anyway, these are all the sorts of things I could imagine a Solar with incredible charisma, the throne of a powerful nation, but not much more wisdom than anyone else, doing even with good intentions. What mortal's going to tell the God-Queen she's wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T07:31:11-08:00","id":1267836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267827#post1267827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lundgren, I didn't quite get the point you were making. Was it that you think the Lunar Bond should be able to start at a higher level than Minor?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a thought I got from this thread, on how to handle those &quot;epic&quot; and &quot;mythological weighted&quot; ones that spans lifetimes.<br /> <br /> Strong emotions carrying over from one exaltation to the next wouldn't be out of tune for Exalted, and it would be one way to handle it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm not that interested in those kind of stories myself. So I might go with an inherited intimacy (including the Bond) can at most be a minor, or that it can be at most one level less than in the previous life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T07:46:43-08:00","id":1267840,"title":"","content":"Well, the rules for 3rd ed have it be a Minor intimacy, so that works for you. Although since you do 2.5-based Lundgrenzalted, I don't know if you use Intimacy strengths, as 2.5 just had Motivation and Intimacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T07:47:54-08:00","id":1267844,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, has anyone else run/played a game where there were Solar-Lunar pairs both played by PCs? How'd it go? How do you think the 3rd ed changes will affect it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T07:50:15-08:00","id":1267845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267824#post1267824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But saying it is just based on their initial impression of them would seem to make it little different from other intimacy. I mean, your first feelings about anyone is based on your initial impression of them. There's nothing magical there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other Intimacies don't provide special benefits to Charms in that particular manner, and indelibly reassert themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tldr; I agree with Elfive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think that Elfive is really saying a different thing to myself.<br /> <br /> I think that some of the mechanical implications of the Solar Bond need to be approached practically, and getting the mythic weight out of it includes a holistic examination rather than every component going up to 11.<br /> <br /> Essence Fever in particular being a big thing to it, which is almost entirely roleplay.<br /> <br /> I would say that the Charms benefits (and the fact that it's somebody with the power of a Solar) is a major element to incentivizing the Lunar to stick around with their mate, creating scenarios in which they can have more continuous exposure to relevant past life flashbacks, and the relationship can otherwise develop organically. I like the idea of a mystical element to the Bond, but still think that the game should shy away from things such as being hooked into another person without much say so, and having to feel too much of a prior incarnation's emotions.<br /> <br /> At least given some of the unfortunate history of how the Bond has been written.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T07:55:50-08:00","id":1267846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267840#post1267840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the rules for 3rd ed have it be a Minor intimacy, so that works for you. Although since you do 2.5-based Lundgrenzalted, I don't know if you use Intimacy strengths, as 2.5 just had Motivation and Intimacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It uses the intimacy and social conflict system of Ex3 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not really mechanically integrated yet, but I tend to just approximate mechanics anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T08:05:23-08:00","id":1267849,"title":"","content":"It's been a difficult thread to follow (in other words, <i>a Lunar thread</i>) but to me I took the 3e approach as a lot less than an inherited emotion or impression of a person and more of an incessant connection that you can't ignore. You <b>feel</b> for this person you've just met and you can't <b>not </b>feel for them. How you interpret that determines the context of the intimacy, but it could have NOTHING to do with past live memories or emotions. You just know that you can't ignore them if you want to, can't put them out of your head completely, can't pretend they don't exist. Some part of you is always aware.<br /> <br /> Maybe you like that and you get to know them and it becomes a friendship.<br /> Maybe you love that and it grows into something more.<br /> Maybe that bugs you and you become rivals and compete in things.<br /> Maybe you hate that and you just want to be rid of that person and you become enemies.<br /> <br /> My impression is that the context isn't what carries over, it's the root connection. Whatever happens, whatever you think or feel for the person, you're not forced to feel a certain way about them, you're just forced to feel <b><i>at all</i></b>. My 2 cents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T08:21:48-08:00","id":1267852,"title":"","content":"Reading this thread, I appreciate the intra-Lunar conflict and its sabatoge-esque implications to the campaign to overthrow the Realm.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, I want the Scarlet Empress to die and the Dragon-Blooded to know their place. But I sure don't want <i>her</i> [Insert Lunar Elder with actual chance of doing so] to lead the charge because of how much legitimacy that will give her in the Lunar faction. So I'll start a side-war to bring down her chances of doing so. We'll conquer the Realm eventually. My way.&quot;<br /> <br /> Who put those envious political thoughts in the rival Lunar's head? Perhaps a faction known for their indirect actions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T09:15:39-08:00","id":1267871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267849#post1267849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a difficult thread to follow (in other words, <i>a Lunar thread</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div> Pretty much! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You <b>feel</b> for this person you've just met and you can't <b>not </b>feel for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Essentially, as the feeling is only Minor and can be negative or positive... I just don't think this is very interesting or significant. PCs pretty much always have intimacies towards other PCs and significant recurring NPCs anyway. My late Night Caste had intimacies to 7 specific Exalts (Solar and Lunar) and a demon, as well as a general one towards Exalts anyway.<br /> <br /> I mean if other people find it interesting, sure. I'm not going to stop them. But nor do I want the plot of reincarnated sworn brothers whose fraternal love transcends lifetimes to not be allowed (or for that matter, the eternal hatred between reincarnated foes).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really think that Elfive is really saying a different thing to myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>On re-reading, I think you're right (?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Essence Fever in particular being a big thing to it, </div> </div> </div>I don't really see the link there, could you say more?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would say that the Charms benefits (and the fact that it's somebody with the power of a Solar) is a major element to incentivizing the Lunar to stick around with their mate, creating scenarios in which they can have more continuous exposure to relevant past life flashbacks, and the relationship can otherwise develop organically. </div> </div> </div>Now this, this is interesting. I think you're right.<br /> <br /> I suspect that incentivising Lunars (and Solars, since apparently my Lunar doctor would be better at healing her Solar Mate than she is at healing the other Solar PCs) mechanically to build a bond is more likely to get the players to roleplay the intimacy more than saying &quot;we've got an intimacy. It's on our sheet.&quot; Which I don't always find actually gets roleplayed very well.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but since it encourages them to do stuff together, they're more likely to be in situations where their feelings for each other grow in an organic-seeming way; for example, fighting alongside each other, healing each other, etc.<br /> <br /> This also applies for recurring rivals, of course, though perhaps that'd have a bit less of an effect in practice, since your charms being more powerful against a certain enemy isn't necessarily going to make you go after them more than others (though it might a bit).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-16-2018, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T09:32:19-08:00","id":1267877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267871#post1267871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Essentially, as the feeling is only Minor and can be negative or positive... I just don't think this is very interesting or significant. PCs pretty much always have intimacies towards other PCs and significant recurring NPCs anyway. My late Night Caste had intimacies to 7 specific Exalts (Solar and Lunar) and a demon, as well as a general one towards Exalts anyway.<br /> <br /> I mean if other people find it interesting, sure. I'm not going to stop them. But nor do I want the plot of reincarnated sworn brothers whose fraternal love transcends lifetimes to not be allowed (or for that matter, the eternal hatred between reincarnated foes).</div> </div> </div> </div>True that it starts at minor, but it cannot be erased. Or rather, if it is erased, it is replaced by another minor one. The idea is that you may not feel the need to move heaven and earth for them, but you can't just ignore them forever. And perhaps that incessant feeling grows into your epic brotherhood that once was.<br /> <br /> By no means does my idea preclude yours. I agree that all possibilities should be on the table. This is my &quot;bare minimum&quot; approach to the bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T13:07:29-08:00","id":1268001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1267871#post1267871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really see the link there, could you say more?</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have been slightly mixing up some things there, but...<br /> <br /> Okay, so as has been brought up in this thread, the corebook, and the preview about the Solar Bond, part of the significance that it has to the Lunars is in their overall mindset and stability. Establishing the Bond with Solars is part of what allowed Lunars to adapt to the First Age, and definitively losing it by means of most of the Solars being removed indefinitely (and quite possibly still for those Lunars whose mates' Exaltations remained free, if circumstances in which they ever met again became vanishingly rare) has destabilised them a bit, and is a driving force in their vendetta against the Realm.<br /> <br /> These are supposed to be important parts of the Lunar experience, but they can't really be represented mechanically. They even go beyond concrete or emergent elements of the connection between Lunars and Solars, because they're about something that it does for Lunars internally, rather than examining the nature of the relationship itself.<br /> <br /> Even if that's not explicitly part of Lunar Essence Fever, developer comment has clarified that it would function along the same principles of being a description of the inner experience of being that kind of Exalt, that the onus is on the players to fulfil (and which is hopefully written in a compelling enough manner to warrant it).<br /> <br /> So there are factors to it other than the actual strength of the Intimacy that can give it a mythic weight, and set it apart from Ties to other people. <br /> <br /> It will be interesting to see how the book portrays the manner in which the Silver Pact has talked about the Bond in the interim. Presuming that it's not some big secret kept from initiate Lunars (which seems like it would be hard to sustain and counterproductive), there's the matter of how it might be a thing that a few Lunars have spent a fair amount of time thinking about, and in the event that it actually comes to them, might be something that they're intrigued to pursue even if they're not yet at the level where they're willing to risk significant sacrifices or inconveniences for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that incentivising Lunars (and Solars, since apparently my Lunar doctor would be better at healing her Solar Mate than she is at healing the other Solar PCs) mechanically to build a bond is more likely to get the players to roleplay the intimacy more than saying &quot;we've got an intimacy. It's on our sheet.&quot; Which I don't always find actually gets roleplayed very well.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but since it encourages them to do stuff together, they're more likely to be in situations where their feelings for each other grow in an organic-seeming way; for example, fighting alongside each other, healing each other, etc.<br /> <br /> This also applies for recurring rivals, of course, though perhaps that'd have a bit less of an effect in practice, since your charms being more powerful against a certain enemy isn't necessarily going to make you go after them more than others (though it might a bit).</div> </div> </div> </div>The possibility of a rivalry with a Lunar is something that I think might be owed a lot to some common Lunar dispositions crossed over with something that a Solar might have done to give offense, and a bit of ego (if there have been Lunars spending a while thinking about Solars, and disdainful about the idea of being outdone by them). And the Bond will ensure that, even if the two are separated for an extended period of time, the Lunar's impression never just fades away to irrelevance.<br /> <br /> Thinking back on what you were saying about a circle being likely to have members with Ties to all other members, I think that touches on another relevant point; the idea that one does not necessarily want to privilege the connection between Lunar and Solar over any of their other relationships, at least not too much.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T13:18:22-08:00","id":1268011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268001#post1268001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Establishing the Bond with Solars is part of what allowed Lunars to adapt to the First Age</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does this come from? I have seen no hint of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It will be interesting to see how the book portrays the manner in which the Silver Pact has talked about the Bond in the interim. Presuming that it's not some big secret kept from initiate Lunars (which seems like it would be hard to sustain and counterproductive), there's the matter of how it might be a thing that a few Lunars have spent a fair amount of time thinking about, and in the event that it actually comes to them, might be something that they're intrigued to pursue even if they're not yet at the level where they're willing to risk significant sacrifices or inconveniences for it. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T18:37:25-08:00","id":1268115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268011#post1268011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where does this come from? I have seen no hint of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit that I'm inferring from a few references to things that Vance said on the Discord about how forming the Bond helped them chill out a lot, the general timing of the two things, and the drastic effect ascribed to the Bond being broken off.<br /> <br /> I'll also admit that I may simply be conflating, or otherwise running off half-cocked with a misreading shaped by my own preferences and presumptions. It would not be the first time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T22:14:11-08:00","id":1268167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268115#post1268115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit that I'm inferring from a few references to things that Vance said on the Discord about how forming the Bond helped them chill out a lot, the general timing of the two things, and the drastic effect ascribed to the Bond being broken off.<br /> <br /> I'll also admit that I may simply be conflating, or otherwise running off half-cocked with a misreading shaped by my own preferences and presumptions. It would not be the first time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's something somehwat derivable from the 3e prestige spread for them too:<br /> <br /> &quot;Once, the Lunar Exalted matched their aptitudes to their Solar counterparts, the better to protect the world they made. ...&quot;<br /> <br /> The write-up in the blog post implies that too. What Lunar Exalted were in the First Age might not have been during the War of the Gods. What they were in the First Age was a change they made to suit the needs of thata ge. What they are now suits the needs of what the Age has become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T00:39:53-08:00","id":1268198,"title":"","content":"Or to put it differently:<br /> <br /> Original Lunars: \u201cOMNOMNOM THE TITANS.\u201d<br /> First Age Lunars: \u201cProtect and guide Creation!\u201d<br /> Second Age Lunars: \u201cOMNOMNOM THE SHOGUNATE.\u201d<br /> <br /> That could very well just be a wartime vs. (relative) peacetime thing, but there could also very well be some additional reason why one of these things is not like the others and if there is the Bond is implied to be it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T02:20:46-08:00","id":1268206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268001#post1268001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if that's not explicitly part of Lunar Essence Fever, developer comment has clarified that it would function along the same principles of being a description of the inner experience of being that kind of Exalt, that the onus is on the players to fulfil (and which is hopefully written in a compelling enough manner to warrant it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see the comparison there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It will be interesting to see how the book portrays the manner in which the Silver Pact has talked about the Bond in the interim. Presuming that it's not some big secret kept from initiate Lunars (which seems like it would be hard to sustain and counterproductive), there's the matter of how it might be a thing that a few Lunars have spent a fair amount of time thinking about, and in the event that it actually comes to them, might be something that they're intrigued to pursue even if they're not yet at the level where they're willing to risk significant sacrifices or inconveniences for it. </div> </div> </div>I remember in 2nd ed the Sun King Seneschals told all their initiates about how the Gods had given each a wonderful Solar partner, and trained them to be ready to meet and work with this partner... which made no sense to me. That's like teaching your kid the proper rituals to propitiate Jupiter and Juno, or how to ride a chariot. Might be interesting, but it's utterly theoretical.<br /> <br /> I could think that there might well be some Lunars who've spent time thinking about the effect of the Solar Bond, but in a very theoretical sense. And of course, very much in the context of something the Lunars have lost, and how losing it has affected them.<br /> After all, there's probably only less than 10 Lunars out of 400-ish who've ever experienced it, and it was a very long time ago.<br /> <br /> So I wonder if they speak about it in very vague terms, as something they've lost.<br /> And it could even be something that's somewhat over-glamourised, so they can rage about how the Usurpation stole it from them. Or on the other hand, made to sound more constricting than it actually is.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think that a Lunar meeting their mate probably has heard about the Bond, but doesn't really have an exact idea of how it works. Lunars may be intrigued, yet simultaneously worried, to track down their Solar Mate, as they're not 100% sure what it'll mean.<br /> <br /> Plus of course, throw in the varying personalities of Solars. Plus Abyssals and Infernals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The possibility of a rivalry with a Lunar is something that I think might be owed a lot to some common Lunar dispositions crossed over with something that a Solar might have done to give offense, and a bit of ego (if there have been Lunars spending a while thinking about Solars, and disdainful about the idea of being outdone by them). And the Bond will ensure that, even if the two are separated for an extended period of time, the Lunar's impression never just fades away to irrelevance. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but if an NPC is separated from the PCs for an extended period of time, I don't think it really matters.<br /> <br /> Admittedly this is from the other side, but we have a Solar who met his Lunar mate like twice. While there was a bond, the two of them were operating in different areas, with different interests (she actually came to visit his Lunar friend, not him). She wondered off back East to her pack, he stayed with us. He doesn't really have any intimacy to her, and whether she still has a Minor intimacy to him or not I think makes pretty much no difference, because she's far away.<br /> <br /> If she'd been an enemy, and had left to do something else, or if we'd left to go a far off-country, then, again I'm not sure it makes much difference if she has a Minor intimacy of rivalry to him or not.<br /> <br /> I guess if the ST wants to ensure she comes back again and again even if there's not much plot reason to do so, he could, but he could do that anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thinking back on what you were saying about a circle being likely to have members with Ties to all other members, I think that touches on another relevant point; the idea that one does not necessarily want to privilege the connection between Lunar and Solar over any of their other relationships, at least not too much. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is a slightly tricky one.<br /> On the one hand, the whole point about the Bond is that it is, you know, a special bond.<br /> On the other hand, you don't really want a PC to be much more connected to one PC than the others.<br /> <br /> With my own Lunar, his Solar Bond 5 stuck him to the Night Caste, Prince Meek. And this stuck him to the other PCs too, because the other Night worked with/for Prince Meek, the Changing Moon is married to Prince Meek, etc. And if I play another Lunar in the future, I could do the same (though that'd mean my old retired character had died, which'd probably really upset Meek and his wife, my adopted daughter).<br /> Occasionally, he did side with Prince Meek over other PCs, but as Meek is basically the party's leader it didn't really matter. And the PCs all got on well, so they didn't have big arguments or anything.<br /> <br /> But that's not always the case.<br /> <br /> <br /> As I've previously mentioned, I ran a long-running game that I eventually stopped because I thought it would become unrunnable. But by popular demand, another ST took over.<br /> Anyway, we have the big problem that most of the PCs just... don't like each other very much.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">One is a semi-righteous bumbling priest, one is a radical theocratic revolutionary, one is a transhumanist absolute monarch, one is an anarchist atheist (she believes in Gods, she just dislikes them), and one is a fundamentalist zealot and ultra-nationalist warlord.<br /> It wasn't too bad before, but now several of them are actually in power in nations that border each other and thus have tensions over resources, their radically different approaches to rule have caused relations to break down, to the extent that despite the threat of Realm invasion, the warlord and queen went to war for a couple of sessions.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> I made a Solar that was a member of the Cult, since 2 PCs are members, so I thought it'd be a good way to build links with the party.<br /> But it turned out that by having more links with some PCs than others, he ended up (despite resisting) on one side against others, leading to his death.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Cult and the Queen were almost at war, as she refused to withdraw a garrison from a Cult-aligned city. The Changing Moon, who doesn't trust or like the Queen at all, asked me to sneak in to the Queen's palace and listen to the peace negotiations, because if they went to war the Queen would Death Ray the Cult's base, so I should kill her before the war could begin. The negotiations ended inconclusively but acrimoniously. I didn't actually want to kill her, as I wanted to work together with her against the Realm, and she generally tried to be friends with me, so I tried kidnapping her, so I could take her to the Cult and force people to sit down in person. I failed, was captured, and chose death over magical slavery.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, for the last 2 sessions I've been playing a Lunar, Dr Soma Vaidya, a Snake-totem kung-fu doctor. Poison charms and a lot of martial arts.<br /> <br /> I'm not really sure what to do about having a Solar Mate. On the one hand, it seems a good way to have an excuse to like one of the PCs, even if they're not very likeable people. Just go &quot;yep, I've got a magical positive intimacy to that PC, and even if they come off as a pretty mean person it'll keep coming back so Soma would keep working with them, rather than leaving the party.&quot;<br /> But the problem is that, if they keep arguing, then I might end up siding with my Solar Mate rather than trying to get them all to work together.<br /> <br /> I did actually ask the guy playing the character I considered least likely to fight others, but he didn't want a Lunar Mate.<br /> <br /> The ST's hopeful that his next session's plot will bring most of the PCs together, away from their nations, to work together in Varang and start a revolution. So ideally I'd see how that goes, and pick accordingly (probably pick the character who my PC would be least likely to like). But, in theory, you're supposed to know your Solar Mate as soon as you meet them, not after a couple of sessions of hanging out together.<br /> <br /> I can sympathise with the poster (I forget who) on this forum who was complaining that you can't have more than one Solar Mate! Just having the entire party as Mates would solve the issue.<br /> <br /> I am considering asking the least likeable character's (the Dawn) player if I can be his Mate, and asking the other players (who unlike the Dawn have very good social stats) to just throw a lot of social influence at me so I have equal positive intimacies to everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-17-2018, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T06:00:39-08:00","id":1268239,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;maltheist,&quot; &quot;dystheist,&quot; or &quot;misotheist&quot; might be a better fit than &quot;atheist,&quot; since she believes in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T06:05:34-08:00","id":1268241,"title":"","content":"Anti-theist? Not sure. Liberal Immaculate?<br /> Anyway, you see the issue, and why bonding with one PC in particular might be awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-17-2018, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T06:33:58-08:00","id":1268252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268206#post1268206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's like teaching your kid the proper rituals to propitiate Jupiter and Juno, or how to ride a chariot. Might be interesting, but it's utterly theoretical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, presuming somebody that isn't part of a reconstructed religion.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there have to be chariot enthusiasts somewhere out there...<br /> <br /> I take your point, it's just that your examples don't seem to go far enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly this is from the other side, but we have a Solar who met his Lunar mate like twice. While there was a bond, the two of them were operating in different areas, with different interests (she actually came to visit his Lunar friend, not him). She wondered off back East to her pack, he stayed with us. He doesn't really have any intimacy to her, and whether she still has a Minor intimacy to him or not I think makes pretty much no difference, because she's far away.<br /> <br /> If she'd been an enemy, and had left to do something else, or if we'd left to go a far off-country, then, again I'm not sure it makes much difference if she has a Minor intimacy of rivalry to him or not.<br /> <br /> I guess if the ST wants to ensure she comes back again and again even if there's not much plot reason to do so, he could, but he could do that anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some of it would come down to a hook that the player has the option of picking up on or not, and if they don't it's not a huge deal, but it's there if they change their mind.<br /> <br /> And that the particulars of the Bond still give it a distinct texture in addition to Storyteller fiat to bring back characters as they please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T06:59:21-08:00","id":1268259,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there are chariot enthusiasts. That's kind of the point: it might interest some people, but no one has to use it for practical reasons. I don't want to say no Lunars would think about it; it seems like something No Moons might debate or philosophise about, because it's interesting, because it tells them something about their own evolution and roots, etc. But not something anyone expects to come up in their own life.<br /> <br /> Although the Solars have been back for 5 years now, which is not an insignificant amount of time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-17-2018, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T10:41:59-08:00","id":1268334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268198#post1268198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or to put it differently:<br /> <br /> Original Lunars: \u201cOMNOMNOM THE TITANS.\u201d<br /> First Age Lunars: \u201cProtect and guide Creation!\u201d<br /> Second Age Lunars: \u201cOMNOMNOM THE SHOGUNATE.\u201d<br /> <br /> That could very well just be a wartime vs. (relative) peacetime thing, but there could also very well be some additional reason why one of these things is not like the others and if there is the Bond is implied to be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually raises an interesting question - how much, if at all, did breaking the Lunar Castes affect their Charm set? If their goal was to totally reinvent themselves following the Usurpation, it seems like the changes would have to run a lot deeper than switching around Anima powers and XP discounts on Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T11:09:25-08:00","id":1268345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268334#post1268334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This actually raises an interesting question - how much, if at all, did breaking the Lunar Castes affect their Charm set? If their goal was to totally reinvent themselves following the Usurpation, it seems like the changes would have to run a lot deeper than switching around Anima powers and XP discounts on Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the Lunars can change themselves to that degree. I think the importance of altered Castes is primarily in the alterations to mindset, of how and why and what they do (which would also be represented mechanically in Lunar XP, creating a feeback loop in which effectively living within those principles lets them become better more quickly). Although given what some people in the know have said, Anima powers aren't quite to be written off.<br /> <br /> They're not totally reinvented, just adapted to the needs of the Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T13:18:13-08:00","id":1268384,"title":"","content":"I could see it as changing their charms slightly. Giving them a slightly different focus, etc.<br /> <br /> But probably not a significant change.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'm fine if they did, but that's not the impression I get. They were different, but still in some sense recognisably Lunars as they are now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T14:58:56-08:00","id":1268410,"title":"","content":"I wasn\u2019t thinking a wholesale rewrite of their entire Charm set, but unless the new Anima powers are <i>significantly</i> different from the old ones, the grand undertaking to remake the castes looks like an awful lot of effort for little clear benefit, especially since <i>every last Lunar</i> had to get onboard with the project. I dunno, maybe the new Anima powers are just that impressive! But without any knowledge of what they were versus what they became...well, see above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T15:19:18-08:00","id":1268412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268410#post1268410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn\u2019t thinking a wholesale rewrite of their entire Charm set, but unless the new Anima powers are <i>significantly</i> different from the old ones, the grand undertaking to remake the castes looks like an awful lot of effort for little clear benefit, especially since <i>every last Lunar</i> had to get onboard with the project.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think that's the form that it took. I mean sure, at some point they'll have needed to tattoo most of them, but I don't think that the change quite took the form of &quot;gather all of the existing Lunars and do a thing to them&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or even if it did, I don't know... you might as well, rather than keep a useless courtier caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T15:39:02-08:00","id":1268418,"title":"","content":"IMO the Lunar caste remakings almost certainly affected their Charms to at least a moderate degree... in the sense that non-Sidereal Charmsets are already mutable to begin with.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it differently, while a hypothetical First Age Lunar Charm list may have quite a bit of divergence from the post-Usurpation one we\u2019ll be getting, it\u2019d be a difference of what kinds of Charms a typical First Age vs. contemporary Lunar would want rather than a difference in what a Lunar Charm \u201cis.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T17:12:07-08:00","id":1268432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268412#post1268412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really think that's the form that it took. I mean sure, at some point they'll have needed to tattoo most of them, but I don't think that the change quite took the form of &amp;quot;gather all of the existing Lunars and do a thing to them&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Or even if it did, I don't know... you might as well, rather than keep a useless courtier caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m curious - what exactly do you think a courtier is, and how would they be useless to the Lunars of the Second Age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T17:22:43-08:00","id":1268434,"title":"","content":"Um about Charm sets, just reminding everyone that they aren't actually a thing in setting outside for like Sidereals and Alchemicals. They are abstractions, expressions of what they can do with their Essence. Whether they were changed from how it was in the First is a little bit irrelevant since it actually isnt a thing they would be aware of. Now I'm not saying that their powers didn't change, it most likely did. But let me ask why would it?<br /> <br /> About them changing their Castes, you know from the sounds of I don't think their First Age Castes are any different from their post Ursurptation Castes. Going by the implications in the preview. It pretty much sounds like they created those Castes for themselves as well. From the looks of it, Lunars natural state is Casteless. So if that's the case why create Castes in the first place? That is because giving themselves Castes is giving themselves Roles they want to fulfill. All Lunars have a choice on what Castes they want, so it's a way of expressing exactly what they wish to do. During the First Age, they probably created Castes for themselves to nurture and protect the era, to be its guardians and stewards. That was their duty and the way they want about expressing and enforcing that was through their Castes. So what exactly happens when such duties is torn away from you and the world you knew was gone. What would these Castes mean now? If they were created to enforce a duty would it be even possible now if that duty is dead? Thus they changed, they took new Castes to give themselves new purpose and a way of accomplishing it. So did their Charms changed in a way? Maybe it did. Why? Because Charms is simply a way for an Exalted to express their powers under the lens of their Exaltation. They aren't literal. Their extrapolation of what you can do. If your First Age Caste was about being a teacher, you abilities would most likely revolved around that, would it be useful in the current situation where you were facing literally the whole world against you? No so you change, you take the mark of the Full Moon so you could fight down these oppressors and take about what was yours. Think less on what Castes can do, think on why they can do what they can do and why is that important on what they want do with those powers. Full Moons are warriors and warlords, Changing Moons are infiltrators and manipulators, No Moons are witches and tricksters. These Castes all have a firm idea of what the specific Lunar wants to do, that is why they were made. They abandoned the First Age for the same reason, under those they weren't able to do what they want to now. And that is one simple thing, fight back the Realm. Well that's how I think of it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 11-17-2018, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T19:20:20-08:00","id":1268455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268432#post1268432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what exactly do you think a courtier is</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that they make barrels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">how would they be useless to the Lunars of the Second Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm primarily going by that being an example that Holden once used, and secondarily from a notion that it's a role that kind of requires them to be welcome in polite society.<br /> <br /> That contrast is also apparent in the way that the core book describes the old castes (&quot;They were priests and courtiers, spies, observers, knives in the night. The Lunars shed those narrow definitions long ago, leaving them behind in the fallen ruin of the First Age.&quot;), and the new ones that are both broader and more focused, framed in terms of survival in a hostile world and using power to overcome enemies.<br /> <br /> The Changing Moon Caste is most socially oriented, but still from a perspective that Lunars have to hide who they are, using wit and guile and magnetism to conceal and overwhelm and take what they please or need.<br /> <br /> The powers are presumably not altogether very different, but the context in which they're used is, and I'd say that Lunar XP can help to make that feel like it matters. A First Age Lunar would grow as a person through a different set of priorities and achievements than a Changing Moon would, and the latter one is probably more optimal to the position that they're in.<br /> <br /> Really, given the basic element of how all Editions portray Castes, I would imagine that one could run with a notion in Third Edition that the Lunars experienced their own form of them breaking, not because of being warped by continuous exposure to the Wyld, but because the circumstances in which one could effectively be tested or conduct themselves to settle into one of those Castes just didn't exist anymore.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps were actively abandoned... wait, no, the idea that they stopped being able to settle into the old Castes doesn't really cover it, since you have First Age Lunars adopting the new Castes... no, lean more into the idea that the Lunars were abandoning and outright breaking their Castes as a mission statement. Your courtier Lunar isn't becoming whichever of the new three best suits them just from an extra form of power, but as a declaration of intent in the new world, a statement to themselves, one another and their new enemies that it's not going to be a clean war. They leave the old ways behind and embrace the new ones developed by the mystics, rougher, leaner, dangerous. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T19:36:22-08:00","id":1268457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268434#post1268434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full Moons are warriors and warlords, Changing Moons are infiltrators and manipulators, No Moons are witches and tricksters.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, while it's popular and straightforward to describe the Lunar Castes in terms of these roles (past and present developers have gone with the same), and even if they're referenced in that preview*, I actually think the core takes the right approach with describing them less in terms of these specific roles and more in terms of the method and mindset in approaching the universal Lunar issues. This is because, unlike the other Celestial Castes, or even the Dragon Blooded Aspects, there's less space to differentiate them due to the smaller pool of Attributes, and with both the system of &quot;two out of three Caste, two Favoured&quot; and the Totem keyword, there's more room for crossover than ever.<br /> <br /> Take warlords for instance; Charms for commanding troops belongs to one of the Attributes that is not covered by the Full Moon, I can't remember precisely which, but it means that Caste will also have equal claim to the image, while a Full Moon will be able to take them as Strength Charms if they've got the Totem of a pack hunter.<br /> <br /> And as infiltration and sabotage go, well, there's at least one Strength Charm with which to psychically assault from a distance, being able to inflict terror and acquire shapes, so that also goes into the Full Moon wheelhouse by default (and it has a certain witchy element to it and all).<br /> <br /> I think that's a thing worth emphasizing, both as a way of conveying that sense of Lunar diversity and really making the Castes feel rough and mean... crude, if that could be applied without being pejorative.<br /> <br /> That and how much is going to need to fall under each Attribute's umbrella; it doesn't really make sense to play a Dawn Caste if you don't want to focus on at least one fighting Ability, and all of the Terrestrial Aspects have qualities of fighters/warriors, but you can probably legitimately make a Full Moon Caste who doesn't take any of their Caste Attributes Charms for fighting, and end up with somebody who bears a closer resemblance to a Solar's Zenith, Night or even Eclipse Castes.<br /> <br /> * I can't remember precisely, and there's a certain thing with how my browser history works that makes me reluctant to visit the same page twice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T00:40:53-08:00","id":1268490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268457#post1268457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as infiltration and sabotage go, well, there's at least one Strength Charm with which to psychically assault from a distance, being able to inflict terror and acquire shapes, so that also goes into the Full Moon wheelhouse by default (and it has a certain witchy element to it and all).</div> </div> </div> </div>Does &quot;witchy&quot; even mean anything anymore? I still don't get a clear image of what it's supposed to mean, and given the process association of &quot;witch = magic-user&quot;, it conjures to mind a kind of grab bag of effects without much of a theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that's a thing worth emphasizing, both as a way of conveying that sense of Lunar diversity and really making the Castes feel rough and mean... crude, if that could be applied without being pejorative. </div> </div> </div>Raw, perhaps? The core book also used the term &quot;unfinished&quot;, which can have a neat double-meaning of not just being raw, but also perpetually-changing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That and how much is going to need to fall under each Attribute's umbrella; it doesn't really make sense to play a Dawn Caste if you don't want to focus on at least one fighting Ability, and all of the Terrestrial Aspects have qualities of fighters/warriors, but you can probably legitimately make a Full Moon Caste who doesn't take any of their Caste Attributes Charms for fighting, and end up with somebody who bears a closer resemblance to a Solar's Zenith, Night or even Eclipse Castes.<br /> <br /> * I can't remember precisely, and there's a certain thing with how my browser history works that makes me reluctant to visit the same page twice. </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of my great loathing of the expanded mortal chargen chapter of Scroll of Heroes. Associate Full Moons and No Moons with one specific profession category each, and then make Changing Moons a wastebasket caste. It's hard to process that it came out about 10 years ago...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T06:02:28-08:00","id":1268526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268490#post1268490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does &quot;witchy&quot; even mean anything anymore?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means Macbeth.<br /> <br /> In this context, it also means Strength Charms being able to do nightmare stuff, rather than that being confined to No Moon Attributes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T10:05:36-08:00","id":1268575,"title":"","content":"I see the traditional meaning of \u201cwitchy\u201d as being creepy and unsettling. Uncanny might be a good word too. All curses and unpredictable nature and evil. Which makes sense as the word was a tool of social pressure to keep people in line and designate who are the \u201cwrong sort of people.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 11-18-2018, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T12:39:23-08:00","id":1268611,"title":"","content":"Witch derives from the Old English Wicca (m) and Wicce (f) meaning a spellcaster of some kind.<br /> <br /> They themselves are probably related to old Germanic words for divining, &quot;divide sacredly&quot; (probably something about divination via drawing lots), soothsaying, and possibly to a word for making mysterious gestures. One theory is it related to a Proto-Germanic word for &quot;one who wakes the dead&quot;.<br /> Another theory that fell out of favour, but may be true, is that it relates to an Indo-Germanic word for &quot;to know&quot;.<br /> There was also a theory that it was related to the word for willow, but that's discredited now.<br /> <br /> &quot;Witch&quot; (wiccan) was often used by early medieval English writers to translate Latin words for augurs and soothsayers. You can also see it in an English translation of a Scandinavian source that I think is quite interesting:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Some men are so blind that they bring their offering to earth-fast stone and also to trees and to wellsprings, as the witches teach, and are unwilling to understand how stupidly they do or how that dead stone or that dumb tree might help them or give forth health when they themselves are never able to stir from their place.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Not all, but the majority of early medieval usage of the word is in relation to soothsaying; specifically, the kind not approved of by the government and main religion.<br /> From a 10th century homily:<br /> &quot;</span></span></span><i>Ne sceal se cristena befrinan tha fulan wiccan be his gesundfulnysse.&quot;</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">(Christians should not consult Witches to find out their future)<br /> <br /> Of course, medieval people were into magic all the time, at all levels of society. As BrilliantRain said, this word is mostly used for people doing the &quot;wrong kind&quot; of magic. It's not the only kind: the laws of King Alfred banned the following kind of magics: &quot;</span></span></span><i>gealdorcraeftigan and scinlaecan and wiccan&quot;. </i>But that's the word we maintained.<br /> The other thing about medieval views of &quot;good&quot; and &quot;bad&quot; magic, is that it's often simply about whether it's a blessing or a curse. A monk or cunning man/woman might use magic to bless people; a witch would use it to curse people.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">So we've got associates with:<br /> sooth-saying,<br /> divination (via runes, lots, etc, not astrology),<br /> necromancy,<br /> healing and blessing through sacred spots in nature, trees, etc,<br /> curses,<br /> being considered &quot;unclean magic&quot; by the main governmental and religious structures.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think this gives quite a different feel to Lunar magic than Dragonblood magic.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-18-2018, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T15:50:43-08:00","id":1268655,"title":"","content":"I think that there's a definite narrative space for a synthesis of what both BrilliantRain and The Wizard of Oz have said. Notably, all of those magics that TWoZ lists as &quot;unclean&quot; are in fact things that <i>Dragon-Blooded </i>Sorcerers do. These things are permitted, but tightly-controlled - the Realm doesn't like necromancy because traffic with ghosts is the first step down the path of heretical ancestor-worship. Gods and demons are acknowledged, but dealings with them are forbidden to all but the Dragon-Blooded - ostensibly for the sake of mortals' physical and spiritual safety, but also because spirits can grant mortals power that the laws say they should not have. Divination is restricted because it's knowledge that the authorities can't censure or control.<br /> <br /> These laws, these proscriptions against <i>witchcraft</i>, are all about the authorities' fear of the <i>wrong people</i> gaining any kind of power - the slave, the foreigner, the dissident. It is not merely that they seek power through forbidden avenues, but that any avenue that might grant them power is forbidden. The Lunar witch embodies the realization of these fears. They reject the &quot;legitimate&quot; constraints of society because they are acutely-aware that legitimacy has been socially-constructed around them as a prison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T18:50:56-08:00","id":1268689,"title":"","content":"Bringing up the point about the broadness and crossover potential of Lunar Castes has me now wondering how that might work with the First Age ones...<br /> <br /> I'm thinking something like more rigidity in the Caste Attributes (of which they get to take more, although each layout mixes it up a bit more, similar to Alchemical Castes), and less options with the Favoured. <br /> <br /> Although, thinking about the Charms a bit more (since it would still have that matter of a single Attribute being able to cover a lot of ground)\u2026 heh, I don't really see a basis for the powers themselves being different, but I've got a picture in which the had different Keywords back then. Still had Protean and Totemic, but maybe something that would designate sections within the wider Attribute as resonating with a particular Caste, creating an incentive to focus on that aspect to reinforce the Caste role.<br /> <br /> It's pretty silly. Almost certainly wouldn't really work as something to implement mechanically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T19:39:28-08:00","id":1268698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268655#post1268655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that there's a definite narrative space for a synthesis of what both BrilliantRain and The Wizard of Oz have said. Notably, all of those magics that TWoZ lists as &quot;unclean&quot; are in fact things that <i>Dragon-Blooded </i>Sorcerers do. These things are permitted, but tightly-controlled - the Realm doesn't like necromancy because traffic with ghosts is the first step down the path of heretical ancestor-worship. Gods and demons are acknowledged, but dealings with them are forbidden to all but the Dragon-Blooded - ostensibly for the sake of mortals' physical and spiritual safety, but also because spirits can grant mortals power that the laws say they should not have. Divination is restricted because it's knowledge that the authorities can't censure or control.<br /> <br /> These laws, these proscriptions against <i>witchcraft</i>, are all about the authorities' fear of the <i>wrong people</i> gaining any kind of power - the slave, the foreigner, the dissident. It is not merely that they seek power through forbidden avenues, but that any avenue that might grant them power is forbidden. The Lunar witch embodies the realization of these fears. They reject the &quot;legitimate&quot; constraints of society because they are acutely-aware that legitimacy has been socially-constructed around them as a prison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that, it doesn't seem to be nailing much down for the Lunars, thematically speaking. It's like describing a Naruto character as a ninja. The series is lousy with shinobi of all types and conceivable power types. It's like saying that the No Moons are the Exalted Lunars, in a way, and that kind of loose, symbolic association feels way closer to Sidereals using a Resplendent Destiny of the Sorcerer than it does divine predators/carnivores (still not sure which parts of either are playing into the Lunar themes, but it's probably a better topic discussion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T02:02:54-08:00","id":1268765,"title":"","content":"I think there's a line somewhere that suggests the first age castes were closer in function to the solar castes than at current.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T11:06:08-08:00","id":1268913,"title":"","content":"I'm not talking about a uniquely-Lunar mechanical approach to witchcraft so much as describing the narrative and thematic space that Lunar mystics occupy, especially within the cultural imagination of the hegemonic power. The fact that this characterization is nebulous and kinda bullshit if you look at it closely is sort of the point - mechanically, I would hope that Lunar &quot;witchcraft&quot; is far more varied than that, and that their powers offer plenty of means to define, realize, and express their selves <i>as people</i>.<br /> <br /> They should certainly be divine predators/carnivores<i> in addition</i>, but I worry that overemphasis on those aspects could be too much of a straitjacket. My main frame of reference for &quot;divine predators&quot; is Werewolf: the Forsaken, in which that theme absolutely IS a straitjacket and that is exactly the point because W:tF is a game about how career violence stunts your ability to relate to people outside of your in-group and estranges you from society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T11:41:30-08:00","id":1268930,"title":"","content":"Well for one thing, the context of divine predators between the games is completely different for one thing. They are similar given the original idea for Exalted but between those two they have slightly different definitions on what they mean. Similar but ultimately is different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T12:03:06-08:00","id":1268941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268913#post1268913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about a uniquely-Lunar mechanical approach to witchcraft so much as describing the narrative and thematic space that Lunar mystics occupy, especially within the cultural imagination of the hegemonic power. The fact that this characterization is nebulous and kinda bullshit if you look at it closely is sort of the point - mechanically, I would hope that Lunar &quot;witchcraft&quot; is far more varied than that, and that their powers offer plenty of means to define, realize, and express their selves <i>as people</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The narrative and thematic space of Lunar witchcraft is largely defined by the mythic inspirations they draw from. Baba Yaga is a massive part of that, but so is Odin, with his galdr and sei\u00f0r, as well as Circe and Medea. Revolutionary Girl Utena's treatment of witchcraft is also informative, if not as direct an influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They should certainly be divine predators/carnivores<i> in addition</i>, but I worry that overemphasis on those aspects could be too much of a straitjacket. My main frame of reference for &quot;divine predators&quot; is Werewolf: the Forsaken, in which that theme absolutely IS a straitjacket and that is exactly the point because W:tF is a game about how career violence stunts your ability to relate to people outside of your in-group and estranges you from society. </div> </div> </div>While I'm not familiar with Werewolf, I can ensure you that the Lunars' nature as divine apex predators isn't a straitjacket on what they can be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 11-19-2018, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:44:22-08:00","id":1268965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268941#post1268941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The narrative and thematic space of Lunar witchcraft is largely defined by the mythic inspirations they draw from. Baba Yaga is a massive part of that, but so is Odin, with his galdr and sei\u00f0r, as well as Circe and Medea. Revolutionary Girl Utena's treatment of witchcraft is also informative, if not as direct an influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool, and good to know. My main worry is that, as BrilliantRain noted, a lot of myth and folklore surrounding witches is actually thinly-veiled suspicion directed at the subaltern - Circe, for instance, existed within the context of the heavily-patriarchal Hellenic culture that feared female agency with <i>religious </i>fervor. She wasn't just Odysseus' frenemy fuckbuddy, but a commentary on the danger of allowing women to have any kind of power because as everyone* knew, women just couldn't control their baser urges and would naturally get up to all kinds of wickedness without men to keep them in line. If Circe is going to be an inspiration, I'd like to see the story told from Circe's perspective, not Odysseus'. I'd like for her account to markedly different from Odysseus' <i>The Tale Of The Cannibal Monster-Lady Whom I Heroically Tamed With My Dick.</i><br /> <br /> <sub>*Literate male Athenian landowners</sub><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268941#post1268941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I'm not familiar with Werewolf, I can ensure you that the Lunars' nature as divine apex predators isn't a straitjacket on what they can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as a US citizen, the true genius of Forsaken is that it asks you to imagine a world built on pervasive, systemic violence that most people ignore as a matter of self-preservation, policed by violent, authoritarian, quasi-military gangs who hate being scrutinized or held accountable by outsiders, and are at best paternalistic and at worst outright-hostile toward the civilian populace, and then you realize how little would actually have to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:53:32-08:00","id":1268974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If Circe is going to be an inspiration, I'd like to see the story told from Circe's perspective, not Odysseus'. I'd like for her account to markedly different from Odysseus' </span></span></span></div><i>The Tale Of The Cannibal Monster-Lady Whom I Heroically Tamed With My Dick.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I think that sounds plausible, although context suggests to me a format in which Circe edifies what Greeks would have found to be strange and dangerous about her.<br /> <br /> I think it depends on how much they retain the line of Lunars having responded to being demonized by those in power by leaning in to the portrayal.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T14:35:34-08:00","id":1268985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268965#post1268965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's cool, and good to know. My main worry is that, as BrilliantRain noted, a lot of myth and folklore surrounding witches is actually thinly-veiled suspicion directed at the subaltern - Circe, for instance, existed within the context of the heavily-patriarchal Hellenic culture that feared female agency with <i>religious </i>fervor. She wasn't just Odysseus' frenemy fuckbuddy, but a commentary on the danger of allowing women to have any kind of power because as everyone* knew, women just couldn't control their baser urges and would naturally get up to all kinds of wickedness without men to keep them in line. If Circe is going to be an inspiration, I'd like to see the story told from Circe's perspective, not Odysseus'. I'd like for her account to markedly different from Odysseus' <i>The Tale Of The Cannibal Monster-Lady Whom I Heroically Tamed With My Dick.</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this example, the Immaculate Texts would be telling Odysseus' perspective, while <b>Fangs at the Gate </b>tells Circe's.<br /> <br /> (same deal with Beowulf/Grendel)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T17:04:47-08:00","id":1269027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268985#post1268985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this example, the Immaculate Texts would be telling Odysseus' perspective, while <b>Fangs at the Gate </b>tells Circe's.<br /> <br /> (same deal with Beowulf/Grendel)</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! Where do the Solars fit into this analogy? I\u2019ve always seen Odysseus and Beowulf as iconic Solar inspirations, but then again 2E made that comparison explicit with Desus, so I can see why you wouldn\u2019t want to go down that road again in 3E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T17:32:15-08:00","id":1269034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269027#post1269027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do the Solars fit into this analogy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Somebody famous who died a long time ago?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve always seen Odysseus and Beowulf as iconic Solar inspirations, but then again 2E made that comparison explicit with Desus, so I can see why you wouldn\u2019t want to go down that road again in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't you bring the analogy in as a comment on the relationship between Dragon Blooded and Lunars? I don't think the Terrestrial Exalted need to have anything more in common with the hero figures in this particular context, and it certainly isn't something that proscribes their capabilities and personalities (as opposed to their place in the power dynamic) from being something that informs Solar Exalted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T17:46:19-08:00","id":1269038,"title":"","content":"I did, the comparison just struck me as odd because I have never seen Odysseus and Beowulf, specifically, described as any type of Exalted but Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T18:24:46-08:00","id":1269050,"title":"","content":"In the style of successor empires of history, I\u2019m sure the Dragonblooded are keen for some of ye olde Solar heroic glory to rub off on them I\u2019m sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T18:42:12-08:00","id":1269055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269038#post1269038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did, the comparison just struck me as odd because I have never seen Odysseus and Beowulf, specifically, described as any type of Exalted but Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... if you made... why would your own... I'm so confused!!!<br /> <br /> Going back to the original question, I'm struck by the point of how, even if a lot of witch imagery might have originated in rhetoric for patriarchal oppression, there's something to be said for latter day woman who deliberately claimed and appropriated it as an empowering standard for themselves, both from a perspective of having an alternative perspective on such powerful figures and a specific desire to adopt a form that has been signalled to them as something threatening and transgressive.<br /> <br /> I think that would be something that also plays into the experience and history of Lunar Exalted; they're not just Circe, they're people who heard stories about Circe and decided that's who they wanted to be, except where they could control the narrative so that they could win.<br /> <br /> In that sense, I'd say the significance of Odysseus is less as a character and more as a story that is told, and who it speaks to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269050#post1269050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the style of successor empires of history, I\u2019m sure the Dragonblooded are keen for some of ye olde Solar heroic glory to rub off on them I\u2019m sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm is more like the empire that elevates itself by demonizing its predecessors, with maybe a bit of laying claim to their achievements, such as... offhand I cannot remember them, the two Chinese Dynasties prior to the Warring States period. No Terrestrial in the Scarlet Dynasty is going to openly express a desire to emulate the Solar Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T19:17:48-08:00","id":1269062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269027#post1269027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neat! Where do the Solars fit into this analogy? I\u2019ve always seen Odysseus and Beowulf as iconic Solar inspirations, but then again 2E made that comparison explicit with Desus, so I can see why you wouldn\u2019t want to go down that road again in 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the Solar would be someone like Circe's All-Slaying Sword Wife, feared and reviled by all Aegeans, who does not actually show up in the Odyssey because she's been trapped in Tartarus.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">The alternative answer would be to say that the metaphor I picked had to do with hero/monster narratives moreso than particular types of Exalted, but not engaging with the question's premise is a chump move.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T19:51:06-08:00","id":1269073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268913#post1268913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about a uniquely-Lunar mechanical approach to witchcraft so much as describing the narrative and thematic space that Lunar mystics occupy, especially within the cultural imagination of the hegemonic power. The fact that this characterization is nebulous and kinda bullshit if you look at it closely is sort of the point - mechanically, I would hope that Lunar &quot;witchcraft&quot; is far more varied than that, and that their powers offer plenty of means to define, realize, and express their selves <i>as people</i>.<br /> <br /> They should certainly be divine predators/carnivores<i> in addition</i>, but I worry that overemphasis on those aspects could be too much of a straitjacket. My main frame of reference for &quot;divine predators&quot; is Werewolf: the Forsaken, in which that theme absolutely IS a straitjacket and that is exactly the point because W:tF is a game about how career violence stunts your ability to relate to people outside of your in-group and estranges you from society.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still seems functionally identical to sorcery in general, but with shaping rituals that the authorities don't like. Any Exalted, hence, could be witches; it doesn't seem a thing that can be used to define any one type of hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T19:58:28-08:00","id":1269074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269055#post1269055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But... if you made... why would your own... I'm so confused!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I'm not the one who originally said that Solars were myth-heroes and Lunars were things like the Hydra or the Nemean Lion (beings which said aforementioned myth-heroes rather pointedly <i>slew</i>), that was John M\u00f8rke! I thought it was weird at the time, too, but that's what I was given to work with!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T20:04:43-08:00","id":1269075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269073#post1269073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It still seems functionally identical to sorcery in general, but with shaping rituals that the authorities don't like. Any Exalted, hence, could be witches; it doesn't seem a thing that can be used to define any one type of hero.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Lots of Exalted could probably use sorcery to change shape as well, but it still says something particular about Lunars that they do it under their own power.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269074#post1269074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, I'm not the one who originally said that Solars were myth-heroes and Lunars were things like the Hydra or the Nemean Lion (beings which said aforementioned myth-heroes rather pointedly <i>slew</i>), that was John M\u00f8rke! I thought it was weird at the time, too, but that's what I was given to work with!</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, there are like three layers of mixed metaphors here, and a couple of instances of reading some things a bit too literally.<br /> <br /> Just... just examine the context in which the line about the Immaculate philosophy telling the Greek or Old English hero's perspective and Fangs telling the witch or monster's was said. It should clear up any confusion about who is analogous to what and what it says about their relationships.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T20:11:17-08:00","id":1269078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269062#post1269062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the Solar would be someone like Circe's All-Slaying Sword Wife, feared and reviled by all Aegeans, who does not actually show up in the Odyssey because she's been trapped in Tartarus.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:white\">The alternative answer would be to say that the metaphor I picked had to do with hero/monster narratives moreso than particular types of Exalted, but not engaging with the question's premise is a chump move.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay I approve of this answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T20:29:03-08:00","id":1269085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269075#post1269075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Lots of Exalted could probably use sorcery to change shape as well, but it still says something particular about Lunars that they do it under their own power.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can probably get a much more concise set of Charms out of animal-related shapeshifting than from being proscribed, too. It's also not like the other Exalted that the Immaculates hate don't hit the &quot;witch&quot; buttons in strong thematic ways in their own respective rights. Solar-ish Exalted in particular have higher tiers of sorcery to call upon, and they're an &quot;old evil&quot; sealed away and then broken free, like they're the Dragon-Blooded's collective Bandora/Rita Repulsa. The Getimians are also probably going to have a fair bit of witch cred for being part of a war on heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-19-2018, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T20:59:00-08:00","id":1269090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269085#post1269085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar-ish Exalted in particular have higher tiers of sorcery to call upon</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a far more pertinent argument would be for their scary Lore Charms, since those actually exemplify the Solar power, and even then those are more in the vein of being a prophet of doom.<br /> <br /> I feel as though this is another case of somebody taking the wrong direction with reading somebody else's metaphor; as though you're reading it as Lunars having powers because people in character find them to be scary, rather than using some templates consistent across scary people in real life mythologies and using them as the guideline for designing Lunars.<br /> <br /> Your argument seems to be kind of going on a weird course; it's like, you ask for a concise definition of witchy stuff, but then when one is offered it doesn't count because a Solar could also do it, but only if they use sorcery? So, what, as long as sorcery exists as a thing that is available to any Exalted, in parallel to their own Charms that actually say something about them, then nobody gets to have their own Charms described in certain terms applied for various kinds of magic user because... it's not technically correct? Do you object to describing Sidereals as kung fu ninja bureaucrats because none of those things are limited to them either?<br /> <br /> Like, you ask for a concise definition, but then reject it because it's not specific enough to the Exalted in question, even if other Exalted getting in on it isn't really something they do with their Charms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Getimians are also probably going to have a fair bit of witch cred for being part of a war on heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>For one thing, I kind of doubt that the Realm knows much or anything about that, in contrast to the whole thing with the Lunars making a big spectacle of themselves, and being part of the Realm's background mythology because they existed famously back in the First Age.<br /> <br /> For another thing, that doesn't really matter, because I think we're primarily talking about things in terms of how Lunar powers work, rather than how they're seen by an antagonistic group.<br /> <br /> What are you looking for here?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T07:31:58-08:00","id":1269221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269073#post1269073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still seems functionally identical to sorcery in general, but with shaping rituals that the authorities don't like. Any Exalted, hence, could be witches; it doesn't seem a thing that can be used to define any one type of hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you have to remember that it's about broad themes, rather than very exact definitions. And as I tried to show, &quot;witch-yness&quot; is not purely about any one thing.<br /> <br /> It's not<i> just</i> magic the authorities don't like. That's just part of it.<br /> <br /> On the subject of witches, it's not like one day the governments of Europe made a list of &quot;bad magic and good magic&quot; or a rule that &quot;boys can do magic, girls can't.&quot; (In fact, while two-thirds of witch executions during the Witch craze, 1 third were still men.)<br /> <br /> Rather certain kinds of magic, such as those involving curses, spirits and nature, were seen as dangerously pagan, and so became frowned on. This mixed with sexism, and the fact that women had a bigger role in magic in pagan societies (the Vikings thought magic was for girls; sometimes in their myths the other gods make fun of Odin because he's god of magic. What a girl!), as well as classism, meant it became associated with women, especially rural ones, as well as magicians who didn't attend university (no one accuses John Dee of being a witch). <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Witchy&quot; is a reasonable way to view Lunar magic. It's not a 100% dividing line between Lunars and other things. It's just a large part of the inspiration behind their mysticism, compared to Sidereal astrology, Getimian yin/yang alchemy (maybe?), or Dragonblood elementalism.<br /> <br /> <br /> To take a different tack, as Isator said, others can turn into animals. That doesn't stop it being a major Lunar theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-20-2018, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T07:43:37-08:00","id":1269225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269085#post1269085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also not like the other Exalted that the Immaculates hate don't hit the &quot;witch&quot; buttons in strong thematic ways in their own respective rights. Solar-ish Exalted in particular have higher tiers of sorcery to call upon, and they're an &quot;old evil&quot; sealed away and then broken free, like they're the Dragon-Blooded's collective Bandora/Rita Repulsa. The Getimians are also probably going to have a fair bit of witch cred for being part of a war on heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh........................<br /> No, I don't think so.<br /> <br /> The point of Solars isn't that they take inspiration from the monsters, witches, dark magicians, etc, of human myth.<br /> <br /> Lunars are raging bestial cannibal predators who wield dark magic, seduce mortals, and wish to tear down civilisation. The deconstruction, is that actually they're kind of presented as the good guys (with exceptions who are pretty stereotypical villains), because are great Empires actually good?<br /> <br /> Solars are shining heroes empowered by God to save the world. They're the rightful Kings. They've been falsely accused of being demons, but they're not. They don't command the power of Hell*, they don't gain power by consuming their foes.<br /> The deconstruction is that the Kings aren't quite rightful, that being a shining hero doesn't prove you're good, and when the rightful Kings ruled they went mad with power.<br /> <br /> Immaculates may consider the Solars unclean monsters, but the theme is that they're not really, they're heroes.<br /> The theme of Lunars is that they are monsters, but why does being a monster mean you're evil?<br /> <br /> *Except when they do... because Solomon does. They do it not by foul pacts, but because they have God's authority over demons.<br /> <br /> (Before anyone points out that the above doesn't fit 100% of characters, I'm talking about overall themes.)<br /> <br /> As Thesaurus referenced, Lunars are the Nemean Lion or the Hydra.<br /> Exalted asks why the Nemean Lion and the Hydra are the bad guys; aren't they just defending their territory? Aren't they just trying to eat?<br /> <br /> Solars are King David... but didn't he totally murder a guy? Is he really a hero?* They're Hercules... but is Hercules the hero? He went mad and killed his family. Odysseus is a Solar. Why is he the hero when he travelled to a foreign city and helped destroy it just to help salve a King's ego?<br /> I mean, maybe they are the hero. Exalted asks the question, but you can still decide they are.<br /> And you can decide that Lunars really are the monster if you want.<br /> <br /> But even if you decide Solars and Lunars are both heroes, or they're both monsters, that doesn't mean they're the same. Exalted asks the question about both, but it's not the same starting point.<br /> <br /> *To be fair to King David, the question is asked of him, and he realises he's not the hero he thought he was. Not all ancient stories are stereotypical. <hr />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-20-2018, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T07:48:01-08:00","id":1269226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1268965#post1268965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as a US citizen, the true genius of Forsaken is that it asks you to imagine a world built on pervasive, systemic violence that most people ignore as a matter of self-preservation, policed by violent, authoritarian, quasi-military gangs who hate being scrutinized or held accountable by outsiders, and are at best paternalistic and at worst outright-hostile toward the civilian populace, and then you realize how little would actually have to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friends, a lot of whom played a lot of Apocalypse, hated Forsaken, because it was new, so I'm not very familiar with it.<br /> <br /> Except the Forsaken: UK supplement, where the Pure are the country aristocrats and the Forsaken are the urban working class. It fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T07:56:23-08:00","id":1269228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269055#post1269055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm is more like the empire that elevates itself by demonizing its predecessors, with maybe a bit of laying claim to their achievements, such as... offhand I cannot remember them, the two Chinese Dynasties prior to the Warring States period. No Terrestrial in the Scarlet Dynasty is going to openly express a desire to emulate the Solar Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shang and Zhou.<br /> I honestly didn't know how the Zhou depicted the Shang, it's not an area of history I'm very familiar with, but you inspired me to read up on it. Wikipedia tells me the Zhou created the Mandate of Heaven ideology to justify their defeat of the Shang, so I assume they were big into talking about how terrible the Shang were. I assume that's what you're referring to?<br /> <br /> <br /> And certainly there are many other examples throughout history. The current CCP justifies it's rule heavily by demonising the KMT, Warlord Era, and Qing. Many nationalist regimes justify themselves by criticising the colonial Empires they were formerly part of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rrototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the style of successor empires of history, I\u2019m sure the Dragonblooded are keen for some of ye olde Solar heroic glory to rub off on them I\u2019m sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, I can actually see this point, but I think it more likely applies to the Shogunate. &quot;Look at the glories of the Dragonblood Shogunate! If only everyone accepted the Realm as their ruler, we could bring back the Shogunate's greatness and unity! But if people support the Solars, we'll go back to the dark and terrible times of the Age of Nightmares!&quot;<br /> <br /> I suppose there could also be &quot;Ah, you found an ancient wondrous city full of blessings? It must have been made in the Shogunate by Dragonblood. The statue of the Eclipse caste? No, that's just the Mon of House Nellens on his head. It derives from an ancient Dragonblooded House you know.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-20-2018, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T08:08:00-08:00","id":1269231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269062#post1269062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the Solar would be someone like Circe's All-Slaying Sword Wife, feared and reviled by all Aegeans, who does not actually show up in the Odyssey because she's been trapped in Tartarus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This made me laugh, I'll be honest.<br /> <br /> But it made me wonder. One thing that irritated me about the 2e Lunars book is that it seemed rather over-obsessed with Solars. There was even a faction that taught its members to consider themselves one-half of a whole being, training themselves to be the perfect mate for someone they'd never meet, and had no expectation would ever return.<br /> <br /> It seemed almost as if the Lunars were waiting for the Solars to return (almost as if the writers knew the Solars would return! I'm sure there's a specific name for this bad writing trope, but I don't remember it), which they might have done for a few hundred years, but by 1500 years, they really ought to have moved on.<br /> <br /> How do you make it clear the Lunars weren't moping around waiting for their wonderful Masters to return, tell them what to do, and fix everything the Lunars had failed to do... yet at the same time emphasise the deep-rooted rage of the Lunars at the Usurpation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-20-2018, 11:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T08:22:08-08:00","id":1269241,"title":"","content":"Well, I think one thing that helps is that the lunars don't think they've failed at anything. They're playing the long game, and the realm is shaping up to be prime for the killing blow. <br /> <br /> So the reaction to the solars returning is something between &quot;Oh, you're back. Want to help?&quot; and &quot;Screw you, we got this.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T08:47:29-08:00","id":1269253,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269225#post1269225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The deconstruction, is that actually they're kind of presented as the good guys (with exceptions who are pretty stereotypical villains), because are great Empires actually good?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Although I think even Fangs at the Gate will still present Lunars in general as having a bit of an edge.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I suppose that the deconstruction will be less along the lines of the Lunars being in the right as it will be that there are recognizable, even understandable reasons behind their anger that motivates their actions, but a lot of what they do is still dubious at best. There's a real injustice against them, but that doesn't detract from how it's being opposed in a generally violent manner.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's a depiction that I can find compelling through the aid of cultural background because, you know, Irish.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think that's different from some of the other things because I don't think it will be very subtextual; that there being something dangerous about Lunars will be integrated right into the foreground.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">After all, look at the title of the book. That's an ominous image there.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269226#post1269226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My friends, a lot of whom played a lot of Apocalypse, hated Forsaken, because it was new, so I'm not very familiar with it.<br /> <br /> Except the Forsaken: UK supplement, where the Pure are the country aristocrats and the Forsaken are the urban working class. It fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the point about being constrained by violence is inaccurate, although I'm unsure how much of it is the point of Forsaken, especially in its Second Edition.<br /> <br /> I mean... that could be an underlying point to The Wolf Must Hunt... that it's not specifically about creating a thorough and nuanced picture of this society of spirit hunter monsters, but as used as the framework with which to make that point... I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> But yeah, in its Second Edition, it's a very focused game. It kind of overhauled the Uratha power list to make <i>everything</i> related to some element of hunting, whether in empowering the werewolf or mitigating the advantages of targets. I can see how one would talk about that as their clearest example of divine apex predators.<br /> <br /> The different direction for the Lunar Exalted can be seen in their powers being focused through those Attributes, so one can see the predatory aspect include socially shaping a society from the margins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269228#post1269228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shang and Zhou.<br /> I honestly didn't know how the Zhou depicted the Shang, it's not an area of history I'm very familiar with, but you inspired me to read up on it. Wikipedia tells me the Zhou created the Mandate of Heaven ideology to justify their defeat of the Shang, so I assume they were big into talking about how terrible the Shang were. I assume that's what you're referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I kept thinking that I would call them Zhang and Shou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269231#post1269231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This made me laugh, I'll be honest.<br /> <br /> But it made me wonder. One thing that irritated me about the 2e Lunars book is that it seemed rather over-obsessed with Solars. There was even a faction that taught its members to consider themselves one-half of a whole being, training themselves to be the perfect mate for someone they'd never meet, and had no expectation would ever return.<br /> <br /> It seemed almost as if the Lunars were waiting for the Solars to return (almost as if the writers knew the Solars would return! I'm sure there's a specific name for this bad writing trope, but I don't remember it), which they might have done for a few hundred years, but by 1500 years, they really ought to have moved on.<br /> <br /> How do you make it clear the Lunars weren't moping around waiting for their wonderful Masters to return, tell them what to do, and fix everything the Lunars had failed to do... yet at the same time emphasise the deep-rooted rage of the Lunars at the Usurpation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep liking to think that the progress that the Lunars have been making is part of why the Solars have returned in the first place.<br /> <br /> Including how a lot of plans would probably gather significant momentum in the face of a Realm sans the Scarlet Empress. And Silver Pact plans anticipating another few centuries of bleeding the Realm out probably didn't see that coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T10:23:47-08:00","id":1269278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269231#post1269231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This made me laugh, I'll be honest.<br /> <br /> But it made me wonder. One thing that irritated me about the 2e Lunars book is that it seemed rather over-obsessed with Solars. There was even a faction that taught its members to consider themselves one-half of a whole being, training themselves to be the perfect mate for someone they'd never meet, and had no expectation would ever return.<br /> <br /> It seemed almost as if the Lunars were waiting for the Solars to return (almost as if the writers knew the Solars would return! I'm sure there's a specific name for this bad writing trope, but I don't remember it), which they might have done for a few hundred years, but by 1500 years, they really ought to have moved on.<br /> <br /> How do you make it clear the Lunars weren't moping around waiting for their wonderful Masters to return, tell them what to do, and fix everything the Lunars had failed to do... yet at the same time emphasise the deep-rooted rage of the Lunars at the Usurpation?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sun King Seneschals and the ideology they embodied is definitely a thing of the past. The murder of the Lunar's Solar mates in the Usurpation is a part of the Silver Pact's <i>casus belli</i>, but not the exclusive one; Lunars died in the Usurpation, and the Wyld Hunt's continued murder of Lunars throughout the ages is often far more relevant to younger Lunars than some ancient crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","user":"Robert Vance","date":". 11-21-2018, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T10:51:16-08:00","id":1269285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269253#post1269253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Although I think even Fangs at the Gate will still present Lunars in general as having a bit of an edge.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. What's the point of asking &quot;Is the Hydra the real monster in this story?&quot; if the answer is &quot;of course it's not.&quot;<br /> <br /> Exalted isn't a total deconstruction; you can ask &quot;are the Solars really the good guys?&quot; because maybe they aren't, but, you know, maybe they are.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it another way, last session my Lunar, Dr Soma, and her Lunar friend Loyal Fox captured a Realm spy.<br /> If she doesn't tell us what we want to know, and possibly even if she does, Dr Soma offered to do the following:<br /> Let the spy go.<br /> Hunt her mercilessly for hours.<br /> Bite her, causing the spy's blood to coagulate, causing a painful death.<br /> Rip open the spy's chest with Soma's bare hands.<br /> Pull out her heart as it beats it's last.<br /> Eat the bloody heart raw.<br /> <br /> That's not something I want Lunars to no longer do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I suppose that the deconstruction will be less along the lines of the Lunars being in the right as it will be that there are recognizable, even understandable reasons behind their anger that motivates their actions, but a lot of what they do is still dubious at best. There's a real injustice against them, but that doesn't detract from how it's being opposed in a generally violent manner.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It's a depiction that I can find compelling through the aid of cultural background because, you know, Irish.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Resistance fighters against an Imperial or colonising power are probably an excellent inspiration for the Lunar was against the Realm.* The IRA, Hamas, the Mau Mau, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like... the IRA bombed a hotel in my city in the 80s, killing 5 civilians and injuring 31 people.<br /> But... are they definitely the bad guys? What's the cultural context behind it? What drove them to it? Isn't it ultimately England/Britain's fault? But can you be the &quot;good guys&quot; and bomb a hotel?<br /> It's complex, and messy, and brutal.<br /> <br /> *Although... probably not one I expect the writers to big up. Too close and too sensitive, compared to talking about Teutoborg Forest. It's certainly the kind of parallels I expect to crop up in our group's games, but not something I expect to see very explicitly in the gameline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think that's different from some of the other things because I don't think it will be very subtextual; that there being something dangerous about Lunars will be integrated right into the foreground.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">After all, look at the title of the book. That's an ominous image there.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think it needs to be pretty clear and explicit that the Lunars are terrifying to the people of the inner Threshold, so that you can then deconstruct it (or not). They shouldn't seem like just nice guys, cute cuddly animals, who've been cruelly slandered.<br /> <br /> Even if the Lunar in question is a moral exemplar... well, Aslan's not a tame lion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think the point about being constrained by violence is inaccurate, although I'm unsure how much of it is the point of Forsaken, especially in its Second Edition.<br /> <br /> I mean... that could be an underlying point to The Wolf Must Hunt... that it's not specifically about creating a thorough and nuanced picture of this society of spirit hunter monsters, but as used as the framework with which to make that point... I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> But yeah, in its Second Edition, it's a very focused game. It kind of overhauled the Uratha power list to make <i>everything</i> related to some element of hunting, whether in empowering the werewolf or mitigating the advantages of targets. I can see how one would talk about that as their clearest example of divine apex predators. </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I'm not familiar enough with Forsaken to follow this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I keep liking to think that the progress that the Lunars have been making is part of why the Solars have returned in the first place. </div> </div> </div>Hmm....... How do you see that working?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-20-2018, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T10:53:05-08:00","id":1269286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269241#post1269241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think one thing that helps is that the lunars don't think they've failed at anything. They're playing the long game, and the realm is shaping up to be prime for the killing blow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I mean this was a perception of the fans. That the Lunars are just second-rate Solars who couldn't accomplish anything significant. And the references to Solars in the Lunar book seemed to me to reinforce that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T10:54:24-08:00","id":1269289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269278#post1269278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sun King Seneschals and the ideology they embodied is definitely a thing of the past. The murder of the Lunar's Solar mates in the Usurpation is a part of the Silver Pact's <i>casus belli</i>, but the exclusive one; Lunars died in the Usurpation, and the Wyld Hunt's continued murder of Lunars throughout the ages is often far more relevant to younger Lunars than some ancient crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you mean it's not the exclusive one.<br /> <br /> Is your approach in Fangs at the Gate then partly to de-emphasise the Solars' importance to Lunars, compared to how they were presented in 2nd ed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T11:12:18-08:00","id":1269294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269285#post1269285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like... the IRA bombed a hotel in my city in the 80s, killing 5 civilians and injuring 31 people.<br /> But... are they definitely the bad guys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah; fuck the Provisional IRA.<br /> <br /> ...Okay, even then I've got to acknowledge some details. After all, that was the Thatcher government, and it wasn't exactly conducting itself well on its own soil, let alone with Irish prisoners.<br /> <br /> Still, my background has also effectively instilled in me an attitude of &quot;fuck the Provisional IRA&quot;.<br /> <br /> I kind of prefer my IRA references to stick closer to the 1920s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too close and too sensitive, compared to talking about Teutoborg Forest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the retreat from Kabul in 1842<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think it needs to be pretty clear and explicit that the Lunars are terrifying to the people of the inner Threshold, so that you can then deconstruct it (or not). They shouldn't seem like just nice guys, cute cuddly animals, who've been cruelly slandered.<br /> <br /> Even if the Lunar in question is a moral exemplar... well, Aslan's not a tame lion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I also want to consider things in the direction of a Lunar that isn't particularly murderous; someone whose shapes are gathered from broken oaths, who inflicts mischief and humiliation upon people that have transgressed in some manner, who directs a society through challenges of social mores, a few other things that the Charms probably allow; more roguish, impious, somewhat unnerving without being explicitly threatening. Not quite gloriously inspirational hero material, and still fitting in with a lot of the rest of the Silver Pact, but perhaps not so compromised in their own person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I'm not familiar enough with Forsaken to follow this.</div> </div> </div> </div>In summary, hunting animistic spirits pervades werewolf society and powers, and Uratha is their name for themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm....... How do you see that working?</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics of the Solar return being largely a result of the Sun coming around to there being a need for them, and seeing that need coming from seeing a lot of Time of Tumult stuff on the horizon.<br /> <br /> I like a lot about the direction the Silver Pact is going in, including cheerfully embracing the notion that their general success if nothing new had been added to the mix would have been a horrible disaster.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T11:30:05-08:00","id":1269296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269294#post1269294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah; fuck the Provisional IRA.<br /> <br /> ...Okay, even then I've got to acknowledge some details. After all, that was the Thatcher government, and it wasn't exactly conducting itself well on its own soil, let alone with Irish prisoners.<br /> <br /> Still, my background has also effectively instilled in me an attitude of &quot;fuck the Provisional IRA&quot;.<br /> <br /> I kind of prefer my IRA references to stick closer to the 1920s.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the retreat from Kabul in 1842</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I don't expect any modern references to be used in Exalted. Too real to people's own experience.<br /> <br /> Probably 19th century and earlier. The retreat from Kabul works.<br /> <br /> Though saying that, since it involves kung-fu guys wearing magic amulets attempting to essentially free their country from being a Satrapy via the killing of anyone associated with the foreign oppressors (say, by having the same religion), the Boxer Rebellion of 1899-1901 is probably an excellent reference for Exalted.<br /> <br /> So, if you'd prefer to avoid the Provs, let's go with:<br /> <br /> <br /> Like... the Fists of Harmony and Justice marauded across the countryside killing Christians, and besieged the Foreign Legation, trapping a couple of hundred Brits (including my great-great-uncle, a 24 year-old student Mandarin-English translator) and 2000 innocent Chinese Christians inside for 80 days. My great-great-uncle ate his horse to survive, but died of typhoid anyway.<br /> <br /> But... were the Militia United in Righteousness definitely the bad guys? What's the cultural context behind it? What drove them to it? Isn't it ultimately England/Britain's fault? But can you be the &quot;good guys&quot; and kill civilians?<br /> It's complex, and messy, and brutal.<br /> <br /> Maybe nothing past 1901 though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now I also want to consider things in the direction of a Lunar that isn't particularly murderous; someone whose shapes are gathered from broken oaths, who inflicts mischief and humiliation upon people that have transgressed in some manner, who directs a society through challenges of social mores, a few other things that the Charms probably allow; more roguish, impious, somewhat unnerving without being explicitly threatening. Not quite gloriously inspirational hero material, and still fitting in with a lot of the rest of the Silver Pact, but perhaps not so compromised in their own person. </div> </div> </div>I suppose they're still socially disruptive, so may well be considered &quot;monstrous&quot; by concerned citizens, even if they're not actually eating people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The mechanics of the Solar return being largely a result of the Sun coming around to there being a need for them, and seeing that need coming from seeing a lot of Time of Tumult stuff on the horizon. </div> </div> </div> I mean, I can see that, but not necessarily the link with Lunar progress.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like a lot about the direction the Silver Pact is going in, including cheerfully embracing the notion that their general success if nothing new had been added to the mix would have been a horrible disaster. </div> </div> </div>So... you're saying the Unconquered Sun sent back the Solars to save the world from the Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-20-2018, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T12:09:43-08:00","id":1269311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269296#post1269296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I don't expect any modern references to be used in Exalted. Too real to people's own experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there aren't going to be car bombs because there aren't any cars. I'm not really sure what your standards for a real world/modern reference are here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... you're saying the Unconquered Sun sent back the Solars to save the world from the Lunars?</div> </div> </div> </div>I said a lot of Time of Tumult stuff.<br /> <br /> Even in that subset, not so much the Lunars as potential disastrous consequences of widespread success in that particular context.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T12:12:02-08:00","id":1269312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269289#post1269289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you mean it's not the exclusive one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll confirm that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269289#post1269289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is your approach in Fangs at the Gate then partly to de-emphasise the Solars' importance to Lunars, compared to how they were presented in 2nd ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The importance of the Solars to the Lunars hasn't been entirely removed, but it has been de-emphasized. Lunars are the protagonists of their own stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T12:47:01-08:00","id":1269315,"title":"","content":"Though unsupported, I do like the idea that the Lunar Exalted used the creation of the Solar Bond to fashion new Castes for themselves for the First Age; Castes that matched or supplemented those of their Solar Mates and aided in protecting and ruling Creation as kings and queens.<br /> <br /> It definitely jives with the idea that losing the Solars hurt the Lunars badly, and left their current Castes ill-suited to their new needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T13:05:00-08:00","id":1269322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269228#post1269228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shang and Zhou.<br /> I honestly didn't know how the Zhou depicted the Shang, it's not an area of history I'm very familiar with, but you inspired me to read up on it. Wikipedia tells me the Zhou created the Mandate of Heaven ideology to justify their defeat of the Shang, so I assume they were big into talking about how terrible the Shang were. I assume that's what you're referring to?<br /> <br /> And certainly there are many other examples throughout history. The current CCP justifies it's rule heavily by demonising the KMT, Warlord Era, and Qing. Many nationalist regimes justify themselves by criticising the colonial Empires they were formerly part of.</div> </div> </div> </div>National successors to foreign empires in general doing this sort of thing is probably no new thing - Yuan to Ming probably has some element of this.<br /> <br /> Changes in religious ideology also matter - Jahiliyyah and all that. There's possibly somewhat analogous ideas at work in orthodox Immaculate conception of the past?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269285#post1269285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Although... probably not one I expect the writers to big up. Too close and too sensitive, compared to talking about Teutoborg Forest. It's certainly the kind of parallels I expect to crop up in our group's games, but not something I expect to see very explicitly in the gameline</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's the up close and personal issue, but I also think that there are degrees to which using more ancient or pre-modern references directly tends to frame the ideas involved in more useful ways. Movements based on modern nationalism (ideas probably absent in creation, at least inasmuch as relate to aspirations to nation states) or based on trying to pressure a mass democratic government aren't as directly useful as the ancient references that could be directly cited. <br /> <br /> (Like how 19th and 20th century imperialism, or &quot;neocolonialism&quot;, to my mind, isn't actually very useful for describing the Realm compared to earlier empires across the world - Spanish and British in Americas and within Europe, Russia in Siberia, Ottomans, Rome, Persia, Chinese, etc. - that weren't experiencing the kind of very unusual world historical technological revolutions that happened in the 19th-20th century and which the Realm sees nothing much like. For all that people want to talk about ideas that affect the modern world today, I think this can be conflict with the actual differences in the fictional setting being described, and sometimes difficult. But that's a whole other derail that should not go in this thread!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T13:05:33-08:00","id":1269323,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I would rather see Lunars have &quot;that certain edge&quot; to them because they're engaged in a war of resistance, and resistance against empire is always an ugly, brutal struggle, and the idea of a &quot;clean war&quot; is a self-serving myth promulgated after the fact by the winners, than because Lunars are essentially and inalienably monstrous. Once again, Werewolf: the Forsaken is a useful point of reference here, because the Uratha <i>are</i> essentially and inalienably monstrous. Yes, their hunting serves a vital ecological purpose. Yes, they can try to minimize collateral damage. The fact remains that they're obligate predators for whom ritualistic murder is something like orgasmic release paired with a religious experience, and who feel no more instinctual aversion to killing humans than wolves do to eating rabbits. The question in Forsaken isn't whether the PCs are secretly misunderstood good guys. They're monsters. They lie, steal, and kill as naturally as they breathe. The question is whether the World of Darkness could function without them to keep all of its <i>other </i>monsters in check.<br /> <br /> I don't feel that this laser focus on inherent monstrosity is needed for the Lunars. They're fighting a war. War has all the baked-in moral conflict you could ever need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T13:42:13-08:00","id":1269334,"title":"","content":"As the preview puts it, they're effectively monstrous and human simultaneously. They don't have an issue with needing to maintain a balance (which Forsaken Second Edition interestingly put in terms of there being problems with acting too human as well as too spirit).<br /> <br /> The monstrous side seems to play a significant part in starting and perpetuating that conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T18:52:57-08:00","id":1269413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269090#post1269090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think a far more pertinent argument would be for their scary Lore Charms, since those actually exemplify the Solar power, and even then those are more in the vein of being a prophet of doom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Along with nearly all of the Occult Charms, particularly the ones dealing with spirits. One even manifests every allied spirit if the roll has exactly three 6s, which seems right on the nose with a steely gauntlet. Or the Brawl Charm that pulls out someone's heart, presumably to sacrifice to the Unconquered Sun. Also, any Charms that conjure up magical objects or mounts. Sail also seems like it has a lot of weirdness in it, especially when it allows you to speak in strange maritime tongues or claim ships mystically as your own. Craft also whips up Artifacts in little time at all, which is probably freaky to see when someone hammers on steel ingots with closed fists, exhales onto them, and then produces a blade of unparalleled quality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel as though this is another case of somebody taking the wrong direction with reading somebody else's metaphor; as though you're reading it as Lunars having powers because people in character find them to be scary, rather than using some templates consistent across scary people in real life mythologies and using them as the guideline for designing Lunars. </div> </div> </div>I was making a metatextual comment there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your argument seems to be kind of going on a weird course; it's like, you ask for a concise definition of witchy stuff, but then when one is offered it doesn't count because a Solar could also do it, but only if they use sorcery? </div> </div> </div>But we established above that Solars do have disturbing powers without sorcery, so allow me to amend that there are certain facets of sorcery that I don't find to be compelling Charm territory. The setting itself tends to isolate conjuring of large-scale objects and structures like shelter and ships in sorcery, for example, and to others, it adds a ritual flair, like in how Spoke the Wooden Face requires preparatory carving of a tree. I'm fairly certain that Dragon-Blooded or Exigents of arbor-gods could do something like that, but they probably wouldn't require the carving part.<br /> <br /> So, when Lunars, for some reason, get wide-scale, long-lasting tracts of territory that can turn humans into beastfolk, I question why it's not a spell or even just a common example of a working. It seems too large-scale for a Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what, as long as sorcery exists as a thing that is available to any Exalted, in parallel to their own Charms that actually say something about them, then nobody gets to have their own Charms described in certain terms applied for various kinds of magic user because... it's not technically correct? Do you object to describing Sidereals as kung fu ninja bureaucrats because none of those things are limited to them either? </div> </div> </div>Sidereals have a culture of bureaucracy (every one of them retrieved by the Bureau of Destiny is, well, working for a governmental organ titled the Bureau of Destiny), wield martial arts that no one else can without their tutelage, and the ninja part at least emphasizes stealth and misdirection, which is readily displayed in their Charms and aided substantially in their Arcane Fate, as they broke the cosmos to make it so that no one would remember them clearly. In contrast, Lunars shapeshift into animals more easily than anyone else, have tended to be very visceral, and their culture is one of insurgents who trade favors, occasionally decided by kicking someone's ass in a dispute, and work to take down their mutual enemies when not doing their own thing. Their powers centered on alteration of their own bodies without preamble, ritual, or even thought, and along the lines of fierce, predatory actions. &quot;Witch&quot; seems to lack the raw, visceral feel that the splat has claimed; it can be polished up and put in classrooms, described as a variation of a wizard, and made to operate in a very Solar fashion with great ease - and when the witches go &quot;awry&quot;, they can become Abyssals or Infernals.<br /> <br /> (Also, kung fu ninja bureaucrat more of a fan appellation, though admittedly one somewhat less flippant and jokey than &quot;teacup ninja&quot; or &quot;fate Jedi&quot;. It still gives no hint as to their mastery and manipulation of destiny, for example, so as a summation, it doesn't really cover their essence.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, you ask for a concise definition, but then reject it because it's not specific enough to the Exalted in question, even if other Exalted getting in on it isn't really something they do with their Charms? </div> </div> </div>But the other Exalted do get in on it with their Charms. Abyssals and Infernals were the go-to splats for that in previous editions; it's not even relegated just to Exalted, since Fair Folk felt that way, too, and Dragon Kings may or may not be there, but certainly were when the Dark Paths were in their book. Lunars joining the club doesn't mean that they take on the term as a definition of their essence, even if we stop calling Infernals warlocks. Abyssals even serve beings known as witch-kings of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> I suppose the tl;dr is that the witch business seems like an ill-fitting, 11th-hour change of nomenclature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T23:43:30-08:00","id":1269456,"title":"","content":"Given how successful the Lunars have been at bleeding the Realm and running it to ground, I find I really have to question the Sidereal\u2019s decision to embark on the Usurpation back then. Or, at least, I have to wonder how Chejop is still managing to say \u201cEverything is fine. This is good.\u201d even several centuries ago when it should have become fairly clear that the Lunars are slowly winning.<br /> <br /> I mean, from everything we\u2019ve been hearing about the Lunars it seems like the general reaction to \u201cWe\u2019re going to drive them off to the edge of the World where they\u2019ll simply wither away and die\u201d is that the guy saying that plan should have had a hard time keeping a straight face before everyone breaks down laughing and then someone says \u201cno, seriously, what are we actually gonna do about the Lunars?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T23:57:55-08:00","id":1269458,"title":"","content":"Well it probably would have worked if most of the Dragonblood hadn't dropped dead of plague and their world-spanning Empire hadn't collapsed into ruin.<br /> <br /> (Obviously many Lunars died at the same time; but they just reincarnate. The number of DBs per Lunar dropped massively.)<br /> <br /> At least, that's how the Sidereals and Dragonblood see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T01:08:39-08:00","id":1269477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269323#post1269323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I would rather see Lunars have &quot;that certain edge&quot; to them because they're engaged in a war of resistance, and resistance against empire is always an ugly, brutal struggle, and the idea of a &quot;clean war&quot; is a self-serving myth promulgated after the fact by the winners, than because Lunars are essentially and inalienably monstrous. ...<br /> <br /> I don't feel that this laser focus on inherent monstrosity is needed for the Lunars. They're fighting a war. War has all the baked-in moral conflict you could ever need.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, if you want to play a character who's actions are questionable because of the inherent issues of fighting a war against a ruling power...<br /> Well, you can do that with Solars.<br /> <br /> Every single Lunar is Exalted with the power to steal other humans' identity via cannibalism (in 3rd ed). Cannibalism is one of humanity's most ancient taboos (not universally, but generally). <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not saying that all their charms have to work that way. But they're not just Silver Shapeshifting Solars. They are bestial monsters, the Fangs at the Gate, the howl in the mountains from which cowering peasants hide. Their hearts burn with rage, their fangs drip with blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One even manifests every allied spirit if the roll has exactly three 6s, which seems right on the nose with a steely gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you're referring to the fact that 666 is an extremely lucky number in Chinese numerology?<br /> <br /> (One time I came out of my Chinese church with some very conservative American friends and walking past our church was a local guy in a shirt with a giant inverted pentagram with &quot;666 Satan&quot; written on it, which horrified my friends. That was pretty funny. My students were rather shocked when I told them 666 is seen in a bad light in the West.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we established above that Solars do have disturbing powers without sorcery</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of your examples were things that people might be shocked by because they're so amazing (like crafting with no tools), but, other than an Essence 5 charm from Miracles, they don't really seem freaky.<br /> <br /> I mean, we shouldn't go too far here. Lunars' theme is not they are &quot;witchy&quot;.<br /> <br /> No Moons are &quot;mystics, witches and shamans.&quot; It's a sub-theme. And it doesn't mean no-one else can ever do anything &quot;witchy&quot;. Just that Lunars are more into it.<br /> <br /> (I'll also point out that sorcery is inherently theme-busting, so anything done with sorcery doesn't stop things being a theme of a certain splat. Solars summoning demons doesn't mean they're the &quot;demon Exalts&quot;, Infernals are.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, when Lunars, for some reason, get wide-scale, long-lasting tracts of territory that can turn humans into beastfolk, I question why it's not a spell</div> </div> </div> </div>Because:<br /> a) territory charms are a Lunar thing (and have been for ages, that's not new)<br /> b) beastmen are a Lunar thing<br /> c) this is Lunar-only tech. A Solar can't learn it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Their powers centered on alteration of their own bodies without preamble, ritual, or even thought, and along the lines of fierce, predatory actions. &quot;Witch&quot; seems to lack the raw, visceral feel that the splat has claimed</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in 1st ed and 2nd ed No Moons had a problem.<br /> WTF do they do?<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting isn't much use for mental stats. It's pretty difficult to be &quot;visceral&quot; with Intelligence charms. There were some examples; I used to mutate people with my Intelligence charms, for example.<br /> But it was definitely limited compared to the physical attributes. Intelligence had 15 charms in the Lunar book, 13 if you don't include sorcery. A third of those were just mental defence charms. <br /> Compare that to Stamina's 28 charms.<br /> <br /> At the beginning of 3rd ed John Morke said he wanted to even more emphasise the visceral, physical, shapeshifting nature of Lunar charms. No illusions or things like that.<br /> People asked &quot;well, what about No Moons?&quot; He said he could do something with lizard brains.<br /> <br /> It... honestly did not at all feel to me like No Moons were going to end up with a competitive number of charms. Or interesting ones.<br /> <br /> But now that Lunars have been further developed, the devs are going with Shamanism as the No Moon's primary inspiration, with Night-Witches as a secondary thing.<br /> <br /> Is that about alteration of their own bodies? Probably not (alteration of thought... honestly, sounds to me like it'll end up with a few boring and indistinct charms that aren't necessarily that different from, say, Solar persona charms). Is it raw and visceral? There may be some blood-magic and things like that, I certainly hope so, but frankly if that's all there was it'd be too limiting. They've got to be wider than that if I'm going to get at least 40 charms per Mental Attribute.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T05:43:19-08:00","id":1269520,"title":"","content":"I might address the rest of the post some other time when I have more energy, but for the moment, something simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the witch business seems like an ill-fitting, 11th-hour change of nomenclature.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The eleventh hour was something like four years ago.<br /> <br /> Terrifying Argent Witches got that name for a reason.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T06:39:28-08:00","id":1269543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269456#post1269456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how successful the Lunars have been at bleeding the Realm and running it to ground, I find I really have to question the Sidereal\u2019s decision to embark on the Usurpation back then. Or, at least, I have to wonder how Chejop is still managing to say \u201cEverything is fine. This is good.\u201d even several centuries ago when it should have become fairly clear that the Lunars are slowly winning.</div> </div> </div> </div>He says it louder and slower, with audible punctuation between each word and a pronounced twitch in his eye.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269456#post1269456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, from everything we\u2019ve been hearing about the Lunars it seems like the general reaction to \u201cWe\u2019re going to drive them off to the edge of the World where they\u2019ll simply wither away and die\u201d is that the guy saying that plan should have had a hard time keeping a straight face before everyone breaks down laughing and then someone says \u201cno, seriously, what are we actually gonna do about the Lunars?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Well, the Solars' madness and our prophecy of impending doom are such a big deal that we can't really address ALL the issues perfectly. We'll trust that driving the Lunars to the edge of the world will suffice to buy time for us to come up with a more-detailed plan for them later.&quot;<br /> <br /> Narrator Voice: &quot;It did not suffice.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T06:51:19-08:00","id":1269548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269456#post1269456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how successful the Lunars have been at bleeding the Realm and running it to ground, I find I really have to question the Sidereal\u2019s decision to embark on the Usurpation back then. Or, at least, I have to wonder how Chejop is still managing to say \u201cEverything is fine. This is good.\u201d even several centuries ago when it should have become fairly clear that the Lunars are slowly winning.<br /> <br /> I mean, from everything we\u2019ve been hearing about the Lunars it seems like the general reaction to \u201cWe\u2019re going to drive them off to the edge of the World where they\u2019ll simply wither away and die\u201d is that the guy saying that plan should have had a hard time keeping a straight face before everyone breaks down laughing and then someone says \u201cno, seriously, what are we actually gonna do about the Lunars?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever form the Sidereal Great Curse takes this time around, I think it will be reasonable for it to include something that might have interfered with their reasoning on this.<br /> <br /> Still, my basic idea would be that they either hoped Lunars would adapt in a direction that would be accepting of the new dynamic, or had confidence that pervasive military power could keep a handle on them.<br /> <br /> Either idea is based on a perspective that the Sidereals had gotten used to Realm Lunars in a manner that blinded them a bit to what they're capable of when fighting from a position of persecution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T07:58:10-08:00","id":1269564,"title":"","content":"I have had the sobering realisation that this exact same model of conversation has happened with Saur Ops Specialist before, except with beastfolk rather than the idea of witchery being associated with Lunars, going along a similar trajectory until I just had to throw my hands up and suggest asking the developers.<br /> <br /> And I'm noticing here a disparaging reference to the notion of Lunars having a power to transform people into beastfolk that suggests being kind of salty about the answer to that question. <br /> <br /> And I think about some other conversations that were really contentious over some Lunar ideas while seemingly unaware of or disregarding some elements about them that had already been introduced or confirmed...<br /> <br /> I don't know, I'm starting to feel as though these arguments are not being made in good faith. :s","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T09:40:37-08:00","id":1269590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269520#post1269520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The eleventh hour was something like four years ago.<br /> <br /> Terrifying Argent Witches got that name for a reason.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Which was a homebrew that the previous dev team repudiated acerbically. <br /> <br /> Thanks Wizard of Oz for chiming in with a reminder of that, because I've been wanting to bring it up but I wasn't entirely sure of my own memory. <br /> <br /> And THANK YOU Minton &amp; Vance for taking things in another direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T09:44:22-08:00","id":1269593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269548#post1269548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either idea is based on a perspective that the Sidereals had gotten used to Realm Lunars in a manner that blinded them a bit to what they're capable of when fighting from a position of persecution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see that actually. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In the Divine Revolution, the Lunars were monsters that even the most nightmarish among the enemies of the gods learned to fear.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As the First Age\u2019s glories arose from the Exalted\u2019s triumph, the Lunars enjoyed the fruit of the paradise they\u2019d helped to win, and transformed themselves into the Lunar Exalted of an Age of Dreams. Though never forsaking the divine monstrosity at the heart of their Essence, they became guardians, guides, world-walkers, judges, and mystics. </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to over-estimate it and say Lunars became completely soft and decadent. After all, they &quot;never forsook the divine monstrosity at the heart of their essence&quot;.<br /> But &quot;Guardians, guides, world-walkers, judges and mystics&quot; sounds like much less of a threat to the Shogunate than &quot;monsters that even most nightmarish amongst the enemies of the gods learned to fear.&quot; I can certainly see the Sidereals underestiming their threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T10:09:43-08:00","id":1269604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269590#post1269590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which was a homebrew that the previous dev team repudiated acerbically.<br /> <br /> Thanks Wizard of Oz for chiming in with a reminder of that, because I've been wanting to bring it up but I wasn't entirely sure of my own memory.<br /> <br /> And THANK YOU Minton &amp; Vance for taking things in another direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but they got the name because &quot;witch&quot; was a term that those developers frequently used for the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> And we're having this argument because &quot;witch&quot; is a term that <i>these</i> developers are using for the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> So calling it an eleventh hour addition is completely ludicrous.<br /> <br /> Just as one last reference to the argument; a major difference between the Solar Exalted and the Lunars is that, to the extent that the former has Charms that might kind of touch on that kind of element, they're almost entirely confined to the Abilities that are actually about that thing.<br /> <br /> As opposed to Lunars, who will have a Charm to haunt people's nightmares in Strength.<br /> <br /> Part of the thing with the Sidereal Exalted having been kung-fu sage bureaucrats is that they have things that invoke martial arts imagery, sorcerous imagery and bureaucracy imagery <i>throughout</i> their Charms, rather than just confined to Abilities conventionally about those things. It distinguishes them significantly from the Solar Exalted by being a lot more focused, but not in a manner that means that they only do a few things.<br /> <br /> Same with references to an Exigent of some healing god, who could be written as focusing medical imagery through any of the Abilities, rather than only having Medicine Charms.<br /> <br /> So Lunars have it as a reference to them as a whole because it's a lot easier for more of them to have the image, since it is spread across their Charms, and because they have fewer stats they need to build up to be able to go for those Charms if they want them; a Solar that is a really powerful fighter and has no Occult has to go through a lot more to get stuff to mess with dreams than a Lunar that is really good at fighting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T10:19:43-08:00","id":1269606,"title":"","content":"Oh wait... even the trajectory of telling Saur Ops to ask the developers about it with regards to the complaint that witch covers too broad of a term is kind of futile, because looking back it's apparent that he actually did that already (with regards to Arms of the Chosen), and the answer there wasn't good enough for him either, so... not really much of anywhere else to go from there, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T10:42:02-08:00","id":1269610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269413#post1269413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the tl;dr is that the witch business seems like an ill-fitting, 11th-hour change of nomenclature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grabowski was <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/IfTheLunarsWin\" target=\"_blank\">comparing Lunars to Baba Yaga back in the days of First Edition.</a> There's nothing eleventh hour about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T10:42:34-08:00","id":1269611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269456#post1269456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how successful the Lunars have been at bleeding the Realm and running it to ground, I find I really have to question the Sidereal\u2019s decision to embark on the Usurpation back then. Or, at least, I have to wonder how Chejop is still managing to say \u201cEverything is fine. This is good.\u201d even several centuries ago when it should have become fairly clear that the Lunars are slowly winning.<br /> <br /> I mean, from everything we\u2019ve been hearing about the Lunars it seems like the general reaction to \u201cWe\u2019re going to drive them off to the edge of the World where they\u2019ll simply wither away and die\u201d is that the guy saying that plan should have had a hard time keeping a straight face before everyone breaks down laughing and then someone says \u201cno, seriously, what are we actually gonna do about the Lunars?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hold the line while waiting for the wind to change&quot; is a risky strategy despite its conservatism, but it isn't necessarily fundamentally unsound. It was, after all, the early Silver Pact's predominant approach during the middle to late Shogunate, when the Wyld Hunt was often more powerful and pervasive than even at the Scarlet Realm's height. Things didn't turn in the Silver Pact's favor (even by its own elders' estimation) until the Contagion struck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T11:08:10-08:00","id":1269620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269604#post1269604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As opposed to Lunars, who will have a Charm to haunt people's nightmares in Strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot about that.<br /> Obviously we haven't seen the tree leading up to it, we just know the prerequisite is called Terrifying Predator Consumption.<br /> <br /> I wondered if it was at the top of some kind of fear tree, or maybe a tree about gaining forms (though I wouldn't think that'd be very long).<br /> <br /> Anyway, the charm is interesting, because it shows that the warrior/trickster/shaman thing is a bit through all castes: Full Moon attributes are primarily about being strong, tough, fast... but they have some shamanic stuff like dream-hunting in as well. I'd expected that shamanic themes would be pretty much just a Mental Attributes thing. But I can see Trickery in Wits, Warrior-stuff in Charisma (war-charms are apparently in Charisma, Manipulation and Intelligence), etc.<br /> <br /> And that diverges a bit from the core parts of the attribute; obviously haunting someone's nightmares isn't a straightforward extrapolation of Strength.<br /> <br /> Solars have this as well; summoning a sword out of light isn't a straightforward extrapolation of being really good at swordsmanship. But I wonder if Lunars have a bit more of this, especially as there only 9 attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T11:10:50-08:00","id":1269621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269611#post1269611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hold the line while waiting for the wind to change&quot; is a risky strategy despite its conservatism, but it isn't necessarily fundamentally unsound. It was, after all, the early Silver Pact's predominant approach during the middle to late Shogunate, when the Wyld Hunt was often more powerful and pervasive than even at the Scarlet Realm's height. Things didn't turn in the Silver Pact's favor (even by its own elders' estimation) until the Contagion struck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there goes my idea of imagining a lot of the woes besetting the Shogunate as portrayed in the Aspect books (such as economic crisis caused by widespread death in sheep herds, right before a forecasted as terrible winter) being the result of Lunar work, that the whole thing was teetering on collapse, and that the Contagion and resulting Raksha invasion actually set the Lunars <i>back</i> by a significant degree by killing a lot of them, scattering the rest, and letting the remains of their enemies reconstitute with shored up defences and shorter interior lines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T11:17:22-08:00","id":1269622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269456#post1269456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how successful the Lunars have been at bleeding the Realm and running it to ground, I find I really have to question the Sidereal\u2019s decision to embark on the Usurpation back then. Or, at least, I have to wonder how Chejop is still managing to say \u201cEverything is fine. This is good.\u201d even several centuries ago when it should have become fairly clear that the Lunars are slowly winning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a couple ways to address this without making the Bronze Faction Sidereals look like <i>total </i>idiots (the explanations still involve some willful self-delusion, but hopefully not more than any other type of character could get into).<br /> <br /> First, you can assume that the Vision of Bronze was very high-level, showing the whole &quot;Creation is greatly diminished but survives&quot;, but without showing much exact details, and the Sidereals just assumed that they'd always be in charge. The Vision could still be correct, but the Sids' assumption about who'd eventually be in command is simply wrong - Creation will still survive, even if it won't regain the heights of the First Age, under Lunar stewardship.<br /> <br /> Second, you can assume that the Sidereals <i>did</i> predict the eventual fall of the Dragonbloods to the Lunars, and simply assumed that they'd be able to transition from being the power behind the Dragonbloods' throne to being the power behind the Lunar throne. This might not even be <i>too</i> grossly arrogant an assumption. The Lunars' feud appears to mostly be with the Realm and the Dragonbloods, not the Sidereals per se. Sure, the Lunar eldars seem to know that the Sids were neck-deep in the Usurpation, and they've no doubt explained to the youngsters that Sidereal fate-manipulation is very helpful to Wyld Hunts, but for most younger Lunars, Dragonbloods are still likely the face of their enemy, not Sidereals. If, when the Realm looks like it's finally going to fall in the next century or so, the Sidereals stop helping the Dragonbloods altogether, they might stand a chance of making an offer to assist the Lunars once they become the new power in Creation, counting on the pragmatism of the younger Lunars to ensure they're not just turned down flat (possibly literally). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T11:18:17-08:00","id":1269623,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling that this is an actual preview of a Lunar Linguistics Protean Charm. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">(in other words, I'm flat lost in this thread but excited to see what's coming)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T11:26:03-08:00","id":1269628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269620#post1269620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Jeez, I think it's been one of the most interesting things previewed so far. Not even for its implications, just for what it does and what it can mean for how a Lunar operates.<br /> <br /> I've got to imagine that Leviathan has a library of shapes arising from his terrifying reputation across the Western ocean; lot of people having nightmares of having their boats shattered and being swallowed up by giant orcas out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, the charm is interesting, because it shows that the warrior/trickster/shaman thing is a bit through all castes: Full Moon attributes are primarily about being strong, tough, fast... but they have some shamanic stuff like dream-hunting in as well. I'd expected that shamanic themes would be pretty much just a Mental Attributes thing. But I can see Trickery in Wits, Warrior-stuff in Charisma (war-charms are apparently in Charisma, Manipulation and Intelligence), etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I were saying! Also, the Totem Keyword, allowing for even more cross-pollination; if you're a wolf shaped Full Moon, commanding battle groups is Strength Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that diverges a bit from the core parts of the attribute; obviously haunting someone's nightmares isn't a straightforward extrapolation of Strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, since I brought it up, I'm gonna be perfectly, 100% honest... I see some similarities in a few previewed Charms to some of the TAW stuff, and I don't really see that as a bad thing. I think that's a good direction to go in, and if it represents a change in course with a change in developers, I see this as the better one. I actually think that harping too closely on the physicality stuff was a shortcoming of the prior descriptions.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I've had reason this past year to re-evaluate quite a few things about the prior development team, but that's something to talk about another time, if at all. For the sake of this topic, I'll just say that I now think they weren't really conducting themselves the best as the TAW stuff went.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that I think everything from that fan project should find its way into the published Lunars, I'm just laying my cards on the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars have this as well; summoning a sword out of light isn't a straightforward extrapolation of being really good at swordsmanship. But I wonder if Lunars have a bit more of this, especially as there only 9 attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of some conversations over on RPG.Net about Solars that talked about the shortcomings of speaking strictly in terms of good skill, with one person laying out how it's more accurate to describe in terms of high skill, iconic tricks and feats from various kinds of heroic figures from myth, literature and some pop culture, rounded out a bit with some divine sunlight and golden fire imagery.<br /> <br /> As that pertains to Lunars... well, moonlight doesn't really have the literary cachet of sunlight and fire, but it <i>does</i> have association with certain kinds of mysticism, and really the closest analogue in Lunars to the gross physical manifestations is probably in the shapechanging itself anyway. Point is, in practical terms, it would probably need to encompass more things than just one thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T12:24:43-08:00","id":1269640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269621#post1269621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there goes my idea of imagining a lot of the woes besetting the Shogunate as portrayed in the Aspect books (such as economic crisis caused by widespread death in sheep herds, right before a forecasted as terrible winter) being the result of Lunar work, that the whole thing was teetering on collapse, and that the Contagion and resulting Raksha invasion actually set the Lunars <i>back</i> by a significant degree by killing a lot of them, scattering the rest, and letting the remains of their enemies reconstitute with shored up defences and shorter interior lines. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that the Lunars were ineffectual at the time, any more than the Sidereals are ineffectual now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T12:41:51-08:00","id":1269646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269640#post1269640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that the Lunars were ineffectual at the time, any more than the Sidereals are ineffectual now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it's still a far cry from &quot;they were just a few decades off from being ready to land a death blow, before the Contagion interrupted them and threw them off&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T20:52:39-08:00","id":1269735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269606#post1269606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wait... even the trajectory of telling Saur Ops to ask the developers about it with regards to the complaint that witch covers too broad of a term is kind of futile, because looking back it's apparent that he actually did that already (with regards to Arms of the Chosen), and the answer there wasn't good enough for him either, so... not really much of anywhere else to go from there, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of my animosity and confusion is quite genuine. All the references still don't line up in my point of view, and likely still wouldn't even if a bunch of people didn't name a fan project &quot;Terrible Argent Witches&quot; after razzing on me, personally, in threads about various Lunar topics such as the spirit shape back in 2012. Well, the insults were a bit more serious than that, but I would have left it there, had Revlid not decided back after new year's 2015 to revisit many of the same topics in a couple of attack posts on the GITP mega thread because I dared to voice issues with TAW.<br /> <br /> And then Revlid got hired as a freelancer to work on Lunars, so there's no staying in a different part of the community and ignoring him. So there's that to consider, too, but I think I'm edging up on a ban for talking about that on this forum. I might as well try to quit Exalted again like in July... not that it worked very well, as you can tell from the fact that I eventually came back. There's no landing zone for that launch; just crashing back into the pad. In any case, apologies for not divulging that sooner, but my head is not in a good place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Grabowski was </span></span></span><a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Thus_Spake_Zargrabowski/IfTheLunarsWin\" target=\"_blank\">comparing Lunars to Baba Yaga back in the days of First Edition.</a><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> There's nothing eleventh hour about it.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> That was in tandem with a reference to Old Man Spider, so it still didn't and doesn't click in my head. It was also jarring to me at the time he made it because of the longtime &quot;claim&quot; on the character held by V:tM, and this was back around 2002. It's still jarring to me that it sticks with other people, because first edition Lunars were reportedly the very essence of 11th hour design changes, a lack of any sort of structure or outline, and other various issues, like the method of producing beastfolk.<br /> <br /> But if that's the direction, I guess that's the direction.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T22:55:04-08:00","id":1269759,"title":"","content":"&quot;This person wrote this fanwork&quot; and &quot;this person will work on a project that repudates part of that fanwork&quot; aren't actually opposed ideas.<br /> <br /> Consider how Ex3's core repudates the Yozis as actors, magitech as an everyday thing, and tries to reinsert mystery into the setting... and was written by two of the writers who were significant factors in the perception of charm-robot Primordials, the Sun as a spaceship, and the explain ALL THE THINGS trend of late 2e.<br /> <br /> I don't like TAW. But neither was it waste and dross. Part of the Lunar theme is embracing seeming contradictions, and the TAW theme of &quot;I *am* the monster in the darkness&quot; works well there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T00:27:20-08:00","id":1269763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269646#post1269646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but it's still a far cry from &quot;they were just a few decades off from being ready to land a death blow, before the Contagion interrupted them and threw them off&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As we all know, many people in 2nd ed complained that Lunars seemed really ineffectual in the setting, just losing to the Sidereals and Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> That's why the new direction is that the Lunars are actually winning (if very slowly).<br /> <br /> But at the same time, you don't want to do the opposite and have the Dragonblood look totally ineffectual. (One of my playgroup often complained that, as far as he was concerned, the setting fiction always made the Dragonblood look kind of rubbish.)<br /> <br /> So, the Dragonblood were winning for the first 500 years (or however long the Shogunate ends up being), but then have been declining for the next 800-ish years while the Lunars push them back (overall; obviously there's a back-and-forth dynamic), seems more balanced.<br /> <br /> The Lunars are on the long road to victory now; but there was a time when they were doing really badly and the Dragonblood had conquered most of the world. Just as Solars can look back at the High First Age as a time of Solar greatness, Dragonblood should be able to look back at their golden age, the Shogunate.*<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that the Lunars can't have been partially behind the late Shogunate's economic decline and political infighting.<br /> <br /> But I don't think &quot;the Lunars almost defeated the Dragonblood 800 years ago, but then the Dragonblood escaped their trap and became really powerful again so the Lunars have had to spend another 800 years grinding them down&quot; quite works, for either Lunars or Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Of course, the Shogunate had a lot of problems. Just like the High First Age. It doesn't have to be perfect, but it does have to be good enough to take the place in the setting of &quot;lost golden age&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-22-2018, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T00:48:42-08:00","id":1269766,"title":"","content":"On the debate points about &quot;witches&quot;; I would offer that:<br /> <br /> Baba-Yaga to me seems to be mentioned in early Lunar discussions by Grabowski that offered up other figures who were tricksters and monsters (Old Man Spider), not witches specifically. (I find Saur Ops has said this, now that my post is wrote!). So I'm a bit with the folk who see it as not particularly an early thing, though I think that's fine and every edition changes. <br /> <br /> On Terrifying Argent Witches, I will speak a bit more. They may have been inspired by comments from previous devs, but ended up with some shade from former developers because it hewed to a template of being derivative of the Infernal Exalted, which those devs had come to believe was a mistake. Though the developers didn't speak much of them. <br /> <br /> I believe (though there is some degree of interpretation here) the &quot;bad&quot; derivative elements of Infernals: Their strongly purely thematically bound trees (not structured around human heroic actions through abilities and attributes). The malevolence their powers had bundled up into them. Their removal of choice about how to act from and how to characterize their PC from players hands and placing it into the Charm mechanics (buying more Charms sort of a process of becoming more of an inhuman thing). Their often hugely overwritten structure. Their &quot;symbolic mechanics&quot;. Most tentatively, perhaps they way they imply that &quot;edgy&quot; heroes who must do evil acts for the good of all are the best that you can get (as opposed to the good people who must do bad things you sometimes find along the moral spectrum in other splats, where those bad things emerge more organically from their social context, circumstances and human limitations, which seems to me more true to life).<br /> <br /> All from Infernals (and anyway I have spoken of this elsewhere enough that it's not useful and probably unwanted to regurgitate it again).<br /> <br /> This is less about whether &quot;witches&quot; is a good theme and more about &quot;Don't do it like TAW&quot; though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T01:18:22-08:00","id":1269767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269611#post1269611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Hold the line while waiting for the wind to change&amp;quot; is a risky strategy despite its conservatism, but it isn't necessarily fundamentally unsound. It was, after all, the early Silver Pact's predominant approach during the middle to late Shogunate, when the Wyld Hunt was often more powerful and pervasive than even at the Scarlet Realm's height. Things didn't turn in the Silver Pact's favor (even by its own elders' estimation) until the Contagion struck.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me think we should stumble upon various projects and ideas to the Lunar issue. After all it\u2019s not wise to have the Exalts whose population can grow or shrink be the rivals to the consistently 400 strong warmonsters. So I imagine they brainstormed and funded several projects. Like have the Exigents reinstated to act as foils to the Lunars. Trick the Lunars into some other world. Convert a sizable number of Lunars to your side or at least against the others so they are large enough to always train replacements. Lunar soul cages. Or even Creation of new Exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T02:35:35-08:00","id":1269775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269763#post1269763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As we all know, many people in 2nd ed complained that Lunars seemed really ineffectual in the setting, just losing to the Sidereals and Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> That's why the new direction is that the Lunars are actually winning (if very slowly).<br /> <br /> But at the same time, you don't want to do the opposite and have the Dragonblood look totally ineffectual. (One of my playgroup often complained that, as far as he was concerned, the setting fiction always made the Dragonblood look kind of rubbish.)<br /> <br /> So, the Dragonblood were winning for the first 500 years (or however long the Shogunate ends up being), but then have been declining for the next 800-ish years while the Lunars push them back (overall; obviously there's a back-and-forth dynamic), seems more balanced.<br /> <br /> The Lunars are on the long road to victory now; but there was a time when they were doing really badly and the Dragonblood had conquered most of the world. Just as Solars can look back at the High First Age as a time of Solar greatness, Dragonblood should be able to look back at their golden age, the Shogunate.*<br /> <br /> This isn't to say that the Lunars can't have been partially behind the late Shogunate's economic decline and political infighting.<br /> <br /> But I don't think &quot;the Lunars almost defeated the Dragonblood 800 years ago, but then the Dragonblood escaped their trap and became really powerful again so the Lunars have had to spend another 800 years grinding them down&quot; quite works, for either Lunars or Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Of course, the Shogunate had a lot of problems. Just like the High First Age. It doesn't have to be perfect, but it does have to be good enough to take the place in the setting of &quot;lost golden age&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is that the first significant things that I ever read about the Shogunate were some very interesting posts that Holden wrote about the interesting ways in which it was gradually falling apart, and I read the Records of the Before chapters of the Aspect books in that light (not that it's much of a stretch, if any), and my perspective is too heavily shaped in having been strongly compelled by that image of the Shogunate as a thing that was very glorious in its manner of decaying. There's something operatic to it.<br /> <br /> I do find that you misread me when you talk about Lunars being <b>behind</b> the Shogunate's political infighting; part of what makes the image so compelling to me is that they were perfectly, enthusiastically capable of that on their own. More that they harassed it, exacerbated it, and were waiting in the margins to rush in and finish it off when it had spent so long exhausting itself. The Shogunate was prey that very obligingly insisted on biting and clawing at itself, and just needed the occasional fly to buzz in and nip at it to make it a bit more furious in the right spots, until it was too tired to fight back.<br /> <br /> I don't think that necessarily made the Dragon Blooded look bad conceptually, if the process consisted of multiple groups of Dragon Blooded very effectively and impressively tearing one another apart (as well as grandiose wars against frequently invading Fair Folk and Lunars).<br /> <br /> I think to say that it had problems just because things do is to bely the significance of how things transitioned into a world wide military government.<br /> <br /> I mean, hell, I'm not saying that the Lunars were the ones who came up with the idea that there can only be one shogun. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T02:55:26-08:00","id":1269779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269735#post1269735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's that to consider, too, but I think I'm edging up on a ban for talking about that on this forum.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've never known anyone get banned for that. It's taken into account if someone's using what's been said on other forums to troll this one or using it to harass somebody. But most likely you'll simply be asked not to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might as well try to quit Exalted again like in July... not that it worked very well, as you can tell from the fact that I eventually came back.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry to hear that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T16:54:12-08:00","id":1269933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269611#post1269611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things didn't turn in the Silver Pact's favor (even by its own elders' estimation) until the Contagion struck.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s what I figured. Actually I\u2019ve been going further and assuming it took until a few centuries after the Contagion once the Treshold had recovered enough for the Pact to have anything to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T18:22:07-08:00","id":1269954,"title":"","content":"I guess that it all clicks for me because, as different as the various concepts are, they\u2019re all united as \u201cthe monster in the wild.\u201d The Dragon, Grendle, the Wolfman, Baba Yaga, they\u2019re all outsiders, wild and dangerous. <br /> <br /> And....well, as others have noted, if Lunars just have Shapeshifting and Animals, it\u2019s hard to come up with thematic angles for the mental charms. You could go with the \u201cAnimal Totem\u201d route and define, say, the Owl as Wise and the Cat as Curious, and so on and then build charms that fit those concepts, but then you\u2019re saying \u201cOwls embody wisdom\u201d as a fundamental aspect of the setting\u2019s metaphysics and kind of turning Lunars into a collection of the Fera, instead of shapeshifters who can be anything.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, without some unifying vision for the Lunars, mental charms become a random grab bag of effects that don\u2019t feel connected to the rest of the charmset (and possibly even each other). So there needs to be some unifying theme.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, I get that \u201cDark and Creepy\u201d overlaps a bunch with Abyssals....and potentially Liminals and Infernals and maybe a few others too. I\u2019m not sure how they\u2019re gonna separate Abyssal \u201cDark and Creepy\u201d from Lunar \u201cDark and Creepy\u201d but... to be honest, I kinda feel like Abyssal and Lunar charms should overlap to some degree. I mean, the Moon and the Night go together, both splats tend to do the \u201cblood drinking monster\u201d thing, there should be some overlap. That said, there should also be a difference. The Moon is not the Night. A difference in mechanics, in how core things are to the charmset, and a bunch of other factors can serve to make the Lunars feel distinct from anyone else with similar abilities, including Sorcerers. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m hopeful that they\u2019ll do a good job explaining to us how those distinctions work in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T23:10:46-08:00","id":1270016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269954#post1269954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess that it all clicks for me because, as different as the various concepts are, they\u2019re all united as \u201cthe monster in the wild.\u201d The Dragon, Grendle, the Wolfman, Baba Yaga, they\u2019re all outsiders, wild and dangerous.<br /> <br /> And....well, as others have noted, if Lunars just have Shapeshifting and Animals, it\u2019s hard to come up with thematic angles for the mental charms. You could go with the \u201cAnimal Totem\u201d route and define, say, the Owl as Wise and the Cat as Curious, and so on and then build charms that fit those concepts, but then you\u2019re saying \u201cOwls embody wisdom\u201d as a fundamental aspect of the setting\u2019s metaphysics and kind of turning Lunars into a collection of the Fera, instead of shapeshifters who can be anything.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, without some unifying vision for the Lunars, mental charms become a random grab bag of effects that don\u2019t feel connected to the rest of the charmset (and possibly even each other). So there needs to be some unifying theme.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, I get that \u201cDark and Creepy\u201d overlaps a bunch with Abyssals....and potentially Liminals and Infernals and maybe a few others too. I\u2019m not sure how they\u2019re gonna separate Abyssal \u201cDark and Creepy\u201d from Lunar \u201cDark and Creepy\u201d but... to be honest, I kinda feel like Abyssal and Lunar charms should overlap to some degree. I mean, the Moon and the Night go together, both splats tend to do the \u201cblood drinking monster\u201d thing, there should be some overlap. That said, there should also be a difference. The Moon is not the Night. A difference in mechanics, in how core things are to the charmset, and a bunch of other factors can serve to make the Lunars feel distinct from anyone else with similar abilities, including Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m hopeful that they\u2019ll do a good job explaining to us how those distinctions work in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Lunars aren't werewolves (either pop-culture or WoD-style), and Abyssals aren't vampires, I suggest that's the core of the difference. Lunars are dark and creepy in the way nature is dark and creepy, red in tooth and claw. Abyssals are dark in creepy in the way <i>death</i> is dark and creepy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T02:07:17-08:00","id":1270052,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think it's pretty easy to differentiate between the creepy witch of the woods and a Lich.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s what I figured. Actually I\u2019ve been going further and assuming it took until a few centuries after the Contagion once the Treshold had recovered enough for the Pact to have anything to work with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh, scattered survivors living in a post-apocalyptic wasteland of marauding hobgoblins and hungry ghosts with basically no government whatsoever... is probably a good time for the Lunars, because that's much more to their advantage than it is to Dragonblood or Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Dragonblood take years from Exaltation to being ready to be an adventuring hero, because Exaltation isn't going to be enough to take down a pack of Hobgoblins when you've only just started puberty. So they need a certain amount of institutional support. Not a ton, but some. Also, because they're bred not chosen (except according to some theologians), the more Dragonblood you have, the more you can produce. Therefore the less you have (because 80% of them died in the last few years), the less you can produce.<br /> <br /> Also, one key advantage of the Dragonblood is that they can get pretty much as much power out of Jade weapons and armour as a Solar. But making Jade artefacts takes time, mining Jade needs infrastructure, and even scavenging places where Dragonblood may have lost their weapons when they fell to the Crusade requires maps, a search party, exorcists to ward off hungry ghosts, etc.<br /> It's not necessarily extremely hard, but it does require some organisation.<br /> <br /> Sidereals also take years to produce. When a Sidereal dies, it will be 15-30 years before another one is ready.<br /> And it's difficult to manipulate society by making sure the right people are in the right place at the right time (or the right people die) when there's basically no society. The easiest way to manipulate a lot of people is to manipulate their government; with no government, you have to manipulate them individually.<br /> <br /> <br /> Whereas when a young scavenger in the ruins of a Shogunate City is surrounded by a pack of Hungry Ghosts and Exalts, she's ready to turn into a huge magic bear and rip them up <i>right now</i>. A post-apocalyptic wasteland of ruined cities, monsters, bandits, warlords and tribes gone feral is no big deal for a Lunar.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I imagine is something like this:<br /> <br /> The Usurpation happens. Many Lunars die, others flee.<br /> The Lunars fight back in a guerilla insurgency. But they're massively outnumbered by organised legions with powerful artefacts who are already in control of society at multiple levels, and their masters who foresee when and where the Lunars will strike.<br /> The Lunars reshape themselves, abandoning their castes and forming the Silver Pact. They become more successful, exacerbating tensions between Daimyos, stoking the fires of civil war... but they're still living in a world almost entirely controlled by their enemies. While the Dragonblood don't cooperate well, they do unite when they need to, to kill Lunars. Not all Lunars try to burn down the Shogunate, some prefer to rule isolated communities on the very edge of the world, or pursue other aims in secret.<br /> Civil war wracks the Shogunate. The Lunars lurk in the shadows, weakening their foes. They slowly grind down the number of experienced Sidereals, but also lose many of their own leaders.<br /> They're 400 against the world, and they're losing. Silver Pact leaders believe that if they can make civil war so perpetual that the Shogunate's unified anti-Lunar culture breaks down, they might be able to seize territory and have Daimyos ignore it. They do acquire territory in the more isolated parts of the world, but much of humanity is still under the control of Daimyos and their Wyld Hunts. Anti-Lunar propaganda has seeped into the consciousness of humans across the world, even those of whom the Daimyos' control is more de jure than de facto.<br /> <br /> The Contagion happens. Most Dragonblood die. So do most Lunars, but they're reborn in battle against the Balorian Crusade. Many die to the Fae Horde, but more rise to take their place. When the Crusade ends, the Dragonblood legions are shattered and broken. But the Lunars, while most are young, still stand at twenty-score veterans of the Crusade.<br /> <br /> Across the world, lesser scions of the Daimyos claim their right to rule Provinces... and die at the hands of the Lunars. Only the Blessed Isle, and a few other places like Dehelesen, are too strong for the Lunars to bring down. But in the North, the South, the West and the East, the remnants of the Shogunate are smothered into nothing. Dragonblood wielding their great-aunts' daiklaives and wearing their great-grandmother's armour, and the callow youth of their ancestral guard, die at the hands of the feral children of dead cities, led by beast-gods out of nightmare.<br /> <br /> For a hundred years, the remnants of the Shogunate are ground to nothing, until to the grand-daughters of apocalypse, it's ancient dead history. In Coral the Daimyo's palace is a temple of Siakal; in Chiaroscoro its a market; in Great Forks housing for a hundred tribesmen who don't even know what it was; in Thorns it houses a popular brothel. Only a few isolated cities maintain the traditions of hundreds of years of their ancestors: Prasad, Cherak, Lookshy.<br /> <br /> But on the Blessed Isle survivors and refugees have united under the Scarlet Empress, who has declared a new Realm. 10,000 Dragons are nothing to the strength of the Shogunate; but they're enough. On great ships the massed legions of Creation's safest continent attack the North, the South, the East. An-Teng, Thorns, Chiaroscoro, the Lap, Cherak, Pneuma, Medo, the Caul... soon they control the coastlines of two continents. The Lunars manage to stop them from making much progress in-land, but there are exceptions, such as Prasad, Linowan and Greyfalls. <br /> <br /> In every direction, 400 Lunars battle 10,000 Dragons. The Realm expands and contracts, expands and contracts, allying with other Shogunate remnants like Cherak and Prasad, but the Lunars can't stop its rise to power. But it hits a peak; as the Realm expands, it gets weaker under its own weight, it takes more effort to maintain the ambitions of a rising number of powerful Dragonblood. The Lunars change tactics, get more experienced. After hundreds of years, they become confident; perhaps they're winning? Then, the great victory in the Caul; in a co-ordinated Silver Pact campaign, the Dragonblood are driven out of four sacred cities. Their armies unite in the last city, Faxai. Lunars now control almost all of the Caul. <br /> <br /> Now the Lunars are confident. It may take another hundred years, but the momentum is with them. Their tactics, their War Dominions, are working. Lunars are dying to Wyld Hunts less and less, growing more and more experienced. The Realm mostly just controls the coasts. Driving them back to the Blessed Isle is in sight. It was reborn after the Contagion, but after over a thousand years, Dragonblood civilisation totters. And <i>soon Kejak will die</i>. It is foreseen. The leader of the enemy is almost dead, and there's no clear successor. <br /> <br /> And then, suddenly, the Solars are back. But it seems a lot of them, somehow tainted, now serve the Deathlords, pushing those ancient ghosts from a minor threat to a major one. And the Empress appears to be... just gone. Will she return? Is she dead? No-one knows, and a Realm civil war is imminent. <br /> Should the Silver Pact maintain its tactics?<br /> Or should they form one giant co-ordinated campaign, and in 4 or 5 years strike? Could they drive the Realm out of the Threshold, not in 100 years, but 10?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T02:29:04-08:00","id":1270057,"title":"","content":"To put it a different way:<br /> <br /> The Shogunate is the Roman Republic and the Principate. It has civil wars, it has periods of dictatorship and murder. Sulla, Julius Caesar, etc. And the barbarians have their Teutoburg Forest. But Rome is powerful, and massive. There are periods when the whole Empire is split amongst feuding generals, but it still stays strong. The barbarians are no great threat.<br /> <br /> The Contagion/Balorian Crusade is the Crisis of the Third Century and the Barbarian invasions of the West, in the 4th and 5th.<br /> Civil war+famine+barbarian invasion almost makes Rome fall... but it doesn't. It survives, but only in the East.<br /> <br /> The first period of the Realm is Eastern Rome (aka the Byzantine Empire) circa 300-700 AD.<br /> The Eastern Roman Empire survives. The West falls. Rome survives in a weakened form. It expands in a series of brutal wars; taking parts of Italy, Egypt, eventually taking back the Middle East. But it's inconsistent. The Vandals seize North Africa.<br /> <br /> But all that war exhausts it. The barbarians slowly become more powerful, more organised. They rise, in the desert, in the forests, on the steppes. Constantinople slowly loses more and more of Italy to the Lombards. Wars with Persia devastate its easternmost lands. Then comes the desert horde, taking Egypt, Palestine, Algeria, Syria. The horse nomads from the great plains take Anatolia, the men of the north-east forests swarm over Dalmatia.<br /> <br /> The Eastern Roman Empire is still rich. Its still powerful. It controls many territories. Its still a major world power with a huge population, but it has lost momentum.<br /> <br /> But then comes the Civil War.<br /> <br /> And that's when the barbarians* invade and the whole thing falls apart, leaving just a few isolated rump states.<br /> <br /> *I'm referring to the French. And a few Italians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T02:41:12-08:00","id":1270061,"title":"","content":"I suppose I could also say the Solar Deliberative is the Han, the Shogunate is the Six Dynasties, and the Realm is the Southern Song (because barbarians control the North), and the Lunars want to go full Yuan and, as Grabowski said, turn half the cities into grazing pastures, but I don't think it quite works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T15:37:56-08:00","id":1270206,"title":"","content":"Very thought provoking analogies. Not surprisingly for me, they do bring out a slightly critical line of thought (might be right, might be wrong, putting it out there as food for thought).<br /> <br /> In the prior editions you had a Realm and the Sidereals as basically defined by internal conflict - factions, Houses. So that's why, even though they're the Powers That Be and masters of the world, they're somewhat ill prepared and flat footed when the Solars return at the same time as they have a leadership crisis. Then this is what sets the scene for the game as it is - defunded Wyld Hunt, Houses withdrawing their legions to the isle, etc.<br /> <br /> They're like that fundamentally because they can afford to be like that - they've faced no real long term external threats that motivate them to unite, and they've only an empire that has waxed and expanded and succeeded and never, ever been on the backfoot. It's &quot;decadence&quot;.<br /> <br /> But that kind of infighting is harder for me to think about if it's obviously the case that there's this huge external foe out there, recognizably a coherent entity, that's slowly but palpably gaining ground. <br /> <br /> You, in a House, don't fight the other House, you go out and kill the common enemy that will burn both your possessions to ash. You, as the Empress, don't allow, much less create and support political structures that create infighting in to preserve your own rule, if they weaken you such that an external enemy will wipe you out in a hundred years - you make the necessary reforms and do away with wasteful internal competition, as to do anything else would be to ignore the immediate threat (the external enemy) to avoid the less immediate one (insurrection). Sidereals don't worry so much about whether they support Solars or Dragonblooded, but about an enemy that would destroy the entire ability of the Bureau of Fate to function in world as the preserver of human civilization at all. That's what your politics will *all* be about because it's *the* existential threat. (They especially do this if they're the greatest predictionists in the world who have a tendency to look at the long term).<br /> <br /> This isn't a stance on whether the Lunars should or should not pose the sort of threat and the Realm be in the sort of long term decline that kind of comes through in some of the posts above. I'm just questioning and wondering aloud really on whether it feels a bit like there's a bit of a combination of a Dragonblooded and Sidereal politics predicted on the absence of a significant external threat, and an empire that's on the expanse and knows no challenge (what largely was in 1e and 2e), and a building of heat for Lunars as actually a much more successful challenger making that a declining empire (3e's Lunars), as bits that don't really quite fit perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T22:33:18-08:00","id":1270286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270206#post1270206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that kind of infighting is harder for me to think about if it's obviously the case that there's this huge external foe out there, recognizably a coherent entity, that's slowly but palpably gaining ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it appropriate for Wizard to compare the Realm to the Southern Song, considering what that polity did when first made aware of the growing activity of the Mongols.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You, in a House, don't fight the other House, you go out and kill the common enemy that will burn both your possessions to ash.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fine principle in the abstract, but can feel a bit hard to maintain if there aren't enough strong examples to bring it home and your neighbour is still right over there being a dick.<br /> <br /> As Eric has kind of alluded to earlier in the thread, smart Lunars avoided doing things that would make their threat feel very immediate and visceral in a manner that would make the Dragon Blooded feel a lot more unified and galvanize them to take action en masse.<br /> <br /> There's also something to be said for the idea that everybody agrees with unity in principle, but are still fighting over who is going to be in charge (and are too heavily conditioned to accept something more parliamentary without a lot more pushing).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You, as the Empress, don't allow, much less create and support political structures that create infighting in to preserve your own rule, if they weaken you such that an external enemy will wipe you out in a hundred years - you make the necessary reforms and do away with wasteful internal competition, as to do anything else would be to ignore the immediate threat (the external enemy) to avoid the less immediate one (insurrection).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure precisely how the Thousand Hazy Paths will be framed this time around, but I think there's room for a system in which the Empress could carefully balance keeping divisions of power and personality within the Dynasty to prevent anybody from becoming big enough to challenge her, and being able to leverage their collective strength against Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Especially if a lot of Lunars were ready to take the long road of bleeding the Realm slowly and letting its own complacency and internal issues help their goals along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals don't worry so much about whether they support Solars or Dragonblooded, but about an enemy that would destroy the entire ability of the Bureau of Fate to function in world as the preserver of human civilization at all. That's what your politics will *all* be about because it's *the* existential threat. (They especially do this if they're the greatest predictionists in the world who have a tendency to look at the long term).</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly suspect that the Sidereals will maintain the general byline of having too many things to deal with and not enough resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just questioning and wondering aloud really on whether it feels a bit like there's a bit of a combination of a Dragonblooded and Sidereal politics predicted on the absence of a significant external threat, and an empire that's on the expanse and knows no challenge (what largely was in 1e and 2e), and a building of heat for Lunars as actually a much more successful challenger making that a declining empire (3e's Lunars), as bits that don't really quite fit perfectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>And finally I'll note that among the ways in which What Fire Has Wrought has shaken up the Scarlet Dynasty a bit is by focusing on the manner in which several Houses have organized around consistent responses to external threats and have profited by it, have disputes based on differing approaches and ideals for it, and in at least one case might have been damned by it.<br /> <br /> Houses Cathak and Peleps are militarily very powerful, in a manner that creates complications around the question of exactly whom that power will serve.<br /> <br /> None of this is particularly unrealistic. It's the kind of counterproductive internal politicking and fighting that has occurred for numerous powers, with or without external enemies, throughout human history, and continuing in certain forms to the present day. One can't even say being in a total war situation is something that will get a society and its leaders to straighten up and fly right, because while that worked a lot more for each of the Allies (and to a lesser extent, between the three big ones, although even that was a tenuous thing that could have easily fallen apart with the right pressures; Churchill freaking hated communism, and could be less than discrete about that in meetings with Stalin, regardless of the benefits of cooperation with the USSR), it was quite a shitshow for the Germans.<br /> <br /> That and it's written that way because people pulling apart when they ought to be drawing together is one of the key conflicts and tragedies of the setting, and has a background of compelling conflict. Like, on the grounds of being thematic and facilitating gameplay alone, it wouldn't particularly need to be realistic.<br /> <br /> It just is, almost distressingly so, as an added benefit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T01:34:49-08:00","id":1270293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it appropriate for Wizard to compare the Realm to the Southern Song, considering what that polity did when first made aware of the growing activity of the Mongols.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! <br /> <br /> One of the reasons I didn't write so much about the Chinese example is I'm not so familiar with it. I mostly know they allied with the Mongols against the Jin; did they also fight each other over what to do?<br /> <br /> (I wanted to do an American example; like the Shogunate was the Mayans, the Realm is the Aztecs but they love Mayans instead of Toltecs, and the Lunars are the Spanish, taking advantage of the Aztecs' angry subjects to conquer Central America and destroy the Aztecs' religion and rule. But again, it's not an area of history I know a ton about. Still, it inspires me to read more.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Eric has kind of alluded to earlier in the thread, smart Lunars avoided doing things that would make their threat feel very immediate and visceral in a manner that would make the Dragon Blooded feel a lot more unified and galvanize them to take action en masse.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder, Ghosthead has pointed out that it seems counter-productive for the Empress to encourage division if the Lunars are going to win in a hundred years.<br /> But I'm thinking:<br /> a)Maybe she set that system up when the Realm was in its earlier expansionist phase, and can't change it now<br /> b)It's the only way she can see to stay in power, so what choice does she have?<br /> c)The Dragonblood don't know they're losing.<br /> <br /> Or at least, until they recently lost the Caul and the Tepet Legions, they didn't know they were losing. So we're talking shortly before the Scarlet Empress vanished.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... I suppose that the point is, as you say, to &quot;build heat&quot; for the Lunars. So you don't want to make this too small. But maybe, in their arrogance, the Dragonblood of, say, 100 years ago (I wouldn't want to say the Lunars were winning 300 years ago), didn't realise the tide was beginning to turn? Maybe it wasn't obvious to most, but only the hyper-intelligent strategists of the Silver Pact?<br /> I don't know, that's a difficult one.<br /> <br /> Essentially, it's very difficult to:<br /> Make Dragonblood look awesome<br /> Make the Realm look scary and powerful<br /> Make its enemies, the Lunars, also look awesome, scary and powerful<br /> <br /> Saying this, I actually don't think it's necessary for the Lunars to have been winning to do this though. Most of the playgroup I play with actually didn't think the new fluff was really any big change, because they never thought the Lunars looked like losers.<br /> But I think it's partly a reaction to fans on forums constantly talking about how lame the Lunars seemed, so the devs have decided to go completely the other way. I don't think there's an easy way to square the circle.<br /> <br /> <br /> One last point though, about opposition. Isator's mentioned historical examples (and, in fact, political division in the face of external and internal threats is why many Empires have fallen in history). But I'll mention an Exalted one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, in our game, we have three power centres:<br /> The Djala jungle, ruled by a council, including the aggressive and fanatical Warmaster and Dawn-Caste Fulgens Cruciatus.<br /> The magical kingdom of H'hui'shan, ruled by the enchantress and absolute monarch Queen Enhenduanna.<br /> The free town of Hen Ling, fast becoming the centre of the Cult of the Illuminated in the South (Kether Rock was destroyed), home of the priest Reborn in Golden Light.<br /> <br /> Outside this area? Two great enemies.<br /> The Leopard Empire, formerly led by Ahlat's daughter who the PCs killed. It persecutes the Cult, and built an armada to invade Hen Ling. It has since morphed into a member of a great Alliance of Gods. Ahlat, Plentimon, the goddess of dinosaurs, etc, have decided to carve up this part of the world between them.<br /> The Realm, which controls the areas to the north and east. The 3rd Legion is marching from the north, the 17th from the east, and they also control a pass allowing an army from Prasad to follow them.<br /> <br /> So, what should the PCs do? Unite against external threats of course.<br /> <br /> What did they do? War with each other, obviously!<br /> Fulgens and Enhenduanna went to war for a while, a Cult Solar tried and failed to kill Fulgens, Reborn in Golden Light burned down one of Fulgens' towns, Enhenduanna demanded the Cult withdraw from an area or there'd be war, and a Cult Solar tried and failed to kidnap her so she killed him.<br /> <br /> Luckily, NPCs have reigned in most of the PCs, and the Realm destroyed a garrison the Cult and Enhenduanna were arguing about.<br /> But there's still unresolved issues like how one Solar NPC is planning to kill a monster she doesn't know serves Enhenduanna; Fulgens' slaving; how most of the Cult Solars don't yet know Enhenduanna killed their Night Caste; and the town which Enhenduanna believes is strategically significant (I don't agree, but that's not important) switched to the Cult and will consider her trying to replace her destroyed garrison an act of war.<br /> <br /> Apparently there's been a call for all the PCs to go East to Varang and overthrow its divine ruler (Plentimon) while troops prepare for the Realm, and everyone's agreed, but we'll see if that actually works.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, I think if the Realm was actually invading right now, PCs would fight it together (though maybe without good co-ordination), but as the Realm's merely preparing to invade, it's a known but not in-your-face threat, people are looking at threats closer to home, like neighbouring countries.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, I can see Dynasts doing the same thing. Yeah, the Lunars are a known threat out in the Satrapies. But Sesus Yuzzim is trying to get that promotion by blackmailing your boss, and that promotion should be yours, and she's right here!<br /> <br /> When 5 Dragonblood are out in a Satrapy far from the Realm and there's a Lunar murdering government officials, they probably work together much more effectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T05:01:47-08:00","id":1270315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270293#post1270293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons I didn't write so much about the Chinese example is I'm not so familiar with it. I mostly know they allied with the Mongols against the Jin; did they also fight each other over what to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly thinking about the angle on having failed to recognise the threat of the Mongols when it was right on their doorstep. As I recall, there was more often infighting during the battles against the Jin.<br /> <br /> Although that puts me in mind of certain Korean court intrigues against an accomplished admiral at a time when they were being invaded by the Japanese.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, Ghosthead has pointed out that it seems counter-productive for the Empress to encourage division if the Lunars are going to win in a hundred years.<br /> But I'm thinking:<br /> a)Maybe she set that system up when the Realm was in its earlier expansionist phase, and can't change it now<br /> b)It's the only way she can see to stay in power, so what choice does she have?<br /> c)The Dragonblood don't know they're losing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> I mean, I would need to see the Fangs text again, but I feel as though it might be written to convey the Lunar biases (that are not wholly inaccurate) while not quite defining the truth of the setting. I would see issues in definitively stating that the Lunars were going to win in the long term (although maybe they're not major ones... I can definitely see how, in-character, there's a problem with fighting the Lunars as a whole over an extended period of time, because what's your win condition?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or at least, until they recently lost the Caul and the Tepet Legions, they didn't know they were losing. So we're talking shortly before the Scarlet Empress vanished.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as references to both of those subjects go, the people on the ground struggle to make the rest take it seriously. Dragon Blooded who see fighting for the Caul as a wasteful extravagance wouldn't necessarily see being down to Faxai as losing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... I suppose that the point is, as you say, to &quot;build heat&quot; for the Lunars. So you don't want to make this too small. But maybe, in their arrogance, the Dragonblood of, say, 100 years ago (I wouldn't want to say the Lunars were winning 300 years ago), didn't realise the tide was beginning to turn? Maybe it wasn't obvious to most, but only the hyper-intelligent strategists of the Silver Pact?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't see it as something with an overt tide to turn as much as a model that the Realm can't ultimately sustain itself against, and that the Realm as a whole should be subject to the typical authoritarian problem of its rhetoric making it bad at objectively assessing the strength of enemies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying this, I actually don't think it's necessary for the Lunars to have been winning to do this though. Most of the playgroup I play with actually didn't think the new fluff was really any big change, because they never thought the Lunars looked like losers.<br /> But I think it's partly a reaction to fans on forums constantly talking about how lame the Lunars seemed, so the devs have decided to go completely the other way. I don't think there's an easy way to square the circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even without forums, I think it just helps to write a book if there's something that one can point to as Lunars having done during the interim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I can see Dynasts doing the same thing. Yeah, the Lunars are a known threat out in the Satrapies. But Sesus Yuzzim is trying to get that promotion by blackmailing your boss, and that promotion should be yours, and she's right here!<br /> <br /> When 5 Dragonblood are out in a Satrapy far from the Realm and there's a Lunar murdering government officials, they probably work together much more effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sworn Kinship helps a lot with that. Indeed, I think that's a detail with new emphasis that helps to place it in the current context; the Empress encourages division on the institutional level, but also promotes the Oath in terms that make it especially good as a context in which disparate Exalted can function together when there's something bigger than them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T05:32:39-08:00","id":1270322,"title":"","content":"All good comments in response. This is a very subjective and qualitative thing that probably benefits from a deep reading of all the sources and some creativity in how they're used in the setting as realised in people's games rather than a matter of absolutes. So I'm more just raising this question than looking to answer it.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm saying here that, if it looks like the Lunars are going to win in a relatively short space of time (relative to their Exalted lifespans and the length of their concerns!), then if the Lunars feel certain of it... The Sidereals are gonna be predicting it with high certainty, and they're gonna be orienting and responding and changing their behaviour, and they're gonna make sure this filters to the Dragonblooded leadership and especially the Empress. Or at least they will be trying to. If civilization is losing, all these parties are going to be very conscious and aware of the recession, and they'd be planning in this knowledge. We'd see signs of this happening in the setting.<br /> <br /> The Sidereals defining power, their defining thing, is being able to look at the long term and have a good idea of where things are going, beyond other Exalted, so your strategy against them will always have to be more &quot;You can probably see this, but you can't do anything about it because you're too restricted to move and you've got too much inertia&quot; and not &quot;I can see this, but you can't&quot;. Like Wizard says about a system set up by the Empress that is hard to now change. You would still have the tragedy of &quot;people pulling apart when they ought to be drawing together&quot;, which is a common thing in Exalted like Isator says, but they should certainly be very aware of it. (The Sidereals can be of course be totally blindsided by some things, but these are definitely things that cut to the heart of their divisions (the Usurpation) and by elements that are vastly powerful and outside of Fate (the Unconquered Sun returns his favour to the Solars, etc.)).<br /> <br /> It's all good if we have confidence that the setting as described in 3e does fulfil all this. I've def. not read as deeply the 3e sourcebooks as most in this thread, so I'm actually relatively ill positioned to say whether that's the case, and I'll take the judgement of the more expert posters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270293#post1270293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons I didn't write so much about the Chinese example is I'm not so familiar with it. I mostly know they allied with the Mongols against the Jin; did they also fight each other over what to do?<br /> <br /> (I wanted to do an American example; like the Shogunate was the Mayans, the Realm is the Aztecs but they love Mayans instead of Toltecs, and the Lunars are the Spanish, taking advantage of the Aztecs' angry subjects to conquer Central America and destroy the Aztecs' religion and rule. But again, it's not an area of history I know a ton about. Still, it inspires me to read more.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea; I have to say though when we think about those comparison, like the Spanish being like the Lunars and the Realm being like Central American groups, we have to consider how much the information on each side and the framing could be different. The Spanish had not been engaged in a thousand years war in which they'd made abundantly clear that the had genocidal intentions and no place for any of the other groups across most of that span, and their capabilities were ill understood. I'm not sure the Central American groups would've acted at all as they did if they were if that's the information they were working from (though again I'm far from an expert). They (the Spanish) look and feel a bit more like the reborn Solars than the Lunars, to me, I guess, in this scenario.<br /> <br /> I don't know enough about the Mongols either, though from what I understand there's a similar element where no one, and not really even the Mongols themselves, really expected Temujin to be able to do what he did in unifying the clans, innovating tactically, being able to embrace and adopt elements from his enemies into his order and it was a sudden and surprising eruption to them as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T07:53:23-08:00","id":1270356,"title":"","content":"Something else to consider is that the Empress was born into the Shogunate, where \u201clegitimacy\u201d in a ruler was a novel concept, and she came to power via the authority inherent in \u201cI have the biggest beatstick in the box,\u201d and a whole bunch of people tried to take it away from her. Later on in her life, her first son decided HE was going to be the heir and had all her other children murdered until she made him stop.<br /> <br /> The Empress is, pretty clearly, a woman who knows how fragile a throne is and has formed her government in response to that. She intentionally set it up with infighting built in and with her as the only referee, so she can absolutely make sure that no-one else can ever be strong enough to take power from her (and, if they ever thought they had a shot, Chejop would warn her about the coup being in the works years earlier).<br /> <br /> Would another governmental model work better? Maybe, but, as far as the Scarlet Empress was concerned, any other model of government would have seen her either dethroned and executed or assassinated long ago, and that\u2019s pretty clearly the main thing she wanted to keep from happening this entire time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T09:59:00-08:00","id":1270373,"title":"","content":"Something to note is that the Lunars winning thing isn't undefeated. While Lunars are happy they may have delayed the Realm getting into the West and having set up a weaker presence, they still did it not long ago. (Last couple centuires last I saw). And as the Lunars who remember the First Age pass on, there's probably soemthing long term Lunar elders migh have had. &quot;success&quot; was still like, centuries away. What happens when it's nearly there but everyone who careda bout the original goals has died?<br /> <br /> I also think the &quot;inevitabiltiy&quot; is moot a bit in a world where any sure vicotry was centuries away, and the world is in a huge bit of upheaval <i>now</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T10:10:57-08:00","id":1270375,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar226_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"226\" data-vbnamecard=\"226\">BrilliantRain</a>, totally. It's only, if the writing is on the wall that it's either Mnemon or some Lunar that will desecrate everything she's built and believes in, she's gonna go Mnemon every time. Or there's even anything close between those two options, and if there's any probability that she's just trading off being replaced by one of her descendents for a Lunar in general, and this is at all predictable to anyone involved (Bronze Faction, Lunar elders, Realm inner circle).<br /> <br /> Of course, if it looked one way and has become the other, the inertia might be hard to stop, and it may be too late, but if its changed and been obvious for some time all the significant figures on the Realm side (including Big Red) should be aware of it, if it's obvious, and be responding at the point in the timeline when play begins (if it is in fact obvious).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T10:29:27-08:00","id":1270377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1266311#post1266311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally agree, but in this particular example he's being ordered to kill one of the most influential Dragon-Blooded alive whose presumably at least an ocean away.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also a Dragon-Blooded charm called Secret Wind Revelation which allows them to 'spot' immaterial creatures as though they were attempting mundane stealth. So telling him to ambush Cainan in his private study is far less likely to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T12:53:32-08:00","id":1270407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270375#post1270375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, totally. It's only, if the writing is on the wall that it's either Mnemon or some Lunar that will desecrate everything she's built and believes in, she's gonna go Mnemon every time. Or there's even anything close between those two options, and if there's any probability that she's just trading off being replaced by one of her descendents for a Lunar in general, and this is at all predictable to anyone involved (Bronze Faction, Lunar elders, Realm inner circle).<br /> <br /> Of course, if it looked one way and has become the other, the inertia might be hard to stop, and it may be too late, but if its changed and been obvious for some time all the significant figures on the Realm side (including Big Red) should be aware of it, if it's obvious, and be responding at the point in the timeline when play begins (if it is in fact obvious).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it\u2019s mainly that the situation looked one way for a very long time. I mean, the Realm measures its victories in land and resources claimed, while the Lunars measure theirs in irreplaceable treasures lost and Realm Scions dead. A Lunar might spend a decade or two building up a tribe, granting them mutations, and then toss them at a satrapy expecting them to be defeated, which will look like a \u201cwin\u201d to the Realm... but, if they do enough damage to the infrastructure so that Ragara will need to send their geomancer to fix it and you can assassinate her and reclaim the Singing Staf of Kal Bax himself, that\u2019s...probably worth it to the Lunar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T13:39:35-08:00","id":1270416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270407#post1270407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it\u2019s mainly that the situation looked one way for a very long time. I mean, the Realm measures its victories in land and resources claimed, while the Lunars measure theirs in irreplaceable treasures lost and Realm Scions dead. A Lunar might spend a decade or two building up a tribe, granting them mutations, and then toss them at a satrapy expecting them to be defeated, which will look like a \u201cwin\u201d to the Realm... but, if they do enough damage to the infrastructure so that Ragara will need to send their geomancer to fix it and you can assassinate her and reclaim the Singing Staf of Kal Bax himself, that\u2019s...probably worth it to the Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. Though I'd imagine that at senior levels the Sidereals and the Realm's leadership is probably fairly well aware of this bias, and if it's strategically a bad move, probably have some use of imperial power and rigging Fate to ensure that it's discouraged - &quot;No, Cathak Shortterm, the Empress really does not favour your attempts to gain land at the expense of priceless irreplaceable relics and the blood of your cousins, and neither do the twists and turns of Fate!&quot;, and even publicly stating that this is What The Lunars Want. But compensating totally for the incentives to gain land and treasure is probably very tricky and involves a lot of active monitoring that's tough on overworked Sidereals and has to be balanced with other goals.<br /> <br /> (There's probably also a bit of information warfare going on with the Realm operating to bait the Lunars into thinking that they can gain Dragonblooded deaths and loss of artefacts that are greater than what is actually possible.)<br /> <br /> (Some difficulties also on incentives the Lunar side though - &quot;We'll use our ability to replace our losses more easily than the Dragonblooded to defeat them through attrition on both sides! Genius!&quot; sounds like good strategy on some level, until you talk to a young Lunar and he says &quot;So... the strategy is... I... die? And some future reincarnation of me and you high elder guys get to eventually win.... Uh-huh.&quot; and you find yourself offering him land and loot and palaces to keep him loyal and willing to make the sacrifice, and then that commits you and ties you down.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T14:23:01-08:00","id":1270427,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m actually not entirely sure the senior decision makers in the Realm do, really. I mean, assuming I\u2019m understanding correctly, the Lunars are basically executing hit and run tactics that, most of the time, look like banditry or local revolutions. If you assume that the Lunars are basically throwing tantrums, trying to hurt the Realm that hurt them, and you\u2019re already drowning in other things that need handling, you might not realize there\u2019s a larger game at work until several hundred years later when you go to requisition a Warstrider, discover it\u2019s not been maintained, and start digging to find out why and you realize that the Realm has been sliding down a very, very gentle downward slope and picking up speed.<br /> <br /> Honestly doing it that way, it really could evade the Sidereals\u2019 notice, because each day would be just slightly worse and the Lunars victory would be anything but inevitable ...until it was too late to do anything about it, because governments are vast and hard to steer. I could imagine that, even if the Empress hadn\u2019t vanished, trying to get all the modern Houses to cooperate in a massive Lunar Wyld Hunt to go after all of the most powerful Lunars would be problematic at best. <br /> <br /> Because ...well, let\u2019s say you want to go after Raksi. She lives deep in the jungle, has an army of ape beastkin, all the local tribes are allied to her, and she\u2019s an amazingly powerful sorceress. So you have to sail a bunch of troop transports up a bunch of rivers, through territory that you probably don\u2019t control and might try to dispute your travel, then you have to march a long distance through jungle, while being harried by the locals who are just trying to whittle down your numbers with hit and run tactics, the weather is always horrible (because sorcery), and at some point Raksi is going to drop an army killer spell on you. If you have a big enough army left to actually fight when you get there, she has her own army of ape people and sorcerers and maybe even a few other Lunars so she\u2019s not going down easily. And, even if you do kill everyone there... how sure are you that Raksi didn\u2019t just fly away ten minutes ago?<br /> <br /> Well, or you could try to send in an elite team of commandos, but there\u2019s nearly always something better that an Essence 4 DB or Sid could be doing than going on a hugely risky probable suicide mission to kill a demon goddess and they\u2019d still have to go through all that stuff I listed earlier to get there.<br /> <br /> Point is that, trying to organize an attack that would have a decent chance at killing an elder Lunar is probably on the same level as trying to assult Lookshy in terms of difficulty with a very dubious result in terms of ultimate gains, so that\u2019s a hard sell and the Empress can\u2019t just tell people to go do this stupid and useless thing all the time without her empire collapsing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 11-24-2018, 05:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T14:39:04-08:00","id":1270432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270416#post1270416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;No, Cathak Shortterm, the Empress really does not favour your attempts to gain land at the expense of priceless irreplaceable relics and the blood of your cousins, and neither do the twists and turns of Fate!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, any time the Dragon Blooded go out to fight something, there's technically a risk to it, but one might presume in a lot of cases it's something that's important enough to be worth the risk if it requires Exalted and strong Artifacts to go out to deal with it.<br /> <br /> It seems like a lot of the time, the Lunars might present a catch-22; either you take the risk and possibly lose something important and irreplaceable, or you don't and lose something <i>else</i> important and irreplaceable. <br /> <br /> If there are any times at which a Lunar Exalt led forces against some holding in the Threshold and the Dynasts responsible for it decided they were better off not fighting to recover it, that's probably just fine with the Lunar, because it still accomplishes a result of incrementally weakening the Realm as a whole, and any House that would have been responsible; they're losing both face in front of their peers, and an additional revenue stream, which weakens their capacity to project force in the Threshold and makes them look more vulnerable to their peers.<br /> <br /> The actions of the Scarlet Empress might not be the only one actively fostering division in the Realm.<br /> <br /> , and even publicly stating that this is What The Lunars Want. But compensating totally for the incentives to gain land and treasure is probably very tricky and involves a lot of active monitoring that's tough on overworked Sidereals and has to be balanced with other goals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Some difficulties also on incentives the Lunar side though - &quot;We'll use our ability to replace our losses more easily than the Dragonblooded to defeat them through attrition on both sides! Genius!&quot; sounds like good strategy on some level, until you talk to a young Lunar and he says &quot;So... the strategy is... I... die? And some future reincarnation of me and you high elder guys get to eventually win.... Uh-huh.&quot; and you find yourself offering him land and loot and palaces to keep him loyal and willing to make the sacrifice, and then that commits you and ties you down.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you're getting the idea that the Silver Pact actively wants young Lunars to die fighting. They're probably the ones with the highest mortality rate since they're the least powerful, but that doesn't mean that they're at extremely high risk every time they do something contrary to the Realm.<br /> <br /> Something helped by the likelihood that a huge number of Lunars, even young ones, probably have at least one shape that is very small and very fast and has a form of mobility that is hard for enemies to effectively chase. The developers have mentioned that, on the whole, the Wyld Hunt can have difficulties pinning Lunars down when so many are willing and capable of turning into small birds and flying away when an encounter turns south.<br /> <br /> Honestly, while I'm usually a person averse to approaching the setting or even player characters with the metagaming of &quot;this thing is too useful for everybody to not have&quot;, when it comes to Lunar Exalted I'm somewhat of the opinion that your only excuse if you've been around for more than a year and don't have at least one shape of a flying bird is if you happen to live somewhere that doesn't have those animals. <i>Maybe</i> somebody with a fairly deep conviction against killing other animals or some other disposition against certain forms of shapeshifting, but it's still idiosyncratic.<br /> <br /> Because Lunar shapeshifting is kind of unlike sorcery or Charms or even building up an Ability in that even in character, it doesn't really correspond to something with some kind of variable aptitude; acquiring new shapes is explicitly supposed to be fairly easy, and the range of advantages it can provide without having to buy with XP or spend very much Essence has often been raised as a selling point.<br /> <br /> So with that in mind, it's by and large going to be difficult to have an encounter in which a Lunar can't bail when things aren't going their way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T15:43:59-08:00","id":1270453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270427#post1270427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, or you could try to send in an elite team of commandos, but there\u2019s nearly always something better that an Essence 4 DB or Sid could be doing than going on a hugely risky probable suicide mission to kill a demon goddess and they\u2019d still have to go through all that stuff I listed earlier to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be really cool if that had happened a couple times throughout history, though. It'd be a neat thematic similarity with the Fallen Houses of the Realm and a way to model for storytellers how a successful counter-operation from the Bronze faction and the Realm might look. <br /> <br /> Could even be communicated through the flavor of a Vengeancemurder themed daiklaive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T15:51:56-08:00","id":1270454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270427#post1270427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m actually not entirely sure the senior decision makers in the Realm do, really. I mean, assuming I\u2019m understanding correctly, the Lunars are basically executing hit and run tactics that, most of the time, look like banditry or local revolutions. If you assume that the Lunars are basically throwing tantrums, trying to hurt the Realm that hurt them, and you\u2019re already drowning in other things that need handling, you might not realize there\u2019s a larger game at work until several hundred years later when you go to requisition a Warstrider, discover it\u2019s not been maintained, and start digging to find out why and you realize that the Realm has been sliding down a very, very gentle downward slope and picking up speed.<br /> <br /> Honestly doing it that way, it really could evade the Sidereals\u2019 notice, because each day would be just slightly worse and the Lunars victory would be anything but inevitable ...until it was too late to do anything about it, because governments are vast and hard to steer. I could imagine that, even if the Empress hadn\u2019t vanished, trying to get all the modern Houses to cooperate in a massive Lunar Wyld Hunt to go after all of the most powerful Lunars would be problematic at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you could go like that and assume they see it like that but... to argue the opposite end:<br /> <br /> Sidereals are the specialists in stratagists of the host, and its spymasters (or they were represented well among them). They're all about long term planning, foresight and gathering intel. They're very manipulative and skilled at discerning intrigues and secrets (they have a Caste that's all about that). The Lunars have been doing this for hundreds of years. The strengths and weaknesses of the Lunars and their weak dependence on artefacts are well known. They know that the Lunar elders are smart and want to win. Are they gonna assume this is all irrational and crazy or see the trend? Banking that they don't work out at least this much seems like banking on the opposite of all their known strengths relative to other Celestial Exalted.<br /> <br /> So that's why I'd have to guess that surely, the Sidereals to some extent can kind of see where this is going and try to hedge against it? That hedging may not work! It may fall apart under the weight of managing the different pressures! And the Lunars are very good. But I can't see the Sidereals just totally not getting the message and trying to do the obvious thing to put opposing incentives into play and frustrate their opponents strategy, or to use that strategy against them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270432#post1270432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, any time the Dragon Blooded go out to fight something, there's technically a risk to it, but one might presume in a lot of cases it's something that's important enough to be worth the risk if it requires Exalted and strong Artifacts to go out to deal with it.<br /> <br /> It seems like a lot of the time, the Lunars might present a catch-22; either you take the risk and possibly lose something important and irreplaceable, or you don't and lose something <i>else</i> important and irreplaceable.<br /> <br /> If there are any times at which a Lunar Exalt led forces against some holding in the Threshold and the Dynasts responsible for it decided they were better off not fighting to recover it, that's probably just fine with the Lunar, because it still accomplishes a result of incrementally weakening the Realm as a whole, and any House that would have been responsible; they're losing both face in front of their peers, and an additional revenue stream, which weakens their capacity to project force in the Threshold and makes them look more vulnerable to their peers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose you kind of could go that way. It seems a bit less interesting if it's &quot;Heads I win, tails I win&quot; a lot though, as much as that kind of thing to some degree is a relatively common dilemma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270432#post1270432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure where you're getting the idea that the Silver Pact actively wants young Lunars to die fighting. They're probably the ones with the highest mortality rate since they're the least powerful, but that doesn't mean that they're at extremely high risk every time they do something contrary to the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really *want*, so much as that it's an expected cost of the strategy and everyone within the Pact is fairly away of this. Kind of from comments that the Lunars win when they lose X Lunars for Y Dragonblooded scions, because of replacement rates. The idea that they tend to define victory purely in taking down Dynast numbers, at whatever cost, because they can replace themselves faster. Seems like that implies that they are intending losses, not quite kamikaze like but certainly with the idea that heroic deaths are expected? <br /> <br /> So my comment was, if that is the strategy, then you have to balance things to give them material incentives and status so that they personally feel committed (like, they're not going to do it &quot;For the cause&quot; any more than Dragonbloods would do similar things! they wanna live).<br /> <br /> If that's not representative, then absolutely I'm getting a wrong idea here!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T16:15:43-08:00","id":1270457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270454#post1270454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereals are the specialists in stratagists of the host, and its spymasters (or they were represented well among them). They're all about long term planning, foresight and gathering intel. They're very manipulative and skilled at discerning intrigues and secrets (they have a Caste that's all about that). The Lunars have been doing this for hundreds of years. The strengths and weaknesses of the Lunars and their weak dependence on artefacts are well known. They know that the Lunar elders are smart and want to win. Are they gonna assume this is all irrational and crazy or see the trend? Banking that they don't work out at least this much seems like banking on the opposite of all their known strengths relative to other Celestial Exalted.<br /> <br /> So that's why I'd have to guess that surely, the Sidereals to some extent can kind of see where this is going and try to hedge against it? That hedging may not work! It may fall apart under the weight of managing the different pressures! And the Lunars are very good. But I can't see the Sidereals just totally not getting the message and trying to do the obvious thing to put opposing incentives into play and frustrate their opponents strategy, or to use that strategy against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is another thing covered by the underlying point in the Silver Pact is that it's ultimately not one strategy, it's dozens or hundreds of them, and that while it's not outside the realms of possibility for the Sidereals to have documented most of the playbooks, being able to track and keep on top of all of them is going to present a challenge.<br /> <br /> Some of this dependent on the exact forms that Sidereal prescience takes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose you kind of could go that way. It seems a bit less interesting if it's &quot;Heads I win, tails I win&quot; a lot though, as much as that kind of thing to some degree is a relatively common dilemma.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only that if you're absolutely certain that the Dragon Blooded (possibly with some Sidereals in tow) are going to lose.<br /> <br /> The advantage of making such a nuisance of yourself that the Realm not only can't allow things to continue, but send out people with warstriders, is that you get a shot at taking one of the Realm's warstriders out of commission, making a significant dent in their offensive, defensive, and power projection capabilities.<br /> <br /> The disadvantage is that you have to fight a fucking warstrider!<br /> <br /> Like, somebody up there talking about suicide missions for commando squads consisting of a bunch of Essence 4 Dragon Blooded... Essence 4 Dragon Blooded are pretty dang formidable. It might be a suicide mission if they have to go up against, say, freaking Mahicara (in which case, injuring that thing enough to drive it away may well qualify as something worth giving your life for, especially considering how often being Essence 4 means that you're probably old and retired and just about ready to get your old band back together and go out to find a blaze of glory to end your life in), but they're liable to give a good number of Lunars a run for their money.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really *want*, so much as that it's an expected cost of the strategy and everyone within the Pact is fairly away of this. Kind of from comments that the Lunars win when they lose X Lunars for Y Dragonblooded scions, because of replacement rates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is making these comments? I have <b>words</b> for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that they tend to define victory purely in taking down Dynast numbers, at whatever cost, because they can replace themselves faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, the last time that I recall the developers elucidating at length on Lunar strategies, back in the thread about survival rates for Realm generals, it seemed as though they were rather of the exact opposite of this sentiment. That taking down Dynasts, even important ones like legion commanders, at all costs whenever the opportunity presented itself was in fact not a winning strategy of the Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> I mean, I was talking earlier in the thread about the idea of marginalized schools, and one that idealized this kind of &quot;burn fast and hard&quot; strategy seems prime for that spot, but given the write-up in this preview, I imagine that most are teaching their charges that it's better to leave a bleeding or venomous wound and then run away or allow the enemy to escape, rather than leave a death grip that doesn't let go even when you cut the head off.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T18:15:25-08:00","id":1270478,"title":"","content":"Someone made a valid point upthread that it's hard to strike a balance between Lunars seeming awesome and scary and effectual, and Dynasts seeming awesome and scary and effectual. This is very true. But for whatever reasons, people seem to be ignoring or sidelining the third party to this conflict -- Sidereals. Who also should seem awesome and scary and effectual, and who thus far have...well, not, really.<br /> <br /> The discussion so far has also focused heavily on Lunars doing damage to the Realm, and ignoring or dismissing the idea of the converse, which doesn't help. And it seems to me like these problems can be synthesized to help solve each other. So here's my vision of the Shogunate, the Contagion and the present day, in an attempt to make everyone look as cool as they should.<br /> <br /> Eric Minton said upthread that the Lunars were effectively losing until the Contagion. The Shogunate was full of warring daimyos and infighting, but by and large, it ran on its own; this means that the Sidereals allied with it had a freer hand to go on the offensive. Meanwhile, angry Lunar Exalted were building up armies at the edge of the world -- but the larger their armies got, the more of their time they had to dedicate to vigilance and paranoia, just as the Realm had to do the same against Lunar infiltrators. Young, ambitious Lunar warlords might come back from a recruiting drive to find their hunters caught in their own snares, their crop yields through the floor, their armies fragmented by a half-dozen new cults who hate each other, half their chain of command killing the other half over grievances that only sound ludicrous after the bodies have cooled, and then when they're distracted by trying to fix all this mess, some innocuous traveler looks up at them with stars in their eyes and pokes a pressure point that makes their soul fall off. Sure, it's not going to work as well on Raksi, but most Lunars aren't Raksi, and even Raksi might not have had the same secure powerbase then as she does now.<br /> <br /> (As a side note, this is the kind of stuff I would love to see Sidereals doing to their enemies. I don't know why it never seems to happen in canon materials.)<br /> <br /> So Lunars learned the hard way not to gather huge masses of troops, to fragment their operations, to always be ready to run, and to bleed their enemies rather than going for knockout blows. The trouble is, the Shogunate legions are well-trained, well-disciplined, well-armed and culturally militant, so bleeding them tends to hurt the Lunars more than it does their enemies. And maybe Sidereals can't disrupt every bigger operation, but they can hit the most likely to succeed (and, just as importantly, know which ones those are) until the threat of their involvement becomes something that helps shape Lunar strategies just as much as Legion doctrine does.<br /> <br /> Then, of course, comes the Contagion, and everything goes to hell.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, the Realm has to rebuild itself from the ashes of the Shogunate, and its Sidereal allies have to develop and spread a new religion to support it, and help guide and advise the Empress so that the new empire takes an agreeable shape. Suddenly the world is full of Wyld zones, remnant raksha, shadowlands, and other threats to Fate, which means that Sidereals have a much harder time finding the space to do, well, anything else. Suddenly, the Dragon-blooded are decimated and have to rebuild their numbers over generations. And meanwhile, the Lunars at the edge of the world are finding that the same tactics they used against the Realm and the Fivescore Fellowship are working even better than before. Moving on to the next after a society they built destroyed itself is what they've always been doing, after all, and while the Contagion is more thorough it's also far more even-handed.<br /> <br /> So <i>now</i> we reach Creation as it stands. Sidereals allied with the Realm now find themselves in the position of having to pick their battles very carefully; they could go mess up that barbarian horde, or they could defuse the tension between Great Houses that would lead to civil war in a decade or so. At least with barbarian hordes, the Legions can deal with them; civil war doesn't have that stopgap. So Lunars now have a much freer hand to build their power bases and bleed the Realm -- a Realm which never recovered to Shogunate levels -- without interference, and are themselves freer to put their enemies on the defensive. The momentum that was against them before the Contagion is now theirs to ride to eventual victory...<br /> <br /> ...and then the Solars appeared, and everything changed again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T18:30:33-08:00","id":1270482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270478#post1270478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eric Minton said upthread that the Lunars were effectively losing until the Contagion. The Shogunate was full of warring daimyos and infighting, but by and large, it ran on its own; this means that the Sidereals allied with it had a freer hand to go on the offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>A freer hand to go on the offensive seems like it's still something that needs to account for how few they are, how important what they do is, and how it always takes years, if not decades, for a Sidereal to be reborn. And when you've got armies of the Shogunate right there...<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt still dates back to that time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, angry Lunar Exalted were building up armies at the edge of the world -- but the larger their armies got, the more of their time they had to dedicate to vigilance and paranoia, just as the Realm had to do the same against Lunar infiltrators.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes it sound like a terrible tactic that ought to be abandoned quickly.<br /> <br /> I don't know, while it's different from the manner in which I was conceiving it, there's nothing wrong with and quite a few things positive to the idea that the Shogunate was less vulnerable. But I don't think it's well served by a suggestion that it was a result of the Lunars trying to make their own Realms, and being consistently bad at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(As a side note, this is the kind of stuff I would love to see Sidereals doing to their enemies. I don't know why it never seems to happen in canon materials.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the general writing intention has been that they're more surgical than that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T18:37:35-08:00","id":1270483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270454#post1270454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Not really *want*, so much as that it's an expected cost of the strategy and everyone within the Pact is fairly away of this. Kind of from comments that the Lunars win when they lose X Lunars for Y Dragonblooded scions, because of replacement rates. The idea that they tend to define victory purely in taking down Dynast numbers, at whatever cost, because they can replace themselves faster. Seems like that implies that they are intending losses, not quite kamikaze like but certainly with the idea that heroic deaths are expected?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar replacement process <i>sucks</i> compared to Dynastic Dragonblooded. The Silver Pact trades in one trained Lunar for a complete unknown newbie. There is only the vague 'passed life' connection between each excarnation, and only Luna knows where or <i>when</i> the successor will appear.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile every adventurous Dynastic Dragonblood that leaves the Blessed Isle <i>already</i> has replacements being raised among their cousins or siblings if not children. New Dynasts have a connection of familial emotion and traditions to the old, and may well <i>know</i> their elder. This steady rate of trained replacements only encounters glitches with exceptional circumstances -- such as the Tepet expedition. And they can draw on Lost Eggs to replenish.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal replacement process is a bit worse than Lunars, in that they have to wait until the candidate matures; but at least they have the ability to track and train them while the wait.<br /> <br /> So, no, Lunars don't win when they trade exalted lives. Lunars win when they erode the Realm's <i>influence</i>, exhast its more <i>irreplacable</i> resources, and erode faith in the Immaculate traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 11-24-2018, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T18:44:44-08:00","id":1270485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270482#post1270482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A freer hand to go on the offensive seems like it's still something that needs to account for how few they are, how important what they do is, and how it always takes years, if not decades, for a Sidereal to be reborn. And when you've got armies of the Shogunate right there...<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt still dates back to that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're kind of missing the point here; part of the goal of what I was proposing was that Sidereals should seem awesome and scary and effectual. Having them hiding behind the Shogunate does not accomplish that goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270482#post1270482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes it sound like a terrible tactic that ought to be abandoned quickly.<br /> <br /> I don't know, while it's different from the manner in which I was conceiving it, there's nothing wrong with and quite a few things positive to the idea that the Shogunate was less vulnerable. But I don't think it's well served by a suggestion that it was a result of the Lunars trying to make their own Realms, and being consistently bad at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't thinking of &quot;Lunars trying to make their own Realms&quot;; more the practice of &quot;let's build a society-backed army and hurl it against the vulnerable bits of the Shogunate&quot; that we all know today, except for two major differences: one, they tried to do it on a bigger scale at first and two, their enemies are more active in disrupting that strategy than they currently are. I agree that the tactic would have been abandoned before the end of the Shogunate; what I'm saying is that the <i>reasons</i> it was abandoned can be used to build some heat for Sidereals, which they sorely need in this edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270482#post1270482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the general writing intention has been that they're more surgical than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's fine, but they need to not be so surgical that an outside perspective can't perceive them, or us outside observers start to think that Sidereals aren't actually doing anything. And on the scale of Creation, causing a nascent barbarian horde to collapse into infighting and starvation is pretty surgical. Surgical precision doesn't mean that the result isn't spectacular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T19:00:03-08:00","id":1270488,"title":"","content":"It's probably worth considering strategies of asymmetrical warfare, and while the beef of a Lunar elder is not the same of a younger Exalt, they are often going to come from places under the boot of the Realm and all too happy to make it bleed.<br /> <br /> As for Sids... previously, higher-essence things were harder to manipulate with astrology. If that holds, that and the general disunity of the Sidereals seems enough to explain why they don't unerringly crush all Lunar opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T19:45:13-08:00","id":1270497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270485#post1270485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're kind of missing the point here; part of the goal of what I was proposing was that Sidereals should seem awesome and scary and effectual. Having them hiding behind the Shogunate does not accomplish that goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you frame it like that.<br /> <br /> Do you call the character who rolls Intelligence + War somebody hiding behind their army?<br /> <br /> Pulling the strings is not the sole Sidereal schtick, but it's generally presented as something they're good at and often have an incentive to do.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, a lot of the modes of attack you're suggesting... well, it depends on the vectors, and resulting defence mechanisms. It <i>feels</i> a lot like the charge from their First Edition book that they got a lot of powers to severely mess things up without a method of defence or reversal and little difficulty for the user, and how it kind of bent the setting around it.<br /> <br /> Even in the Shogunate, even among those Lunars that have the inclination to set up armies of &quot;barbarians&quot; (where have they come from in this era), I propose that the Sidereal who opts to go in and plant curses on the palms of their hands should be concerned with the possibility that a Lunar will sniff them out.<br /> <br /> This preview is building Lunar heat, but it's doing so with an eye towards their internal limitations. It's not saying that Lunars would wade effortlessly through rivers of blood if they didn't happen to be really distracted. You're going too far in pursuit of your goal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't thinking of &quot;Lunars trying to make their own Realms&quot;; more the practice of &quot;let's build a society-backed army and hurl it against the vulnerable bits of the Shogunate&quot; that we all know today, except for two major differences: one, they tried to do it on a bigger scale at first and two, their enemies are more active in disrupting that strategy than they currently are. I agree that the tactic would have been abandoned before the end of the Shogunate; what I'm saying is that the <i>reasons</i> it was abandoned can be used to build some heat for Sidereals, which they sorely need in this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I find is that it doesn't really seem to fit the tone of their Second Age Castes, and makes the Lunars look really bad. The Lunar heat is making the Sidereals look generally worse; I understand that's a cardinal rule of building heat, you don't make an established act look like a chump.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's fine, but they need to not be so surgical that an outside perspective can't perceive them</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's a major thing with Sidereals. It's so major to them that it was incorporated into their original hardcover as a metaphysical thing.<br /> <br /> Presuming Arcane Fate is still a thing, the outside perspectives that perceive them will generally forget that they did so within a few days.<br /> <br /> I can get wanting to re-write from that foundational premise (which I would have arguments against), but taking that premise as given to them and running with it was not a fault of previous writings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">us outside observers start to think that Sidereals aren't actually doing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>That</i> has been a fault in the writing, yes, but one that I think can be reconciled by a future imperative to point out times in which Sidereals got involved carefully and precisely to hit shatterpoints, rather than giving them a lot of achievements in which they stopped a problem society by unloading disasters upon it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T20:04:38-08:00","id":1270501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270497#post1270497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>That</i> has been a fault in the writing, yes, but one that I think can be reconciled by a future imperative to point out times in which Sidereals got involved carefully and precisely to hit shatterpoints, rather than giving them a lot of achievements in which they <b>stopped a problem society by unloading disasters upon it.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>But I thought that they were <i>meant </i>to be modeled off of an intelligence agency! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T20:08:33-08:00","id":1270502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270497#post1270497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not if you frame it like that.<br /> <br /> Do you call the character who rolls Intelligence + War somebody hiding behind their army?</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's all they're presented as doing, yes, I do. It's also not exactly a fun play experience, in my opinion; I want Sidereals to be capable of, and more importantly be presented as capable of, more than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270497#post1270497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pulling the strings is not the sole Sidereal schtick, but it's generally presented as something they're good at and often have an incentive to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that in what's been presented so far, it <i>has</i> been presented as the sole Sidereal schtick. We need more examples of Sidereals getting their hands dirty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270497#post1270497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Otherwise, a lot of the modes of attack you're suggesting... well, it depends on the vectors, and resulting defence mechanisms. It <i>feels</i> a lot like the charge from their First Edition book that they got a lot of powers to severely mess things up without a method of defence or reversal and little difficulty for the user, and how it kind of bent the setting around it.<br /> <br /> Even in the Shogunate, even among those Lunars that have the inclination to set up armies of &quot;barbarians&quot; (where have they come from in this era), I propose that the Sidereal who opts to go in and plant curses on the palms of their hands should be concerned with the possibility that a Lunar will sniff them out.<br /> <br /> This preview is building Lunar heat, but it's doing so with an eye towards their internal limitations. It's not saying that Lunars would wade effortlessly through rivers of blood if they didn't happen to be really distracted. You're going too far in pursuit of your goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think I am.<br /> <br /> (I did originally have a footnote in that paragraph that said something like &quot;and of course sometimes a vigilant Lunar catches the itinerant in the act, and then there's a big epic fight&quot;, but I felt like it weakened the image I was presenting. So, yes, I'm not suggesting that Sidereals would have been universally successful in their counterassaults, just as I'm sure all the people who posit Lunars casually infiltrating the Realm with their shapeshifting skills aren't suggesting that those efforts are universally successful.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270497#post1270497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I find is that it doesn't really seem to fit the tone of their Second Age Castes, and makes the Lunars look really bad. The Lunar heat is making the Sidereals look generally worse; I understand that's a cardinal rule of building heat, you don't make an established act look like a chump.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here we have the exact problem I'm trying to point out and resolve. Quite a lot of the heat that Lunars are building in this edition is stolen from Sidereals, which makes them look like chumps. Worse, the heat that's being built for <i>the Dragon-blooded</i> is also, if less directly, being drawn from Sidereals, by making the Realm less dependent on their guidance. I actually strongly approve of that...but it does contribute to Sidereals looking ineffectual, and that I do not approve of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270497#post1270497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's a major thing with Sidereals. It's so major to them that it was incorporated into their original hardcover as a metaphysical thing.<br /> <br /> Presuming Arcane Fate is still a thing, the outside perspectives that perceive them will generally forget that they did so within a few days.<br /> <br /> I can get wanting to re-write from that foundational premise (which I would have arguments against), but taking that premise as given to them and running with it was not a fault of previous writings.</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;an outside perspective&quot;, I meant you and me, the fans of Exalted, reading sourcebooks from Earth. I apologize if that was unclear. What I meant was that we, the readers, need to have examples of Sidereals doing things even if other in-setting actors don't realize that's what's going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270497#post1270497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>That</i> has been a fault in the writing, yes, but one that I think can be reconciled by a future imperative to point out times in which Sidereals got involved carefully and precisely to hit shatterpoints, rather than giving them a lot of achievements in which they stopped a problem society by unloading disasters upon it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be very happy if we got more of this, yes. But I do want to point out that it's needed, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":39,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","user":"ysadrel","date":".  even IF 11-24-2018, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T21:17:51-08:00","id":1270518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270497#post1270497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar heat is making the Sidereals look generally worse</div> </div> </div> </div>...the fuck did I mean by this? Did I just mix up the proper nouns, or... have something else in mind?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270502#post1270502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's all they're presented as doing, yes, I do. It's also not exactly a fun play experience, in my opinion; I want Sidereals to be capable of, and more importantly be presented as capable of, more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>When you phrase it in pejorative terms, you're actively denigrating a play style that is valid enough to have gotten an entry in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that in what's been presented so far, it <i>has</i> been presented as the sole Sidereal schtick. We need more examples of Sidereals getting their hands dirty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder about that... the question of how frequently, outside of their hardbacks, many Exalted ever got described in heavy detail at all. Like in setting sourcebooks, if they were generally intent on describing the stage rather than some of the particular actors.<br /> <br /> And from there, maybe analyse the premise that the Sidereal hardbacks didn't sufficiently describe them as hands on either.<br /> <br /> That's not so much suggesting that the sentiment is incorrect as analysis of the context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I don't think I am.<br /> <br /> (I did originally have a footnote in that paragraph that said something like &quot;and of course sometimes a vigilant Lunar catches the itinerant in the act, and then there's a big epic fight&quot;, but I felt like it weakened the image I was presenting. So, yes, I'm not suggesting that Sidereals would have been universally successful in their counterassaults, just as I'm sure all the people who posit Lunars casually infiltrating the Realm with their shapeshifting skills aren't suggesting that those efforts are universally successful.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I think that some might be.<br /> <br /> Like I said, this preview is making a point of it. I don't think a concession of sometimes Lunars are able to fight back at the end is going far enough when there's a whole process before it, and it doesn't cover that your base principle is that the Sidereals had the Lunars on the run because they weren't distracted enough.<br /> <br /> I think I may actually just be arguing the finer details; I'm still all over the idea that the Shogunate was a bad time for Lunars because they were driven to the margins, and that the Sidereals put a lot of force behind making that work. And that it would include things like riding in with a bunch of Immaculate adherents and using mystical martial arts to maim and kill them.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think I dislike the image of the big barbarian armies primarily because I don't want it to have been a thing that the Lunars were doing, more than anything to do with the Sidereals. Both as an aesthetic thing, and a quality one. That's the main reason I don't care for it; I think it would make the Lunars look bad even without Sidereals, and so don't like it as an element grafted onto them to give the Sidereals a punching bag. I'd much rather that the Sidereals be literally and figuratively punching the Lunars directly, as aided more by things like having the heavily equipped and world-spanning structure of the Shogunate to back them up or branch out in front of them, and the Usurpation meaning that Lunars started off in a position of weakness that the Sidereals were effectively able to make it really hard to rise out of.<br /> <br /> If it didn't have that, I wouldn't even care as much about the element of Sidereals being able to keep up the pressure because they were less harried (although I would still have trouble fully reconciling that with my preferred vision of the Shogunate, but that's an issue to be resolved elsewhere).<br /> <br /> As long as Lunars didn't have a detail of &quot;the first thing that a lot of them tried was building bag armies&quot; hanging around their neck, I would be perfectly okay with things like a lot of Lunars that would have liked to build big armies continuously coming to places where the Sidereals got there first, and poisoned the well against them.<br /> <br /> \u2026 And a bit of nasty sabotage. Some ways to texture it so that it feels sufficiently different from Lunar methods of the same, not too front and centre to keep it from feeling too much like the Celestial Exalted competing with the same methods, and there's still a place for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite a lot of the heat that Lunars are building in this edition is stolen from Sidereals, which makes them look like chumps. Worse, the heat that's being built for <i>the Dragon-blooded</i> is also, if less directly, being drawn from Sidereals, by making the Realm less dependent on their guidance. I actually strongly approve of that...but it does contribute to Sidereals looking ineffectual, and that I do not approve of.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Lunars... I sincerely want to know how it is seen so, so that I don't feel as though I'm flailing or strawmanning.<br /> <br /> For the Realm... how much did the books in the prior Editions attribute to Sidereals anyway? The Dragon Blooded books have always been Terrestrials first and foremost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By &quot;an outside perspective&quot;, I meant you and me, the fans of Exalted, reading sourcebooks from Earth. I apologize if that was unclear. What I meant was that we, the readers, need to have examples of Sidereals doing things even if other in-setting actors don't realize that's what's going on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would be very happy if we got more of this, yes. But I do want to point out that it's needed, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I misread &quot;or&quot; as a connection to a contrast, rather than a causal sequence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T23:23:21-08:00","id":1270534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270518#post1270518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...the fuck did I mean by this? Did I just mix up the proper nouns, or... have something else in mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>I frankly have no idea. I read it as an acknowledgement of my point, since that's something that's been bugging me for a while, but I'll expand on that below; no need to do it twice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270518#post1270518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you phrase it in pejorative terms, you're actively denigrating a play style that is valid enough to have gotten an entry in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>This comes across as trying to punch a hole in an argument I'm not making, in a really nitpicky way. A playstyle can be supported without being the only playstyle supported, if that makes sense. I agree completely that string-pulling should be a Sidereal theme, something they're good at, and a major tool in their toolbox. I don't think they should be portrayed as if it's the only thing they can do, and I think that's important for showing how Sidereals act and interact with other Exalted in particular. I personally don't particularly like the kind of playstyle where a character's primary means of asserting agency is through their minions, so I don't feel particularly bad about being a little pejorative about it, but my point is that it should be a subset of Sidereal capabilities rather than the entire set.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270518#post1270518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder about that... the question of how frequently, outside of their hardbacks, many Exalted ever got described in heavy detail at all. Like in setting sourcebooks, if they were generally intent on describing the stage rather than some of the particular actors.<br /> <br /> And from there, maybe analyse the premise that the Sidereal hardbacks didn't sufficiently describe them as hands on either.<br /> <br /> That's not so much suggesting that the sentiment is incorrect as analysis of the context.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication here being that we should wait for the Sidereal hardback to fix this problem? Nah, I don't buy it. We've had plenty of examples of Lunars being badasses in the corebook and DB book and I expect we'll see more in The Realm, as well as their own hardback.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270518#post1270518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as Lunars didn't have a detail of &quot;the first thing that a lot of them tried was building bag armies&quot; hanging around their neck, I would be perfectly okay with things like a lot of Lunars that would have liked to build big armies continuously coming to places where the Sidereals got there first, and poisoned the well against them.<br /> <br /> \u2026 And a bit of nasty sabotage. Some ways to texture it so that it feels sufficiently different from Lunar methods of the same, not too front and centre to keep it from feeling too much like the Celestial Exalted competing with the same methods, and there's still a place for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I picked the big-societal-army thing because that's one of their major tactics in the modern age, as far as I can tell, and I wanted a clear path between &quot;we tried this in the heyday of the Shogunate and it didn't work&quot; to &quot;now our enemies are disorganized enough that we can try this again and it will work&quot; as a way to emphasize the degree to which the Contagion favored the Lunars and turned their fortunes around. So it's not something I saw grafted on so much as something I was trying to draw a historical line of descent for, knowing that it already existed. I honestly don't share your aesthetic objection, but tastes differ, and I don't have a strong feeling about Lunar aesthetics in general.<br /> <br /> That said, the important thing to me is twofold. One is how Sidereals are portrayed, as awesome and scary and effectual, as I've said before. The other, related, is that the Lunar war machine (or, more accurately, the numerous distinct Lunar war machines) should be portrayed as potentially vulnerable to disruption of various kinds, and that their enemies have been attacking those points of failure. I don't particularly care about the existence or nonexistence of weaponizing societies on the edge of the world during the Shogunate if there's an alternative that still fulfills those criteria.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270518#post1270518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Lunars... I sincerely want to know how it is seen so, so that I don't feel as though I'm flailing or strawmanning.<br /> <br /> For the Realm... how much did the books in the prior Editions attribute to Sidereals anyway? The Dragon Blooded books have always been Terrestrials first and foremost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I'm going to try to distill the strong impression I have into concrete examples, but I can't go fish for quotes since Nishkriya is down, so keep in mind that this is my own perception, and some of it's from exposure to the community instead of all being word of dev, and I can't readily distinguish which is which at the moment.<br /> <br /> * There's a relatively well-known quote going around that Lunars are the number-one cause of death of Sidereals, and that the reverse is not true. It's easy enough to say that this just means that Sidereals don't lead most Wyld Hunts, but it's a bit of an unfortunate implication that's never been corrected to my knowledge, regarding the outcome of Lunar/Sidereal clashes. The latter was backed up under the previous devs by some commentary about how going into Creation is like entering Vietnam for Sidereals because of the potential for Lunar attacks.<br /> * The Caul was originally conceived as a place where the Lunars had built their own Loom of Fate. This has, fortunately, been retconned (in the Q&amp;A thread, if not explicitly), but it lingered in the public consciousness for quite a while, and was flat-out one of the biggest heat-thefts I could imagine. It's certainly possible that this being one of the first things I learned about 3E Lunars has tainted my perception of how they're written.<br /> * Lunar infiltrators on the Blessed Isle are common enough to be mentioned prominently in the corebook, despite Sidereal and Terrestrial defenses. This has led to a perception that Lunars can easily slide past Sidereal and Dynastic vigilance, even though foresight and preparation are supposed to be Sidereal strong points; we even had a thread about this not long ago, asking how Realm generals even survived on the march.<br /> * To an extent, Lunars being set up as opponents to Sidereals and then being shown operating freely, without concern about Sidereal interference or disruption, means that Sidereals suddenly look pretty ineffectual. If Lunars are only ever shown on the offensive (and that's all we've seen so far to my knowledge; I challenge you to name a major Lunar defeat after the Usurpation) then their opponents naturally look toothless.<br /> * A contributing factor is that we've seen a lot of New Cool Mechanics Stuff for Lunars, but Sidereals tend to get the worst of that so far. They're the worst by far at Evocations, they're not getting any new tiers of sorcery or necromancy (that we know of; it's not likely but I can still hope), they don't get consistent Mastery in martial arts or the ability to combine it with their native Charms, and their Charmset is still closed. The devs have not been encouraging on the idea of them getting anything shiny and new this edition, other than a Charmset expansion (which, don't get me wrong, will help!). Meanwhile Lunars get the revision to animals which gives shapeshifting real combat teeth, the ability to take on Legendary Size in battle at chargen, a new tier of necromancy, and all kinds of thematic expansion leading to nifty new tricks. I know that the Sidereal book is still in the planning stages and at least two years out, and I know I'm comparing that to a splat who's in the middle of its hype cycle, but it still contributes to my perception, you know? Mechanical heat is still heat.<br /> <br /> As for Terrestrials, as I said, it's mostly more indirect effects of other changes and a general shift of emphasis away from Sidereals taking an actively guiding and supporting role in the Realm. The Wyld Hunt has moved from an institution primarily directed by Sidereals to something the Dragon-Blooded operate by and for themselves; few if any houses have active contact with and support of the Fivescore Fellowship (whereas House Ledaal, for one, once had significant Sidereal involvement in previous editions; I don't remember my Aspect-books well enough to name others, but that one I remember). Let me emphasize again that I like these changes; I think it's great that the writing is focusing on the Terrestrials for themselves instead of how they dance on the strings of outside interests, howevermuch those outside interests align with their own. But since we don't have much to show what Sidereals have been doing since the Usurpation other than advising and guiding the Realm, when that gets deemphasized, it leaves a hole in their accomplishments.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I'll admit the possibility that I'm blowing stuff out of proportion, but that's more or less my position on heat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T00:21:30-08:00","id":1270538,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that 3e has a few references to Dragon-Blooded imprisoning Anathema, so even if they could convince the younger Lunars to engage in kamikaze attacks it might not work out as planned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T01:31:30-08:00","id":1270553,"title":"","content":"Well, you don't post for a day or two and 3 more pages appear!<br /> <br /> <br /> I think I was the very first person to mention Lunar attrition in relation to Dragonblood attrition on this thread, when I was talking about the Contagion, and how it was a much bigger problem for the Dragonblood (who are harder to replace the less of them there are) than the Lunars.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that necessarily leads into Lunar leaders saying &quot;we will win via Lunar vs Dragonblood attrition&quot; (I think they're not that bothered about beating the Realm's legions with barbarian armies using attrition; that's basically their overall strategy).<br /> <br /> Partly because, unlike just after the Shogunate, they're massively outnumbered by Dragonblood, partly because it's a bad tactic (because of the loss of skills*), partly because who'd want to join up with that strategy.<br /> <br /> *In WW2, Britain and America's air forces improved over time. The Japanese air force got worse. The reason is that the Japanese used their best pilots to fly missions, where they died. The Americans and British retired a lot of good pilots after a certain amount of missions and used them as trainers for new pilots. So over time, the Japanese air force lost its skills and ended up with badly-trained pilots. This is one of the reasons for the increasing use of Kamikaze. Which, you'll note, did not win them the war.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying that, I'm sure the Lunar elders are aware that, over the long term, a lot of Lunars are going to die, and get replaced. But that doesn't mean they actually think suicide attacks are a good idea. I mean, when they're the elite of the elite, while Dragonblood are merely the elite, what Dragonblood elder is actually worth a suicide attack anyway? The Empress maybe... other than that, I don't think anyone's really worth it. Not even Mnemon.<br /> <br /> Real-world guerilla movements who use suicide bombers don't use their leaders and best fighters.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the Shogunate; I'd think that building barbarian armies would probably be the worst tactic for the Lunars. Against a world-spanning Empire with massive armies whose advisors see the future? No, I think the Shogunate, as the Lunars' weakest time, would be when they were most forced into guerilla tactics, infiltration, assassination, sabotage.<br /> Barbarian armies is probably much more a post-Contagion thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Last of all, on Sidereals, I think it's worth noting there's about 5 times as many Lunars as Sidereals. And there's a fair few Sidereals who actually are not interested in fighting Lunars (unfortunately, the Lunars are quite interested in fighting them, as shouting &quot;I'm not Bronze Faction!&quot; probably isn't going to stop a vengeful were-boar who wants to rip you apart and stomp on your remains). That could be because they're Gold Faction, but more likely it's because they're trying to just get on with their job of making sure demons don't ravage the countryside and people don't meet themselves yesterday-tomorrow, become their own grandfather, or find that their kitchen in Nexus is now in the Southern Middlemarches.<br /> <br /> <br /> So we're probably talking about 40 Sidereals vs, say, 300 Lunars (the other 100 Lunars being ones who don't care about the Sidereals or the Realm, they've got their own stuff going on). Honestly, if the Sidereals are not being crushed utterly and living in constant fear of Lunar assassins, I think they're looking pretty good.<br /> <br /> To put it another way -<br /> <br /> The Sidereals are the secret masters of the world. They are experts of esoteric martial arts and prophecy, advisors behind the throne, agents of order and causality who stop the world falling to the Wyld and the Dead. They are led by some of the world's greatest sorcerers and martial artists. But how can less than 100 beings, powerful as they are, protect an entire world?<br /> <br /> <br /> If one Sidereal martial artist was powerful enough to take 2 or even 3 Lunars in a fight, they'd still be in deep trouble because that isn't enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-25-2018, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T01:38:47-08:00","id":1270554,"title":"","content":"One last thing to consider. Not sure about this, but I thought it was interesting:<br /> <br /> My ST was wondering why the Lunars and Sidereals don't unleash WMDs on each other; Moonsilver or Starmetal warstriders, Celestial Circle Sorcery (you can kill an army with Cantata of Empty Voices), etc.<br /> <br /> So he decided that they have a MAD policy. Generally, the Sidereals let the Realm and the Lunars battle it out. But if the Lunars bring out the big guns, that's when the Sidereals intervene, unleashing their artefacts, Celestial sorcery, Sidereal Martial Arts and so on.<br /> <br /> (I suppose you could say this is what happened with the Bull of the North; Samea brought out the Second Circle Demons, they used warstriders, etc, and that's what led to Sidereals destroying an entire pro-Bull city with sorcery, which they don't generally do)<br /> <br /> This means that generally the Lunars stay to more subtle tactics, or just armies of barbarians, when fighting the Realm. But when they're much further away, in places where the Sidereals are less likely to go due to lack of Dragonblood support, they're more likely to unleash their more overt powers.<br /> <br /> And, rarely, one side or the other think it's worth it anyway, and that's when you get Sidereal vs Lunar deathmatches, swathes of magical devastation, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T03:48:29-08:00","id":1270562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270534#post1270534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally don't particularly like the kind of playstyle where a character's primary means of asserting agency is through their minions, so I don't feel particularly bad about being a little pejorative about it</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The implication here being that we should wait for the Sidereal hardback to fix this problem? Nah, I don't buy it. We've had plenty of examples of Lunars being badasses in the corebook and DB book and I expect we'll see more in The Realm, as well as their own hardback.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. If there's a model in place for that kind of thing to play out going forward, then I agree that it should make room for Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Do you think Arms of the Chosen does a decent job? It attributes a fair number of Artifacts to Sidereals, or otherwise includes them in their stories.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* There's a relatively well-known quote going around that Lunars are the number-one cause of death of Sidereals, and that the reverse is not true. It's easy enough to say that this just means that Sidereals don't lead most Wyld Hunts, but it's a bit of an unfortunate implication that's never been corrected to my knowledge, regarding the outcome of Lunar/Sidereal clashes. The latter was backed up under the previous devs by some commentary about how going into Creation is like entering Vietnam for Sidereals because of the potential for Lunar attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of people read implications into that which didn't particularly make sense, regarding the idea that it meant that Sidereals dying of anything at all was particularly common. There were complementary comments from those developers showing that they thought it was not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* The Caul was originally conceived as a place where the Lunars had built their own Loom of Fate. This has, fortunately, been retconned (in the Q&amp;A thread, if not explicitly), but it lingered in the public consciousness for quite a while, and was flat-out one of the biggest heat-thefts I could imagine. It's certainly possible that this being one of the first things I learned about 3E Lunars has tainted my perception of how they're written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something has to make it to publication before it can be retconned. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I disagree that such a development was harmful to Sidereals, but I can see where you're coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Lunar infiltrators on the Blessed Isle are common enough to be mentioned prominently in the corebook, despite Sidereal and Terrestrial defenses. This has led to a perception that Lunars can easily slide past Sidereal and Dynastic vigilance, even though foresight and preparation are supposed to be Sidereal strong points; we even had a thread about this not long ago, asking how Realm generals even survived on the march.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one touches on the unresolved question of how far the reach of the Sidereals should be, and I think may be biased a bit in favour of the Sidereals. They <i>do</i> need some mechanism for action and intelligence gathering while they're in Yu-Shan, sure, but if that extends to the point of being able to largely cordon off a very large landmass from afar, I think that is too much. Even if there are a few Sidereals resident on the Isle, it becomes a question of what they're doing and how far they can see.<br /> <br /> The shores of the Blessed Isle include a lot of poorer prefectures where the eyes of the Dynasts hardly ever go; those seem like viable entry points for somebody that can crawl out of the ocean and shift through the various evolutionary stages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* To an extent, Lunars being set up as opponents to Sidereals and then being shown operating freely, without concern about Sidereal interference or disruption, means that Sidereals suddenly look pretty ineffectual. If Lunars are only ever shown on the offensive (and that's all we've seen so far to my knowledge; I challenge you to name a major Lunar defeat after the Usurpation) then their opponents naturally look toothless.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Caul disappearing, and the fact that since it came back it has repeatedly had the full pilgrimage route under the control of the Realm, seem like major defeats to me. The many supposed deaths of Sha'a Oka might as well, depending on the details.<br /> <br /> The notion that the Sidereals seem toothless if Lunars aren't afraid of them all the time is rather problematic. Even then, I expect the full Fangs book to have a more complex approach to the subject of them.<br /> <br /> Indeed, considering the subject matter... I know that there are people who would say that a Lunars book is the place to talk them up and make them look impressive, and not the place to give props to their enemies, but I say such references establish their stakes and their background and gives a sense to Storytellers of what their challenges should be. So yeah, this is absolutely a good chance to describe things that the Sidereals do, both in terms of the kinds of projects that Lunars might target, and ways that they are threats to Lunars. If that isn't in the book, then I will be right there with you on there being a problem with the portrayal of Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">* A contributing factor is that we've seen a lot of New Cool Mechanics Stuff for Lunars, but Sidereals tend to get the worst of that so far. They're the worst by far at Evocations, they're not getting any new tiers of sorcery or necromancy (that we know of; it's not likely but I can still hope), they don't get consistent Mastery in martial arts or the ability to combine it with their native Charms, and their Charmset is still closed. The devs have not been encouraging on the idea of them getting anything shiny and new this edition, other than a Charmset expansion (which, don't get me wrong, will help!). Meanwhile Lunars get the revision to animals which gives shapeshifting real combat teeth, the ability to take on Legendary Size in battle at chargen, a new tier of necromancy, and all kinds of thematic expansion leading to nifty new tricks. I know that the Sidereal book is still in the planning stages and at least two years out, and I know I'm comparing that to a splat who's in the middle of its hype cycle, but it still contributes to my perception, you know? Mechanical heat is still heat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... Lunars need it. Even in the bad realisation of Second Edition, the basic concepts of the Sidereal stuff was still cool, and that's the foundation on which a future development can work on. The Evocations thing strikes me as referring back to an early established point of Sidereals being highly focused in what they do and how.<br /> <br /> Lunars have been underserved in the past, so they need the development and the hype for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T04:04:45-08:00","id":1270564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270483#post1270483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sidereal replacement process is a bit worse than Lunars, in that they have to wait until the candidate matures; but at least they have the ability to track and train them while the wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in canon it can seem like that. Personal headcanon is that there are actually a lot more hidden benefits to Sidereals being &quot;bespoke&quot; tailored up by the Maidens from (and before birth), with Sidereals happening to have complementary skills* that boost their effectiveness, and more relevant early life experiences that happen to come up later and stuff like that. All things that boost their effectiveness very slightly beyond their numbers, that make it worth it for the Maidens to use the way to Exalt their chosen that they do.<br /> <br /> Personal headcanon though, I just sort of dislike the meme that the way the Sidereals are replaced with probably a longer &quot;cycle&quot; is a strictly worse, weakening thing, for them, compared to the Solars and Lunars, and so I'm interested in emphasizing the ways it might not be!<br /> <br /> *not in the sense of being better at working together exactly in the sense of morale and liking each other, indeed sometimes in the opposite direction, but just turning out more effective (including rivalries that push them up, etc.).<br /> <br /> Also: edit, yeah, it seems like I've misread the comments on Lunar attrition generally, or something got lost along the way, and the last page has clarified / rebalanced a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":929,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","user":"Ghosthead","date":". 11-25-2018, 07:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T04:26:38-08:00","id":1270566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270562#post1270562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a good point. If there's a model in place for that kind of thing to play out going forward, then I agree that it should make room for Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Do you think Arms of the Chosen does a decent job? It attributes a fair number of Artifacts to Sidereals, or otherwise includes them in their stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did think Arms does a reasonable job of this (and, more generally, I really liked the book). I would've liked to see a starmetal warstrider, though, just to see what crazy shit it was capable of. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270562#post1270562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of people read implications into that which didn't particularly make sense, regarding the idea that it meant that Sidereals dying of anything at all was particularly common. There were complementary comments from those developers showing that they thought it was not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to say you're wrong about this, especially since it's a lot harder to come up with references at the moment, but I will say I somehow managed to miss those quotes completely. Which could well be on me, of course. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270562#post1270562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one touches on the unresolved question of how far the reach of the Sidereals should be, and I think may be biased a bit in favour of the Sidereals. They <i>do</i> need some mechanism for action and intelligence gathering while they're in Yu-Shan, sure, but if that extends to the point of being able to largely cordon off a very large landmass from afar, I think that is too much. Even if there are a few Sidereals resident on the Isle, it becomes a question of what they're doing and how far they can see.<br /> <br /> The shores of the Blessed Isle include a lot of poorer prefectures where the eyes of the Dynasts hardly ever go; those seem like viable entry points for somebody that can crawl out of the ocean and shift through the various evolutionary stages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I think it should be roughly as difficult for the Lunars to have agents in the heart of their enemies' power as it is for the Sidereals (Dragon-blooded can have more issues, due to secret agent games not being as core to their themes as the other two.) Granted that this means Yu Shan rather than the Realm per se -- but I've seen some dev commentary and a fair bit of community speculation that Lunars should be able to get agents into Heaven as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270562#post1270562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Caul disappearing, and the fact that since it came back it has repeatedly had the full pilgrimage route under the control of the Realm, seem like major defeats to me. The many supposed deaths of Sha'a Oka might as well, depending on the details.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit I didn't count the Caul since the story of &quot;ceaseless back-and-forth fighting&quot; doesn't really lend itself to decisive victories, and I seem to have missed the part where its disappearance was due to the actions of the Lunars' enemies somehow, but okay, fair enough. Sha'a Oka doesn't count until he's dead for good, though. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270562#post1270562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The notion that the Sidereals seem toothless if Lunars aren't afraid of them all the time is rather problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also an exaggeration of what I was saying, fortunately. My argument was actually the converse: Sidereals seem toothless when Lunars aren't afraid of them any of the time, especially when Sidereals are definitely afraid of Lunars some or most of the time. It does a disservice to both of them if the fear (or respect, or caution, or whatever) only goes one way, but that's all we've seen so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270562#post1270562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even then, I expect the full Fangs book to have a more complex approach to the subject of them.<br /> <br /> Indeed, considering the subject matter... I know that there are people who would say that a Lunars book is the place to talk them up and make them look impressive, and not the place to give props to their enemies, but I say such references establish their stakes and their background and gives a sense to Storytellers of what their challenges should be. So yeah, this is absolutely a good chance to describe things that the Sidereals do, both in terms of the kinds of projects that Lunars might target, and ways that they are threats to Lunars. If that isn't in the book, then I will be right there with you on there being a problem with the portrayal of Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I genuinely hope that you don't need to be. And I have some reason to be hopeful for that, given that What Fire Has Wrought struck what I thought was a nice balance of making Terrestrials look impressive while still doing what you're talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270562#post1270562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... Lunars need it. Even in the bad realisation of Second Edition, the basic concepts of the Sidereal stuff was still cool, and that's the foundation on which a future development can work on. The Evocations thing strikes me as referring back to an early established point of Sidereals being highly focused in what they do and how.<br /> <br /> Lunars have been underserved in the past, so they need the development and the hype for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who played a Sidereal for half a decade or more under 2E, I dearly hope you're not claiming they weren't underserved. :P Not just because their mechanics were broken (goose, accordion, stairs, you remember the metaphor), but because the closed Charmset meant that when other Exalts got new content, Sidereals got...a martial arts style, if they were lucky, until Greater Astrology showed up, and don't get me started on <i>that</i>. I'm not saying Lunars weren't underserved, and don't need what they're getting, but I am saying that Sidereals had it pretty rough too, especially in 2E.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T05:35:18-08:00","id":1270574,"title":"","content":"Re; big barbarian armies, this is probably well verging into personal headcanon, but I would tend to see them perhaps in the light that they are things which happen among mortals and which Lunars infiltrate and use, perhaps more than, y'know, large hordes of beastmen and things like that.<br /> <br /> To explain: It seems to me that barbarian armies are going to be a fact of life for the Realm, whether the Lunars are involved or not - there are going to be a lot of regions that border somewhere rich but don't couldn't pay for themselves in taxes, extraction and trade but can support fairly militarized populations (large shares of the population who spend a lot of time fighting each other), and afford to import weapons and such enough to be a threat to the richer places the Realm dominates.<br /> <br /> The Realm can make such place border marches under garrisons, but this imposes costs of paying all those soldiers, and also the costs of &quot;No one can pay me enough to be posted to Hadrian's Wall&quot; where soldiers really want to be back in the capital and part of civilization, so you have to really pay to recreate &quot;civilized&quot; life out there, and get the locals to buy into this all as well. You don't want a gaggle of bored soldiers who pile a litany of abuses on the locals and inflame rebellion and conflict, before marching back themselves in rebellion against the core empire or its rich provinces!<br /> <br /> Often it's just cheaper to let these places be, and even pay them off.... but in the longer term that inspires flareups of opportunistic hordes, particularly when the pay offs become tight, and this coincides with general reductions in how much jade the Realm has about on the whole and so the legions it can pay. Then you get barbarian armies.<br /> <br /> That is, I expect, often when the Lunars get involved. They infiltrate silently, or if they can, join publicly, taking control or &quot;advising&quot; in various degrees of overtness (depending on how open the cultural beliefs are to them, how much they can engineer it, the competency of the mortal leaders in play). They have the supernatural skills and the access to supernatural allies (perhaps including their own elite beastman child heroes?) enough to give mortals a complement of magical forces that can make them more vital threats against the Realm and the magic it can bring to bear, and offer a &quot;partnership&quot; that's hard for barbarian leaders to refuse.<br /> <br /> I'd see a fair amount of groundwork building before that; building the base of skepticism that allows them to operate without troublesome Immaculate beliefs and building the conditions that make these forces likely to happen together, and smaller forces that the Realm seems as unconnected join together to make a larger horde.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that seems to me like a reasonable compromise on the idea that Lunars build barbarian hordes from scratch, in the knowledge they'll be sacrificed (like &quot;donkeys leading lions&quot;), which seems rather callous and makes them committed, particularly in ways that are perhaps boring to play, with the opposing idea that they're rarely involved in barbarian armies. There might be something very wrong with it though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T06:38:06-08:00","id":1270584,"title":"","content":"Since people are trying to remember it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Lunars are the leading cause of Sidereal mortality, and one of the leading causes of Dragon-Blooded mortality. They're active and they're scary.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Also how do Lunars even find Sidereals? Sids have the backing of heaven, the support of the most powerful nation on the planet and officially don't exist to like 99 percent of the population of creation. What tools and abilities do lunars have that let them overcome these problems to get that leading cause of death slot?</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">For the most part, Lunars don't go looking for Sidereals. Rather, they kill Sidereals who come after them as part of a Wyld Hunt (or, occasionally, who wander into their neck of the woods while unsnarling the tangles of destiny). These battles are on the Lunars' own turf.<br /> <br /> (Also, Lunars are shapeshifting witch-demigods. They are not wholly lacking in supernatural talent or mundane support.)</span></div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be safe to say that in the conext of &quot;Lunars are the leading cause of Sidereal death&quot; has a caveat that Sidereals, as a whole, probably don't die all that often to begin with?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ceasing to Exist Approach makes tracking those numbers a real pain in the ass.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T06:48:04-08:00","id":1270586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270574#post1270574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To explain: It seems to me that barbarian armies are going to be a fact of life for the Realm, whether the Lunars are involved or not - there are going to be a lot of regions that border somewhere rich but don't couldn't pay for themselves in taxes, extraction and trade but can support fairly militarized populations (large shares of the population who spend a lot of time fighting each other), and afford to import weapons and such enough to be a threat to the richer places the Realm dominates.<br /> <br /> The Realm can make such place border marches under garrisons, but this imposes costs of paying all those soldiers, and also the costs of &quot;No one can pay me enough to be posted to Hadrian's Wall&quot; where soldiers really want to be back in the capital and part of civilization, so you have to really pay to recreate &quot;civilized&quot; life out there, and get the locals to buy into this all as well. You don't want a gaggle of bored soldiers who pile a litany of abuses on the locals and inflame rebellion and conflict, before marching back themselves in rebellion against the core empire or its rich provinces!<br /> <br /> Often it's just cheaper to let these places be, and even pay them off.... but in the longer term that inspires flareups of opportunistic hordes, particularly when the pay offs become tight, and this coincides with general reductions in how much jade the Realm has about on the whole and so the legions it can pay. Then you get barbarian armies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by descriptions of the businesses of Cathak, Tepet and Sesus, and some historical examples of how several Chinese dynasties engaged with northern pastoral nomads (other than the times that they did indeed pay them off), I kind of expect that the Realm finds a much preferable option to maintaining permanent garrisons to be periodically sending in legions to kill and enslave large numbers of people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T06:50:01-08:00","id":1270587,"title":"","content":"There's also probably tributary relations with some, like the Delzahn and the Medoans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T07:11:26-08:00","id":1270589,"title":"","content":"Taking that as vastly the preferred MO, not something I like from verisimilitude or fitting too much with my preferred visions of how the Realm operates, but it's kind of up for grabs, and its their risk of Teutoburg Forests to bear if that's what they want to do all the time with not much variation in tactics and strategy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T08:11:59-08:00","id":1270603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270587#post1270587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also probably tributary relations with some, like the Delzahn and the Medoans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are both satrapies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270589#post1270589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking that as vastly the preferred MO, not something I like from verisimilitude or fitting too much with my preferred visions of how the Realm operates, but it's kind of up for grabs, and its their risk of Teutoburg Forests to bear if that's what they want to do all the time with not much variation in tactics and strategy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the absence of Lunar Exalted, the Teutoberg Forest is probably more difficult when the marching legion has about eighty Dragon Blooded with it.<br /> <br /> Is your preferred vision of the Realm one that manages to empire without consistently murdering large numbers of people?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T08:21:13-08:00","id":1270605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270603#post1270603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the absence of Lunar Exalted, the Teutoberg Forest is probably more difficult when the marching legion has about eighty Dragon Blooded with it.<br /> <br /> Is your preferred vision of the Realm one that manages to empire without consistently murdering large numbers of people?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lot of Dragonblooed. Not really no, not much more or less than the Roman, Chinese, etc. empires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T09:07:15-08:00","id":1270615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270605#post1270605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a lot of Dragonblooed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the number supported by canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T09:27:49-08:00","id":1270617,"title":"","content":"Fair enough - not a number I've ever seen or internalised I guess, and not one I could find when checking through the source I'd expect it. 1e didn't bother giving a numbers of Dragonblooded per legion in its legion writeup in core / Dragonblooded book, while 2e offered:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Imperial Army\u2019s high commanders would like for every legion to have all its officers be Dragon-Blooded, but in fact, this is impossible\u2014the legions could commission every Exalt in the Realm and still need more officers. So the army makes do with what it can get. Each legion\u2019s commanding general and her 10 dragonlords are always Dragon-Blooded, and these <b>11 senior officers</b> become both the foundation and the leadership of the legion. From time to time, a legion may have as many as <b>50 or 60 Terrestrial Exalts in its ranks, but this is unusual</b>.&quot;</i> (Core, page 37)<br /> <br /> So about 11 varying to 50-60 in times of extremity.<br /> <br /> Still if the numbers have gone way up and 80 is the average case in 3e, it's the case.<br /> <br /> However, I still don't think it's good strategy for them to always respond in the way described and that it &quot;lacks nuance&quot; as some would say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T09:29:04-08:00","id":1270619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270483#post1270483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar replacement process <i>sucks</i> compared to Dynastic Dragonblooded. The Silver Pact trades in one trained Lunar for a complete unknown newbie. There is only the vague 'passed life' connection between each excarnation, and only Luna knows where or <i>when</i> the successor will appear.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile every adventurous Dynastic Dragonblood that leaves the Blessed Isle <i>already</i> has replacements being raised among their cousins or siblings if not children. New Dynasts have a connection of familial emotion and traditions to the old, and may well <i>know</i> their elder. This steady rate of trained replacements only encounters glitches with exceptional circumstances -- such as the Tepet expedition. And they can draw on Lost Eggs to replenish.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal replacement process is a bit worse than Lunars, in that they have to wait until the candidate matures; but at least they have the ability to track and train them while the wait.<br /> <br /> So, no, Lunars don't win when they trade exalted lives. Lunars win when they erode the Realm's <i>influence</i>, exhast its more <i>irreplacable</i> resources, and erode faith in the Immaculate traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a note on the Lunar Exaltation too, is that it's not like 400 Exaltations are up and ready every single time as soon as possible. If Luna doesn't have anyone around she thinks fits her bill, they aren't getting Exalted. This is why there's usually the vageuly 300-400 Exaltations thing instead of just 400 this edition. It very might be that there are dozens of Exaltations which have not had anyone Luna found worthy to let inherit.<br /> <br /> This is a big gamble for Lunars then in context of losing bodies. You get a newbie in replacement, and you don't even really know when you'll ever get them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 11-25-2018, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T09:41:51-08:00","id":1270621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270617#post1270617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough - not a number I've ever seen or internalised I guess, and not one I could find when checking through the source I'd expect it. 1e didn't bother giving a numbers of Dragonblooded per legion in its legion writeup in core / Dragonblooded book, while 2e offered:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The Imperial Army\u2019s high commanders would like for every legion to have all its officers be Dragon-Blooded, but in fact, this is impossible\u2014the legions could commission every Exalt in the Realm and still need more officers. So the army makes do with what it can get. Each legion\u2019s commanding general and her 10 dragonlords are always Dragon-Blooded, and these <b>11 senior officers</b> become both the foundation and the leadership of the legion. From time to time, a legion may have as many as <b>50 or 60 Terrestrial Exalts in its ranks, but this is unusual</b>.&quot;</i> (Core, page 37)<br /> <br /> So about 11 varying to 50-60 in times of extremity.<br /> <br /> Still if the numbers have gone way up and 80 is the average case in 3e, it's the case.<br /> <br /> However, I still don't think it's good strategy for them to always respond in the way described and that it &quot;lacks nuance&quot; as some would say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Teutoberg forest wasn't one legion, it was <i>three</i>. Assuming that 11 DBs is the bare minimum for an Imperial Legion and 50-60 is the optimistic case, 80 DBs for three legions sounds about right.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T09:50:37-08:00","id":1270622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270621#post1270621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Teutoberg forest wasn't one legion, it was <i>three</i>. Assuming that 11 DBs is the bare minimum for an Imperial Legion and 50-60 is the optimistic case, 80 DBs for three legions sounds about right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I understand the 2e excerpt to mean that 11 is the median, not the minumum.<br /> <br /> Generally as well, I mean, if a legion does have 80 Dragonblooded now in 3e I'm fine with that being the case and I was not right about that... but if the numbers are the same as 2e in 3e, going from &quot;A marching legion has 80 Dragonblooded&quot; to &quot;Actually they send in 3-4 legions anyway in any case of dealing with areas too troublesome to occupy (which I know for some reason?) so 80 Dragonblooded is sort of right despite not being what was said&quot; is a bit of an odd way to go about things defending that statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T10:45:15-08:00","id":1270634,"title":"","content":"Tbh, that quote looks more like 11 is the minimum than the median. DBs can be lower-ranked than Dragonlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T10:52:30-08:00","id":1270635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270603#post1270603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are both satrapies.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I probably should have said &quot;They do have tributary relations with some barbarian hordes&quot; rather than they &quot;probably have&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's also the Linowan, but while they're warlike barbarians* they're probably not really a horde. I don't think they have a history of uniting to invade anyone except the Haltans (which is probably the way the Realm likes it).<br /> <br /> *Barbarian is quite a culturally loaded term of course. But my point is that giant armies that invade city-and-farming-based satrapies, or tribes that raid them, can be brought under tenuous Realm control. As happened with the Delzahn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T10:59:10-08:00","id":1270637,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Yeah, OK, though that leaves the median pretty open wide, other than that it's typically above 11 and less than 50. Do you know where the 3e equivalent is that Alucard alludes to btw?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T11:27:54-08:00","id":1270647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270617#post1270617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough - not a number I've ever seen or internalised I guess, and not one I could find when checking through the source I'd expect it. 1e didn't bother giving a numbers of Dragonblooded per legion in its legion writeup in core / Dragonblooded book, while 2e offered</div> </div> </div> </div>The Second Edition corebook contains what might be my favourite write-up of the Realm published thus far, but I find its description of Exalted in the officer ranks of a legion to be significantly understated. I was probably overshooting it a little with eighty, but it's still likely to be several score. That's how certain First Edition writers described it, I recall that's how developers at several stages have said it would be put in The Realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I still don't think it's good strategy for them to always respond in the way described and that it &quot;lacks nuance&quot; as some would say.</div> </div> </div> </div>The nuanced view is that the ones doing it are recognisable people, people whom one might even like under different circumstances, rather than orcs. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Look at our shiny new signature Hearth of Dragon Blooded. I like all of those characters, I think some of them are outright adorable, and I find them all to be quite well-rounded and sympathetic.<br /> <br /> They're not written as disabusing the notion that they'd wipe out villages that were harbouring Anathema. The greatest objection that River has to the point is &quot;bristling&quot;.<br /> <br /> You say &quot;not a good strategy&quot;, but what's your value judgement on good here? One that achieves their goals? One that preserves their integrity? One that makes a priority out of not radicalising the local population such that, ten years later, they widely support an extremely severe theocracy?<br /> <br /> What I said before about authoritarians often being intrinsically bad at assessing the strength of enemies, that can apply here, and there's also a case where they can be bad at assessing the strength of themselves.<br /> <br /> And otherwise, whenever I bring something like this up, it's primarily because I think that it's sometimes not well remembered that wars whose express purpose is to kill large numbers of people, break down social institutions, as a pre-emptive measure. From the perspective of people on the ground, and with the mindset of a different era, it might not seem wholly unjustified; the idea that it's just silly to wait until somebody whom you're reasonably certain can be an aggressor based on past events or their current lifestyle, attacks you first once their numbers are devastating, before you pull in forces to defend yourself. People like that might think that it's not wrong to attack them first, and in a pre-modern context, your strategic targets to reduce their capacity to wage war upon you in future can't really be anything <i>but</i> human bodies.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm not suggesting the Realm periodically attacks peaceful people that were just minding their own business; you talked about &quot;barbarian armies&quot;, and I presume that in most cases the precursors to these armies are bands of semi-nomadic people who either have lifestyles based on raiding their neighbours, or are otherwise liable to get into personal or territorial disputes that can spill over into neighbouring regions valuable to Realm interests. Hence the idea that the Realm might see a threat that needs to be dealt with pre-emptively.<br /> <br /> (Although given the way that financial concerns intersect with military power in the Realm, there's probably also the occasional instance of &quot;Julius Caesar needs to enslave a million Gauls and steal gold from the rest, because his debts are <i>gargantuan</i>)<br /> <br /> And in the context of how the Realm isn't really much of a colonising power, so in a lot of cases garrisons (particularly the ones on a model of providing border defence, rather than being a nexus of military power over an area already under control) might be stretching their resources a bit. You talked about Hadrian's Wall, but that's an exceptional example in the overall Roman milieu. In a lot of cases with the Realm, where would they be building a wall that an enemy couldn't just walk around?<br /> <br /> Still, I'm not saying that it's something they would always do, just that they'd probably do a lot, and it might bear repeating if it's a model of war that many people won't readily intuit.<br /> <br /> ...Although I was probably too quick to dismiss the point about the victims' retaliation, since I'm also imagining this kind of thing as being where a lot of inhabitants of a Lunar Dominion come from. I maintain that if the argument is &quot;the Realm wouldn't do something that would make people into their enemies&quot;, than I think in the setting as written that ship has already sailed*, and it's a charge that the Realm might frequently respond to with a challenge to bring it on.<br /> <br /> There are definitely circumstances such as Chiroscuro and Fajad where it's seen as more productive to make concessions in the interests of stability, but these are surely the exceptions (especially with the current developmental mandate that having focused too much on the exceptions in the past made the Realm seem either toothless or reasonable, in contrast to the point it was intended to make).<br /> <br /> * Perhaps to the port city of Nansha.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T11:33:32-08:00","id":1270649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270635#post1270635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know. I probably should have said &quot;They do have tributary relations with some barbarian hordes&quot; rather than they &quot;probably have&quot;.<br /> <br /> There's also the Linowan, but while they're warlike barbarians* they're probably not really a horde. I don't think they have a history of uniting to invade anyone except the Haltans (which is probably the way the Realm likes it).<br /> <br /> *Barbarian is quite a culturally loaded term of course. But my point is that giant armies that invade city-and-farming-based satrapies, or tribes that raid them, can be brought under tenuous Realm control. As happened with the Delzahn.</div> </div> </div> </div>As written in previous Editions, the Delzhan distinctly got to Chiaroscuro <i>before</i> the Realm started establishing control over satrapies, and pre-emptively submitted to their authority in exchange for concessions. An arrangement that the Realm doesn't seem set up to have agreed to if they weren't dealing with one of the most lucrative port cities in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T13:14:02-08:00","id":1270670,"title":"","content":"Possibly there's less of an incentive for the Realm,* but it is an effective measure to ensure the Delzahn (who still have many members far from Chiaroscoro living their traditional life as horse nomads and raiders) raid non-Realm territories rather than Realm territories. (The Delzahn of course get the benefit of not being raided or invaded by the Realm. They know their Northern border is safe.)<br /> <br /> Medo is a lot less lucrative for the Realm, as Medo doesn't have much wealth, but they have evolved this janissary system where Medo supplies them with skilled auxiliary cavalry (which benefits Medoan tribes, as their warriors return battle-hardened and cosmopolitan).<br /> Originally of course, Medo did try and invade Realm territories, but the Realm defeated them and now these barbarian horsemen are under loose Realm control; not enough to give up their religion, but enough to supply troops and raid the Scavenger Lands rather than, say, the lands of House Ferem, which are relatively close to Medo. They can go raid Sijan and Port Calin instead, that'll teach the so-called Shogun of Port Calin to refuse the Realm's offers of protection.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Linowan doesn't provide huge benefits to the Realm, probably less than Medo. They don't have much to pay in tribute, except perhaps slaves and certain woods (but they're a society of fishermen, farmers and warriors, not loggers). But through its House Pelleps satrap, the Realm is able to wield influence over them, directing their aggression towards Halta and not Realm-aligned lands (like Medo, to the south). And all the Realm has to do is defend them against Anathema.<br /> (Which, recently, turned out to be way harder than House Tepet expected. Unless the canon's been changed so the Bull didn't invade Linowan, which is quite possible. I think Vance may have addressed it, but I forget.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Essentially, my overall idea is thinking of China's relations with steppes tribes; some areas you subjugate to make money, like the Tarim basin, but a lot of that land is poor. There's not much money to be made. But relations with them are still very important, because it's easier to send them some (possibly fake) princesses and help them against some other barbarians than have to constantly fight off invasions by a horde of horsemen.<br /> You may need to occasionally invade them, crush their armies, enslave thousands, etc, (as the Realm fought the Touman Prince), but that doesn't mean your relations need to always be hostile. Build cultural and trade links, and direct the horde to invade somewhere else.<br /> <br /> Various other Empires have done the same thing, establishing a buffer of allied &quot;barbarian warriors&quot; via political, religious, and trade links, encouraging them to concentrate on raiding your enemies instead of you. European powers in America with allied American federations (Britain's support of Native federations, arming them to raid the USA rather than Canada, was one of the reasons for the War of 1812), Russia's use of Cossacks and Tartars, the Eastern Roman Empire and Persia's use of Arab tribes against each other*, etc.<br /> <br /> *This one is notable because of the religious dimension. The Romans used Monophysite Arab tribes, the Persians used Nestorian and Jewish tribes. I can well see the Realm using a semi-Immaculate barbarian horde led by a savage Dragonblood outcaste as a buffer against, say, Lunar-worshipping tribes of beastmen.<br /> <br /> Often, the Empire is powerful enough to just invade, kill, and enslave, but that's expensive and leaves a void for another lot of barbarians to migrate into.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying this, I imagine this is the sort of debate Realm politicians might have. A nomadic horde is encroaching on strategically important territory. Do we send some forces to scare them off? Negotiate to bring them under our control, as happened with the Delzahn? Forcibly convert them to the Immaculate Faith? Or invade, crush them, kill the old, crippled and infants, and enslave the rest? Different houses and different Dragonblood will have different ideas. And as you mentioned, personal motives (like the general who has to decide has massive debts and desperately needs to make money via slaving) may push decisions to certain outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-25-2018, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T13:45:02-08:00","id":1270680,"title":"","content":"On the number of Dragonblood in a Legion;<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, at its height there were 80 Legions? And now it's down to about 30, a lot of which are under House control?<br /> <br /> So, if it was 80 a Legion, that'd be 6400 Dragonblood in the Legions at their height (let's say 50 years ago, long before the Battle of Futile Blood and the loss of most of the Caul) and 2400 now.<br /> <br /> If it's 11 per Legion, that'd be 880 at its height and about 300 now.<br /> <br /> The first number seems too high to me, and the second too low. So 11 as a minimum and maybe 30-40 as a normal number seems reasonable. So there's maybe 1000 Dragonblood currently serving in the legions, which is far below its height when about a quarter of Dragonblood were serving in the Legions at any one time.<br /> <br /> (But I might have remembered the number of Legions wrong, or the number of Dragonblood in the Realm. I think it's over 10000, but less than 15k? Anyone remember? The devs did say at some point.)<br /> <br /> Of course, it's not just purely a matter of overall demographics, but also this; if an Imperial Legion arrives to invade a place the PCs live, how many Dragonblood do you want? I think 11 is too low, but I think 80 is too high; they'd just become a featureless mass of generic officers. I think maybe 30 would be a very scary threat for PCs, but with enough to have a variety of interesting characters with a wide range of abilities.<br /> <br /> And I also think 30 is, frankly, enough that a Lunar is not going to want to attack them head on. Even 5 Lunars (which is a hell of a lot of Lunars) are going to want to be careful. 11 is not enough for a pack of Lunars to find very dangerous (it's quite dangerous for one, but I think the Dragonblood won't be in enough places at once to be a huge issue; essentially, they could maybe do minor sabotage to the Legion without being in huge, huge danger, though it depends on the Lunar), 80 is utterly overwhelming.<br /> <br /> So I think 20-40 probably leads to the best play experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T14:20:37-08:00","id":1270686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270680#post1270680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the number of Dragonblood in a Legion;<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, at its height there were 80 Legions? And now it's down to about 30, a lot of which are under House control?<br /> <br /> So, if it was 80 a Legion, that'd be 6400 Dragonblood in the Legions at their height (let's say 50 years ago, long before the Battle of Futile Blood and the loss of most of the Caul) and 2400 now.<br /> <br /> If it's 11 per Legion, that'd be 880 at its height and about 300 now.<br /> <br /> The first number seems too high to me, and the second too low. So 11 as a minimum and maybe 30-40 as a normal number seems reasonable. So there's maybe 1000 Dragonblood currently serving in the legions, which is far below its height when about a quarter of Dragonblood were serving in the Legions at any one time.<br /> <br /> (But I might have remembered the number of Legions wrong, or the number of Dragonblood in the Realm. I think it's over 10000, but less than 15k? Anyone remember? The devs did say at some point.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth keeping in mind that a lot of officers in the Realm legions are found eggs, and a lot of the Realm's outcastes will take the coin. So that can be a few thousand right there.<br /> <br /> I've generally assumed that the time when there were eighty legions was a time when the Realm had too many Dragon Blooded, and part of the point was to pare the numbers down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I also think 30 is, frankly, enough that a Lunar is not going to want to attack them head on. Even 5 Lunars (which is a hell of a lot of Lunars) are going to want to be careful. 11 is not enough for a pack of Lunars to find very dangerous (it's quite dangerous for one, but I think the Dragonblood won't be in enough places at once to be a huge issue; essentially, they could maybe do minor sabotage to the Legion without being in huge, huge danger, though it depends on the Lunar), 80 is utterly overwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will be interesting to see the description of how to handle Realm legions in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T23:47:23-08:00","id":1270780,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that'll be useful for a number of reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T03:53:59-08:00","id":1270797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270647#post1270647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say &quot;not a good strategy&quot;, but what's your value judgement on good here? One that achieves their goals? One that preserves their integrity? One that makes a priority out of not radicalising the local population such that, ten years later, they widely support an extremely severe theocracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just the inflexibility of what seemed to be &quot;always use punitive expeditions as the tactic&quot; (the impression I got, wrong or right) is what seems like a poor strategy for me, from a practical point of view, and a less interesting one, in terms of the Realm encompassing fewer of the tactics and strategies used by the empires from which it draws inspiration.<br /> <br /> But I think I may have had a more irritable and more distracted reaction to that point about whether the Realm pays off &quot;cooked barbarians&quot; to deal with &quot;raw barbarians&quot; than was necessary. And just as much I may have too much emphasized use of this strategy as common in my post you were quoting. (I don't see it as the only card up their sleeve, or always the best one, for sure). That's all less important to the more main point I was interested in. <br /> <br /> Whether or not they purely use punitive expeditions beyond the borders or a more flexible set of strategies, I'd contend regardless there are probably circumstances that create the formation of fair sized populations beyond where they actually rule, and that they try to avoid overreach in where they actually rule*. Whatever they do probably has some limitations in its effectiveness! Those circumstances lead to the formation of &quot;barbarian armies&quot; and I suspect that the Lunars (or at least the Lunars as I think are well written) would try to shepherd, use and complement those, without much of a need for them to be tied down in events creating them, in a way that feels contrary to their strategy as described and impinge of travel and adventure in Lunar actual play.<br /> <br /> Lots of other points in your post of interest, so will just say these are worthy factors to consider in the balance of the Realm using punitive/violent vs negotiating/allying strategies, in lieu of having more time, and given I'm kind of conceding to a bit more agnosticism on this point.<br /> <br /> The only point I'd like to immediately clarify on is my mention of &quot;Hadrian's Wall&quot; - I was not intending a general comment on the effectiveness of walls themselves (I was intending no stance on that!), but just to use it as an example of a far frontier posting to try and emphasise a human dimension of why it's difficult to maintain a fortified frontier (whether by walls, dispersed garrisons and forts, etc.).<br /> <br /> That soldiers are by default not going to be enthused about being posted to the limes far from &quot;civilization&quot;, in some marsh, desert, steppe, mountains, tundra, etc. and that keeping them happy and not rebellious can impose high costs by ending up with a massive export of your &quot;civilization&quot;. Example of Roman Britain - there's a lot of recreation of Roman society in Britain under Roman rule that basically seems to be quite arguably to serve officers posted there, and possibly at cost to the imperial government. Particularly that's the case if you're drawing them from your core (as Dragonblooded officers must be for example) rather than from local recruitment - e.g. again Roman use of Gaulish auxillaries in Britain.<br /> <br /> * Like, on overreach, preview from the Lunars devblog post - &quot;<i>Knowing that overreach would play into Lunar hands, she slowed the Realm\u2019s expansion to a crawl, tolerated greater independence in troublesome satrapies, and grew more reluctant to embark upon grand endeavors \u2014 subjugating the Scavenger Lands, reclaiming Prasad, seizing the West</i>&quot;, which suggests some understanding of the Lunar strategem (what they seek to achieve, and how they seek to achieve it, which is relevant to some of our discussion about how much the Realm and Sidereals are aware of what the Lunars are trying to do and actively work against it) and that the Empress is mitigating against it at least by checking territorial expansion.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a>, those calculations look pretty good to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T10:42:29-08:00","id":1270872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270534#post1270534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs have not been encouraging on the idea of them getting anything shiny and new this edition</div> </div> </div> </div>What about their remarks on astrology being shiny and new this edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T10:48:46-08:00","id":1270874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270534#post1270534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* A contributing factor is that we've seen a lot of New Cool Mechanics Stuff for Lunars, but Sidereals tend to get the worst of that so far. They're the worst by far at Evocations, they're not getting any new tiers of sorcery or necromancy (that we know of; it's not likely but I can still hope), they don't get consistent Mastery in martial arts or the ability to combine it with their native Charms, and their Charmset is still closed. The devs have not been encouraging on the idea of them getting anything shiny and new this edition, other than a Charmset expansion (which, don't get me wrong, will help!).</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason Sidereals aren't getting anything shiny and new in this edition is because what they got in First Edition is so dang solid\u2014an awesome Charmset, astrology, Sidereal Martial Arts\u2014that we don't need to add anything new to it, just give it some polish and shine to bring it up to the level of the rest of Ex3. They're my favorite type of Exalt, and I'm very excited about making their Ex3 debut just as cool as Lunars, Solars, and Dragon-Blooded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T10:51:29-08:00","id":1270877,"title":"","content":"I'll admit that I have biases around the idea of Realm expeditionary forces, which on this occasion I'll elect not to bore people with the details of. I think I can basically summarise it with the idea that, in the absence of major rival powers for the Realm to compete with at war, and in a system in which their expansionism is somewhat limited, I kind of want the legions to consistently have something to do, and I have reservations about the idea that they're constantly on the defensive because that has connotations of problematic narratives that empires use to justify themselves.<br /> <br /> Which <i>is</i> admittedly complicated by the point about how the Silver Pact (and some of the Fair Folk) actually are present in the setting to attack them in a manner resembling those narratives. Hell, I would find those details to actually reinforce the importance of the Realm asserting itself pro-actively and violently, since otherwise I fear the setting would lean too much in the direction of &quot;fantasy/sci-fi nation in which authoritarian militarism is justified by being encircled with an enemy that will continuously attack and cannot be reasoned with&quot;.<br /> <br /> But, again, even with that I have argued somewhat emphatically from a position of having certain biases in values and artistic preferences.<br /> <br /> I've... also probably lost sight of what I was really ever responding to. Whether this thread goes off on another topic or not, I think I'd like to take a moment to step back from this topic and go back over the last several posts to try and get a clearer picture, if my current one is distorted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T13:57:37-08:00","id":1270918,"title":"","content":"I like the Vanguard as a school that doesn't consider itself just another school within the Silver Path, and which is also radically different from how the other Lunars prefer to behave. Obviously there have to be some Lunars who would prefer a bit more social structure, and the writers covered the range of personalities (good and bad) which would gravitate towards that kind of school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T19:06:44-08:00","id":1271008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270874#post1270874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason Sidereals aren't getting anything shiny and new in this edition is because what they got in First Edition is so dang solid\u2014an awesome Charmset, astrology, Sidereal Martial Arts\u2014that we don't need to add anything new to it, just give it some polish and shine to bring it up to the level of the rest of Ex3. They're my favorite type of Exalt, and I'm very excited about making their Ex3 debut just as cool as Lunars, Solars, and Dragon-Blooded.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very happy to hear this, and I appreciate your response. But I do still feel some concern, so I want to lay out the reasons why, in the hopes that it might make clear where I'm coming from and why I'm fretting about my favorite Exalts.<br /> <br /> * I played with the 2E Sidereal Charmset extensively -- much more than I did the 1E Charmset. So when I hear &quot;we're basically giving Sidereals what they got in 1E, and not adding anything new&quot;, I reflexively cringe a little, because...well, hewing too closely to Sidereals 1E is kind of how we got Sidereals 2E, you know? Let me be clear that no part of me expects a disaster of that magnitude; the work I've seen on 3E, both on the line and general and on Arms of the Chosen and What Fire Has Wrought, has been superlative. But it does make me fret a bit, because...<br /> <br /> * ...all of the other classic Exalts have changed and grown and expanded in 3E so far. Dragon-Blooded got to use Charms of all elements with all abilities. Solars got to speak prophecy and learn the ways of spirits, as well as a whole new category of coolness in the form of Evocations and martial arts Mastery. Lunars we've been over in this thread. Compared to all of that, it's a little hard to swallow that 1E Sidereals were conceived so perfectly that nothing could be added or improved. Especially since...<br /> <br /> * ...3E, as a play environment, emphasizes the places where Sidereals are weak a lot more than previous editions did. The low-Essence period of the game gets a lot more focus, and Essence increases substantially slower; since Sidereal Excellencies are based on Essence, that's not great for them. Add that to the fact that they haven't traditionally had a lot of Charm choice per Ability, and that slow Essence gain would limit that even more, and it seems kind of frustrating to play in a mixed party, for a larger chunk of the game than it would have been previously. (As I mentioned above, playing 2E Sidereals was frustrating for quite different reasons.)<br /> <br /> All that said...well, look. I'm just a guy who's maybe too invested in some of my favorite characters. You guys are the devs who've been doing, as I said, superlative work on the line. Really all I'm hoping for is to be blown away in 2020 when the Sidereal book comes out, to be able to say &quot;holy shit, I never expected THAT to be something they could do! That's so cool!&quot; like I've done for all the other splats so far. And even if I fret, I do have faith that I'll get that, in some form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T19:45:25-08:00","id":1271023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271008#post1271008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when I hear &quot;we're basically giving Sidereals what they got in 1E, and not adding anything new&quot;, I reflexively cringe a little, because...well, hewing too closely to Sidereals 1E is kind of how we got Sidereals 2E, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>He's not saying &quot;no new Sidereal Charms&quot;.<br /> <br /> He's talking about new widgets like Evocations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * ...all of the other classic Exalts have changed and grown and expanded in 3E so far. Dragon-Blooded got to use Charms of all elements with all abilities. Solars got to speak prophecy and learn the ways of spirits, as well as a whole new category of coolness in the form of Evocations and martial arts Mastery. Lunars we've been over in this thread. Compared to all of that, it's a little hard to swallow that 1E Sidereals were conceived so perfectly that nothing could be added or improved. </div> </div> </div>If anything, everyone else caught up to the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> A famous poster once said (paraphrased) &quot;Sidereal were supposedly balanced around being glass cannon ninjas who fell apart when caught unprepared, except that they have the Sidereal Martial Arts to kick ass in a face-to-face brawl&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T19:49:23-08:00","id":1271025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270918#post1270918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Vanguard as a school that doesn't consider itself just another school within the Silver Path</div> </div> </div> </div>Just don't let the Vanguard hear you calling them that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T19:53:22-08:00","id":1271027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ysadrel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271008#post1271008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I played with the 2E Sidereal Charmset extensively -- much more than I did the 1E Charmset. So when I hear &quot;we're basically giving Sidereals what they got in 1E, and not adding anything new&quot;, I reflexively cringe a little, because...well, hewing too closely to Sidereals 1E is kind of how we got Sidereals 2E, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're still gonna update Sidereal mechanics to fit with the new system. This includes expanding their Charmset commensurately with the way everyone else's has expaned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * ...all of the other classic Exalts have changed and grown and expanded in 3E so far. Dragon-Blooded got to use Charms of all elements with all abilities. Solars got to speak prophecy and learn the ways of spirits, as well as a whole new category of coolness in the form of Evocations and martial arts Mastery. Lunars we've been over in this thread. Compared to all of that, it's a little hard to swallow that 1E Sidereals were conceived so perfectly that nothing could be added or improved. Especially since... </div> </div> </div>Solars get resonant access to all magical materials. Lunars get access to second circle necromancy, which won't even come out for a while. The disparity in shiny new toys that they're getting isn't as large as you'd think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * ...3E, as a play environment, emphasizes the places where Sidereals are weak a lot more than previous editions did. The low-Essence period of the game gets a lot more focus, and Essence increases substantially slower; since Sidereal Excellencies are based on Essence, that's not great for them. Add that to the fact that they haven't traditionally had a lot of Charm choice per Ability, and that slow Essence gain would limit that even more, and it seems kind of frustrating to play in a mixed party, for a larger chunk of the game than it would have been previously. (As I mentioned above, playing 2E Sidereals was frustrating for quite different reasons.) </div> </div> </div>Those are the kind of things we consider in adjusting and polishing the way Sidereal Charms work. We aren't just copypasting every detail in blind.<br /> <br /> Long story short: when I say &quot;Sidereals aren't getting any shiny new toys,&quot; I don't mean they aren't getting the same level of mechanical refinement and updates that every other type of Exalt is getting, just that that we aren't adding a bunch in the way of mechanical widgets that didn't have an equivalent in 1E.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T21:09:23-08:00","id":1271041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271025#post1271025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just don't let the Vanguard hear you calling them that!</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it would be pretty hard to maintain for a significant length of time, but is there a school that does consider itself part of the Silver Pact, but no one else in the Silver Pact sees them that way? Y'know, as the theoretical total opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T23:00:21-08:00","id":1271051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271027#post1271027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're still gonna update Sidereal mechanics to fit with the new system. This includes expanding their Charmset commensurately with the way everyone else's has expaned.<br /> <br /> <br /> Solars get resonant access to all magical materials. Lunars get access to second circle necromancy, which won't even come out for a while. The disparity in shiny new toys that they're getting isn't as large as you'd think.<br /> <br /> <br /> Those are the kind of things we consider in adjusting and polishing the way Sidereal Charms work. We aren't just copypasting every detail in blind.<br /> <br /> Long story short: when I say &quot;Sidereals aren't getting any shiny new toys,&quot; I don't mean they aren't getting the same level of mechanical refinement and updates that every other type of Exalt is getting, just that that we aren't adding a bunch in the way of mechanical widgets that didn't have an equivalent in 1E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, cool. Thank you for these clarifications; it actually does help put a lot of my fears to rest. I think I took the idea of &quot;just give it some polish and shine&quot; to mean something much less than you intended, and I'll remember not to do so in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T02:43:34-08:00","id":1271085,"title":"","content":"Less broken sidereal martial arts (which will presumably actually be in the sidereal book this time) and less crippling paradox are definitely gonna be upgrades. <br /> <br /> Plus however they fix the problem of the sidereal dice cap not meshing with a lot of MA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T02:52:07-08:00","id":1271086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1270554#post1270554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I suppose you could say this is what happened with the Bull of the North; Samea brought out the Second Circle Demons, they used warstriders, etc, and that's what led to Sidereals destroying an entire pro-Bull city with sorcery, which they don't generally do).</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of hope Fallen Lapis doesn't come back, it feels like it was intended as a cutesy reference to the events of the 1e playtest that took on a life of its own. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For context, the early 1e playtest game run by Elizabeth \u201cFormerly Known As Deidre\u201d Brooks featured Sidereals (lead by an NPC consistently described as Kung Fu Dumbledore) wiping out cities with Cantata of Empty Voices (deployed remotely as bomb-vials via the Crucible of Tarim) and fights at the top of the Imperial Mountain between PC Solars and NPC Alchemicals with jetpacks. It is much, much easier to take \u201clow-power\u201d Exalted and scale it up to late 2e than to take late 2e Exalted and scale it back down to a lower baseline.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T06:56:16-08:00","id":1271110,"title":"","content":"I did not know that.<br /> <br /> But still, breaking out massive sorcery to take down armies and cities is a thing that comes up in games with Celestials. A couple of years ago I ran a war between the PCs and another group of Solars, and massive sorcery got broken out pretty quickly, with armies being blown apart.<br /> <br /> Hey, 3 sessions ago one of our PCs popped over to the armada our enemy's had been building and just... blew it all up. (She hasn't been brave enough <br /> <br /> So I could see where my current ST was going, when he wanted some reason why the Sidereals and Lunars don't constantly break out civilisation-wrecking magicks against each other, and a certain restraint and not wanting to just wreck everything makes sense.<br /> <br /> I think Minton hinted towards something similar, he said something like Lunars will generally avoid going on a murder spree in the Imperial City because it'll just attract too much attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T07:21:00-08:00","id":1271124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271110#post1271110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I could see where my current ST was going, when he wanted some reason why the Sidereals and Lunars don't constantly break out civilisation-wrecking magicks against each other, and a certain restraint and not wanting to just wreck everything makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of this setting, I feel as though it would mostly be a case of limited reach and access and the necessity of the one initiating it generally being at ground zero, in combination with the particular caution of the Sidereal Exalted, more than being held at bay by fear of mutually assured destruction.<br /> <br /> Like, the doctrine of MAD was based on the assumption that both sides could deploy arsenals sufficient to obliterate nations that stretched the length of continents all at once, and that would do their work in a matter of hours, so if one went so far the other could respond in kind and both would be destroyed before very effective defensive measures would be taken. Lunar and Sidereal Exalted trying to act on that scale would take months, if not years, and the process for responding to it is a lot more straightforward; you can't pin a ballistic missile travelling at several hundred kilometres a second down in a kung fu duel.<br /> <br /> I think that your Storyteller is overthinking things.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T07:42:46-08:00","id":1271132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the necessity of the one initiating it generally being at ground zero, in combination with the particular caution of the Sidereal Exalted, </div> </div> </div>That was actually part of it; his idea was that Sidereals didn't generally come down and fight in direct Lunar vs Dragonblood wars, because it's too dangerous. The one time they would is when the Lunars started to break out the kind of magic that could wreck cities and armies quickly, destroying whole Legions and Satrapies and achieving a break-through towards the Realm, rather than just bogging them down. At this point Sidereals would be pushed to intervene personally, which dissuaded the Lunars from pushing the Realm too far and too fast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that your Storyteller is overthinking things. </div> </div> </div>Possibly.<br /> I suspect him thinking this through has something to do with the fact one PC can spray Death Ray around (and another PC had Godspeed Vanguard, which can blind an entire army, though that PC died and his warstrider is wrecked so it doesn't matter), yet some of the players (including, I think, the one with Death Ray) would much rather play a war of Roman Legions than magical ambush wack-an-army with the Wyld Hunt.<br /> <br /> After the sorceress Death Rayed Harborhead's armada, a Sidereal (we assume) turned up and used Cantata of Empty Voices to wipe out a garrison of several hundred magically-enhanced soldiers and a few dragons. The first time anyone had used Celestial Sorcery against the group since their war with a rival Circle of Solars. And my young Lunar was told by an elder (Judo Far-Flung, from the Core) about how Sidereals are cowardly and rarely get involved in battles, except when Lunars start using overt army-killed magic, which is one of the reason young Lunars<br /> <br /> So, I guess the point is that the sorceress can now choose whether to attack Realm forces with sorcery, but Sidereals will attack her lands with sorcery, or she can just have an army-vs-army clash and they won't. But that's just me speculating.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-27-2018, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T07:56:22-08:00","id":1271136,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I don't want to comment too deeply into other people's games, but that might just be an excuse to not look too closely at how some of these things function (or don't) when they actually play out...<br /> <br /> It's a pickle. I'd really rather think of terms and premises for properly integrating the expansion of the Silver Pact fighting strategy from its original phrasing in terms of breaking down magitech, especially under circumstances where the Realm has alternative forms of high power magic through the Evocations of regular Artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T08:03:21-08:00","id":1271139,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by breaking down magitech?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T08:08:46-08:00","id":1271141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271139#post1271139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by breaking down magitech?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shogunate and early Realm would have magitech\u2026 Lunars would break it. That mattered because it was Second Edition. Eventually, no more magitech, the ball would presumably have been in the Lunars' court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T10:53:02-08:00","id":1271182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271136#post1271136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I don't want to comment too deeply into other people's games, but that might just be an excuse to not look too closely at how some of these things function (or don't) when they actually play out...</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I talk about the games I play a lot, because I want to give examples of actual play. But I recognise it's probably a bit difficult to respond to, as you don't play that game.<br /> <br /> Also, of course, it's only my two games (the one I've played for years, and the one I ran, stopped, and recently started playing under a different ST). Which can maybe be a bit misleading, because it somewhat depends on the players. I'm sure if I played Exalted with my DnD group, who haven't been playing Exalted for years, and are much more cooperative (and, ironically, more diverse), then things would probably end up quite different. And other people's groups may also be different; I know me, Irked and Alucard all had quite different experiences with the Craft system.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see others give more examples of how things have worked out in actual play. There are some posters that do that, it's useful. But then, it can end up just being a lot of people talking about their game, rather than the things themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-27-2018, 01:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T10:56:16-08:00","id":1271184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271136#post1271136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a pickle. I'd really rather think of terms and premises for properly integrating the expansion of the Silver Pact fighting strategy from its original phrasing in terms of breaking down magitech, especially under circumstances where the Realm has alternative forms of high power magic through the Evocations of regular Artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so are you asking whether the plan of eroding the Realm's stores of high power magic is still viable in 3rd edition, or saying it isn't and wondering what that does to the presentation of the war?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T11:15:53-08:00","id":1271187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271184#post1271184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so are you asking whether the plan of eroding the Realm's stores of high power magic is still viable in 3rd edition, or saying it isn't and wondering what that does to the presentation of the war?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'm going to lay out a timeline just to put things in order:<br /> <br /> So we were first introduced to this basic principle of what the Silver Pact was up to back with the release of Masters of Jade in 2012. As Holden and John Morke elaborated on it, it was expressed in terms largely focused on the idea of Lunars having had a significant impact on stocks of magitech across Creation, especially for the Realm, because it was still at the stage of talking about it as errata rather than the presentation in a new Edition.<br /> <br /> And even when the new Edition was announced and being hyped up, that image of the Silver Pact retained a lot of traction. Even when there was a lot of talk of magitech being de-emphasized, the transitional period created a certain sense, for me at least, of that coming across in terms of &quot;there used to be a lot of it, and Lunar tactics greatly hastened its decline&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the transitional period lasted for years, with arguments about a change in Lunar presentation being among the more common and contentious during that period, so it gave a lot of time for the idea to take root.<br /> <br /> Now, we're three books into Third Edition, and I find the addition of Evocations to Artifacts to be a major overhaul there. Actually, a lot of things with Artifacts have been overhauled, such as removing the idea that it takes being Essence 6 or having a modifying Charm of a high level to make the highest dot ones, so it's a lot more in reach for even Dragon Blooded to make level 5 Artifacts, whose powers have been enhanced from &quot;provide a few extra dice to keep an army from fleeing&quot; to a suite of powers that can culminate in destroying large buildings or whole cities.<br /> <br /> That and a few other elements... the dynamic of the Realm as something that is strongly dependent on an ever dwindling supply of the legacy of the First Age has changed significantly. They're not exactly on the cutting edge, but there's still a lot that they can do pro-actively. That's not even getting into the weird and experimental stuff attributed to Houses like Ledaal and Ragara.<br /> <br /> So an objective of the Lunars that had become very familiar is obsolete. Really, it has been for a while now, since the core provided sample Lunar Dominions and they were all different tactics for harassing the Realm's imperial apparatus. Actually seeing the Realm and its Exalted first hand has very effectively killed it, and this preview, referring to the successes of the Lunars primarily in terms of things like curbing ambitions to conquer the Scavenger Lands and expand to the West, is nailing up its coffin.<br /> <br /> Which is great. I'm all for it in giving the Lunars a more dynamic range of methods to apply, and letting the Realm itself be a more vigorous and challenging opponent. And it's not as if specifically targeting the old First Age Artifice (still including warstriders) and new Artifacts with Evocations isn't still valid and important (replacing a spear that can bring the heavens down upon a city may not be all but impossible, but it's still difficult beyond the practical reach of many Dragon Blooded artificers), just not as central as it once seemed to be.<br /> <br /> It's not a question I'm asking, it's just a need to adjust a paradigm that had gotten a lot of time and testing to become fairly set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T12:05:23-08:00","id":1271211,"title":"","content":"Is anyone else interested in talking more about Lunar schools, or should I start another thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T12:10:16-08:00","id":1271215,"title":"","content":"No, please go ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T13:40:57-08:00","id":1271240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271215#post1271215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, please go ahead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please consider:<br /> <br /> A singular elder or perhaps even an entire (small) school whose entire mission is to moderate conflicts between other schools, because the elder (and any adherents forming an associated school) are more passionate about maintaining peace among their own kind than spreading chaos among the descendants of the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> They serve as a neutral third party in disputes, but also as brokers of sensitive exchanges. When two parties of the Silver Pact wish to trade valuable assets such as crucial secrets or powerful artifacts, this third party can be the &quot;escrow-holder&quot;.<br /> <br /> The elder or one of his closest disciples is entrusted to learn the secret and determine if it is worth the daiklave (while also being trusted not to share the secret to any fourth party), or hold the daiklave from one party until the other party has completed the task agreed upon as the price for it.<br /> <br /> One of the advantages for the two concerned parties is that, if the third party attempts to take the artifact for itself and flee, the two offended parties can band together and take justice, rather try to settle things between each other, risking a double-cross that could lead to open warfare between the two parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T15:37:17-08:00","id":1271293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271240#post1271240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please consider:<br /> <br /> A singular elder or perhaps even an entire (small) school whose entire mission is to moderate conflicts between other schools, because the elder (and any adherents forming an associated school) are more passionate about maintaining peace among their own kind than spreading chaos among the descendants of the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> They serve as a neutral third party in disputes, but also as brokers of sensitive exchanges. When two parties of the Silver Pact wish to trade valuable assets such as crucial secrets or powerful artifacts, this third party can be the &quot;escrow-holder&quot;.<br /> <br /> The elder or one of his closest disciples is entrusted to learn the secret and determine if it is worth the daiklave (while also being trusted not to share the secret to any fourth party), or hold the daiklave from one party until the other party has completed the task agreed upon as the price for it.<br /> <br /> One of the advantages for the two concerned parties is that, if the third party attempts to take the artifact for itself and flee, the two offended parties can band together and take justice, rather try to settle things between each other, risking a double-cross that could lead to open warfare between the two parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm picturing something like a wandering bard kind of aesthetic, which puts me in mind of the potential for schools to represent an additional axis on which a character might define a role to play into.<br /> <br /> Hmm...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T15:57:00-08:00","id":1271306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271110#post1271110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not know that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that's not Lea saying Fallen Lapis is a direct reference to the playtest, but it goes a long way to explain why the Sidereals were so out of character and gained so little from it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T16:19:22-08:00","id":1271321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271306#post1271306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that's not Lea saying Fallen Lapis is a direct reference to the playtest, but it goes a long way to explain why the Sidereals were so out of character and gained so little from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the Character Creation chapter fiction in the preview for WFHW, it was the Realm legions who razed Fallen Lapis this edition, at least in part because they wanted at least <i>one </i>total and unqualified victory to save face after the disaster that was the rest of the war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T17:15:53-08:00","id":1271334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271293#post1271293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm picturing something like a wandering bard kind of aesthetic, which puts me in mind of the potential for schools to represent an additional axis on which a character might define a role to play into.<br /> <br /> Hmm...</div> </div> </div> </div>After I was finished, I was picturing Argo the Rat, a criminally underutilized background character in the Sword Art Online franchise whom is turned into a main character in the version of the manga told from Asuna\u2019s point of view. <br /> <br /> Argo is an information broker who operates between the forceful figures and powers that be in the world of Aincrad, doing her own part to help the front line Clearers succeed in their efforts to survive and defeat the Floor Bosses.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a fanfic that sets SAO\u2019s Death Game in Alfheim Online instead, where the players are divided into tribes and lead to believe only a few tribes will be allowed to escape while all others will die. Naturally, that leads to a lot more Player Killing.<br /> <br /> In this story, Argo works double-time to create and maintain peace between the tribes and unravel the villain\u2019s logic to find a way for everyone to get out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T17:28:20-08:00","id":1271340,"title":"","content":"I'm afraid that I can't comment one way or the other on a Sword Art Online reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T18:48:07-08:00","id":1271355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271340#post1271340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm afraid that I can't comment one way or the other on a Sword Art Online reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ever have the urge, only pick up the manga labeled &quot;Progressive&quot;, or any adaptation of Gun Gale Online: Alternative. Because neither was written by the original author, and so both are actually really good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T01:37:49-08:00","id":1271398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271240#post1271240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please consider:<br /> <br /> A singular elder or perhaps even an entire (small) school whose entire mission is to moderate conflicts between other schools, because the elder (and any adherents forming an associated school) are more passionate about maintaining peace among their own kind than spreading chaos among the descendants of the Shogunate.<br /> <br /> They serve as a neutral third party in disputes, but also as brokers of sensitive exchanges. When two parties of the Silver Pact wish to trade valuable assets such as crucial secrets or powerful artifacts, this third party can be the &quot;escrow-holder&quot;.<br /> <br /> The elder or one of his closest disciples is entrusted to learn the secret and determine if it is worth the daiklave (while also being trusted not to share the secret to any fourth party), or hold the daiklave from one party until the other party has completed the task agreed upon as the price for it.<br /> <br /> One of the advantages for the two concerned parties is that, if the third party attempts to take the artifact for itself and flee, the two offended parties can band together and take justice, rather try to settle things between each other, risking a double-cross that could lead to open warfare between the two parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't get the bard impression from this that Isator did (though that does make sense). It made think of Semion Mogilevich.<br /> <br /> So, I wrote my dissertation on the history of the Russian Mafiya.*<br /> <br /> *(A misleading title. Organised crime groups of the former USSR is more accurate, but less snappy on the front page.)<br /> <br /> A lot of people think that high-ranking Russian criminals like the <i>vory</i> are like the Mafiya bosses in films; sitting in their hotel, they have a whole bunch of loyal soldiers working for them, who take orders from them everyday.<br /> <br /> In reality, they're more respected figures who help other criminals; money laundering, setting up connections, selling guns, etc. They're very important figures, but it's looser than TV would have you believe. Semion Mogilevich, for example, the Russian-Israeli-Hungarian-Ukrainian businessman who's referred to as the &quot;Boss of Bosses&quot; who has at various points owned one of Russia's biggest banks, a large section of the Hungarian arms industry, the RosUkrEnergo gas company, etc, etc. They describe him as leader of most of the Russian Mafia's gangs... but this isn't really true, in the sense of telling those gangs what to do. What he has done is made links with gangs all over Eastern Europe, Israel and the former USSR, providing them with money laundering services, helping them set up deals with other gangs, and so on. Yes, he does have bodyguards and so on, but he doesn't head an organisation per-se. He's not like the leader of a Mexican cartel.<br /> <br /> Because when two gangs want to do business, they need a respected elder to ensure the deal goes down fairly (it's not like gangsters are trustworthy). Also, if you're a Tajik heroin smuggler, you need to get that heroin into the hands of people in Moscow, who need to get that heroin into the hands of Polish and German heroin wholesalers. You need someone who can set that up. If you're a Georgian arms smuggler, and you want to buy European arms, you need someone who can acquire an export license and send you the guns, so you can then sell them on.<br /> It's not that you're all working <i>for</i> them, you're working <i>with</i> them (despite what TV shows, getting criminals to work for people isn't that easy). But that hasn't stopped Mogilevich from becoming incredibly rich, being friends with high-up intelligence agents, getting the ex-President of Ukraine to shred information on him, and living in Moscow under Putin's protection.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I imagine a respected elder Spider-totem Lunar sitting in a teahouse in a Guild hub town. Younger Lunars come to her to get in contact with other Lunars, to be a trusted broker, to provide information and tell them what other Lunar might be willing to teach them sorcery. Even Shahan-ya and their schools come to her when they do business with another school, just to ensure everything's above board. She knows Guild representatives, bigwigs in local spirit courts, and Lunar Elders across the direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-28-2018, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T02:13:52-08:00","id":1271402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271321#post1271321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the Character Creation chapter fiction in the preview for WFHW, it was the Realm legions who razed Fallen Lapis this edition, at least in part because they wanted at least <i>one </i>total and unqualified victory to save face after the disaster that was the rest of the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I missed that. That fits the Realm much better than the Sidereals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T03:10:30-08:00","id":1271404,"title":"","content":"Where is Fallen Lapis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T03:37:11-08:00","id":1271407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271404#post1271404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is Fallen Lapis?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2ed it was North of Mt. Metagalapa, South East of Lake Sanazata, and South-ish of Chanta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 11-28-2018, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T04:00:37-08:00","id":1271411,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, I've found it.<br /> <br /> So, if it's still in the same place, about 2000 miles from where the Icewalkers live.<br /> (Though saying that, there's a lot more space between Whitewall and Rubylak now, and Linowan is further north... does the Icewalker tundra border Linowan now? I think it might do. The Saltspire League might be slap-bang in the middle of the Icewalker Tundra, not on its Eastern edge.)<br /> <br /> Has anything been said this edition about whether Bull vs Realm still involved Linowan vs Halta?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-28-2018, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T06:25:59-08:00","id":1271424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271411#post1271411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anything been said this edition about whether Bull vs Realm still involved Linowan vs Halta?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not, because we're trying to keep our geographic scale non-ludicrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T06:48:40-08:00","id":1271425,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I thought you'd said that previously.<br /> <br /> So, is 3rd edition Fallen Lapis in a different place to 2nd edition Fallen Lapis? Say, north of Medo or near Cherak, rather than south of Chanta?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T06:56:08-08:00","id":1271426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271425#post1271425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I thought you'd said that previously.<br /> <br /> So, is 3rd edition Fallen Lapis in a different place to 2nd edition Fallen Lapis? Say, north of Medo or near Cherak, rather than south of Chanta?</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven't discussed any specific plans for it, to the best of my recollection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T07:16:47-08:00","id":1271433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271398#post1271398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't get the bard impression from this that Isator did (though that does make sense).</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't an impression, it was an imposition!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reality, they're more respected figures who help other criminals; money laundering, setting up connections, selling guns, etc. They're very important figures, but it's looser than TV would have you believe. Semion Mogilevich, for example, the Russian-Israeli-Hungarian-Ukrainian businessman who's referred to as the &quot;Boss of Bosses&quot; who has at various points owned one of Russia's biggest banks, a large section of the Hungarian arms industry, the RosUkrEnergo gas company, etc, etc. They describe him as leader of most of the Russian Mafia's gangs... but this isn't really true, in the sense of telling those gangs what to do. What he has done is made links with gangs all over Eastern Europe, Israel and the former USSR, providing them with money laundering services, helping them set up deals with other gangs, and so on. Yes, he does have bodyguards and so on, but he doesn't head an organisation per-se. He's not like the leader of a Mexican cartel.<br /> <br /> Because when two gangs want to do business, they need a respected elder to ensure the deal goes down fairly (it's not like gangsters are trustworthy). Also, if you're a Tajik heroin smuggler, you need to get that heroin into the hands of people in Moscow, who need to get that heroin into the hands of Polish and German heroin wholesalers. You need someone who can set that up. If you're a Georgian arms smuggler, and you want to buy European arms, you need someone who can acquire an export license and send you the guns, so you can then sell them on.<br /> It's not that you're all working <i>for</i> them, you're working <i>with</i> them (despite what TV shows, getting criminals to work for people isn't that easy). But that hasn't stopped Mogilevich from becoming incredibly rich, being friends with high-up intelligence agents, getting the ex-President of Ukraine to shred information on him, and living in Moscow under Putin's protection.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me a lot of the way Professor Moriarty was written in his original appearance; that being the &quot;Napoleon of crime&quot; amounted to being somebody in the background who could provide a bit of organisation and assistance to London's various gangs, while personally being far enough removed that you can't really be prosecuted.<br /> <br /> I've often thought with amusement about the difficulty that modern adaptations of Sherlock Holmes have with depicting Moriarty as a criminal genius to an audience for which the basic concept of organised crime has become fairly mundane. He (or she) always needs to have these super-elaborate plans with all these moving parts, and even control of international events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I imagine a respected elder Spider-totem Lunar sitting in a teahouse in a Guild hub town. Younger Lunars come to her to get in contact with other Lunars, to be a trusted broker, to provide information and tell them what other Lunar might be willing to teach them sorcery. Even Shahan-ya and their schools come to her when they do business with another school, just to ensure everything's above board. She knows Guild representatives, bigwigs in local spirit courts, and Lunar Elders across the direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also sounds like a good way to realise the Night Caste crime lord in a manner that doesn't need to awkwardly stray from core Abilities of the Caste or into an idea of extending power directly through subordinate criminals.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, it also reminds me of stuff in the Harry Potter series... there's a curious juxtaposition between the way that Voldemort's activities in either conflict were <i>talked about</i> (he was mostly a lone, self-reliant figure who would operate from a distance, his followers were generally unaware of each other's identities, he would frequently zip away on his own to conduct personal missions) and the way that they would be depicted directly (Voldemort presiding over courts of his followers, addressing them by name when they weren't foregoing the masks altogether, issuing commands and often asserting status through humiliation and torture while talking himself up).<br /> <br /> I kind of find the former Voldemort more interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T07:38:53-08:00","id":1271438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271433#post1271433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That wasn't an impression, it was an imposition!</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry. Anyways, it works. The basic idea can be taken quite a lot of different ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That reminds me a lot of the way Professor Moriarty was written in his original appearance; that being the &quot;Napoleon of crime&quot; amounted to being somebody in the background who could provide a bit of organisation and assistance to London's various gangs, while personally being far enough removed that you can't really be prosecuted. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. If you're actually giving orders, you're too close to the action, and too likely to get arrested (or killed). Especially with 19th century law, which didn't have RICO or other laws targeting organised crime members, rather than just doing an actual crime.<br /> <br /> I remember an amusing crime story I read about a few years ago. Two gangs in Manchester were feuding. Tit-for-tat murders. But then the police got hold of the gun that was used to commit the murders, and used ballistics to prosecute a lot of the killers.<br /> Because, you see, all the murders on both sides were done with the same gun. Neither gang owned a gun; a rich local criminal had one, and rented it out to both gangs in turn. But he himself was above territory and street crime.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also sounds like a good way to realise the Night Caste crime lord in a manner that doesn't need to awkwardly stray from core Abilities of the Caste or into an idea of extending power directly through subordinate criminals. </div> </div> </div>Ah, you mean as opposed to all the Night Caste concepts that rely on, say, Melee? Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Come to think of it, it also reminds me of stuff in the Harry Potter series... there's a curious juxtaposition between the way that Voldemort's activities in either conflict were <i>talked about</i> (he was mostly a lone, self-reliant figure who would operate from a distance, his followers were generally unaware of each other's identities, he would frequently zip away on his own to conduct personal missions) </div> </div> </div>I could definitely see a Lunar elder doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T08:03:50-08:00","id":1271448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271438#post1271438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah, you mean as opposed to all the Night Caste concepts that rely on, say, Melee? Yeah.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No I meant, like, Bureaucracy and... maybe custom Larceny Charms that would allow one to extend powers to people working under you. Stuff that might denote other people's sense of leadership.<br /> <br /> It's the crime lord and spymaster angle on the Night Caste, which I'm not saying are inappropriate as things that really fit the Caste and might entail stray from core Abilities, but it's also good to conceive of them in terms of somebody whose control is exercised through being able to invisibly flit between various subordinates who carry out a lot of the direct grunt work of criminal activity or following and observation, while themselves often being a bit expendable.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T12:22:29-08:00","id":1271533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271448#post1271448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I meant, like, Bureaucracy and... maybe custom Larceny Charms that would allow one to extend powers to people working under you. Stuff that might denote other people's sense of leadership.<br /> <br /> It's the crime lord and spymaster angle on the Night Caste, which I'm not saying are inappropriate as things that really fit the Caste and might entail stray from core Abilities, but it's also good to conceive of them in terms of somebody whose control is exercised through being able to invisibly flit between various subordinates who carry out a lot of the direct grunt work of criminal activity or following and observation, while themselves often being a bit expendable.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Bureaucracy, Larceny, or Attribute Charms that key off of backgrounds like Influence or Backing, representing the ways in which you can make supernatural use of your networks of contacts, allies, and patsies?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T13:07:02-08:00","id":1271548,"title":"","content":"You figure there's a school of Lunars serving the cause of the Silver Pact by causing problems for Sidereals in Yu-Shan?<br /> <br /> Do you think they fight the Celestial Dragon-Blooded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T13:52:45-08:00","id":1271569,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I guess it depends how they're causing problems.<br /> <br /> Going to Yu-Shan and killing Sidereals? I think that'd be far too dangerous. It's the Sidereals place of power, the one place they'd outnumber Lunars, and where they're surrounded by divine bodyguards.<br /> <br /> I could see a Lunar sneaking in to steal things, but I can't see them staying for a long time. They could, of course, hide amongst the gods and intrigue against the Sidereals, but I think while one or two might do it, I can't see a whole pack or school.<br /> <br /> What I could see though, is an Elder whose school is dedicated to manipulating Heaven through manipulating Earth. Finding out which gods are friends with the Bronze Faction, which are useful allies, and working to degrade their purviews in Creation. While learning which gods detest the Bronze Faction (whether for ideological or personal reasons) and working to make them more powerful. Spreading their worship, building temples, and just building up whatever it is they are god of. A school of priests and evangelists who attempt to sway the balance of power in Heaven.<br /> <br /> And of course, they'd be particularly devoted to taking down the Immaculate Order, since any god on the Order's worship calendar is probably in with the Bronze Faction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T13:53:01-08:00","id":1271570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271533#post1271533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Bureaucracy, Larceny, or Attribute Charms that key off of backgrounds like Influence or Backing, representing the ways in which you can make supernatural use of your networks of contacts, allies, and patsies?</div> </div> </div> </div>That whole digression was really more about Solars. I would find that Lunars don't really have the problem I'm talking about with their broader Castes and Attribute Charms; a Changing or No Moon crime lord of either variety isn't really struggling against core competencies when their Caste Attributes are already broad enough to encompass either path.<br /> <br /> And yes, your description sounds like a good way of realising one of the types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T14:18:04-08:00","id":1271575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271548#post1271548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You figure there's a school of Lunars serving the cause of the Silver Pact by causing problems for Sidereals in Yu-Shan?<br /> <br /> Do you think they fight the Celestial Dragon-Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that being a school means that they're ones whose advocacy would be that the Sidereals are a significant danger, and that a higher priority ought to be placed on targeting and harassing them specifically.<br /> <br /> Like, it's definitely something that they would all want to do to some extent, just differences of opinion about how much and why being within or the basis of different schools.<br /> <br /> And I definitely think that Heaven's Dragons would be employed in fighting against Lunars. Come to think of it, they seem very well placed to harass Lunars who live beyond the reach of the Realm, Lookshy or particularly organised outcastes as a source of Wyld Hunts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T15:21:08-08:00","id":1271599,"title":"","content":"I think it's risking making Yu-Shan just another battle ground.<br /> I'm already a little wary of the Heaven's Dragons, the notion of bringing in Heaven's Lunars to fight them just confounds the concerns I have there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-29-2018, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T16:57:06-08:00","id":1271619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271599#post1271599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's risky making Yu-Shan just another battle ground.<br /> I'm already a little wary of the Heaven's Dragons, the notion of bringing in Heaven's Lunars to fight them just confounds the concerns I have there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that, and I was personally thinking in terms of a group of Lunars that doesn't need to be very large having an idea that there should be very quick operations in and out of Yu-Shan and the other 90% of the time do things to lure in Sidereals or find out their itineraries and go to meet them there. The idea of anybody in the Silver Pact trying to embed themselves in Heaven in the long term and make trouble for the Bureau of Destiny seems like it should be suicide.<br /> <br /> Same with the idea that the city's native Dragon Blooded are generally going out to take the fight to Lunars in their home, not within Heaven itself. Except insofar as they might be part of the equation that makes Lunars in general say that trying to start shit in Yu-Shan is almost definitely a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> That and I think there have been references to the idea that the Silver Pact would really rather not turn all of the Celestial Gods against them as well.<br /> <br /> With all of that said, the Sidereal Exalted are still on the Silver Pact's shit list, and often take part in Wyld Hunts, there should be some process by which they fight back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T17:50:18-08:00","id":1271638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271619#post1271619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can see that, and I was personally thinking in terms of a group of Lunars that doesn't need to be very large having an idea that there should be very quick operations in and out of Yu-Shan and the other 90% of the time do things to lure in Sidereals or find out their itineraries and go to meet them there. The idea of anybody in the Silver Pact trying to embed themselves in Heaven in the long term and make trouble for the Bureau of Destiny seems like it should be suicide.<br /> <br /> Same with the idea that the city's native Dragon Blooded are generally going out to take the fight to Lunars in their home, not within Heaven itself. Except insofar as they might be part of the equation that makes Lunars in general say that trying to start shit in Yu-Shan is almost definitely a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> <b>That and I think there have been references to the idea that the Silver Pact would really rather not turn all of the Celestial Gods against them as well.</b><br /> <br /> With all of that said, the Sidereal Exalted are still on the Silver Pact's shit list, and often take part in Wyld Hunts, there should be some process by which they fight back.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall a statement to the opposite effect - that because it isn't <i>terribly</i> difficult for a determined Lunar to get into Yu-Shan, Celestial gods have been hesitant to give the Sidereals their unconditional support. Honestly, I prefer that interpretation because I strongly dislike the idea that a Solar or Lunar can stay out of trouble by just keeping their heads down and trying not to get on anyone's shitlist. It really doesn't comport with my view of the setting, in which the ability to have and maintain such a shitlist is itself a marker of status, because you are making it known that you are not to be crossed - either by going against you, or for the <i>truly </i>powerful or vindictive, by just not indulging your every whim. Absent such a threat of retaliation, I would think that the gods would fall much more strongly on the Bronze Faction's side, because it would be far more inconvenient to make enemies of them than of someone down in Creation who can't fight back. With it, a Celestial deity has to weigh the certainty of causing a petty social slight against the small but <i>very real</i> chance that they'll be murdered in their own sanctum.<br /> <br /> Individual gods will vary to a lesser or greater degree, but as a general rule, I would think that <i>fear of reprisal </i>informs their actions far more than personal sympathies. Between the risk of being struck from the Immaculate prayer calendars and the risk of getting one's self or one's worshipers torn apart by vengeful Lunars, the safest course for most Celestial gods is to just <i>stay the hell out of it.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T18:00:15-08:00","id":1271641,"title":"","content":"I wasn't talking about open war in Yu-Shan. I meant political, social, and economic sabotage and intrigue, with OCCASIONAL back-alley murders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T00:59:16-08:00","id":1271719,"title":"","content":"I can see that, but I think probably not in the sense that there's a bunch of Lunars living in Yu-Shan causing trouble, even if it isn't murders. But coming in occasionally, or doing it from outside, yeah. I think it's a good concept.<br /> <br /> How much do people think of the Shahan-Ya and their students as philosophical or strategic methodologies, and how much as geographically-based?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T02:54:15-08:00","id":1271727,"title":"","content":"Another issue I'm seeing.<br /> <br /> The main reason I'd want to play a Lunar who lived in Yu-Shan would be because they were in a game with Sidereal characters. If the Silver Pact has agents up there who are essentially vandalising the Bureau of Destiny, it's more likely that hypothetical character concept would suffer pushback from the Storyteller or be veto'd outright.<br /> <br /> I think it's more likely I'd encounter that than a game about a pack of Lunars sabotarging Heaven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T04:32:28-08:00","id":1271737,"title":"","content":"The dragonblooded clan in yu shan should have mortal members. What if one of those exalted as a lunar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T05:08:43-08:00","id":1271743,"title":"","content":"They would be out of the reach of the Silver Pack, so they would be A) Casteless and B) have no reason to go with their cause. For one thing I don't think Sidereals are dumb enough to kill a Lunar which Exalted in Heaven. If anything I can see it more likely for them to enroll them. Also another thing about Heaven's Dragons. They should have no beef with the Silver Pack and the Silver Pack with them. They started living in heaven way before the Shogunate was established and thus wouldn't have their practices like the Wyld Hunt. So I'd think they be one of the groups that Lunars would be non hostile to, tho we will have to see what their interaction with Sids are like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T06:03:30-08:00","id":1271750,"title":"","content":"In theory, the Lunars are only against what they see as the heirs to the Shogunate; the Realm being most obvious. Presumably also Lookshy, Cherak, Prasad, etc. <br /> <br /> But in reality, I suspect they're pretty suspicious of any Dragonblood. And for Dragonblood living in Yu-Shan... well I can't really see them being like &quot;Ugh, I hate the Sidereals who helped the Dragonblood take over Creation. Despite the fact they're pretty much the only other group of Exalts in Heaven, live down the street, and love Dragonblood, we're certainly never hanging out with them!&quot;<br /> <br /> No, I suspect the Bronze Faction and Heaven's Dragons regularly invite each other to parties. <br /> <br /> Although saying that, if Heaven's Dragons have the problem that they can never remember the Sidereals's names or faces, it might weird them out too much.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T09:14:20-08:00","id":1271783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271719#post1271719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see that, but I think probably not in the sense that there's a bunch of Lunars living in Yu-Shan causing trouble, even if it isn't murders. But coming in occasionally, or doing it from outside, yeah. I think it's a good concept.<br /> <br /> How much do people think of the Shahan-Ya and their students as philosophical or strategic methodologies, and how much as geographically-based?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t know. But if it\u2019s the former, then we\u2019re probably going to need a lesser title for an adherent who serves as a geographical leader/teacher for younger Lunars in the region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T09:21:36-08:00","id":1271785,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, it's maybe a little boring if it's just &quot;the Lunars who live around the Cinder Coast.&quot; On the other hand, if they're all about philosophy and methodology, you end up with 2nd ed's factions, which were a bit nonsensical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T12:06:41-08:00","id":1271821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271737#post1271737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dragonblooded clan in yu shan should have mortal members. What if one of those exalted as a lunar?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know enough about their culture yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271750#post1271750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I suspect the Bronze Faction and Heaven's Dragons regularly invite each other to parties.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is part of why I'm a little wary about them existing. Giving the Bronze Faction their own Dragon-Blooded Gens is probably the worst thing you could do with the concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 11-29-2018, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T12:17:53-08:00","id":1271825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271750#post1271750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory, the Lunars are only against what they see as the heirs to the Shogunate; the Realm being most obvious. Presumably also Lookshy, Cherak, Prasad, etc.<br /> <br /> But in reality, I suspect they're pretty suspicious of any Dragonblood. And for Dragonblood living in Yu-Shan... well I can't really see them being like &quot;Ugh, I hate the Sidereals who helped the Dragonblood take over Creation. Despite the fact they're pretty much the only other group of Exalts in Heaven, live down the street, and love Dragonblood, we're certainly never hanging out with them!&quot;<br /> <br /> No, I suspect the Bronze Faction and Heaven's Dragons regularly invite each other to parties.<br /> <br /> Although saying that, if Heaven's Dragons have the problem that they can never remember the Sidereals's names or faces, it might weird them out too much.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure if there was a Bronze Faction as such before the Solars returned.<br /> <br /> I could see Heaven's Dragons being involved with fighting Lunars if they share the opinion that those Exalted constitute a danger to the stability of the world, more than being subordinate to the Sidereals or feeling solidarity for their cousin bloodlines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271785#post1271785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, it's maybe a little boring if it's just &quot;the Lunars who live around the Cinder Coast.&quot; On the other hand, if they're all about philosophy and methodology, you end up with 2nd ed's factions, which were a bit nonsensical.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Second Edition factions were nonsensical for reasons including that they weren't really factions (schools would have actually been a term that made sense for them), and the actual content of most of their activities. They were things that were either dull, redundant, or didn't really make sense as things for Lunars to do. <br /> <br /> The basic concept of being divided along lines of philosophy and methodology isn't a problem in its own right, so long as they're functional.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T12:59:42-08:00","id":1271832,"title":"","content":"And \u201cdifferent, sometimes mutually exclusive, methods of destroying the Shogunate\u201d would be very functional, to the extent that such methods can actually differ while still potentially progressing towards that shared goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T13:51:34-08:00","id":1271840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271821#post1271821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is part of why I'm a little wary about them existing. Giving the Bronze Faction their own Dragon-Blooded Gens is probably the worst thing you could do with the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm wondering... I'm thinking of Heaven's Dragons engaging in activity primarily as functionaries of the Celestial Order as a whole, of which Sidereals are a particular and significant part, but not the only one or even the most important.<br /> <br /> Sidereals, in this Edition more than ever, have duties and agendas besides those that concern Solars and Lunars. There are probably things in an official capacity that they can send directives, or at least requisitions, to Yu-Shan's other Exalted about.<br /> <br /> So it becomes a question of whether or not this Edition will approach Sidereal factions as something that they can reasonably formulate official policy to prosecute, or if it's something that they're kind of expected to do on their own time.<br /> <br /> That's a Bronze Faction thing, but it also leaves a hanging question about the Lunars; for however long there have been Sidereals actively advocating for the Solars, I feel as though the hostility from Lunars is going to be a thing separate from that, and one that crosses factional boundaries. So whether or not dealing with the Lunars can be a matter of policy is an entirely distinct hanging question.<br /> <br /> Still, I do believe that Thesasaurus had the right of it when he said that the previous line was in fact about the gods not wanting to be too involved, because they were afraid of being marked as enemies of the Silver Pact as well. So it may indeed come down to the Sidereals being limited in how much they can dedicate Bureau resources in that opposition.<br /> <br /> Which would also possibly handle the question of whether or not Sidereals have impunity to unleash highly destructive sorcery on Lunars, if doing so is going far beyond the boundaries of their mandate.<br /> <br /> Laying all of those hanging questions aside, I will say that I've been convinced that seeing Heaven's Dragons as a source for Wyld Hunts issued directly from Yu-Shan is a bad idea on several counts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T14:36:14-08:00","id":1271849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271821#post1271821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't know enough about their culture yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is part of why I'm a little wary about them existing. Giving the Bronze Faction their own Dragon-Blooded Gens is probably the worst thing you could do with the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, inviting each other to parties isn't quite the same as them being the Sidereal's servants (which I agree, would be quite dull), but I see your point.<br /> <br /> Though, as I said at the end (because it only occurred to me near the end), maybe the fact that Heaven's Dragons can never remember what any individual Sidereal looks like precludes close relations. Though that somewhat depends on the nature of Arcane Fate this edition (in 2nd ed, certain divine employees were immune to it, but I forget how extensive that was).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really sure if there was a Bronze Faction as such before the Solars returned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, I'd say there probably was, though it might not be called that. There'd be Sidereals involved in supporting Dragonblood hegemony, using the Immaculate Order to spread fear of Lunars, casting prophecies to tell the Wyld Hunt where to find new Lunars, and so on.<br /> And then other Sidereals who thought the whole thing was ridiculous, and they should be concentrating on their day jobs of stopping demonic and Wyld incursions, stopping Rakan Thulio and his faction of rogue Sidereals from destroying Fate itself*, and making sure Fate goes as the Maidens decreed (however the whole Samsara, Fate, and committees things ends up in this edition).<br /> <br /> *I assume Kejak, Holok, Syn and so on, were also keen on stopping Rakan Thulio. I just mean that they were also trying to help the Realm and fight Lunars, so they're less able to concentrate on it.<br /> <br /> Bronze Faction and Independents essentially, though they might not be called that in 3rd edition's history. They may just be considered pro-Realm Sidereals and neutral Sidereals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Though my point wasn't that Independents never make friends with Dragonblood in Heaven. They probably do. Some sidereals and some dragonblood have probably been friends in Heaven throughout the millenia.<br /> <br /> Possibly I should have just said Sidereals and Dragonblood invite each other to parties, but I could well imagine that Sidereals who say things like &quot;Why should Dragonblood rule Creation? Wouldn't it be better if the Solars were in charge again?&quot; might not get invited to many Dragonblood parties, nor invite Dragonblood to their parties (or perhaps they do invite them, but the Dragonblood don't go to Gold Faction parties, because no-one likes to stand there while people sit around talking about how people like you are responsible for most of the world's problems. It's pretty awkward, I know that from experience).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Second Edition factions were nonsensical for reasons including that they weren't really factions (schools would have actually been a term that made sense for them), and the actual content of most of their activities. They were things that were either dull, redundant, or didn't really make sense as things for Lunars to do.<br /> <br /> The basic concept of being divided along lines of philosophy and methodology isn't a problem in its own right, so long as they're functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this about 50%.<br /> <br /> You are right that they were problematic in terms of their philosophies. The Winding Path and Swords of Luna were redundant, the Sun King Seneschals and Wardens of Gaia didn't make much sense, and while the Crossroads Society probably made the most sense to me, it was still rather redundant (and was more a mutual teaching club than a political movement).<br /> <br /> But, while that was my main objection, a lot of people also complained about how uniform they seemed across an entire Creation.<br /> <br /> If you're a group of Lunars in the far East who think Solars are pretty awesome, and want to team up with them and help them recreate the First Age... how are you really in a faction led by Leviathan? I doubt he sends any instructions to you. He's probably never heard of you.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you're a group of Lunars in the South-East who believe protecting the Cinder Coast from Raksha is more important than expelling the Realm from An-Teng, are you really part of the same organisation as a group of Lunars in the North-East who help the Realm's ally Linowan to fight Halta's Raksha allies? Yes, you all have the same philosophy, but you're not really in the same school. The first group is probably much more closely linked with the local Cinder Coast pro-Solar Lunar, Lunar aiming to empower ordinary mortals, nature-loving Lunar and Lunar sorcerer than they are with some people on the other side of the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Essentially, I think there's two ways of doing schools. I think the first runs into the issues of 400 iconoclasts across an entire world, but here's two examples, see what you think.<br /> <br /> <u>The Children of the Crow</u><br /> Every weapon must be used against the Realm, even black magicks and the restless dead. The Children of the Crow believe that necromancy is a valuable tool against the Realm, which other Lunars scorn unfairly. Their first Shahan-Ya, Smiling Rat, was killed by other Lunars for opening Shadowlands in Realm Satrapies, and today they are led by Sharvara, the great four-eyed black hound. Crow's Children often dwell in Shadowlands, and have webs of contacts and favours amongst the dead. At their urging, the angry dead command their descendants to resist the Immaculate Philosophy, and the Realm's garrisons find themselves assailed with hauntings and disposable hordes of shambling corpses.<br /> Many other Lunars dislike the Children of the Crow. In defeating the Realm, they leave haunted hellscapes and shadowlands. It's effective, but many in the Silver Pact feel that freeing humanity from the Dragonblood will be of little good when the world is one giant Shadowland. Most Children of the Crow however, are not quite so extreme as their original Shahan-Ya, and they can be a powerful ally.<br /> In the north, Crow's Children empowered the Karnese to resist the Realm, but now find them subjugated to the Bull. In the Scavenger Lands, their centre of power is Sijan, while in the South they they meet in hidden shadowlands in the deep desert. In the West, Skullstone was once a centre of the Children, but when the Silver Prince returned he slew the elder Beak of Black Night, and the other Lunars fled. Now they plot their revenge, but wonder how the ghost of a dead prince can be so powerful as to defeat an elder necromancer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Sharvara</u><br /> Visitors to An-Teng often remark at the beauty of its capital. But this is not the original capital; the City of Dead Flowers once stood as shining capital of An-Teng, but is now a realm of ghosts and fear. And in the midst of it dwells Sharvara, the four-eyed black hound. In his youth, Sharvara learnt sorcery from the demoness Mara, but he realised that if was to avenge his dead parents upon the Realm, he would need a magic they had little experience with. And so he entered the Underworld, swimming through its black waters and into the Labyrinth. A year and a day later, he returned with the dark secrets of Necromancy. In his century-old crusade to rid An-Teng of the hated Realm, Sharvara has gathered a group of younger Lunars to him, teaching them his dread secrets.<br /> The Vulture-totem graverobber Beak of Black Night has embraced this power, and recently drove the Realm's garrison out of the mountains between An-Teng and Gem using an army of zombie wolves and lions.<br /> The ferocious White Tiger Lu and mischievous baboon-girl Grin have little interest or aptitude for the more esoteric secrets Sharvara has to offer, but are happy to have ghostly spies report to them and friendly ancestors bless their troops in their fight to expel the Realm from the Cinder Coast.<br /> With the secrets of the Labyrinth Circle, the exorcist Red-eyed Ngo now commands not one familiar ancestor, like most An-Tengian exorcists, but fifty. She ensures those who resist the Realm suffer no predations from restless ghosts, while the Realm's loyal tax-collectors are haunted and cursed. Her dead relatives have attained many prominent positions amongst An-Teng's dead.<br /> <br /> However, not all Lunars of the region around An-Teng approve of its most prominent Shahan-Ya. Once Sharvara's most promising student, Radiant Moth turned her back on her teacher, believing that his power would lead only to ruin. She believes that Sharvara's hate of the Realm has blinded him to the threat of the black-armoured lord of the Thousand, a dark fortress a month's voyage from the City of Dead Flowers. Radiant Moth damned Sharvara's stupidity, and journeyed west in search of different allies. She has created her own school, which though smaller, now commands a pirate fleet amongst the Cinder Isles. But so far they've had not had great success against the Realm, and one of her students, Lintha Ng Zukarios, suggests alliance with the Lintha. But Radiant Moth fears she'd be making the same mistake she damned Sharvara for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-29-2018, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T14:45:13-08:00","id":1271852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271840#post1271840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now I'm wondering... I'm thinking of Heaven's Dragons engaging in activity primarily as functionaries of the Celestial Order as a whole, of which Sidereals are a particular and significant part, but not the only one or even the most important.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was what I was assuming. One imagines that those Dragonblood who live in Heaven do work in the Celestial Bureaucracy, but there's no reason to think they'd be part of the Bureau of Destiny in particular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sidereals, in this Edition more than ever, have duties and agendas besides those that concern Solars and Lunars. </div> </div> </div> Why this edition more than ever? I've no particular objection, but I didn't get the impression Sidereals were significantly less invested in dealing with Solars/Lunars than previous editions. Unless you mean because of Rakan Thulio and his Getimians?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> for however long there have been Sidereals actively advocating for the Solars, I feel as though the hostility from Lunars is going to be a thing separate from that, and one that crosses factional boundaries. </div> </div> </div>That seems likely to me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which would also possibly handle the question of whether or not Sidereals have impunity to unleash highly destructive sorcery on Lunars, if doing so is going far beyond the boundaries of their mandate. </div> </div> </div>IIRC, in previous editions the Sidereals who destroyed Fallen Lapis got in big trouble, because that's not something they're supposed to be doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Laying all of those hanging questions aside, I will say that I've been convinced that seeing Heaven's Dragons as a source for Wyld Hunts issued directly from Yu-Shan is a bad idea on several counts. </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T15:32:16-08:00","id":1271857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271849#post1271849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right that they were problematic in terms of their philosophies. The Winding Path and Swords of Luna were redundant, the Sun King Seneschals and Wardens of Gaia didn't make much sense, and while the Crossroads Society probably made the most sense to me, it was still rather redundant (and was more a mutual teaching club than a political movement).<br /> <br /> But, while that was my main objection, a lot of people also complained about how uniform they seemed across an entire Creation.<br /> <br /> If you're a group of Lunars in the far East who think Solars are pretty awesome, and want to team up with them and help them recreate the First Age... how are you really in a faction led by Leviathan? I doubt he sends any instructions to you. He's probably never heard of you.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if you're a group of Lunars in the South-East who believe protecting the Cinder Coast from Raksha is more important than expelling the Realm from An-Teng, are you really part of the same organisation as a group of Lunars in the North-East who help the Realm's ally Linowan to fight Halta's Raksha allies? Yes, you all have the same philosophy, but you're not really in the same school. The first group is probably much more closely linked with the local Cinder Coast pro-Solar Lunar, Lunar aiming to empower ordinary mortals, nature-loving Lunar and Lunar sorcerer than they are with some people on the other side of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the mistake is in viewing schools as necessarily organised or collective.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of it's going to be a matter of having learned from, and following the principles established by, a given Shanan-ya. Either because they're connected to the initial Lunars who found you and helped you get your caste, or because their reputation has travelled far and wide and you deliberately sought them out to learn from them.<br /> <br /> Either that, or because you distantly heard about the details, maybe read some literature, and became convinced of or aligned with their particular viewpoint and describe yourself as an adherent of it for a number of reasons, including being a convenient shorthand to describe yourself to other Lunars.<br /> <br /> I read the description in the preview, and my thought went to schools of thought in terms of academia, philosophy, theology, things like that. If one describes themselves as being part of a particular school of interpretation of the Torah, I don't think that needs to imply having direct, frequent contact with other such scholars, or having learned directly from originators of the idea, just that it's the thing that worked most for you in your studies and it's the framework for your views and methods of analysis.<br /> <br /> There are probably going to be distantly removed schools that have independently formed fairly similar ideas, but that probably doesn't need to be talked about much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, not all Lunars of the region around An-Teng approve of its most prominent Shahan-Ya. Once Sharvara's most promising student, Radiant Moth turned her back on her teacher, believing that his power would lead only to ruin. She believes that Sharvara's hate of the Realm has blinded him to the threat of the black-armoured lord of the Thousand, a dark fortress a month's voyage from the City of Dead Flowers. Radiant Moth damned Sharvara's stupidity, and journeyed west in search of different allies. She has created her own school, which though smaller, now commands a pirate fleet amongst the Cinder Isles. But so far they've had not had great success against the Realm, and one of her students, Lintha Ng Zukarios, suggests alliance with the Lintha. But Radiant Moth fears she'd be making the same mistake she damned Sharvara for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just sounds like the basic model for the Silver Pact at work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271852#post1271852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why this edition more than ever? I've no particular objection, but I didn't get the impression Sidereals were significantly less invested in dealing with Solars/Lunars than previous editions. Unless you mean because of Rakan Thulio and his Getimians?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thulio, and a certain responsibility for Exigents.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T16:20:58-08:00","id":1271867,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d be interested in Lunars based in Yu-Shan for sure. It seemed weird to me that the Lunars has almost zero presence in heaven in Ex2. Especially since Lunars had such a great panoply of knacks to just take on the mien of divinities. Now they would have to rely on mixing with those Heavens Dragons and the human populace that exists to entertain the sidereals. Regardless, I think Lunar hijinks in Heaven would be a great campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T16:21:14-08:00","id":1271868,"title":"","content":"As far as party invitations, I'm pretty doubtful.<br /> <br /> Heaven's Dragons are from a society comprised of &quot;tight-knit extended families&quot; that &quot;live on the periphery of Yu-Shan&quot; &quot;within tenements carved from subdivided palaces or divine slums teeming with unemployed gods&quot;. Only &quot;a few rise to prominence as freelance agents of Heaven, gaining employment in the celestial bureaucracy or carrying out the agendas of a divine patron.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even before Arcane Fate, there's a pretty big social and geographic distance from Sidereals, and a pretty clear indication that there isn't substantial work-related contact either. A tendency of the tight-knit clans to dislike/resent &quot;outsider&quot;/&quot;elitist&quot; Sidereals would seem to be the more likely reaction to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T17:19:23-08:00","id":1271877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1271868#post1271868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as party invitations, I'm pretty doubtful.<br /> <br /> Heaven's Dragons are from a society comprised of &quot;tight-knit extended families&quot; that &quot;live on the periphery of Yu-Shan&quot; &quot;within tenements carved from subdivided palaces or divine slums teeming with unemployed gods&quot;. Only &quot;a few rise to prominence as freelance agents of Heaven, gaining employment in the celestial bureaucracy or carrying out the agendas of a divine patron.&quot;<br /> <br /> Even before Arcane Fate, there's a pretty big social and geographic distance from Sidereals, and a pretty clear indication that there isn't substantial work-related contact either. A tendency of the tight-knit clans to dislike/resent &quot;outsider&quot;/&quot;elitist&quot; Sidereals would seem to be the more likely reaction to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow, I must have failed to properly internalise the full extent to those details. It definitely puts a lot of my thinking in a different light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T18:56:48-08:00","id":1271902,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the other week when I was pondering putting Heaven's Dragons in a game I was thinking something like Soul Society with Sids have a close relationship, but they're not that at all. Although in my personal games I'll likely have them as 5 Clans with a Celestial Patron seen as a Divine Ancestor giving them patronage. Just not bound up with Sids.<br /> <br /> Even in 1e they had Lunars with ties to Celestial Gods working to achieve their ends and seeking allies. The Bureau of Nature(obviously) was working with them, and in 2e they go into a lot of detail with how Luna and Gaia's positions gave Lunars ties that could be worked with. With reworking of things I imagine at least one Shahan-ya or two is working with Celestial God allies to achieve their ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T22:30:11-08:00","id":1272125,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m gonna just say that \u201cThe Monkey King beats up Heaven\u201d is too cool a classic image to entirely forbid it from Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/61nuXrvqNgI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/61nuXrvqNgI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/61nuXrvqNgI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/61nuXrvqNgI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T04:34:40-08:00","id":1272149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1272125#post1272125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m gonna just say that \u201cThe Monkey King beats up Heaven\u201d is too cool a classic image to entirely forbid it from Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Classic images get a lot of leeway, because they don't need to function within a balanced game or consistent setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T04:45:08-08:00","id":1272150,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's anything stopping you having a lunar in heaven as an <i>antagonistic</i> force. It's more the &quot;Yeah, they just live there, openly. Everyone's cool with that&quot; thing that needs a bit of thought put into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T05:42:46-08:00","id":1272158,"title":"","content":"We had a getmetian who was employed as a consultant by the Sidereals--I'd be suprised a Lunar would be impossible.<br /> ...<br /> ...Of course, the Monkey King is a high essence lunar, who gets his job by being to powerful to ignore and actually winning almost every fight he has. That would be ...a bizzare character, because it brings to mind an Elder Lunar, camping out in the Heavens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T05:37:15-08:00","id":1272362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1269735#post1269735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of my animosity and confusion is quite genuine. All the references still don't line up in my point of view, and likely still wouldn't even if a bunch of people didn't name a fan project &amp;quot;Terrible Argent Witches&amp;quot; after razzing on me, personally, in threads about various Lunar topics such as the spirit shape back in 2012. Well, the insults were a bit more serious than that, but I would have left it there, had Revlid not decided back after new year's 2015 to revisit many of the same topics in a couple of attack posts on the GITP mega thread because I dared to voice issues with TAW.<br /> <br /> And then Revlid got hired as a freelancer to work on Lunars, so there's no staying in a different part of the community and ignoring him. So there's that to consider, too, but I think I'm edging up on a ban for talking about that on this forum. I might as well try to quit Exalted again like in July... not that it worked very well, as you can tell from the fact that I eventually came back. There's no landing zone for that launch; just crashing back into the pad. In any case, apologies for not divulging that sooner, but my head is not in a good place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That was in tandem with a reference to Old Man Spider, so it still didn't and doesn't click in my head. It was also jarring to me at the time he made it because of the longtime &amp;quot;claim&amp;quot; on the character held by V:tM, and this was back around 2002. It's still jarring to me that it sticks with other people, because first edition Lunars were reportedly the very essence of 11th hour design changes, a lack of any sort of structure or outline, and other various issues, like the method of producing beastfolk.<br /> <br /> But if that's the direction, I guess that's the direction.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div>Is be rather sad if you left and stayed gone. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Far to many people take things to seriously here, including you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, but over all you\u2019ve been quite insightful, especially on matters concerning biology, and linguistics. And too many acronyms! I forgot everyone\u2019s old avatars and names back in the day! I know I sometimes confused Saur ops with Tornado Wolf but I know they is actually Sunder Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T04:18:17-08:00","id":1273246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1272158#post1272158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had a getmetian who was employed as a consultant by the Sidereals--I'd be suprised a Lunar would be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know his exact status, I remember being disapointed by Marilaq a'Lam because I thought the idea of Malfeas having an ambassador in Yu-Shan might open the way to an Infernal Exalt eventually holding the position. Unfortunately Marilaq was both a prisoner and another in a long, long line of Yozi trojan horses, that doesn't mean my dreams of cold war style politics between Heaven and Hell were crushed but that if it happens it'll be in spite of her not because of her. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T05:54:32-08:00","id":1273250,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m supposing that schools have to be political and a-geological, so that storytellers and players can have characters of whatever school they please regardless of geography.<br /> <br /> Shahan-ya was, I think, one of the highest of First Editions preponderance of ranks; fitting for Lunars with potentially global influence.<br /> <br /> It also leaves room for re-using one of the lower ranks to denote a lesser teacher/mentor figure who is more geographically oriented and available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T05:55:16-08:00","id":1273251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">We had a getmetian who was employed as a consultant by the Sidereals--I'd be suprised a Lunar would be impossible.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> I think that a Getimian working for the Bureau of Destiny is something that would make more sense even if there ends up being considerable animosity between those Exalted, because even if the powers are different, they're still operating on a similar axis.<br /> <br /> A Lunar feels rather out of place on grounds of both the significant bad blood, and maybe not really having the appropriate skill set.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T15:31:41-08:00","id":1273340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273251#post1273251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that a Getimian working for the Bureau of Destiny is something that would make more sense even if there ends up being considerable animosity between those Exalted, because even if the powers are different, they're still operating on a similar axis.<br /> <br /> A Lunar feels rather out of place on grounds of both the significant bad blood, and maybe not really having the appropriate skill set.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT]</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it is possible that the Sidereals could attempt to pull a Cult of the Illuminated with Lunars, getting to them before existing Lunars just after Exaltation and selling them a technically true but biased narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T20:03:16-08:00","id":1273377,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but, again, Lunars lack the means to weave the threads of destiny. What would a Lunar in the employ of Heaven even do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T22:27:40-08:00","id":1273394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273377#post1273377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe, but, again, Lunars lack the means to weave the threads of destiny. What would a Lunar in the employ of Heaven even do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they learned their lesson about letting Exalted tend the Peaches of Immortality long ago, so that\u2019s out. A meaningless bureaucratic position might work?<br /> <br /> I mean, if the whole point is to take the Lunar out of circulation, then having them work a random desk job for the rest of their life seems doable in theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T00:35:13-08:00","id":1273405,"title":"","content":"I strongly suspect that being able to actually Weave destinies is a useful but non-core aspect of the fact that this is an <b>Exalt</b>. Titan slaying god-weapons incarnated in the more-than-mortal flesh of a hero chosen by the greatest of the gods to work their will upon the dusty planes of earth.<br /> <br /> If Heaven can't find something productive to do with a loyal Lunar, they are either incredibly uncreative or possessed of the sort of institutional blindness that precedes a terrible collapse when someone with a modicum of flexibility notices them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T03:28:34-08:00","id":1273412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273394#post1273394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if the whole point is to take the Lunar out of circulation, then having them work a random desk job for the rest of their life seems doable in theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Essence Fever? Captain, no it doesn't.<br /> <br /> At least the Cult of the Illuminated sells Solars a narrative that tells them they're destined for greatness and doing things that Solars are already inclined to do, it just tries to steer them along a particular moral axis. Exactly what narrative is one trying to sell a fresh Lunar, that they're likely to particularly buy into?<br /> <br /> It makes me think about how the writers of Manual: Infernals talked about how the Yozi mechanisms to try to entice the Green Sun Princes were ultimately crude and doomed to failure, because there was nothing they could offer that those Exalted couldn't eventually realise that they could acquire for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T04:20:31-08:00","id":1273415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273405#post1273405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I strongly suspect that being able to actually Weave destinies is a useful but non-core aspect of the fact that this is an <b>Exalt</b>. Titan slaying god-weapons incarnated in the more-than-mortal flesh of a hero chosen by the greatest of the gods to work their will upon the dusty planes of earth.<br /> <br /> If Heaven can't find something productive to do with a loyal Lunar, they are either incredibly uncreative or possessed of the sort of institutional blindness that precedes a terrible collapse when someone with a modicum of flexibility notices them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked this post, but a counter argument: Heaven is by canon mostly a huge, corrupt structure that does not achieve much that is productive other than the enrichment of the gods, and as a venue for status and rank games of the gods. This is not to say that it's incompetent in defending its interests, but does not offer much unless you are content to live a life of luxury among beings that are not exactly human (in the manner of the something like the gods of Spirited Away and the Gods of Pegana and the like).<br /> <br /> (Because of the necessities of the game that an actual, active, functional modern massive bureaucratic government staffed by literal deities would probably not lead to a world that looks much like the Age of Sorrows!).<br /> <br /> The Bureau of Destiny is about the only branch that's somewhat functional or active in the world (and because being a Sidereal wouldn't be interesting if it weren't), and that's not a place for Lunar Exalted's talents to be used in the manner that even a Getimian's talents accommodated.<br /> <br /> (Of course, this all was easier with the assumptions of earlier editions, but I think you can still swing it with what we know).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T10:28:40-08:00","id":1273464,"title":"","content":"Considering there's a ton we don't know about Lunars in this edition and what they're capable of. And the few charms we do have suggest Lunars are really good at working over spirits to get what they want I...don't see how folks are coming to the conclusion that Lunars are suddenly fucked. At the bare minimum you have someone with a ton of flexibility that can be tossed at any problem and come out reasonably well unless it completely outclasses them. Just by nature of Attribute Excellencies and stunting in other attributes to increase the cap.<br /> <br /> Heaven is way more than just the Bureau of Destiny. The other Departments and Bureaus would love to have an Exalt willing to go into Creation and troubleshoot problems for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T13:13:28-08:00","id":1273483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273464#post1273464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I...don't see how folks are coming to the conclusion that Lunars are suddenly fucked.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, neither do I!<br /> <br /> ...Is... is it there at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the bare minimum you have someone with a ton of flexibility that can be tossed at any problem and come out reasonably well unless it completely outclasses them. Just by nature of Attribute Excellencies and stunting in other attributes to increase the cap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are characters really thinking in terms of their respective dice caps?<br /> <br /> I know that's kind of nitpicky, it just strikes me as a really underwhelming example to give.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heaven is way more than just the Bureau of Destiny. The other Departments and Bureaus would love to have an Exalt willing to go into Creation and troubleshoot problems for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and people in Hell want the suffering of all humanity in perpetuity. This line of discussion doesn't really go into what Lunars are getting out of the situation, and feels like it does them a bit of a disservice in its approach of treating them like employees to be headhunted.<br /> <br /> With the Sidereal Exalted, that they're functionaries of a system that is larger than themselves is kind of foundational to their image, so it becomes a thing that justifies itself several times over, from the process of their Exaltation to the form and structure of their powers, and this time around probably in the sensibilities conveyed in their Essence (to the point where I'm kind of expecting them to get something more of an Essence Tranquility, or other term that conveys that they're driven to preserve and sustain the harmony of reality's pattern, in lieu of personal grandeurs). They're designed from the ground up to slot into that kind of hierarchical environment.<br /> <br /> Lunars not only aren't, it's arguable that they'll have a lot of sensibilities that are kind of contrary to that, even before considering any elements such as them all basically having a deeply ingrained psychological hangup about the Realm and the Sidereals that even the ones who don't care about the past want to violently divest themselves of.<br /> <br /> Plus the whole thing that just kind of falls into referring to Lunars in an abstract aggregate, rather than any specific personages; in a context of big operational systems, that works more for the Sidereals (who play up their having less flexibility as an asset) and the Dragon Blooded (numerous enough that one can both have a greater array of personalities to sift through for specific qualities, and inclined to form into hierarchical organisations in their own right), but less so for Lunars.<br /> <br /> In short, it's kind of the same problem as when people have talked about a Lunar having a pet bloodline of non-descript Dragon Blooded, just going in the opposite direction. I think a lot of those details would plausibly make the situation sufficiently more complicated than &quot;they're powerful enough to be generally useful&quot; to make it consistent for the setting to not include one or more Lunars that have been indoctrinated into a general service to Heaven.<br /> <br /> Plus, as their powers to deal with spirits go, considering examples such as them having arcane insights into offering highly valued chiminage, and what I'm going to presume are some very fearsome powers to intimidate, I think that many in Yu-Shan might not consider them the best choice to bring people into line, either in terms of reinforcing bad habits or being pretty damn alienating.<br /> <br /> I can imagine situations in which an emissary of Heaven might seek out a particularly renowned or well-placed Lunar to try and bargain for them to do a specific thing on a case by case basis, but that's more an arrangement between peers, or making a diplomatic overture to a sovereign nation of one, than bringing a Lunar into the fold as somebody that you can just hand down orders to. I think they're less well suited to being part of the CIA than occasionally being the Afghani mujahedeen when you want some bloody mayhem inflicted on Soviets.<br /> <br /> (which might also have cases where Sidereals are foresighted enough to say &quot;this kind of support is a really bad idea in the long run)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T14:29:55-08:00","id":1273496,"title":"","content":"The discussion really did appear to lean on the idea that a Lunar would be wrecked in moving about these groups. The potential for a PC being limited by such seemed to me that people were discounting what an individual could bring to the table for their own concepts and ideas. That's why I said that. Not really viewing it as a full-on employee arrangement, but playing on allies and backing for your own ends. <br /> <br /> The nitpicky part about dicecaps is because its the most straightforward way to show off your power. Its also the most simplistic, and easy to say in a discussion that cuts to the heart of the matter. Lunars are nearly equal to Solars in power and their charms reflect this. We've seen like 2 charms for interacting with spirits out of dozens. I figure it can get pretty crazy. Just as they have charms for tearing things apart or disrupting a system I figure they also have them for making things work and<br /> <br /> I'm not really speaking to any of the fuller organizational picture. These are groups that want something and a Lunar is capable of working it to their advantage if they're smart enough. This seems more like you took what I said in a direction I didn't intend.<br /> <br /> Yu-Shan is packed with Divine figures that would be valuable allies or terrible foes. Having connections to them would be interesting for a group to explore at their table. Perhaps I'm just not on the bandwagon of being supernegative with splats interacting, but I think it has legs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T17:42:36-08:00","id":1273520,"title":"","content":"I think it's mostly a matter of how one phrases it. Don't make it a thing that infringes on a Sidereal space. Don't make it something that tries to validate Lunars by giving them a Sidereal thing. Don't make service and action in Heaven a generic thing, tailor it to the circumstances. Certainly don't phrase it in terms of trying to deal with Lunars by getting to new ones first and training them to be servants.<br /> <br /> And given the tone that is being set up for Lunars in things like this preview... Yu-Shan as a whole shouldn't be Sidereal territory, but it's where Sidereal territory is, and the Sidereals are behind the engine that reigns over Creation trying to continuously murder Lunars, so it ought to feel meaningfully dangerous on both sides. Not to an extreme of &quot;you're at risk every second&quot;, but enough that they shouldn't treat it casually. There's too much bad blood on both sides.<br /> <br /> So like, even if a Lunar is there as the guest of or on official business with some ranking god, I think there ought to be an underlying tension that some Sidereals are going to plot to take advantage of an opportunity, or somebody is going to be fairly salty and make a move for personal reasons, because it's likely that in the Fivescore Fellowship, you're never more than two steps away from somebody who lost a colleague to a Lunar in a nasty way.<br /> <br /> And if you're there in secret (or move around secretly in between your official business)... it's probably easier for Sidereals to make dealing with you official business, because that's probably not on for people not doing it officially under any circumstances.<br /> <br /> It makes me think about how... I'm not sure when exactly the idea (or mechanics to back it up) of the Jade Pleasure Dome having wards to detect or fight off intruders, but I think that it's a good idea to make the restrictions on that place enforceable in the face of the Exalted, and I think that they establish a precedent for any official institution of Heaven that would have reason to keep people out or from listening in to have a similar system, that a Lunar might be taking a risk with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T18:34:24-08:00","id":1273527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273412#post1273412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly what narrative is one trying to sell a fresh Lunar, that they're likely to particularly buy into?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it never hurts to start with the one where they\u2019ll have a house and a real job. If that\u2019s not enough you just give them the same pitch Sidereals get: blah blah you\u2019re literally helping the world work correctly blah blah you get to visit interesting places and do big important things blah blah oh and if a Creation Lunar ever tries to turn you against your friends and coworkers well what do <i>they</i> know anyway they didn\u2019t grow up here like you did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-08T19:12:49-08:00","id":1273537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well it never hurts to start with the one where they\u2019ll have a house and a real job.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> The phrasing probably needs to be adjusted a bit to be something that doesn't sound like it's being pitched to a modern-day university graduate. Like, assuming &quot;a real job&quot; is really a phrase that anybody would use in Creation (with appropriate corrections for language), why does somebody who's become a Lunar care? Is a real job something that they were brought up to value and want?<br /> <br /> You're not talking about a world where people are going into a capitalist job market, people are generally growing up with the expectation that their job will either be the same thing that their parents did, or the thing that the person they were effectively sold to was teaching them, when it's not a case of &quot;good job, you managed to survive into your twenties, head on down to the docks or the fields every now and then and try to outbid everybody else to get some hard labour for the day or the harvest season, and be prepared for a lot of hungry nights and aimless days in the meantime&quot;.<br /> <br /> But okay, having established the background of the majority of people in Creation (at least those who live in a stratified society centred around agrarian military, urban, or religious elites), one might go with the idea of telling them &quot;hey, life always seemed like it would suck, but now here's your prospect to get a really prestigious way of exchanging labour for rewards&quot;, but... the Lunar instinctively knows that they're a shapeshifter, right? Like, why should they want a job when they probably have the means of acquiring everything they need or want directly through strength or guile, assuming their power doesn't kind of redefine their priorites in what need or want even is? I think there are good odds that somebody who just acquired the ability to turn into a bird will be interested in seeing what it's like to live as a bird (albeit one that is a lot less susceptible to disease or predators).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that\u2019s not enough you just give them the same pitch Sidereals get</div> </div> </div> </div>That pitch probably works a lot better for Sidereals because they spend their whole lives prior to becoming Exalted being guided and conditioned towards understanding and accepting the role that is going to be ultimately bestowed upon them. Maybe it would be fairly effective on a specific given Lunar who has had a real void of meaning or drive in their life up to that point, leaving them highly susceptible to a charismatic and impressive person coming in and saying &quot;this thing that I'm giving you will be your purpose now&quot;, but I kind of feel like the experience of being a Lunar is going to start giving them alternative answers after a relatively short time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">you get to visit interesting places and do big important things</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though a lot of Lunars have the means and the latitude to go to more interesting places and do more things they value personally than Sidereals do. Like, even apart from the constraints of their job, Sidereals aren't as natively good at going just about anywhere that Lunars can (so long as they can find an animal that can naturally enter that environment). <br /> <br /> I mean, hey, if you want to fly somewhere, you don't need to be at higher Essence and sacrifice a valued and loyal pet or one of the few friends who can remember you when you're not around to do it. You've got decent travel options.<br /> <br /> And a decent amount of the central premise of the game kind of relies on the Exalted intuitively understanding a bunch of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">if a Creation Lunar ever tries to turn you against your friends and coworkers well what do</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>they</i><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> know anyway they didn\u2019t grow up here like you did.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Wait, is this a pitch intended specifically for a Lunar who was Chosen from amongst the small number of humans who actually reside in Yu-Shan?<br /> <br /> If the character concept is &quot;you're the one person ever in the Second Age who had actually grown up in Yu-Shan and then became a Lunar&quot;, I can see that as something in which some Sidereals might decide there's a reasonable basis for indoctrination, and it can actually work, and their voices prevail over the ones who would say the situation is ideal for killing them outright, but it still feels like it should be a precarious situation.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact Lunar might have a harder time selling one on the values of taking one's rightful place as a true Prince of the Earth, unless they try to slip in the idea that the Lunar can bring the people they value in under their own protection.<br /> <br /> Still, Sidereals dealing with the Lunar residing in Heaven within their systems might have a difficult time dealing with the viscerally experienced flashbacks to a bunch of themselves cutting down somebody the Lunar feels they really cared about, and it's probably going to be awkward for Chejop Kejak to explain to the young inductee why seeing him so often provokes the weirdest nagging sense that he's a vile traitor who needs to be destroyed. </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T02:14:40-08:00","id":1273565,"title":"","content":"To reiterate, my horse in this race is what a Lunar could potentially do vs. what Lunars have already done.<br /> <br /> To me there's value in a PC breaking new ground and meeting with gods who had assumed the Lunar Exalted died out at the end of the First Age and the actions of any hypothetical Lunar NPCs who got there before them should be measured against that.<br /> <br /> It's a different scenario to the Heavens Dragons because they need the words to avoid being Kejak's bitches and escape two editions of Yu-Shan not really viewing them as people.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T09:23:30-08:00","id":1273590,"title":"","content":"I was given to understand that in 3E that Lunars from urban or &quot;civilized&quot; backgrounds were now a decent fraction of the newly chosen, and that it was a perfectly viable path of development to focus on being e.g. a social predator rather than some flavor of barbarian. If a lunar could work as an urbanite they could probably get along just fine in Yu-Shan.<br /> <br /> As for the sales pitch, Yu-Shan has a much greater ability to lavish vast amounts of luxuries on a potential recruit. Its libraries contain untold amounts of historical and occult knowledge otherwise scattered as fragments over the face of Creation. Its dojos have instructors in all fields of human and godly endeavors with the power and experience to engage with a young Exalt at their own level rather than as mortal instructing demigods. Even a measure of legitimacy could be a powerful incentive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T10:04:42-08:00","id":1273592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273590#post1273590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was given to understand that in 3E that Lunars from urban or &quot;civilized&quot; backgrounds were now a decent fraction of the newly chosen, and that it was a perfectly viable path of development to focus on being e.g. a social predator rather than some flavor of barbarian. If a lunar could work as an urbanite they could probably get along just fine in Yu-Shan.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably hard to effectively be a social predator in a city filled with powerful gods, where you're in a rather fierce competition with a sector that is powerful and respected and important, and you can't shapeshift into most of the important people (and I'd propose that trying to pass yourself off as a Sidereal while being around other Sidereals for a long time is a fairly dicey proposal).<br /> <br /> Yu-Shan is rather distinct as cities go.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T10:53:48-08:00","id":1273600,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm.... A Lunar learns a number of things from one of the unemployed gods that left for Creation and sneaks into Yu-Shan, goes into the slums, and starts rabble rousing. If they play it right, they might set off a Divine Class War and mess up heaven.<br /> <br /> If they do it wrong, they\u2019ll find out the hard way that Yu-Shan justice is very swift when it wants to be and exceptionally harsh, assuming a couple Sidereals don\u2019t assassinate them first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T16:07:38-08:00","id":1273635,"title":"","content":"Talking about generic incentives for generic Lunars to take up a generic &quot;serving Heaven&quot; job runs into all the problems that pretty much have to exist to explain why large numbers of Lunars aren't an arm of the Heavenly bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, that a particular Lunar was successfully recruited to fill a particular position for Heaven with particular incentives that would appeal to that particular character is a perfectly good story/background that shouldn't be ruled out.<br /> <br /> For example, a Lunar who happens to be a particular lover of secrets and hidden knowledge could plausibly be recruited to serve the Forbidding Manse of Ivy as an infiltration specialist, alternating field work in Creation (surely there are cases where intervention could use the talents of a shape-stealing trickster) with periods of almost-recreational study of secrets from the archives. Or a social predator and sybarite who enjoys the pleasures available in the Cerulean Lute of Harmony between assignments to make sure star-crossed lovers <i>stay</i> star-crossed.<br /> <br /> The important thing is that it be rare, which all the generic arguments do.<br /> <br /> (On the antagonist-of-Sidereals side, a Lunar who stole the shape of one of the members of a clan of Heaven's Dragons would potentially be in an interesting position to cause chaos in Yu-Shan.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T18:17:17-08:00","id":1273641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273537#post1273537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, is this a pitch intended specifically for a Lunar who was Chosen from amongst the small number of humans who actually reside in Yu-Shan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Has this train of thought not been specifically about those ones? Maybe I missed something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T18:51:23-08:00","id":1273644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273635#post1273635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For example, a Lunar who happens to be a particular lover of secrets and hidden knowledge could plausibly be recruited to serve the Forbidding Manse of Ivy as an infiltration specialist, alternating field work in Creation (surely there are cases where intervention could use the talents of a shape-stealing trickster) with periods of almost-recreational study of secrets from the archives. Or a social predator and sybarite who enjoys the pleasures available in the Cerulean Lute of Harmony between assignments to make sure star-crossed lovers <i>stay</i> star-crossed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that part of my objection to this is the manner in which the overall game sets up each of the groups of Exalted as having a group identity based on their common history and capabilities, that I've fairly bought into, and in which entering edge cases such as &quot;the Department of Secrets will accept a non-Sidereal who has a general inclination towards concealment and infiltration&quot; kind of grate against it. It's like, that the Department of Secrets is by default a Sidereal thing is a foundation on which I'm going to try and build explanations for them having a very particular need for the very particular capabilities and personal inclinations of Sidereals (especially of that Caste), because otherwise, why not just have it be a mixed group of Exalted altogether?<br /> <br /> Much like the manner in which the Silver Pact is a particular Lunar thing, rather than an overall alliance of figures arrayed against the Realm and its Sidereal backers.<br /> <br /> It might be a bit contrived, but the initial image is something that I found compelling enough to make it work for.<br /> <br /> The other approach would be to take whatever elements might make one assume that Lunars aren't generally part of the Bureau of Destiny and make tension arising from the presence or possibility of them an explicit source of drama in the narrative; actively harnessing the distinct rarity of it, and why that might be so, to strengthen the story a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(On the antagonist-of-Sidereals side, a Lunar who stole the shape of one of the members of a clan of Heaven's Dragons would potentially be in an interesting position to cause chaos in Yu-Shan.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that a Lunar infiltrating Yu-Shan like that should be a thing that has happened and can happen, but framed as the sort of thing that tends to need to be a short term operation. I think that's necessary for a sense of consistency both with the people who live in Yu-Shan, and the kinds of enemies or infiltrators that they might have; make the presence of powerful gods felt, and make sense of why powerful figures such as other Celestial Exalted can't quite treat the place as their stomping grounds, even when they might reasonably be assumed to want to.<br /> <br /> I think it's a lot like why The Realm is apparently going to address ways that the Dragon Blooded deal with being enemies with shapeshifters, because otherwise that seems like an advantage that should be very large.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T22:07:40-08:00","id":1273668,"title":"","content":"In previous editions, they have in a way been unclear about Exalts working in Heaven. SIdereals working for the Bureaus was often presented as a loophole and there was supposed to be almost a separation of Heaven and Earth on governments. This got kind of effed up with things like the Bureau of Seasons being ran in the First Age by a Solar. In that kind of context, Lunars working in various branches of the Celestila Hierarchy isn't so strange.<br /> <br /> If in 3e there's a bit more stirct well, &quot;Exalts rule Earth&quot; while the Dragons of Heaven and Sidereals are kind of the exception due to loop holes, that would be a way to work on that. Exalts don't get Heavenly jobs normally as those jobs aren't for Exalts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T00:40:30-08:00","id":1273683,"title":"","content":"In agreement really with Verzio and Blaque's emphasis I think (I say emphasis because I think it is emphasis and not a disagreement on the total range of factors?).<br /> <br /> I'm more comfortable with presenting it that it's not improbable that out of the 400(?), there's not one who has been approached at the right time with the balance of incentives and personal history, who is still alive.<br /> <br /> I'm less comfortable with departing from the idea that Exalts who don't serve in Heaven are ill fit to serve in Heaven for reasons that other than because this violates the compact with the Exalted and because their gods do not believe (correctly or incorrectly) this best suits their talents. Particularly because the Bureaucracy of Heaven encompasses some pretty strange and quirky gods who I would guess probably have wilder natures (and natures less suited to being part of a bureaucracy) than the Lunars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-10T05:23:31-08:00","id":1273702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This got kind of effed up with things like the Bureau of Seasons being ran in the First Age by a Solar.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Whereabouts was that? The closest thing that I know of to it was the Solar Deliberative being the ones who designed Creation's climate, which the Bureau of Seasons was then required to implement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that kind of context, Lunars working in various branches of the Celestila Hierarchy isn't so strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a bit reductive, unless elaborated on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If in 3e there's a bit more stirct well, &quot;Exalts rule Earth&quot; while the Dragons of Heaven and Sidereals are kind of the exception due to loop holes, that would be a way to work on that. Exalts don't get Heavenly jobs normally as those jobs aren't for Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm less concerned with making up rules for Heaven than I am with everything I was talking about with the aesthetic elements of different Exalted having their structural niches. A bloodline of Dragon Blooded living in Yu-Shan, with some members uncommonly working for the Celestial Order, violates that less for me when the other side to &quot;Dragon Blooded slot is in ruling the Realm&quot; would be them having slots in being organised groups in dedicated service to another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Particularly because the Bureaucracy of Heaven encompasses some pretty strange and quirky gods who I would guess probably have wilder natures (and natures less suited to being part of a bureaucracy) than the Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T05:44:58-08:00","id":1274698,"title":"","content":"There is always the difference of what is common, rare, or unique. So even if Sids don't have any interest on taking on a Lunar that have shown to align with their interest, there is always that sliver of a chance one of those being indoctrinated in Yu-Shan in preparation for being a Sid becomes a Lunar instead.<br /> <br /> In that case, there is the option to kill the Lunar, and it will Exalt somewhere else in someone most likely not in favor of the Sids way of seeing thing; put the poor sap on something unimportant, or see the Lunar as a potential asset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T07:50:12-08:00","id":1274716,"title":"","content":"That's not really compatible with how Sidereals have been presented. You're either going to be a Sidereal (and thus aren't eligible to become a Lunar), or you aren't (and thus aren't going to be groomed to become a Sidereal).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T08:07:36-08:00","id":1274720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274716#post1274716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really compatible with how Sidereals have been presented. You're either going to be a Sidereal (and thus aren't eligible to become a Lunar), or you aren't (and thus aren't going to be groomed to become a Sidereal).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I disagree.<br /> <br /> Just that the odds that a Lunar shard would be available and a Sid to be would be selected is so slim it has probably never happened.<br /> <br /> Out of Fate stuff can change things so what the Sids believe should happen, and what actually transpires isn't always the same. Just this isn't something they can correct, as that person now isn't available anymore for a Sid Exaltation. Considering how the Great Curse affects Sids, I would say it just isn't anything they ever contemplated.<br /> <br /> After all, not everyone becoming a Sid have been foretold to become one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T08:16:34-08:00","id":1274723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274720#post1274720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I disagree.<br /> <br /> Just that the odds that a Lunar shard would be available and a Sid to be would be selected is so slim it has probably never happened.<br /> <br /> Out of Fate stuff can change things so what the Sids believe should happen, and what actually transpires isn't always the same. Just this isn't something they can correct, as that person now isn't available anymore for a Sid Exaltation. Considering how the Great Curse affects Sids, I would say it just isn't anything they ever contemplated.<br /> <br /> After all, not everyone becoming a Sid have been foretold to become one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It actually depends on a bit. As I understand at least before, while a Sidereal's Exaltation is not foretold, it is fated. They're in effect born already with the Exaltation in 1e at least. It's just the Second Breath is something that's fated to occur later. As kind of already noted, if you were going to Exalt a Sidereal, you're a Sidereal. If youw eren't, you never were going to be.<br /> <br /> Note also in context of 3e, the nature of &quot;out of Fate&quot; as a big &quot;Sidereals can'ta ccount for this and have something big of their thematics not work&quot; is probably not as prevalant. We laso don't know how thier Great Curse operates anymore. In addition, the Maidens still pick likely lifetimes they think fit the needs of their Chosen. I am pretty sure they are good at telling Luna &quot;That one is mine already&quot; if need be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T08:23:42-08:00","id":1274724,"title":"","content":"I think the way sidereal exaltation works is that the exaltation actually &quot;occurs&quot; at birth but sits around dormant for a decade or two until the new sidereal is ready.<br /> <br /> So you can no more exalt a sidereal to be than you could a solar or dragon blooded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T08:27:11-08:00","id":1274725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274723#post1274723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It actually depends on a bit. As I understand at least before, while a Sidereal's Exaltation is not foretold, it is fated. They're in effect born already with the Exaltation in 1e at least. It's just the Second Breath is something that's fated to occur later. As kind of already noted, if you were going to Exalt a Sidereal, you're a Sidereal. If youw eren't, you never were going to be.<br /> <br /> Note also in context of 3e, the nature of &quot;out of Fate&quot; as a big &quot;Sidereals can'ta ccount for this and have something big of their thematics not work&quot; is probably not as prevalant. We laso don't know how thier Great Curse operates anymore. In addition, the Maidens still pick likely lifetimes they think fit the needs of their Chosen. I am pretty sure they are good at telling Luna &quot;That one is mine already&quot; if need be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides how &quot;out of fate&quot; may work, what the Sids think is fated and what the Maidens think is fated may not be the same. A &quot;fated to become a Sidereal, but becomes a Lunar&quot; might also have been fated by the Maidens, but comes as a shock for the Sids.<br /> <br /> I don't see that as conflicting with anything I've read and remembers from either of the previous edition, and not really a conflict with what I've seen of third either from what I've seen so far. Still, I seems to read Exalted a tad different everyone else <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T09:33:12-08:00","id":1274732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1273702#post1273702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point. [/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR][/LEFT]</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. This discussion and Celestial Bureaucracy accommodating strange and quirky and other Exalted moves my mind to considering Exigents (but that's a tangent).<br /> <br /> Re: the Sidereal Lunar thing, it seems really improbable for the Sidereals to a) first mistake a person as a potential Sidereal (getting that bad a read on someone's essence) and not be corrected by the Maidens or events and b) that person then to be Exalted as a Lunar, whether I guess, metaphysically, the Exaltation is *in* them or not yet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T13:31:20-08:00","id":1274763,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I guess I have to agree. I mean, the Maidens did inform the Sids they missed such an important thing as the Great Contagion, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If it is possible for a &quot;fated for a Sidereal exaltation&quot; to exalt as a Solar or Lunar, it still is such a small chance it most likely only happen at the most once or twice during the entire existence of creation. So not wanting it still makes it easy to put in the &quot;it didn't even happened once&quot; category.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it is in the &quot;this is more important than the GC&quot; category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T14:00:56-08:00","id":1274768,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... My understanding is that, when a Sidereal dies, an unborn child is destined to inherit that Exaltation, much like how it works for the Dali Lama. Said destined children are usually left in place to fulfill their fates and Exalt, though I suspect they\u2019re watched to make sure they live that long. After they Exalt, they\u2019re scooped up and taken to Heaven for their real training.<br /> <br /> Sometimes said children are taken up to Heaven right after they\u2019re born and raised as Sidereals to be, but it\u2019s a pretty rare circumstance.<br /> <br /> As such, for one of those children to end up as a Lunar seems improbable enough that it can\u2019t just be a mistake. <br /> <br /> That said, if I was running a Sid focused game and one of the players came to me with this background, I\u2019d probably allow it with the proviso that whoever or whatever caused this whole sequence of events was going to become part of the campaign and that it meant that someone wanted your group to do something that required a Lunar bad enough to arrange this whole mess.<br /> <br /> Basically rather than random happenstance, I\u2019d make it enemy action and let that help drive the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T14:40:01-08:00","id":1274778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274768#post1274768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... My understanding is that, when a Sidereal dies, an unborn child is destined to inherit that Exaltation, much like how it works for the Dali Lama. Said destined children are usually left in place to fulfill their fates and Exalt, though I suspect they\u2019re watched to make sure they live that long. After they Exalt, they\u2019re scooped up and taken to Heaven for their real training.<br /> <br /> Sometimes said children are taken up to Heaven right after they\u2019re born and raised as Sidereals to be, but it\u2019s a pretty rare circumstance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. That don't match my interpretation of 2nd edition. Is that from 1st edition?<br /> <br /> This is from 2ed's MoEP: Sidereals<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Historically, elder Sidereals had considerable advance<br /> notice when one of the Five-Score Fellowship was destined<br /> to die and which mortal would take the Sidereal\u2019s place. In<br /> the First Age, mortals destined for Sidereal Exaltation were<br /> often spirited away from their families at a young age, to be<br /> trained in their future duties. Before the Usurpation, the<br /> Chosen of Endings had refined the process so well that a<br /> future Sidereal would usually be actively employed by his<br /> division in some menial capacity, prepared to take over<br /> his duties at the very moment of Exaltation. Those days<br /> are long gone. </div> </div> </div>Your interpretation must have made the Sids extremely understaffed for a couple of decades after the Great Contagion, instead of staffed with a lot of inexperienced Sids. That is, if the Sids lost a lot of their numbers as 2ed hints at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As such, for one of those children to end up as a Lunar seems improbable enough that it can\u2019t just be a mistake. </div> </div> </div>I agree, because in that case they have sort of already Exalted; just not with any powers yet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T14:49:50-08:00","id":1274779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274763#post1274763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I guess I have to agree. I mean, the Maidens did inform the Sids they missed such an important thing as the Great Contagion, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Er... like, is the idea that the Maidens don't ever tell their chosen anything, give them any orders, send them any messages, etc.? I don't think that's the canon! Or that they are as good at perceiving and passing on information about who they have themselves exalted as a vast out of fate conspiracy by the Deathlords, with huge implications that they may have mysterious reasons for allowing to unfold as the collapse of civilization?<br /> <br /> Like, I can see that they might consciously manipulate events to that outcome to serve some end (the Maidens are pretty much carte blanche characters to do whatever because they see and understand further than you can), with the big assumption that they can tell who Luna will choose (which is a big assumption I have more trouble with being in their purview actually, as a bit of an exception to their general foresight). Fodder for a weird NPC with divided loyalties and unusual history, raised in one house, come to power in another and so on, go for it (if you're willing to make that big assumption). But making a mistake themselves about it, or not passing the info on without such designs seems weird.<br /> <br /> (Though, mind, the Maidens actually telling the Sidereals about such a mistake is in my post actually the least of the hurdles I'd see it falling at, the main being the Sidereals own insight into their own nature and what is consistent with one who shows that nature before they are Exalted.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T14:54:19-08:00","id":1274781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274778#post1274778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your interpretation must have made the Sids extremely understaffed for a couple of decades after the Great Contagion, instead of staffed with a lot of inexperienced Sids. That is, if the Sids lost a lot of their numbers as 2ed hints at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I mean, they probably did and were, but a combination of having Fate on your side and rigging things along those lines and Sidereals being able to do Great Contagion medical care for their own lot (but unable to scale to the population as a whole; I mean, Citrine Poxes Style is pretty cool, for one) may have ended up arranging matters so that didn't happen as much. Though I don't know if 2nd hints they lost 9/10 of their numbers or something (oh 2nd, you incorrigible little scamp).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T15:09:37-08:00","id":1274784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274778#post1274778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. That don't match my interpretation of 2nd edition. Is that from 1st edition?<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>It is mentioend again in the book <i>Scroll of Heroes</i> actually. When a Sidereal dies, her successor is conceived shortly after. It is literally their fate to have a Second Breath as a Sidereal when they take their first breath. It's not just that the Maidens take people from lives that fit their Chosen. They select people who <i>will lead lives that lead to them being Chosen</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274778#post1274778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your interpretation must have made the Sids extremely understaffed for a couple of decades after the Great Contagion, instead of staffed with a lot of inexperienced Sids. That is, if the Sids lost a lot of their numbers as 2ed hints at.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is as I gather exactly what happened. Sidereals have had a few major notable generational shifts, those being the Usurpation, Contagion and now a bit ofa die-off now in previous editions. Part of the reason Sidereal deaths are so painful is that i'ts not just a matter of someone experienced showing up in the next hwile. That person might not <i>even be born</i> for a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274778#post1274778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, because in that case they have sort of already Exalted; just not with any powers yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is basically how Sidereal Exaltation works in everything that's talkeda bout it since Sidereals 1e, save the 2e book which for some reason doesn't go into it (and then every book after that it comes up <i>does</i> go into it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T15:14:31-08:00","id":1274786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274781#post1274781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm... I mean, they probably did and were, but a combination of having Fate on your side and rigging things along those lines and Sidereals being able to do Great Contagion medical care for their own lot (but unable to scale to the population as a whole; I mean, Citrine Poxes Style is pretty cool, for one) may have ended up arranging matters so that didn't happen as much. Though I don't know if 2nd hints they lost 9/10 of their numbers or something (oh 2nd, you incorrigible little scamp).</div> </div> </div> </div>Second edition says on of the caught it through the Loom (which I find being in contradiction of Yu-Shan closing its gates for a long time). It also mention the Sids was the first to die, fighting the Balorean Crusade (which either ignores the Lunars, or have the Lunars being a lot better at fighting the Crusade).<br /> <br /> So I think they lost far less than 90%, but having to wait from the birth of the new host to the Exaltation would be a much harder blow than having the next Exalt right away even if they &quot;just&quot; lost 40-50%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T15:26:46-08:00","id":1274788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274784#post1274784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is mentioend again in the book <i>Scroll of Heroes</i> actually. When a Sidereal dies, her successor is conceived shortly after. It is literally their fate to have a Second Breath as a Sidereal when they take their first breath. It's not just that the Maidens take people from lives that fit their Chosen. They select people who <i>will lead lives that lead to them being Chosen</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so it is a matter of another case of 2nd ed contradicts itself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is as I gather exactly what happened. Sidereals have had a few major notable generational shifts, those being the Usurpation, Contagion and now a bit ofa die-off now in previous editions. Part of the reason Sidereal deaths are so painful is that i'ts not just a matter of someone experienced showing up in the next hwile. That person might not <i>even be born</i> for a bit. </div> </div> </div>A generation shift is one thing (as the Lunars have as well), and having the positions vacant for a couple of decades (assuming Sids normaly Exalts around 20 years of age).<br /> <br /> I also see the Usurpation being a lot more drawn out incident when it comes to Sids dying (and not being in the same numbers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is basically how Sidereal Exaltation works in everything that's talkeda bout it since Sidereals 1e, save the 2e book which for some reason doesn't go into it (and then every book after that it comes up <i>does</i> go into it.) </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned earlier, if the shard have already been attached, but being dormant, then it makes sense they are locked out from Exalting as anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T16:23:46-08:00","id":1274800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274784#post1274784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is mentioend again in the book <i>Scroll of Heroes</i> actually. When a Sidereal dies, her successor is conceived shortly after. It is literally their fate to have a Second Breath as a Sidereal when they take their first breath. It's not just that the Maidens take people from lives that fit their Chosen. They select people who <i>will lead lives that lead to them being Chosen</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I could find is this on page 157:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sidereals are also chosen before they are born,<br /> destined to Exalt as Viziers. As with Dragon-Blooded,<br /> weak-willed Sidereals either die early or learn to adapt<br /> to their situation, accepting their roles as guardians of<br /> Heaven and fate, however reluctantly. Those Chosen of<br /> the Maidens who were adventuring heroic mortals look<br /> at their earlier lives as training sessions that taught them<br /> valuable lessons. </div> </div> </div>While this somewhat supports a &quot;the shard is put in the next host while still in the uterus,&quot; I find it also supporting &quot;they sids can track the next host back to the parents before the new host is born&quot; combined with a bit of 2nd ed writing.<br /> <br /> Do you have a page number for what you referred to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T16:45:02-08:00","id":1274803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274800#post1274800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All I could find is this on page 157:<br /> <br /> While this somewhat supports a &quot;the shard is put in the next host while still in the uterus,&quot; I find it also supporting &quot;they sids can track the next host back to the parents before the new host is born&quot; combined with a bit of 2nd ed writing.<br /> <br /> Do you have a page number for what you referred to?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I meant actually. And generally how it's been talkeda bout by devs and the 1e book, which I don't have now. But yeah, when a Sidereal died, itw as a huge blow because well, their replacement and all that.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting in 3e &quot;shard&quot; isn't the right term for this, since this is a 3e thread and about Lunars in context of that. It's not quite a host and more like, you're born already Chosen and fated to have a Second Breath. Think it less an object and like, your life is pretty much decided before you were born by the forces of the Maidens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T16:53:41-08:00","id":1274804,"title":"","content":"Random First Age Scholar: &quot;Thinking of an exaltation as a distinct object is not particularly accurate, but it is occasionally a useful fiction when trying to understand the process.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T16:56:08-08:00","id":1274805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274803#post1274803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I meant actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we really are reading very different things into that text <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And generally how it's been talkeda bout by devs and the 1e book, which I don't have now. But yeah, when a Sidereal died, itw as a huge blow because well, their replacement and all that. </div> </div> </div>I guess I should dig into 1st ed a bit as well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's worth noting in 3e &quot;shard&quot; isn't the right term for this, since this is a 3e thread and about Lunars in context of that. It's not quite a host and more like, you're born already Chosen and fated to have a Second Breath. Think it less an object and like, your life is pretty much decided before you were born by the forces of the Maidens. </div> </div> </div>And I thought 2nd ed was contradicting itself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, I guess I should remind myself this is a thread about a dev blog for Ex3 Lunars and I'm arguing things that seems to go a bit off topic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T17:58:19-08:00","id":1274810,"title":"","content":"\u2026.. Nnnnnnope<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274732#post1274732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Amoth City-Smiter as an example of those gods who are still part of the system despite grating a bit, there was also a thing about how, when there were more Lunars into destroying civilisation on principle, he was said to make use of providing aid to them or hiring them for some specific work that he wanted. Probably aren't going to be as many Lunars of that bent, but that model of interaction can probably work for a few gods.<br /> <br /> At the moment, I'm thinking that taking up a residence and some work might be something that the odd Lunar can manage, but might often be unsatisfying for them in the long term (even if that's on the order of several centuries in relative peace).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T21:25:14-08:00","id":1274834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274810#post1274810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment, I'm thinking that taking up a residence and some work might be something that the odd Lunar can manage, but might often be unsatisfying for them in the long term (even if that's on the order of several centuries in relative peace).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's right about where I am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T08:56:00-08:00","id":1274897,"title":"","content":"I find it most useful to think of Exaltations -- at least, CELESTIAL Exaltations and their derivatives -- as divine, reincarnating souls born from the celestial gods.<br /> <br /> This is obviously not the case for Alchemicals, Liminals, or Dragon-Blooded. For the Alchemical Exalted, their bodies and condition are their Exaltation. For Liminals, their own personal souls seem indistinguishable from their Exaltation.<br /> <br /> For Dragon-Blooded, Exaltation seems like more of a second lower Po soul than a second higher Hun soul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T09:16:29-08:00","id":1274899,"title":"","content":"A terrestrial exaltation seems to be more rooted in the physical than other types, a bit like alchemicals.<br /> <br /> It's a soul, but one born of the mystic properties of their blood and unable to survive the death of their body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T11:02:44-08:00","id":1274909,"title":"","content":"The view I think is less like, a soul, which still has this discreet object quality to it, and more like a legacy or title. If that makes any sense. A bit I notice is langauge like &quot;host&quot; or something. It gives this sense of it being a parasite and separate. While being the inheritor of an Exaltation's like, lineage or legacy or whatnot, has a different feel to me about how it exists spaciotemporily.<br /> <br /> This matters especially with Sidereals. The Exaltation isn't so much a thing in the baby when they're born. It's a process that they are part of from birth, that continues whatever their predecessor was a part of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T11:50:07-08:00","id":1274921,"title":"","content":"I can't help but feel we've started a very interesting but also very distinct thread here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T12:19:52-08:00","id":1274928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1265540-dev-blog-the-lunar-exalted?p=1274921#post1274921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel we've started a very interesting but also very distinct thread here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. A bit of musing before we maybe spin this off into its own thing:<br /> <br /> For Terrestrials, Exaltation is very much a particular type of legacy, the legacy of blood family and their place within it.<br /> <br /> For Alchemicals, they are the embodiment of a legacy of heroism, brought to life by Autochthon's power.<br /> <br /> Liminals play up a very different angle on this - they were brought to life through someone else's driving emotions, through someone else's body/bodies. In an existence that has been/is shaped by others, they have to figure out who they are in relation to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}